u du langage","Polymorphisme en temps de compilation ou d''exécution"],"de":["Wahl zwischen Generics und Trait-Objekten","Leistungsverbesserung","Lesbarkeit des Codes","Abstraktion auf Sprachenebene","Polymorphismus zur Compile- oder Laufzeit"],"pt":["Escolha entre generics e trait objects","Polimorfismo em tempo de compilação ou execução","Otimização de desempenho","Minimização de custos de execução","Melhoria da legibilidade do código"],"ru":["Выбор между generics и trait objects","Полиморфизм во время компиляции или выполнения","Оптимизация производительности","Минимизация затрат на выполнение","Улучшение читаемости кода"],"ar":["اختيار بين generics و trait objects","التعددية في وقت الترجمة أو التنفيذ","تحسين الأداء","تقليل التكاليف في وقت التنفيذ","تحسين قراءة الكود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["零成本抽象","编译时多态性","运行时多态性","代码性能","可维护性","代码设计","编程概念"],"ja":["ゼロコスト抽象","コンパイル時多態性","ランタイム多態性","コードパフォーマンス","メンテナンス性","コード設計","プログラミング概念"],"ko":["제로 코스트 추상화","컴파일 타임 다형성","런타임 다형성","코드 성능","유지 보수성","코드 설계","프로그래밍 개념"],"es":["abstracción de costo cero","generics","trait objects","polimorfismo","rendimiento","legibilidad del código","programación","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["abstraction à coût nul","generics","trait objects","polymorphisme","performances","lisibilité du code","programmation","développement de logiciels"],"de":["kostenlose Abstraktion","Generics","Trait-Objekte","Polymorphismus","Leistung","Lesbarkeit des Codes","Programmierung","Softwareentwicklung"],"pt":["abstração de custo zero","polimorfismo","generics","trait objects","otimização de desempenho","programação eficiente"],"ru":["нулевая абстракция стоимости","полиморфизм","generics","trait objects","оптимизация производительности","эффективное программирование"],"ar":["تخفيض التكلفة الى الصفر","التعددية","generics","trait objects","تحسين الأداء","برمجة فعالة"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T04:13:19.580Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"m04-zero-cost","description":"CRITICAL: Use for generics, traits, zero-cost abstraction. Triggers: E0277, E0308, E0599, generic, trait, impl, dyn, where, monomorphization, static dispatch, dynamic dispatch, impl Trait, trait bound not satisfied, 泛型, 特征, 零成本抽象, 单态化","bodyPreview":"# Zero-Cost Abstraction\n\n> **Layer 1: Language Mechanics**\n\n## Core Question\n\n**Do we need compile-time or runtime polymorphism?**\n\nBefore choosing between generics and trait objects:\n- Is the type known at compile time?\n- Is a heterogeneous collection needed?\n- What''s the performance priority?\n\n---\n\n## Error → Design Question\n\n| Error | Don''t Just Say | Ask Instead |\n|-------|----------------|-------------|\n| E0277 | \"Add trait bound\" | Is this abstraction at the right level? |\n| E0308 | \"Fix t","body":"# Zero-Cost Abstraction\n\n> **Layer 1: Language Mechanics**\n\n## Core Question\n\n**Do we need compile-time or runtime polymorphism?**\n\nBefore choosing between generics and trait objects:\n- Is the type known at compile time?\n- Is a heterogeneous collection needed?\n- What''s the performance priority?\n\n---\n\n## Error → Design Question\n\n| Error | Don''t Just Say | Ask Instead |\n|-------|----------------|-------------|\n| E0277 | \"Add trait bound\" | Is this abstraction at the right level? |\n| E0308 | \"Fix the type\" | Should types be unified or distinct? |\n| E0599 | \"Import the trait\" | Is the trait the right abstraction? |\n| E0038 | \"Make object-safe\" | Do we really need dynamic dispatch? |\n\n---\n\n## Thinking Prompt\n\nBefore adding trait bounds:\n\n1. **What abstraction is needed?**\n   - Same behavior, different types → trait\n   - Different behavior, same type → enum\n   - No abstraction needed → concrete type\n\n2. **When is type known?**\n   - Compile time → generics (static dispatch)\n   - Runtime → trait objects (dynamic dispatch)\n\n3. **What''s the trade-off priority?**\n   - Performance → generics\n   - Compile time → trait objects\n   - Flexibility → depends\n\n---\n\n## Trace Up ↑\n\nWhen type system fights back:\n\n```\nE0277 (trait bound not satisfied)\n    ↑ Ask: Is the abstraction level correct?\n    ↑ Check: m09-domain (what behavior is being abstracted?)\n    ↑ Check: m05-type-driven (should use newtype?)\n```\n\n| Persistent Error | Trace To | Question |\n|-----------------|----------|----------|\n| Complex trait bounds | m09-domain | Is the abstraction right? |\n| Object safety issues | m05-type-driven | Can typestate help? |\n| Type explosion | m10-performance | Accept dyn overhead? |\n\n---\n\n## Trace Down ↓\n\nFrom design to implementation:\n\n```\n\"Need to abstract over types with same behavior\"\n    ↓ Types known at compile time → impl Trait or generics\n    ↓ Types determined at runtime → dyn Trait\n\n\"Need collection of different types\"\n    ↓ Closed set → enum\n    ↓ Open set → Vec<Box<dyn Trait>>\n\n\"Need to return different types\"\n    ↓ Same type → impl Trait\n    ↓ Different types → Box<dyn Trait>\n```\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Pattern | Dispatch | Code Size | Runtime Cost |\n|---------|----------|-----------|--------------|\n| `fn foo<T: Trait>()` | Static | +bloat | Zero |\n| `fn foo(x: &dyn Trait)` | Dynamic | Minimal | vtable lookup |\n| `impl Trait` return | Static | +bloat | Zero |\n| `Box<dyn Trait>` | Dynamic | Minimal | Allocation + vtable |\n\n## Syntax Comparison\n\n```rust\n// Static dispatch - type known at compile time\nfn process(x: impl Display) { }      // argument position\nfn process<T: Display>(x: T) { }     // explicit generic\nfn get() -> impl Display { }         // return position\n\n// Dynamic dispatch - type determined at runtime\nfn process(x: &dyn Display) { }      // reference\nfn process(x: Box<dyn Display>) { }  // owned\n```\n\n## Error Code Reference\n\n| Error | Cause | Quick Fix |\n|-------|-------|-----------|\n| E0277 | Type doesn''t impl trait | Add impl or change bound |\n| E0308 | Type mismatch | Check generic params |\n| E0599 | No method found | Import trait with `use` |\n| E0038 | Trait not object-safe | Use generics or redesign |\n\n---\n\n## Decision Guide\n\n| Scenario | Choose | Why |\n|----------|--------|-----|\n| Performance critical | Generics | Zero runtime cost |\n| Heterogeneous collection | `dyn Trait` | Different types at runtime |\n| Plugin architecture | `dyn Trait` | Unknown types at compile |\n| Reduce compile time | `dyn Trait` | Less monomorphization |\n| Small, known type set | `enum` | No indirection |\n\n---\n\n## Object Safety\n\nA trait is object-safe if it:\n- Doesn''t have `Self: Sized` bound\n- Doesn''t return `Self`\n- Doesn''t have generic methods\n- Uses `where Self: Sized` for non-object-safe methods\n\n---\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n| Anti-Pattern | Why Bad | Better |\n|--------------|---------|--------|\n| Over-generic everything | Compile time, complexity | Concrete types when possible |\n| `dyn` for known types | Unnecessary indirection | Generics |\n| Complex trait hierarchies | Hard to understand | Simpler design |\n| Ignore object safety | Limits flexibility | Plan for dyn if needed |\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n| When | See |\n|------|-----|\n| Type-driven design | m05-type-driven |\n| Domain abstraction | m09-domain |\n| Performance concerns | m10-performance |\n| Send/Sync bounds | m07-concurrency |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-20T05:08:25.267Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Rust-focused Agents needing advanced polymorphism and abstraction techniques, particularly those working with compile-time and runtime polymorphism.","zh":"非常适合需要高级多态性和抽象技术的Rust专注代理，特别是那些处理编译时和运行时多态性的代理。","ja":"Rustに焦点を当てたエージェントが高度な多相性と抽象化技術を必要とする場合、特にコンパイル時とランタイムの多相性を扱うエージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 다형성 및 추상화 기술이 필요한 러스트에 중점을 둔 에이전트에게 적합하며, 특히 컴파일 타임 및 런타임 다형성을 처리하는 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes centrados en Rust que necesitan técnicas avanzadas de polimorfismo y abstracción, particularmente aquellos que trabajan con polimorfismo en tiempo de compilación y en tiempo de ejecución.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents axés sur Rust nécessitant des techniques de polymorphisme et d''abstraction avancées, en particulier ceux qui travaillent avec le polymorphisme à la compilation et à l''exécution.","de":"Perfekt für auf Rust fokussierte Agenten, die erweiterte Polymorphismus- und Abstraktionstechniken benötigen, insbesondere solche, die mit Compile-Time- und Laufzeit-Polymorphismus arbeiten.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes focados em Rust que necessitam de técnicas avançadas de polimorfismo e abstração, particularmente aqueles que trabalham com polimorfismo em tempo de compilação e tempo de execução.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов, ориентированных на Rust, которым необходимы продвинутые техники полиморфизма и абстракции, особенно тех, кто работает с полиморфизмом во время компиляции и выполнения.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذين يركزون على Rust وهم بحاجة إلى تقنيات متقدمة من التعددية الشكلية والاستهلاك، خاصة أولئك الذين يعملون مع تعددية الشكل في وقت الترجمة ووقت التشغيل."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to make informed decisions between generics and trait objects, leveraging error codes like E0277 and E0308 to guide design questions and optimize performance priorities, while considering factors like heterogeneous collections and type knowledge at compile time.","zh":"赋予代理权衡泛型和特征对象之间的选择的能力，利用错误代码如E0277和E0308来指导设计问题和优化性能优先级，同时考虑编译时的异构集合和类型知识等因素。","ja":"エージェントがジェネリックとトレイトオブジェクトの間の選択を比較検討する能力を付与し、E0277やE0308などのエラーコードを使用して設計上の疑問を解決し、パフォーマンスの優先順位を最適化する，同时考虑编译时的异构集合和类型知识等因素。","ko":"에이전트가 제네릭과 트레이트 객체 간의 선택을 비교検討할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, E0277 및 E0308과 같은 오류 코드를 사용하여 설계 관련 문제를 해결하고 성능 우선순위를 최적화하며, 컴파일 타임의 이종 컬렉션 및 타입 지식 등을 고려합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes tomar decisiones informadas entre genéricos y objetos de rasgos, aprovechando códigos de error como E0277 y E0308 para guiar preguntas de diseño y optimizar prioridades de rendimiento, considerando factores como colecciones heterogéneas y conocimiento de tipos en tiempo de compilación.","fr":"Permet aux agents de prendre des décisions éclairées entre les génériques et les objets de traits, en exploitant les codes d''erreur tels que E0277 et E0308 pour guider les questions de conception et optimiser les priorités de performances, en tenant compte de facteurs tels que les collections hétérogènes et la connaissance des types au moment de la compilation.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, fundierte Entscheidungen zwischen Generics und Trait-Objekten zu treffen, indem sie Fehlercodes wie E0277 und E0308 nutzen, um Gestaltungsfragen zu leiten und Leistungsprioritäten zu optimieren, unter Berücksichtigung von Faktoren wie heterogenen Sammlungen und Typkenntnissen zur Compile-Zeit.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a tomar decisões informadas entre genéricos e objetos de traço, utilizando códigos de erro como E0277 e E0308 para orientar questões de design e otimizar prioridades de desempenho, considerando fatores como coleções heterogêneas e conhecimento de tipo em tempo de compilação.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью принимать обоснованные решения между generics и объектами trait, используя коды ошибок, такие как E0277 и E0308, для руководства вопросами дизайна и оптимизации приоритетов производительности, учитывая факторы, такие как гетерогенные коллекции и знания типов во время компиляции.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على اتخاذ قرارات مستنيرة بين العوامل العامة وأو tượng الصفة، باستخدام رموز الخطأ مثل E0277 و E0308 لتوجيه أسئلة التصميم وتحسين أولويات الأداء، مع مراعاة عوامل مثل المجموعات المتنوعة وال معرفة النوعية في وقت الترجمة."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging polymorphism-related errors using E0277 and E0308","Optimizing performance by choosing between compile-time and runtime polymorphism","Designing abstractions at the right level to avoid common pitfalls"],"zh":["使用E0277和E0308调试多态性相关错误","通过选择编译时和运行时多态性来优化性能","在合适的层次设计抽象以避免常见的陷阱"],"ja":["E0277とE0308を使用して多相性関連のエラーをデバッグする","コンパイル時とランタイムの多相性の選択によってパフォーマンスを最適化する","適切なレベルで抽象化を設計して一般的な落とし穴を避ける"],"ko":["E0277 및 E0308을 사용하여 다형성 관련 오류를 디버깅합니다.","컴파일 타임 및 런타임 다형성의 선택을 통해 성능을 최적화합니다.","적절한 수준에서 추상화를 설계하여 일반적인 함정을 피합니다."],"es":["Depuración de errores relacionados con el polimorfismo utilizando E0277 y E0308","Optimización del rendimiento eligiendo entre polimorfismo en tiempo de compilación y en tiempo de ejecución","Diseño de abstracciones a nivel adecuado para evitar trampas comunes"],"fr":["Débogage des erreurs liées au polymorphisme en utilisant E0277 et E0308","Optimisation des performances en choisissant entre polymorphisme à la compilation et à l''exécution","Conception d''abstractions au niveau approprié pour éviter les pièges courants"],"de":["Fehlerbehebung von Polymorphismus-bezogenen Fehlern unter Verwendung von E0277 und E0308","Leistungsoptimierung durch Auswahl zwischen Compile-Time- und Laufzeit-Polymorphismus","Entwurf von Abstraktionen auf geeignetem Niveau, um gängige Fallstricke zu vermeiden"],"pt":["Depurar erros relacionados ao polimorfismo usando E0277 e E0308","Otimizar o desempenho escolhendo entre polimorfismo em tempo de compilação e tempo de execução","Projetar abstrações no nível certo para evitar armadilhas comuns"],"ru":["Отладка ошибок, связанных с полиморфизмом, с помощью E0277 и E0308","Оптимизация производительности путем выбора между полиморфизмом во время компиляции и выполнения","Проектирование абстракций на правильном уровне, чтобы избежать распространенных ловушек"],"ar":["تصحيح أخطاء متعلقة بالتعددية الشكلية باستخدام E0277 و E0308","تحسين الأداء bằng اختیار بین التعددية الشكلية في وقت الترجمة ووقت التشغيل","تصميم التصرّفات على المستوى الصحيح لتجنب الفخاخ الشائعة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of Rust programming language","Focused on polymorphism and abstraction in Rust, may not be directly applicable to other languages"],"zh":["需要了解Rust编程语言","专注于Rust中的多态性和抽象化，可能不直接适用于其他语言"],"ja":["Rustプログラミング言語の知識が必要","Rustにおける多相性と抽象化に焦点を当てているため、他の言語には直接適用できない可能性がある"],"ko":["러스트 프로그래밍 언어에 대한 지식이 필요합니다.","러스트의 다형성 및 추상화에 중점을 둔 것으로 다른 언어에 직접 적용할 수 없습니다."],"es":["Requiere conocimiento del lenguaje de programación Rust","Centrado en polimorfismo y abstracción en Rust, puede que no sea directamente aplicable a otros lenguajes"],"fr":["Nécessite une connaissance du langage de programmation Rust","Axé sur le polymorphisme et l''abstraction dans Rust, il peut ne pas être directement applicable à d''autres langages"],"de":["Erfordert Kenntnisse der Programmiersprache Rust","Fokussiert auf Polymorphismus und Abstraktion in Rust, möglicherweise nicht direkt auf andere Sprachen anwendbar"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento da linguagem de programação Rust","Focado em polimorfismo e abstração em Rust, pode não ser diretamente aplicável a outras linguagens"],"ru":["Требует знания языка программирования Rust","Фокусируется на полиморфизме и абстракции в Rust, может не быть直接 применимым к другим языкам"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة بلغة البرمجة Rust","يركز على التعددية الشكلية والاستهلاك في Rust، وقد لا يكون قابلا للتطبيق مباشرة على لغات أخرى"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"3a2eed8faf0a0087aa5c823d66341123cc6f43ef36d1767c3fdbcc86cf8b4b54","qualityScore":0}');
