de composants React","de":"KI-Tools: Refaktorierung von React-Komponenten","pt":"Ferramentas de Refatoração de Componentes AI","ru":"ИИ Агенты для Рефакторинга Компонентов","ar":"أدوات إعادة هيكلة المكونات الذكية","en":"component-refactoring"},"description":{"zh":"Dify组件重构AI技能，用于简化高复杂度的React组件，提高代码质量和性能","ja":"DifyコンポーネントリファクタリングAIスキルは、Reactコンポーネントを簡素化し、コードの品質とパフォーマンスを向上させるために使用されます","ko":"Dify 컴포넌트 리팩토링 AI 스킬은 React 컴포넌트를 단순화하고 코드 품질과 성능을 향상시키는 데 사용됩니다","es":"Refactoriza componentes React de alta complejidad en Dify frontend para mejorar el rendimiento y la escalabilidad","fr":"Réfactorez des composants React de haute complexité dans Dify frontend pour améliorer les performances et la scalabilité","de":"Refaktorieren Sie komplexe React-Komponenten in Dify frontend, um die Leistung und Skalierbarkeit zu verbessern","pt":"A skill de refatoração de componentes da Dify ajuda a otimizar componentes React complexos, reduzindo a complexidade e melhorando a performance","ru":"Навык рефакторинга компонентов Dify помогает оптимизировать сложные компоненты React, уменьшая сложность и улучшая производительность","ar":"مهارة إعادة هيكلة المكونات في Dify تساعد على تحسين المكونات React المعقدة، وتقليل التعقيد وتحسين الأداء","en":"Refactor high-complexity React components in Dify frontend. Use when `pnpm analyze-component --json` shows complexity > 50 or lineCount > 300, when the user ..."},"definition":{"en":"Refactor high-complexity React components in Dify frontend. Use when `pnpm analyze-component --json` shows complexity > 50 or lineCount > 300, when the user asks for code splitting, hook extraction, or complexity reduction, or when `pnpm analyze-component` warns to refactor before testing; avoid for simple/well-structured components, third-party wrappers, or when the user explicitly wants testing without refactoring."},"features":{"zh":["简化高复杂度的React组件","提高代码质量和性能","使用pnpm analyze-component进行组件分析","支持代码分割和Hook抽取","减少复杂度和代码行数"],"ja":["Reactコンポーネントを簡素化する","コードの品質とパフォーマンスを向上させる","pnpm analyze-componentを使用したコンポーネント分析","コード分割とHook抽出をサポート","複雑度とコード行数を減らす"],"ko":["React 컴포넌트를 단순화하는 기능","코드 품질과 성능을 향상시키는 기능","pnpm analyze-component를 사용한 컴포넌트 분석","코드 분割과 Hook 추출을 지원","복잡도와 코드 행수를 줄이는 기능"],"es":["Análisis de complejidad de componentes","Refactorización de componentes React","Mejora del rendimiento y la escalabilidad","Integración con Dify frontend","Soporte para comandos CLI"],"fr":["Analyse de la complexité des composants","Réfactoration de composants React","Amélioration des performances et de la scalabilité","Intégration avec Dify frontend","Prise en charge des commandes CLI"],"de":["Komplexitätsanalyse von Komponenten","Refaktorierung von React-Komponenten","Leistungs- und Skalierbarkeitsverbesserung","Integration mit Dify frontend","Unterstützung von CLI-Befehlen"],"pt":["Otimização de componentes React complexos","Redução da complexidade do código","Melhoria da performance da aplicação","Análise de componentes com `pnpm analyze-component`","Refatoração de componentes com `refactor-component`"],"ru":["Оптимизация сложных компонентов React","Уменьшение сложности кода","Улучшение производительности приложения","Анализ компонентов с `pnpm analyze-component`","Рефакторинг компонентов с `refactor-component`"],"ar":["تحسين المكونات React المعقدة","تقليل تعقيد الشفرة","تحسين أداء التطبيق","تحليل المكونات مع `pnpm analyze-component`","إعادة هيكلة المكونات مع `refactor-component`"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能体","Dify组件重构","React组件","代码质量","性能优化","pnpm analyze-component","代码分割","Hook抽取"],"ja":["AIエージェント","Difyコンポーネントリファクタリング","Reactコンポーネント","コード品質","パフォーマンス最適化","pnpm analyze-component","コード分割","Hook抽出"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","Dify 컴포넌트 리팩토링","React 컴포넌트","코드 품질","성능 최적화","pnpm analyze-component","코드 분割","Hook 추출"],"es":["herramientas de ia","refactorización de componentes","react","dify frontend","análisis de complejidad","optimización de código"],"fr":["outils d''ia","réfactoration de composants","react","dify frontend","analyse de complexité","optimisation de code"],"de":["ki-tools","refaktorierung von komponenten","react","dify frontend","komplexitätsanalyse","code-optimierung"],"pt":["refatoração de componentes","componentes React","otimização de código","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento","Dify","AI","IA"],"ru":["рефакторинг компонентов","компоненты React","оптимизация кода","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки","Dify","ИИ","AI"],"ar":["إعادة هيكلة المكونات","مكونات React","تحسين الشفرة","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير","Dify","الذكاء الاصطناعي","AI"]}},"owner":"langgenius","repo":"dify","repoPath":"langgenius/dify","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T05:23:02.896Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"component-refactoring","description":"Refactor high-complexity React components in Dify frontend. Use when `pnpm analyze-component --json` shows complexity > 50 or lineCount > 300, when the user asks for code splitting, hook extraction, or complexity reduction, or when `pnpm analyze-component` warns to refactor before testing; avoid for simple/well-structured components, third-party wrappers, or when the user explicitly wants testing without refactoring.","bodyPreview":"# Dify Component Refactoring Skill\n\nRefactor high-complexity React components in the Dify frontend codebase with the patterns and workflow below.\n\n> **Complexity Threshold**: Components with complexity > 50 (measured by `pnpm analyze-component`) should be refactored before testing.\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Commands (run from `web/`)\n\nUse paths relative to `web/` (e.g., `app/components/...`).\nUse `refactor-component` for refactoring prompts and `analyze-component` for testing prompts and metrics.","body":"# Dify Component Refactoring Skill\n\nRefactor high-complexity React components in the Dify frontend codebase with the patterns and workflow below.\n\n> **Complexity Threshold**: Components with complexity > 50 (measured by `pnpm analyze-component`) should be refactored before testing.\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Commands (run from `web/`)\n\nUse paths relative to `web/` (e.g., `app/components/...`).\nUse `refactor-component` for refactoring prompts and `analyze-component` for testing prompts and metrics.\n\n```bash\ncd web\n\n# Generate refactoring prompt\npnpm refactor-component <path>\n\n# Output refactoring analysis as JSON\npnpm refactor-component <path> --json\n\n# Generate testing prompt (after refactoring)\npnpm analyze-component <path>\n\n# Output testing analysis as JSON\npnpm analyze-component <path> --json\n```\n\n### Complexity Analysis\n\n```bash\n# Analyze component complexity\npnpm analyze-component <path> --json\n\n# Key metrics to check:\n# - complexity: normalized score 0-100 (target < 50)\n# - maxComplexity: highest single function complexity\n# - lineCount: total lines (target < 300)\n```\n\n### Complexity Score Interpretation\n\n| Score | Level | Action |\n|-------|-------|--------|\n| 0-25 | 🟢 Simple | Ready for testing |\n| 26-50 | 🟡 Medium | Consider minor refactoring |\n| 51-75 | 🟠 Complex | **Refactor before testing** |\n| 76-100 | 🔴 Very Complex | **Must refactor** |\n\n## Core Refactoring Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Extract Custom Hooks\n\n**When**: Component has complex state management, multiple `useState`/`useEffect`, or business logic mixed with UI.\n\n**Dify Convention**: Place hooks in a `hooks/` subdirectory or alongside the component as `use-<feature>.ts`.\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Before: Complex state logic in component\nconst Configuration: FC = () => {\n  const [modelConfig, setModelConfig] = useState<ModelConfig>(...)\n  const [datasetConfigs, setDatasetConfigs] = useState<DatasetConfigs>(...)\n  const [completionParams, setCompletionParams] = useState<FormValue>({})\n  \n  // 50+ lines of state management logic...\n  \n  return <div>...</div>\n}\n\n// ✅ After: Extract to custom hook\n// hooks/use-model-config.ts\nexport const useModelConfig = (appId: string) => {\n  const [modelConfig, setModelConfig] = useState<ModelConfig>(...)\n  const [completionParams, setCompletionParams] = useState<FormValue>({})\n  \n  // Related state management logic here\n  \n  return { modelConfig, setModelConfig, completionParams, setCompletionParams }\n}\n\n// Component becomes cleaner\nconst Configuration: FC = () => {\n  const { modelConfig, setModelConfig } = useModelConfig(appId)\n  return <div>...</div>\n}\n```\n\n**Dify Examples**:\n- `web/app/components/app/configuration/hooks/use-advanced-prompt-config.ts`\n- `web/app/components/app/configuration/debug/hooks.tsx`\n- `web/app/components/workflow/hooks/use-workflow.ts`\n\n### Pattern 2: Extract Sub-Components\n\n**When**: Single component has multiple UI sections, conditional rendering blocks, or repeated patterns.\n\n**Dify Convention**: Place sub-components in subdirectories or as separate files in the same directory.\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Before: Monolithic JSX with multiple sections\nconst AppInfo = () => {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {/* 100 lines of header UI */}\n      {/* 100 lines of operations UI */}\n      {/* 100 lines of modals */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\n// ✅ After: Split into focused components\n// app-info/\n//   ├── index.tsx           (orchestration only)\n//   ├── app-header.tsx      (header UI)\n//   ├── app-operations.tsx  (operations UI)\n//   └── app-modals.tsx      (modal management)\n\nconst AppInfo = () => {\n  const { showModal, setShowModal } = useAppInfoModals()\n  \n  return (\n    <div>\n      <AppHeader appDetail={appDetail} />\n      <AppOperations onAction={handleAction} />\n      <AppModals show={showModal} onClose={() => setShowModal(null)} />\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n**Dify Examples**:\n- `web/app/components/app/configuration/` directory structure\n- `web/app/components/workflow/nodes/` per-node organization\n\n### Pattern 3: Simplify Conditional Logic\n\n**When**: Deep nesting (> 3 levels), complex ternaries, or multiple `if/else` chains.\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Before: Deeply nested conditionals\nconst Template = useMemo(() => {\n  if (appDetail?.mode === AppModeEnum.CHAT) {\n    switch (locale) {\n      case LanguagesSupported[1]:\n        return <TemplateChatZh />\n      case LanguagesSupported[7]:\n        return <TemplateChatJa />\n      default:\n        return <TemplateChatEn />\n    }\n  }\n  if (appDetail?.mode === AppModeEnum.ADVANCED_CHAT) {\n    // Another 15 lines...\n  }\n  // More conditions...\n}, [appDetail, locale])\n\n// ✅ After: Use lookup tables + early returns\nconst TEMPLATE_MAP = {\n  [AppModeEnum.CHAT]: {\n    [LanguagesSupported[1]]: TemplateChatZh,\n    [LanguagesSupported[7]]: TemplateChatJa,\n    default: TemplateChatEn,\n  },\n  [AppModeEnum.ADVANCED_CHAT]: {\n    [LanguagesSupported[1]]: TemplateAdvancedChatZh,\n    // ...\n  },\n}\n\nconst Template = useMemo(() => {\n  const modeTemplates = TEMPLATE_MAP[appDetail?.mode]\n  if (!modeTemplates) return null\n  \n  const TemplateComponent = modeTemplates[locale] || modeTemplates.default\n  return <TemplateComponent appDetail={appDetail} />\n}, [appDetail, locale])\n```\n\n### Pattern 4: Extract API/Data Logic\n\n**When**: Component directly handles API calls, data transformation, or complex async operations.\n\n**Dify Convention**: Use `@tanstack/react-query` hooks from `web/service/use-*.ts` or create custom data hooks.\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Before: API logic in component\nconst MCPServiceCard = () => {\n  const [basicAppConfig, setBasicAppConfig] = useState({})\n  \n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (isBasicApp && appId) {\n      (async () => {\n        const res = await fetchAppDetail({ url: ''/apps'', id: appId })\n        setBasicAppConfig(res?.model_config || {})\n      })()\n    }\n  }, [appId, isBasicApp])\n  \n  // More API-related logic...\n}\n\n// ✅ After: Extract to data hook using React Query\n// use-app-config.ts\nimport { useQuery } from ''@tanstack/react-query''\nimport { get } from ''@/service/base''\n\nconst NAME_SPACE = ''appConfig''\n\nexport const useAppConfig = (appId: string, isBasicApp: boolean) => {\n  return useQuery({\n    enabled: isBasicApp && !!appId,\n    queryKey: [NAME_SPACE, ''detail'', appId],\n    queryFn: () => get<AppDetailResponse>(`/apps/${appId}`),\n    select: data => data?.model_config || {},\n  })\n}\n\n// Component becomes cleaner\nconst MCPServiceCard = () => {\n  const { data: config, isLoading } = useAppConfig(appId, isBasicApp)\n  // UI only\n}\n```\n\n**React Query Best Practices in Dify**:\n- Define `NAME_SPACE` for query key organization\n- Use `enabled` option for conditional fetching\n- Use `select` for data transformation\n- Export invalidation hooks: `useInvalidXxx`\n\n**Dify Examples**:\n- `web/service/use-workflow.ts`\n- `web/service/use-common.ts`\n- `web/service/knowledge/use-dataset.ts`\n- `web/service/knowledge/use-document.ts`\n\n### Pattern 5: Extract Modal/Dialog Management\n\n**When**: Component manages multiple modals with complex open/close states.\n\n**Dify Convention**: Modals should be extracted with their state management.\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Before: Multiple modal states in component\nconst AppInfo = () => {\n  const [showEditModal, setShowEditModal] = useState(false)\n  const [showDuplicateModal, setShowDuplicateModal] = useState(false)\n  const [showConfirmDelete, setShowConfirmDelete] = useState(false)\n  const [showSwitchModal, setShowSwitchModal] = useState(false)\n  const [showImportDSLModal, setShowImportDSLModal] = useState(false)\n  // 5+ more modal states...\n}\n\n// ✅ After: Extract to modal management hook\ntype ModalType = ''edit'' | ''duplicate'' | ''delete'' | ''switch'' | ''import'' | null\n\nconst useAppInfoModals = () => {\n  const [activeModal, setActiveModal] = useState<ModalType>(null)\n  \n  const openModal = useCallback((type: ModalType) => setActiveModal(type), [])\n  const closeModal = useCallback(() => setActiveModal(null), [])\n  \n  return {\n    activeModal,\n    openModal,\n    closeModal,\n    isOpen: (type: ModalType) => activeModal === type,\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 6: Extract Form Logic\n\n**When**: Complex form validation, submission handling, or field transformation.\n\n**Dify Convention**: Use `@tanstack/react-form` patterns from `web/app/components/base/form/`.\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ Use existing form infrastructure\nimport { useAppForm } from ''@/app/components/base/form''\n\nconst ConfigForm = () => {\n  const form = useAppForm({\n    defaultValues: { name: '''', description: '''' },\n    onSubmit: handleSubmit,\n  })\n  \n  return <form.Provider>...</form.Provider>\n}\n```\n\n## Dify-Specific Refactoring Guidelines\n\n### 1. Context Provider Extraction\n\n**When**: Component provides complex context values with multiple states.\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Before: Large context value object\nconst value = {\n  appId, isAPIKeySet, isTrailFinished, mode, modelModeType,\n  promptMode, isAdvancedMode, isAgent, isOpenAI, isFunctionCall,\n  // 50+ more properties...\n}\nreturn <ConfigContext.Provider value={value}>...</ConfigContext.Provider>\n\n// ✅ After: Split into domain-specific contexts\n<ModelConfigProvider value={modelConfigValue}>\n  <DatasetConfigProvider value={datasetConfigValue}>\n    <UIConfigProvider value={uiConfigValue}>\n      {children}\n    </UIConfigProvider>\n  </DatasetConfigProvider>\n</ModelConfigProvider>\n```\n\n**Dify Reference**: `web/context/` directory structure\n\n### 2. Workflow Node Components\n\n**When**: Refactoring workflow node components (`web/app/components/workflow/nodes/`).\n\n**Conventions**:\n- Keep node logic in `use-interactions.ts`\n- Extract panel UI to separate files\n- Use `_base` components for common patterns\n\n```\nnodes/<node-type>/\n  ├── index.tsx              # Node registration\n  ├── node.tsx               # Node visual component\n  ├── panel.tsx              # Configuration panel\n  ├── use-interactions.ts    # Node-specific hooks\n  └── types.ts               # Type definitions\n```\n\n### 3. Configuration Components\n\n**When**: Refactoring app configuration components.\n\n**Conventions**:\n- Separate config sections into subdirectories\n- Use existing patterns from `web/app/components/app/configuration/`\n- Keep feature toggles in dedicated components\n\n### 4. Tool/Plugin Components\n\n**When**: Refactoring tool-related components (`web/app/components/tools/`).\n\n**Conventions**:\n- Follow existing modal patterns\n- Use service hooks from `web/service/use-tools.ts`\n- Keep provider-specific logic isolated\n\n## Refactoring Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Generate Refactoring Prompt\n\n```bash\npnpm refactor-component <path>\n```\n\nThis command will:\n- Analyze component complexity and features\n- Identify specific refactoring actions needed\n- Generate a prompt for AI assistant (auto-copied to clipboard on macOS)\n- Provide detailed requirements based on detected patterns\n\n### Step 2: Analyze Details\n\n```bash\npnpm analyze-component <path> --json\n```\n\nIdentify:\n- Total complexity score\n- Max function complexity\n- Line count\n- Features detected (state, effects, API, etc.)\n\n### Step 3: Plan\n\nCreate a refactoring plan based on detected features:\n\n| Detected Feature | Refactoring Action |\n|------------------|-------------------|\n| `hasState: true` + `hasEffects: true` | Extract custom hook |\n| `hasAPI: true` | Extract data/service hook |\n| `hasEvents: true` (many) | Extract event handlers |\n| `lineCount > 300` | Split into sub-components |\n| `maxComplexity > 50` | Simplify conditional logic |\n\n### Step 4: Execute Incrementally\n\n1. **Extract one piece at a time**\n2. **Run lint, type-check, and tests after each extraction**\n3. **Verify functionality before next step**\n\n```\nFor each extraction:\n  ┌────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │ 1. Extract code                        │\n  │ 2. Run: pnpm lint:fix                  │\n  │ 3. Run: pnpm type-check:tsgo           │\n  │ 4. Run: pnpm test                      │\n  │ 5. Test functionality manually         │\n  │ 6. PASS? → Next extraction             │\n  │    FAIL? → Fix before continuing       │\n  └────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Step 5: Verify\n\nAfter refactoring:\n\n```bash\n# Re-run refactor command to verify improvements\npnpm refactor-component <path>\n\n# If complexity < 25 and lines < 200, you''ll see:\n# ✅ COMPONENT IS WELL-STRUCTURED\n\n# For detailed metrics:\npnpm analyze-component <path> --json\n\n# Target metrics:\n# - complexity < 50\n# - lineCount < 300\n# - maxComplexity < 30\n```\n\n## Common Mistakes to Avoid\n\n### ❌ Over-Engineering\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Too many tiny hooks\nconst useButtonText = () => useState(''Click'')\nconst useButtonDisabled = () => useState(false)\nconst useButtonLoading = () => useState(false)\n\n// ✅ Cohesive hook with related state\nconst useButtonState = () => {\n  const [text, setText] = useState(''Click'')\n  const [disabled, setDisabled] = useState(false)\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false)\n  return { text, setText, disabled, setDisabled, loading, setLoading }\n}\n```\n\n### ❌ Breaking Existing Patterns\n\n- Follow existing directory structures\n- Maintain naming conventions\n- Preserve export patterns for compatibility\n\n### ❌ Premature Abstraction\n\n- Only extract when there''s clear complexity benefit\n- Don''t create abstractions for single-use code\n- Keep refactored code in the same domain area\n\n## References\n\n### Dify Codebase Examples\n\n- **Hook extraction**: `web/app/components/app/configuration/hooks/`\n- **Component splitting**: `web/app/components/app/configuration/`\n- **Service hooks**: `web/service/use-*.ts`\n- **Workflow patterns**: `web/app/components/workflow/hooks/`\n- **Form patterns**: `web/app/components/base/form/`\n\n### Related Skills\n\n- `frontend-testing` - For testing refactored components\n- `web/docs/test.md` - Testing specification\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-24T08:21:20.483Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Frontend Agents specializing in React component optimization and code refinement.","zh":"适合专注于 React 组件优化和代码精炼的前端代理。","ja":"React コンポーネントの最適化とコードの洗練に特化したフロントエンド エージェントに適しています。","ko":"React 컴포넌트 최적화 및 코드 정련에 전문적인 프론트엔드 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de frontend especializados en la optimización de componentes de React y refinamiento de código.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de frontend spécialisés dans l''optimisation des composants React et l''affinement du code.","de":"Ideal für Frontend-Agents, die sich auf die Optimierung von React-Komponenten und Code-Verfeinerung spezialisieren.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Frontend especializados em otimização de componentes React e refinamento de código.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Frontend, специализирующихся на оптимизации компонентов React и усовершенствовании кода.","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة المستخدم الأمامية الذين يختصون بتحسين مكونات React وتنقية الشفرة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to refactor high-complexity React components using `pnpm analyze-component` and `refactor-component` commands, reducing complexity and improving code maintainability with techniques like code splitting and hook extraction.","zh":"赋予代理重构高复杂度 React 组件的能力，使用 `pnpm analyze-component` 和 `refactor-component` 命令，通过代码分割和钩子提取等技术减少复杂度，提高代码的可维护性。","ja":"エージェントに高い複雑度を持つ React コンポーネントをリファクタリングする能力を付与します。`pnpm analyze-component` および `refactor-component` コマンドを使用して、コード分割やフック抽出などの技術で複雑性を減らし、コードの保守性を向上させます。","ko":"에이전트가 높은 복잡도를 가진 React 컴포넌트를 리팩토링할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다. `pnpm analyze-component` 및 `refactor-component` 명령을 사용하여 코드 분할 및 훅 추출 등의 기술로 복잡성을 줄이고 코드의 유지 보수를 개선합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a refactorizar componentes de React de alta complejidad utilizando los comandos `pnpm analyze-component` y `refactor-component`, reduciendo la complejidad y mejorando la mantenibilidad del código con técnicas como la división de código y la extracción de hooks.","fr":"Permet aux agents de réorganiser les composants React à complexité élevée en utilisant les commandes `pnpm analyze-component` et `refactor-component`, en réduisant la complexité et en améliorant la maintenabilité du code avec des techniques comme la division de code et l''extraction de hooks.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, React-Komponenten mit hoher Komplexität mit den Befehlen `pnpm analyze-component` und `refactor-component` umzustrukturieren, die Komplexität zu reduzieren und die Wartbarkeit des Codes mit Techniken wie Code-Splitting und Hook-Extraktion zu verbessern.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a reestruturar componentes React de alta complexidade usando os comandos `pnpm analyze-component` e `refactor-component`, reduzindo a complexidade e melhorando a manutenibilidade do código com técnicas como divisão de código e extração de hook.","ru":"Предоставляет агентам возможность перестраивать компоненты React высокой сложности с помощью команд `pnpm analyze-component` и `refactor-component`, снижая сложность и улучшая поддерживаемость кода с помощью таких методов, как разделение кода и извлечение хуков.","ar":"تمكّن العميل من إعادة هيكلة مكونات React المعقدة باستخدام أوامر `pnpm analyze-component` و `refactor-component`، وتقليل التعقيد وتحسين صيانة الشفرة باستخدام تقنيات مثل تقسيم الشفرة واستخراج المحاكي."},"useCases":{"en":["Refactoring complex React components with high line counts or complexity scores","Improving code readability and structure through hook extraction and code splitting","Optimizing component performance by reducing complexity and improving maintainability"],"zh":["重构具有高行数或复杂性评分的复杂 React 组件","通过钩子提取和代码分割提高代码的可读性和结构","通过减少复杂性和提高可维护性来优化组件的性能"],"ja":["行数や複雑性スコアが高い複雑な React コンポーネントのリファクタリング","フック抽出やコード分割によってコードの可読性と構造を改善する","複雑性の削減と保守性の向上によってコンポーネントのパフォーマンスを最適化する"],"ko":[" 높은 줄 수 또는 복잡성 점수를 가진 복잡한 React 컴포넌트를 리팩토링"," 훅 추출 및 코드 분할을 통해 코드의 가독성과 구조를 개선"," 복잡성을 줄이고 유지 보수를 개선하여 컴포넌트의 성능을 최적화"],"es":["Reorganización de componentes de React complejos con recuentos de líneas altos o puntuaciones de complejidad","Mejora de la legibilidad y la estructura del código a través de la extracción de hooks y la división de código","Optimización del rendimiento de los componentes reduciendo la complejidad y mejorando la mantenibilidad"],"fr":["Réorganisation de composants React complexes avec des comptes de lignes élevés ou des scores de complexité","Amélioration de la lisibilité et de la structure du code grâce à l''extraction de hooks et à la division de code","Optimisation des performances des composants en réduisant la complexité et en améliorant la maintenabilité"],"de":["Umstrukturierung komplexer React-Komponenten mit hohen Zeilenanzahlen oder Komplexitätswerten","Verbesserung der Lesbarkeit und Struktur des Codes durch Hook-Extraktion und Code-Splitting","Optimierung der Leistung von Komponenten durch Reduzierung der Komplexität und Verbesserung der Wartbarkeit"],"pt":["Reestruturação de componentes React complexos com contagens de linhas altas ou escores de complexidade","Melhoria da legibilidade e estrutura do código por meio da extração de hook e divisão de código","Otimização do desempenho do componente reduzindo a complexidade e melhorando a manutenibilidade"],"ru":["Перестройка сложных компонентов React с высокими счетчиками строк или показателями сложности","Улучшение читаемости и структуры кода за счет извлечения хуков и разделения кода","Оптимизация производительности компонента за счет снижения сложности и улучшения поддерживаемости"],"ar":["إعادة هيكلة مكونات React المعقدة ذات عدد كبير من الأسطر أو درجات التعقيد","تحسين قراءة الشفرة وهيكلتها من خلال استخراج المحاكي وتقسيم الشفرة","تحسين أداء المكون عن طريق تقليل التعقيد وتحسين صيانة الشفرة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Dify frontend codebase access","Limited to React components with complexity > 50 or lineCount > 300","Excludes simple or well-structured components, third-party wrappers, or components explicitly marked for testing without refactoring"],"zh":["需要 Dify 前端代码库访问权限","仅限复杂度 > 50 或行数 > 300 的 React 组件","排除简单或结构良好的组件、第三方包装器或明确标记为不需要重构的组件"],"ja":["Dify フロントエンド コードベースへのアクセスが必要","複雑性 > 50 または行数 > 300 の React コンポーネントに限定","シンプルまたは構造化されているコンポーネント、サードパーティのラッパー、またはリファクタリング不要と明示的にマークされているコンポーネントは除外"],"ko":["Dify 프론트엔드 코드베이스에 대한 액세스가 필요","복잡성 > 50 또는 줄 수 > 300인 React 컴포넌트로 제한","단순하거나 구조화된 컴포넌트, 제3자 래퍼 또는 리팩토링이 필요하지 않음으로 명시적으로 표시된 컴포넌트는 제외"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la base de código de frontend de Dify","Limitado a componentes de React con una complejidad > 50 o un recuento de líneas > 300","Excluye componentes simples o bien estructurados, envolturas de terceros o componentes marcados explícitamente para pruebas sin reorganización"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à la base de code frontend de Dify","Limité aux composants React avec une complexité > 50 ou un nombre de lignes > 300","Exclut les composants simples ou bien structurés, les enveloppes de tiers ou les composants explicitement marqués pour des tests sans réorganisation"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf die Dify-Frontend-Codebasis","Begrenzt auf React-Komponenten mit einer Komplexität > 50 oder einer Zeilenanzahl > 300","Schließt einfache oder gut strukturierte Komponenten, Third-Party-Wrapper oder explizit für Tests ohne Umstrukturierung markierte Komponenten aus"],"pt":["Exige acesso ao código-fonte frontend Dify","Limitado a componentes React com complexidade > 50 ou lineCount > 300","Exclui componentes simples ou bem estruturados, wrappers de terceiros ou componentes explicitamente marcados para teste sem reestruturação"],"ru":["Требует доступа к базе кода frontend Dify","Ограничен компонентами React с сложностью > 50 или lineCount > 300","Исключает простые или хорошо структурированные компоненты, обертки третьих сторон или компоненты, явно помеченные для тестирования без перестройки"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى قاعدة الشفرة الأمامية ل Dify","محدود بمكونات React ذات التعقيد > 50 أو lineCount > 300","استبعاد المكونات البسيطة أو المكونات ذات الهيكل الجيد، أو غطاء الأطراف الثالثة، أو المكونات المحددة بشكل صريح للاختبار دون إعادة الهيكلة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"996349b0b799095aeaa7781bc9646d032f054edd85a7c90ea67b49f3334c98ad","qualityScore":100}');
