locking","Tamaño del paquete","Fugas de memoria","Renderizado","Animaciones"],"fr":["React Native","AI Agents","Optimisation des performances","Hermes","Blocage de threads JS","Taille du paquet","Fuites de mémoire","Rendu","Animations"],"de":["React Native","AI-Agents","Leistungsoptimierung","Hermes","JS-Thread-Blockierung","Paketgröße","Speichellecks","Rendern","Animationen"],"pt":["React Native","otimização de desempenho","FPS","TTI","tamanho do pacote","vazamentos de memória","animações","Hermes","JS thread blocking"],"ru":["React Native","оптимизация производительности","FPS","TTI","размер пакета","утечки памяти","анимации","Hermes","JS thread blocking"],"ar":["رياكت نيتيف","تحسين الأداء","إطارًا في الثانية","وقت إقلاع التطبيق","حجم الحزمة","تسربات الذاكرة","الرسوم المتحركة","Hermes","JS thread blocking"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Mobile Development Agents needing advanced React Native performance optimization capabilities.","zh":"适合需要高级React Native性能优化能力的移动开发代理。","ja":"React Nativeのパフォーマンス最適化機能を必要とするモバイル開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 React Native 성능 최적화 기능이 필요한 모바일 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo móvil que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de optimización de rendimiento de React Native.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement mobile ayant besoin de capacités avancées d''optimisation des performances de React Native.","de":"Perfekt für Mobile Development Agents, die erweiterte React Native-Leistungsoptimierungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Móvel que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de otimização de desempenho do React Native.","ru":"Идеально для агентов мобильной разработки, которым необходимы расширенные возможности оптимизации производительности React Native.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء التطوير المحمول الذين يحتاجون إلى قابليات متقدمة لتحسين أداء React Native."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to optimize React Native applications for improved FPS, TTI, and bundle size, leveraging Hermes optimization, JS thread blocking, and native modules, while debugging jank and frame drops with tools like FlashList.","zh":"赋予代理优化React Native应用程序以提高FPS、TTI和包大小的能力，利用Hermes优化、JS线程阻塞和原生模块，同时使用诸如FlashList的工具调试卡顿和帧掉落。","ja":"エージェントがHermesの最適化、JSスレッドブロック、ネイティブモジュールを利用して、FPS、TTI、バンドルサイズを向上させたReact Nativeアプリケーションを最適化し、FlashListなどのツールを使用してジャンクやフレームドロップをデバッグする能力を提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 Hermes 최적화, JS 스레드 블로킹, 네이티브 모듈을 활용하여 FPS, TTI, 번들 크기를 개선한 React Native 애플리케이션을 최적화하고 FlashList 같은 도구를 사용하여 저하 및 프레임 드롭을 디버깅할 수 있는 능력을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a optimizar aplicaciones de React Native para mejorar los FPS, TTI y el tamaño del paquete, aprovechando la optimización de Hermes, el bloqueo del subproceso JS y los módulos nativos, mientras se depuran los problemas de jank y caídas de frames con herramientas como FlashList.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''optimiser les applications React Native pour améliorer les FPS, TTI et la taille du paquet, en exploitant l''optimisation de Hermes, le blocage du thread JS et les modules natifs, tout en déboguant les problèmes de jank et de chute de frames avec des outils comme FlashList.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, React Native-Anwendungen für eine verbesserte FPS, TTI und Bundle-Größe zu optimieren, indem es die Hermes-Optimierung, JS-Thread-Blockierung und native Module nutzt, während es mit Tools wie FlashList die Probleme von Jank und Frame-Drops debuggt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a otimizar aplicativos React Native para melhorar FPS, TTI e tamanho do pacote, aproveitando a otimização do Hermes, bloqueio de thread JS e módulos nativos, enquanto depura jank e queda de frames com ferramentas como FlashList.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью оптимизировать приложения React Native для улучшения FPS, TTI и размера пакета, используя оптимизацию Hermes, блокировку потока JS и родные модули, а также отладку jank и падения кадров с помощью инструментов seperti FlashList.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تحسين تطبيقات React Native لتحسين FPS و TTI وحجم الحزمة، مستفيداً من تحسين Hermes و حجب خيط JS والوحدات الأصلية، وفي الوقت نفسه يُصلح جанк وإنخفاض الإطارات باستخدام أدوات مثل FlashList."},"useCases":{"en":["Optimizing React Native app performance for smoother animations","Debugging memory leaks and re-renders in complex native modules","Improving JavaScript thread efficiency to reduce bridge overhead"],"zh":["为实现更流畅的动画而优化React Native应用程序性能","调试复杂原生模块中的内存泄漏和重新渲染","提高JavaScript线程效率以减少桥接开销"],"ja":["スムーズなアニメーションのためにReact Nativeアプリケーションのパフォーマンスを最適化する","複雑なネイティブモジュールのメモリリークと再描画をデバッグする","JavaScriptスレッドの効率を向上させてブリッジのオーバーヘッドを削減する"],"ko":["더 부드러운 애니메이션을 위해 React Native 애플리케이션 성능을 최적화하는 것","복잡한 네이티브 모듈의 메모리 누수 및 재 렌더링을 디버깅하는 것","JavaScript 스레드의 효율성을提高하여 브릿지 오버헤드를 줄이는 것"],"es":["Optimizar el rendimiento de la aplicación de React Native para animaciones más suaves","Depurar las filtraciones de memoria y las re-renders en módulos nativos complejos","Mejorar la eficiencia del subproceso JavaScript para reducir la sobrecarga del puente"],"fr":["Optimiser les performances de l''application React Native pour des animations plus fluides","Déboguer les fuites de mémoire et les re-rendus dans des modules natifs complexes","Améliorer l''efficacité du thread JavaScript pour réduire la surcharge du pont"],"de":["Optimieren der Leistung von React Native-Apps für flüssigere Animationen","Debuggen von Speicherlecks und Neu-Renderings in komplexen nativen Modulen","Verbesserung der JavaScript-Thread-Effizienz, um die Bridge-Overhead zu reduzieren"],"pt":["Otimizar o desempenho do aplicativo React Native para animações mais suaves","Depurar vazamentos de memória e re-renderizações em módulos nativos complexos","Melhorar a eficiência do thread JavaScript para reduzir a sobrecarga da ponte"],"ru":["Оптимизировать производительность приложения React Native для более плавных анимаций","Отладить утечки памяти и повторную отрисовку в сложных родных модулях","Улучшить эффективность потока JavaScript, чтобы уменьшить нагрузку на мост"],"ar":["تحسين أداء تطبيق React Native من أجل حركات أكثر سلاسة","تصحيح تسربات الذاكرة وإعادة تحديث في الوحدات الأصلية المعقدة","تحسين كفاءة خيط JavaScript لتقليل عبء الجسر"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires React Native project setup","Limited to optimization of React Native applications","Familiarity with JavaScript, React, and native mobile development (iOS/Android) necessary"],"zh":["需要React Native项目设置","仅限于React Native应用程序的优化","需要JavaScript、React以及原生移动开发（iOS/Android）的熟悉度"],"ja":["React Nativeプロジェクトの設定が必要","React Nativeアプリケーションの最適化のみ","JavaScript、React、ネイティブモバイル開発（iOS/Android）に関する知識が必要"],"ko":["React Native 프로젝트 설정이 필요함","React Native 애플리케이션 최적화에만 제한됨","JavaScript, React, 네이티브 모바일 개발（iOS/Android）에 대한熟悉도가 필요함"],"es":["Requiere configuración del proyecto de React Native","Limitado a la optimización de aplicaciones de React Native","Se requiere familiaridad con JavaScript, React y desarrollo móvil nativo (iOS/Android)"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de projet React Native","Limité à l''optimisation des applications React Native","Nécessite une connaissance de JavaScript, React et du développement mobile natif (iOS/Android)"],"de":["Benötigt React Native-Projektsetup","Begrenzt auf die Optimierung von React Native-Anwendungen","Benötigt Kenntnisse von JavaScript, React und nativer mobiler Entwicklung (iOS/Android)"],"pt":["Requer configuração do projeto React Native","Limitado à otimização de aplicativos React Native","Necessário conhecimento de JavaScript, React e desenvolvimento móvel nativo (iOS/Android)"],"ru":["Требуется настройка проекта React Native","Ограничен оптимизацией приложений React Native","Необходимо знание JavaScript, React и родной мобильной разработки (iOS/Android)"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد مشروع React Native","محدود بتحسين تطبيقات React Native","يُحتاج إلى معرفة JavaScript و React و التطوير المحمول الأصلي (iOS/Android)"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"a65932861017e0fe40c2465db4a1d8732e5f4847ad3411b72e9c0849920dceb2","repoEtag":"W/\"fbec4e53c6069bba17bd5aecbe1a694ffb809605f9853b2bacb8420dabd913c9\"","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('anthropics/skills/internal-comms', 'official', 'anthropics', 'skills', 'anthropics/skills', 'internal-comms', 74575, 7681, 80, '2026-02-24T12:03:15Z', '2026-02-24T12:03:43.383Z', '067b7587a344a928fc6534ef66b1bcd591fc7c26d207ea7ca3334aeb678d6475', '{"id":"anthropics/skills/internal-comms","name":"internal-comms","description":{"zh":"内部通信技能是AI工具的一种功能，用于生成内部报告、新闻稿和FAQ等内容","ja":"内部コミュニケーションは、AIエージェントが内部レポート、ニュースレター、FAQなどのコンテンツを生成する機能です","ko":"내부 커뮤니케이션은 AI 에이전트가 내부 보고서, 뉴스레터, FAQ 등의 콘텐츠를 생성하는 기능입니다","es":"internal-comms es un conjunto de recursos para Agente de AI que ayuda a escribir comunicaciones internas. Aprende a utilizarlo para mejorar la comunicación en tu empresa","fr":"internal-comms est un ensemble de ressources pour les Agents d''IA qui aide à rédiger des communications internes. Découvrez comment l''utiliser pour améliorer la communication dans votre entreprise","de":"internal-comms ist eine Reihe von Ressourcen für KI-Agents, die bei der Erstellung von internen Kommunikationen hilft. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie es verwenden, um die Kommunikation in Ihrem Unternehmen zu verbessern","pt":"O skill internal-comms é uma coleção de recursos para ajudar a criar comunicações internas personalizadas para sua empresa","ru":"Навык internal-comms - это набор ресурсов для создания индивидуальных внутренних коммуникаций для вашей компании","ar":"مهارة internal-comms هي مجموعة من الموارد لمساعدتك في إنشاء اتصالات داخلية مخصصة لشركتك","en":"A set of resources to help me write all kinds of internal communications, using the formats that my company likes to use. Claude should use this skill whenever asked to write some sort of internal communications (status reports, leadership updates, 3P updates, company newsletters, FAQs, incident ..."},"owner":"anthropics","repo":"skills","repoPath":"anthropics/skills","stars":74575,"forks":7681,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T12:03:15Z","topics":["agent-skills"],"skillMd":{"name":"internal-comms","description":"A set of resources to help me write all kinds of internal communications, using the formats that my company likes to use. Claude should use this skill whenever asked to write some sort of internal communications (status reports, leadership updates, 3P updates, company newsletters, FAQs, incident reports, project updates, etc.).","bodyPreview":"## When to use this skill\nTo write internal communications, use this skill for:\n- 3P updates (Progress, Plans, Problems)\n- Company newsletters\n- FAQ responses\n- Status reports\n- Leadership updates\n- Project updates\n- Incident reports\n\n## How to use this skill\n\nTo write any internal communication:\n\n1. **Identify the communication type** from the request\n2. **Load the appropriate guideline file** from the `examples/` directory:\n    - `examples/3p-updates.md` - For Progress/Plans/Problems team upda","body":"## When to use this skill\nTo write internal communications, use this skill for:\n- 3P updates (Progress, Plans, Problems)\n- Company newsletters\n- FAQ responses\n- Status reports\n- Leadership updates\n- Project updates\n- Incident reports\n\n## How to use this skill\n\nTo write any internal communication:\n\n1. **Identify the communication type** from the request\n2. **Load the appropriate guideline file** from the `examples/` directory:\n    - `examples/3p-updates.md` - For Progress/Plans/Problems team updates\n    - `examples/company-newsletter.md` - For company-wide newsletters\n    - `examples/faq-answers.md` - For answering frequently asked questions\n    - `examples/general-comms.md` - For anything else that doesn''t explicitly match one of the above\n3. **Follow the specific instructions** in that file for formatting, tone, and content gathering\n\nIf the communication type doesn''t match any existing guideline, ask for clarification or more context about the desired format.\n\n## Keywords\n3P updates, company newsletter, company comms, weekly update, faqs, common questions, updates, internal comms\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-24T12:03:43.383Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI工具内部通信技能","ja":"AIエージェント内部コミュニケーション","ko":"AI 에이전트 내부 커뮤니케이션","es":"Herramientas de AI: Comunicaciones Internas con internal-...","fr":"Outils d''IA: Communications Internes avec internal-comms","de":"KI-Tools: Interne Kommunikation mit internal-comms","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: internal-comms para Desenvolvedores","ru":"ИИ Агенты: internal-comms для Разработчиков","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: internal-comms لل مطورين","en":"internal-comms"},"description":{"zh":"内部通信技能是AI工具的一种功能，用于生成内部报告、新闻稿和FAQ等内容","ja":"内部コミュニケーションは、AIエージェントが内部レポート、ニュースレター、FAQなどのコンテンツを生成する機能です","ko":"내부 커뮤니케이션은 AI 에이전트가 내부 보고서, 뉴스레터, FAQ 등의 콘텐츠를 생성하는 기능입니다","es":"internal-comms es un conjunto de recursos para Agente de AI que ayuda a escribir comunicaciones internas. Aprende a utilizarlo para mejorar la comunicación e...","fr":"internal-comms est un ensemble de ressources pour les Agents d''IA qui aide à rédiger des communications internes. Découvrez comment l''utiliser pour améliorer...","de":"internal-comms ist eine Reihe von Ressourcen für KI-Agents, die bei der Erstellung von internen Kommunikationen hilft. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie es verwenden, um...","pt":"O skill internal-comms é uma coleção de recursos para ajudar a criar comunicações internas personalizadas para sua empresa","ru":"Навык internal-comms - это набор ресурсов для создания индивидуальных внутренних коммуникаций для вашей компании","ar":"مهارة internal-comms هي مجموعة من الموارد لمساعدتك في إنشاء اتصالات داخلية مخصصة لشركتك","en":"A set of resources to help me write all kinds of internal communications, using the formats that my company likes to use. Claude should use this skill whenev..."},"definition":{"en":"A set of resources to help me write all kinds of internal communications, using the formats that my company likes to use. Claude should use this skill whenever asked to write some sort of internal communications (status reports, leadership updates, 3P updates, company newsletters, FAQs, incident reports, project updates, etc.)."},"features":{"zh":["自动化内部报告生成","支持多种内部通信格式","可自定义内部通信模板","集成AI工具的自然语言处理能力","提高内部通信效率和准确性"],"ja":["内部レポートの自動生成","複数の内部コミュニケーションフォーマットをサポート","内部コミュニケーションテンプレートをカスタマイズ可能","AIエージェントの自然言語処理能力を活用","内部コミュニケーションの効率と正確性を向上"],"ko":["내부 보고서 자동 생성","다양한 내부 커뮤니케이션 형식을 지원","내부 커뮤니케이션 템플릿을 사용자 정의할 수 있음","AI 에이전트의 자연어 처리 능력을 활용","내부 커뮤니케이션의 효율성과 정확성을 향상"],"es":["Escribe informes de estado y actualizaciones de liderazgo","Crea newsletters y respuestas a preguntas frecuentes","Genera informes de incidentes y actualizaciones de proyectos","Utiliza formatos personalizados para tu empresa","Carga guías de estilo desde el directorio examples/","Identifica el tipo de comunicación para cargar la guía adecuada"],"fr":["Rédige des rapports de statut et des mises à jour de leadership","Crée des newsletters et des réponses aux questions fréquentes","Génère des rapports d''incident et des mises à jour de projet","Utilise des formats personnalisés pour votre entreprise","Charge des guides de style depuis le répertoire examples/","Identifie le type de communication pour charger la guide appropriée"],"de":["Erstelle Statusberichte und Führungskräfte-Updates","Erstelle Newsletter und Antworten auf häufig gestellte Fragen","Erstelle Berichte über Vorfälle und Projekt-Updates","Verwende benutzerdefinierte Formate für Ihr Unternehmen","Lade Stilguides aus dem Verzeichnis examples/","Identifiziere den Kommunikationstyp, um die entsprechende Anleitung zu laden"],"pt":["Crie relatórios de status personalizados","Desenvolva atualizações de liderança eficazes","Gerencie FAQs e respostas","Elabore relatórios de incidentes e atualizações de projeto"],"ru":["Создайте индивидуальные отчеты о статусе","Разработайте эффективные обновления руководства","Управляйте FAQ и ответами","Составьте отчеты об инцидентах и обновлениях проекта"],"ar":["أنشئ تقارير حالة مخصصة","طور تحديثات قيادية فعالة","ادفع FAQs والاستجابات","أعد تقارير حوادث وتحديثات المشروع"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI工具","内部通信","自动化","内部报告","新闻稿","FAQ","自然语言处理","AIエージェント"],"ja":["AIエージェント","内部コミュニケーション","自動化","内部レポート","ニュースレター","FAQ","自然言語処理","AIツール"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","내부 커뮤니케이션","자동화","내부 보고서","뉴스레터","FAQ","자연어 처리","AI 툴"],"es":["Agente de AI","comunicaciones internas","informes de estado","actualizaciones de liderazgo","newsletters","respuestas a preguntas frecuentes","informes de incidentes","actualizaciones de proyectos","formatos personalizados","guías de estilo"],"fr":["Agents d''IA","communications internes","rapports de statut","mises à jour de leadership","newsletters","réponses aux questions fréquentes","rapports d''incident","mises à jour de projet","formats personnalisés","guides de style"],"de":["KI-Agents","interne Kommunikation","Statusberichte","Führungskräfte-Updates","Newsletter","Antworten auf häufig gestellte Fragen","Berichte über Vorfälle","Projekt-Updates","benutzerdefinierte Formate","Stilguides"],"pt":["desenvolvedores de IA","ferramentas de IA","comunicações internas","relatórios de status","atualizações de liderança","FAQs","relatórios de incidentes","atualizações de projeto"],"ru":["ИИ разработчики","ИИ инструменты","внутренние коммуникации","отчеты о статусе","обновления руководства","FAQ","отчеты об инцидентах","обновления проекта"],"ar":["مطورو الذكاء الاصطناعي","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","الاتصالات الداخلية","تقارير الحالة","تحديثات القيادة","FAQ","تقارير الحوادث","تحديثات المشروع"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Corporate Agents requiring standardized internal communication templates and formats.","zh":"适用于需要标准化内部沟通模板和格式的企业代理。","ja":"標準化された内部コミュニケーション テンプレートと形式を必要とする企業エージェントに最適です。","ko":"표준화된 내부 커뮤니케이션 템플릿과 형식을 필요로 하는 기업 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes Corporativos que requieren plantillas y formatos de comunicación interna estandarizados.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''entreprise nécessitant des modèles et des formats de communication interne standardisés.","de":"Ideal für Corporate Agents, die standardisierte interne Kommunikationsvorlagen und -formate benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Corporativos que requerem modelos e formatos de comunicação interna padronizados.","ru":"Идеально для корпоративных агентов, требующих стандартизированных шаблонов и форматов внутренней коммуникации.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الشركات الذين يحتاجون إلى قوالب وتنسيقات اتصال داخلي معيارية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate consistent internal communications, including 3P updates, company newsletters, and incident reports, using Markdown files and predefined guidelines from the `examples/` directory.","zh":"使代理能够使用 Markdown 文件和 `examples/` 目录中的预定义指南生成一致的内部通信，包括 3P 更新、公司新闻稿和事件报告。","ja":"エージェントが Markdown ファイルと `examples/` ディレクトリからの事前定義されたガイドラインを使用して、一貫した内部コミュニケーション (3P 更新、会社のニュースレター、インシデント レポートなど) を生成できるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 마크다운 파일과 `examples/` 디렉토리에서 정의된 가이드라인을 사용하여 일관된 내부 커뮤니케이션 (3P 업데이트, 회사 뉴스레터, 인시던트 리포트 등)을 생성할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes generar comunicaciones internas consistentes, incluyendo actualizaciones de 3P, boletines de la empresa y informes de incidentes, utilizando archivos Markdown y directrices predefinidas del directorio `examples/`.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des communications internes cohérentes, notamment des mises à jour 3P, des bulletins d''entreprise et des rapports d''incident, en utilisant des fichiers Markdown et des lignes directrices prédéfinies du répertoire `examples/`.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, konsistente interne Kommunikationen zu generieren, einschließlich 3P-Updates, Firmennewslettern und Vorfallberichten, unter Verwendung von Markdown-Dateien und vordefinierten Richtlinien aus dem Verzeichnis `examples/`.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar comunicações internas consistentes, incluindo atualizações de 3P, boletins da empresa e relatórios de incidentes, usando arquivos Markdown e diretrizes pré-definidas do diretório `examples/`.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать последовательные внутренние коммуникации, включая обновления 3P, корпоративные новости и отчеты об инцидентах, используя файлы Markdown и предопределенные руководства из директории `examples/`.","ar":"يتمكن الوكلاء من إنشاء اتصالات داخلية متسقة ، بما في ذلك تحديثات 3P وأخبار الشركة وتقارير الحوادث ، باستخدام ملفات Markdown والإرشادات المحددة مسبقًا من الدليل `examples/`."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating status report generation","Creating standardized FAQ responses","Drafting leadership updates and project updates"],"zh":["自动化状态报告生成","创建标准化的 FAQ 响应","草拟领导层更新和项目更新"],"ja":["ステータス レポートの生成を自動化する","標準化された FAQ 応答を作成する","リーダーシップ更新とプロジェクト更新を草案する"],"ko":["상태 보고서 생성 자동화","표준화된 FAQ 응답 생성","리더십 업데이트 및 프로젝트 업데이트 초안 작성"],"es":["Automatización de la generación de informes de estado","Creación de respuestas de preguntas frecuentes estandarizadas","Redacción de actualizaciones de liderazgo y actualizaciones de proyectos"],"fr":["Automatisation de la génération de rapports d''état","Création de réponses aux questions fréquentes standardisées","Rédaction de mises à jour de leadership et de mises à jour de projets"],"de":["Automatisierung der Generierung von Statusberichten","Erstellung standardisierter FAQ-Antworten","Erstellung von Führungskräfte-Updates und Projekt-Updates"],"pt":["Automatizar a geração de relatórios de status","Criar respostas de FAQ padronizadas","Redigir atualizações de liderança e atualizações de projeto"],"ru":["Автоматизировать генерацию отчетов о статусе","Создавать стандартизированные ответы на FAQ","Составлять обновления руководства и проектные обновления"],"ar":["توفير آلي لإنشاء تقارير الحالة","إنشاء إجابات عن الأسئلة الشائعة المعيارية","صياغة تحديثات القيادة وتحديثات المشروع"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to company-specific guideline files","Limited to internal communication types specified in the skill"],"zh":["需要访问公司特定的指南文件","仅限于技能中指定的内部通信类型"],"ja":["会社固有のガイド ファイルへのアクセスが必要","スキルで指定された内部コミュニケーション タイプに限定される"],"ko":["회사 고유의 가이드 파일에 접근할 수 있어야 함","스킬에서 지정한 내부 커뮤니케이션 유형으로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere acceso a archivos de directrices específicos de la empresa","Limitado a los tipos de comunicación interna especificados en la habilidad"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès aux fichiers de lignes directrices spécifiques à l''entreprise","Limité aux types de communication interne spécifiés dans la compétence"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf unternehmensspezifische Richtliniendateien","Begrenzt auf die in der Fähigkeit angegebenen Arten interner Kommunikation"],"pt":["Requer acesso a arquivos de diretrizes específicos da empresa","Limitado a tipos de comunicação interna especificados na habilidade"],"ru":["Требует доступа к файлам руководства, специфичным для компании","Ограничен типами внутренней коммуникации, указанными в навыке"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى ملفات إرشادية محددة للشركة","محدود بنواع الاتصالات الداخلية المحددة في المهارة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"067b7587a344a928fc6534ef66b1bcd591fc7c26d207ea7ca3334aeb678d6475","repoEtag":"W/\"8b029149fa94da008a6c4f1a43152b0b329b2e734b696109a05864aae22c5410\"","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('anthropics/skills/mcp-builder', 'official', 'anthropics', 'skills', 'anthropics/skills', 'mcp-builder', 74575, 7681, 80, '2026-02-24T12:03:15Z', '2026-02-24T12:03:43.680Z', '0f4592dcb53cf2b5d6b7febee6b4152018b565551a1c29e3c612f57b218ab295', '{"id":"anthropics/skills/mcp-builder","name":"mcp-builder","description":{"zh":"mcp-builder是创建高质量MCP服务器的指南，用于LLM与外部服务的交互，支持Python和Node/TypeScript","ja":"mcp-builderは、AIエージェントのための高品質のMCPサーバー構築ガイドです。PythonとNode/TypeScriptをサポートしています","ko":"mcp-builder는 AI 에이전트를 위한 고품질의 MCP 서버 구축 가이드입니다. Python 및 Node/TypeScript를 지원합니다","es":"El MCP Builder es una guía para crear servidores MCP que permiten a los LLM interactuar con servicios externos","fr":"Le MCP Builder est un guide pour créer des serveurs MCP qui permettent aux LLM d''interagir avec des services externes","de":"Der MCP Builder ist eine Anleitung zum Erstellen von MCP-Servern, die es LLMs ermöglichen, mit externen Diensten zu interagieren","pt":"O construtor MCP é uma ferramenta para criar servidores MCP que permitem que LLMs interajam com serviços externos. Aprenda a integrar APIs com Python e Node/TypeScript","ru":"ИИ Агенты: MCP Builder - инструмент для создания серверов MCP, которые позволяют LLMs взаимодействовать с внешними сервисами. Узнайте, как интегрировать API с Python и Node/TypeScript","ar":"مبني MCP هو أداة لإنشاء خوادم MCP التي تسمح للنماذج اللغة بالتفاعل مع الخدمات الخارجية. تعلم كيفية интегра واجهات برمجة التطبيقات مع Python و Node/TypeScript","en":"Guide for creating high-quality MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers that enable LLMs to interact with external services through well-designed tools. Use when building MCP servers to integrate external APIs or services, whether in Python (FastMCP) or Node/TypeScript (MCP SDK)."},"owner":"anthropics","repo":"skills","repoPath":"anthropics/skills","stars":74575,"forks":7681,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T12:03:15Z","topics":["agent-skills"],"skillMd":{"name":"mcp-builder","description":"Guide for creating high-quality MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers that enable LLMs to interact with external services through well-designed tools. Use when building MCP servers to integrate external APIs or services, whether in Python (FastMCP) or Node/TypeScript (MCP SDK).","bodyPreview":"# MCP Server Development Guide\n\n## Overview\n\nCreate MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers that enable LLMs to interact with external services through well-designed tools. The quality of an MCP server is measured by how well it enables LLMs to accomplish real-world tasks.\n\n---\n\n# Process\n\n## 🚀 High-Level Workflow\n\nCreating a high-quality MCP server involves four main phases:\n\n### Phase 1: Deep Research and Planning\n\n#### 1.1 Understand Modern MCP Design\n\n**API Coverage vs. Workflow Tools:**\nBalan","body":"# MCP Server Development Guide\n\n## Overview\n\nCreate MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers that enable LLMs to interact with external services through well-designed tools. The quality of an MCP server is measured by how well it enables LLMs to accomplish real-world tasks.\n\n---\n\n# Process\n\n## 🚀 High-Level Workflow\n\nCreating a high-quality MCP server involves four main phases:\n\n### Phase 1: Deep Research and Planning\n\n#### 1.1 Understand Modern MCP Design\n\n**API Coverage vs. Workflow Tools:**\nBalance comprehensive API endpoint coverage with specialized workflow tools. Workflow tools can be more convenient for specific tasks, while comprehensive coverage gives agents flexibility to compose operations. Performance varies by client—some clients benefit from code execution that combines basic tools, while others work better with higher-level workflows. When uncertain, prioritize comprehensive API coverage.\n\n**Tool Naming and Discoverability:**\nClear, descriptive tool names help agents find the right tools quickly. Use consistent prefixes (e.g., `github_create_issue`, `github_list_repos`) and action-oriented naming.\n\n**Context Management:**\nAgents benefit from concise tool descriptions and the ability to filter/paginate results. Design tools that return focused, relevant data. Some clients support code execution which can help agents filter and process data efficiently.\n\n**Actionable Error Messages:**\nError messages should guide agents toward solutions with specific suggestions and next steps.\n\n#### 1.2 Study MCP Protocol Documentation\n\n**Navigate the MCP specification:**\n\nStart with the sitemap to find relevant pages: `https://modelcontextprotocol.io/sitemap.xml`\n\nThen fetch specific pages with `.md` suffix for markdown format (e.g., `https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/draft.md`).\n\nKey pages to review:\n- Specification overview and architecture\n- Transport mechanisms (streamable HTTP, stdio)\n- Tool, resource, and prompt definitions\n\n#### 1.3 Study Framework Documentation\n\n**Recommended stack:**\n- **Language**: TypeScript (high-quality SDK support and good compatibility in many execution environments e.g. MCPB. Plus AI models are good at generating TypeScript code, benefiting from its broad usage, static typing and good linting tools)\n- **Transport**: Streamable HTTP for remote servers, using stateless JSON (simpler to scale and maintain, as opposed to stateful sessions and streaming responses). stdio for local servers.\n\n**Load framework documentation:**\n\n- **MCP Best Practices**: [📋 View Best Practices](./reference/mcp_best_practices.md) - Core guidelines\n\n**For TypeScript (recommended):**\n- **TypeScript SDK**: Use WebFetch to load `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/main/README.md`\n- [⚡ TypeScript Guide](./reference/node_mcp_server.md) - TypeScript patterns and examples\n\n**For Python:**\n- **Python SDK**: Use WebFetch to load `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/main/README.md`\n- [🐍 Python Guide](./reference/python_mcp_server.md) - Python patterns and examples\n\n#### 1.4 Plan Your Implementation\n\n**Understand the API:**\nReview the service''s API documentation to identify key endpoints, authentication requirements, and data models. Use web search and WebFetch as needed.\n\n**Tool Selection:**\nPrioritize comprehensive API coverage. List endpoints to implement, starting with the most common operations.\n\n---\n\n### Phase 2: Implementation\n\n#### 2.1 Set Up Project Structure\n\nSee language-specific guides for project setup:\n- [⚡ TypeScript Guide](./reference/node_mcp_server.md) - Project structure, package.json, tsconfig.json\n- [🐍 Python Guide](./reference/python_mcp_server.md) - Module organization, dependencies\n\n#### 2.2 Implement Core Infrastructure\n\nCreate shared utilities:\n- API client with authentication\n- Error handling helpers\n- Response formatting (JSON/Markdown)\n- Pagination support\n\n#### 2.3 Implement Tools\n\nFor each tool:\n\n**Input Schema:**\n- Use Zod (TypeScript) or Pydantic (Python)\n- Include constraints and clear descriptions\n- Add examples in field descriptions\n\n**Output Schema:**\n- Define `outputSchema` where possible for structured data\n- Use `structuredContent` in tool responses (TypeScript SDK feature)\n- Helps clients understand and process tool outputs\n\n**Tool Description:**\n- Concise summary of functionality\n- Parameter descriptions\n- Return type schema\n\n**Implementation:**\n- Async/await for I/O operations\n- Proper error handling with actionable messages\n- Support pagination where applicable\n- Return both text content and structured data when using modern SDKs\n\n**Annotations:**\n- `readOnlyHint`: true/false\n- `destructiveHint`: true/false\n- `idempotentHint`: true/false\n- `openWorldHint`: true/false\n\n---\n\n### Phase 3: Review and Test\n\n#### 3.1 Code Quality\n\nReview for:\n- No duplicated code (DRY principle)\n- Consistent error handling\n- Full type coverage\n- Clear tool descriptions\n\n#### 3.2 Build and Test\n\n**TypeScript:**\n- Run `npm run build` to verify compilation\n- Test with MCP Inspector: `npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector`\n\n**Python:**\n- Verify syntax: `python -m py_compile your_server.py`\n- Test with MCP Inspector\n\nSee language-specific guides for detailed testing approaches and quality checklists.\n\n---\n\n### Phase 4: Create Evaluations\n\nAfter implementing your MCP server, create comprehensive evaluations to test its effectiveness.\n\n**Load [✅ Evaluation Guide](./reference/evaluation.md) for complete evaluation guidelines.**\n\n#### 4.1 Understand Evaluation Purpose\n\nUse evaluations to test whether LLMs can effectively use your MCP server to answer realistic, complex questions.\n\n#### 4.2 Create 10 Evaluation Questions\n\nTo create effective evaluations, follow the process outlined in the evaluation guide:\n\n1. **Tool Inspection**: List available tools and understand their capabilities\n2. **Content Exploration**: Use READ-ONLY operations to explore available data\n3. **Question Generation**: Create 10 complex, realistic questions\n4. **Answer Verification**: Solve each question yourself to verify answers\n\n#### 4.3 Evaluation Requirements\n\nEnsure each question is:\n- **Independent**: Not dependent on other questions\n- **Read-only**: Only non-destructive operations required\n- **Complex**: Requiring multiple tool calls and deep exploration\n- **Realistic**: Based on real use cases humans would care about\n- **Verifiable**: Single, clear answer that can be verified by string comparison\n- **Stable**: Answer won''t change over time\n\n#### 4.4 Output Format\n\nCreate an XML file with this structure:\n\n```xml\n<evaluation>\n  <qa_pair>\n    <question>Find discussions about AI model launches with animal codenames. One model needed a specific safety designation that uses the format ASL-X. What number X was being determined for the model named after a spotted wild cat?</question>\n    <answer>3</answer>\n  </qa_pair>\n<!-- More qa_pairs... -->\n</evaluation>\n```\n\n---\n\n# Reference Files\n\n## 📚 Documentation Library\n\nLoad these resources as needed during development:\n\n### Core MCP Documentation (Load First)\n- **MCP Protocol**: Start with sitemap at `https://modelcontextprotocol.io/sitemap.xml`, then fetch specific pages with `.md` suffix\n- [📋 MCP Best Practices](./reference/mcp_best_practices.md) - Universal MCP guidelines including:\n  - Server and tool naming conventions\n  - Response format guidelines (JSON vs Markdown)\n  - Pagination best practices\n  - Transport selection (streamable HTTP vs stdio)\n  - Security and error handling standards\n\n### SDK Documentation (Load During Phase 1/2)\n- **Python SDK**: Fetch from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/main/README.md`\n- **TypeScript SDK**: Fetch from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/main/README.md`\n\n### Language-Specific Implementation Guides (Load During Phase 2)\n- [🐍 Python Implementation Guide](./reference/python_mcp_server.md) - Complete Python/FastMCP guide with:\n  - Server initialization patterns\n  - Pydantic model examples\n  - Tool registration with `@mcp.tool`\n  - Complete working examples\n  - Quality checklist\n\n- [⚡ TypeScript Implementation Guide](./reference/node_mcp_server.md) - Complete TypeScript guide with:\n  - Project structure\n  - Zod schema patterns\n  - Tool registration with `server.registerTool`\n  - Complete working examples\n  - Quality checklist\n\n### Evaluation Guide (Load During Phase 4)\n- [✅ Evaluation Guide](./reference/evaluation.md) - Complete evaluation creation guide with:\n  - Question creation guidelines\n  - Answer verification strategies\n  - XML format specifications\n  - Example questions and answers\n  - Running an evaluation with the provided scripts\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-24T12:03:43.680Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理mcp-builder指南","ja":"AIエージェントのmcp-builderガイド","ko":"AI 에이전트 mcp-builder 개발 가이드","es":"Herramientas de AI: Guía de MCP Builder","fr":"Outils d''IA: Guide de construction MCP","de":"KI-Tools: MCP-Builder-Anleitung","pt":"Construtor MCP: Ferramentas de IA para Servidores","ru":"ИИ Агенты: MCP Builder для Серверов","ar":"مبني MCP: أدوات ذكاء اصطناعي للخادم","en":"mcp-builder"},"description":{"zh":"mcp-builder是创建高质量MCP服务器的指南，用于LLM与外部服务的交互，支持Python和Node/TypeScript","ja":"mcp-builderは、AIエージェントのための高品質のMCPサーバー構築ガイドです。PythonとNode/TypeScriptをサポートしています","ko":"mcp-builder는 AI 에이전트를 위한 고품질의 MCP 서버 구축 가이드입니다. Python 및 Node/TypeScript를 지원합니다","es":"El MCP Builder es una guía para crear servidores MCP que permiten a los LLM interactuar con servicios externos","fr":"Le MCP Builder est un guide pour créer des serveurs MCP qui permettent aux LLM d''interagir avec des services externes","de":"Der MCP Builder ist eine Anleitung zum Erstellen von MCP-Servern, die es LLMs ermöglichen, mit externen Diensten zu interagieren","pt":"O construtor MCP é uma ferramenta para criar servidores MCP que permitem que LLMs interajam com serviços externos. Aprenda a integrar APIs com Python e Node/...","ru":"ИИ Агенты: MCP Builder - инструмент для создания серверов MCP, которые позволяют LLMs взаимодействовать с внешними сервисами. Узнайте, как интегрировать API ...","ar":"مبني MCP هو أداة لإنشاء خوادم MCP التي تسمح للنماذج اللغة بالتفاعل مع الخدمات الخارجية. تعلم كيفية интегра واجهات برمجة التطبيقات مع Python و Node/TypeScript","en":"Guide for creating high-quality MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers that enable LLMs to interact with external services through well-designed tools. Use whe..."},"definition":{"en":"Guide for creating high-quality MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers that enable LLMs to interact with external services through well-designed tools. Use when building MCP servers to integrate external APIs or services, whether in Python (FastMCP) or Node/TypeScript (MCP SDK)."},"features":{"zh":["支持Python和Node/TypeScript","高质量的MCP服务器构建","LLM与外部服务的交互","API Coverage和Workflow Tools的平衡","现代MCP设计的深入理解","四个主要阶段的开发过程"],"ja":["PythonとNode/TypeScriptをサポート","高品質のMCPサーバーの構築","LLMと外部サービスとの接続","API CoverageとWorkflow Toolsのバランス","モダンMCP設計の深い理解","4つの主要な開発段階"],"ko":["Python 및 Node/TypeScript 지원","고품질의 MCP 서버 구축","LLM 및 외부 서비스와의 상호 작용","API Coverage 및 Workflow Tools의 균형","최신 MCP 설계에 대한 깊은 이해","4개의 주요 개발 단계"],"es":["Creación de servidores MCP de alta calidad","Integración de APIs externas con LLMs","Herramientas de diseño para interactuar con servicios externos","Compatibilidad con Python y Node/TypeScript"],"fr":["Création de serveurs MCP de haute qualité","Intégration d''API externes avec des LLM","Outils de conception pour interagir avec des services externes","Compatibilité avec Python et Node/TypeScript"],"de":["Erstellung von hochwertigen MCP-Servern","Integration von externen APIs mit LLMs","Design-Tools für die Interaktion mit externen Diensten","Kompatibilität mit Python und Node/TypeScript"],"pt":["Criação de servidores MCP de alta qualidade","Integração com APIs externas","Suporte a Python e Node/TypeScript","Ferramentas de design de workflow","Otimização para LLMs"],"ru":["Создание высококачественных серверов MCP","Интеграция с внешними API","Поддержка Python и Node/TypeScript","Инструменты для проектирования рабочих процессов","Оптимизация для LLMs"],"ar":["إنشاء خوادم MCP عالية الجودة","التكامل مع واجهات برمجة التطبيقات الخارجية","دعم Python و Node/TypeScript","أدوات تصميم سير العمل","تحسين الأداء للنماذج اللغة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","mcp-builder","MCP服务器","LLM","外部服务","Python","Node/TypeScript","API Coverage","Workflow Tools"],"ja":["AIエージェント","mcp-builder","MCPサーバー","LLM","外部サービス","Python","Node/TypeScript","API Coverage","Workflow Tools"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","mcp-builder","MCP 서버","LLM","외부 서비스","Python","Node/TypeScript","API Coverage","Workflow Tools"],"es":["Herramientas de AI","Servidores MCP","LLMs","Integración de APIs","Diseño de herramientas","Python","Node/TypeScript"],"fr":["Outils d''IA","Serveurs MCP","LLMs","Intégration d''API","Conception d''outils","Python","Node/TypeScript"],"de":["KI-Tools","MCP-Server","LLMs","Integration von APIs","Design von Tools","Python","Node/TypeScript"],"pt":["construtor MCP","servidores MCP","LLMs","APIs externas","Python","Node/TypeScript","ferramentas de IA"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты","MCP Builder","серверы MCP","LLMs","внешние API","Python","Node/TypeScript","инструменты ИИ"],"ar":["مبني MCP","خوادم MCP","النماذج اللغة","واجهات برمجة التطبيقات الخارجية","Python","Node/TypeScript","أدوات ذكاء اصطناعي"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Cursor, Windsurf, or Claude Code needing to integrate external services with LLMs through well-designed MCP servers","zh":"适合于像Cursor、Windsurf或Claude Code这样的AI代理，需要将外部服务与LLMs通过设计良好的MCP服务器集成","ja":"Cursor、Windsurf、またはClaude CodeのようなAIエージェントに適しており、外部サービスをLLMsと統合するために、設計の良いMCPサーバーを必要とする","ko":"Cursor, Windsurf 또는 Claude Code와 같은 AI 에이전트에 적합하며, 외부 서비스를 LLM과 잘設計된 MCP 서버를 통해 통합하는 데 필요합니다","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Cursor, Windsurf o Claude Code que necesitan integrar servicios externos con LLMs a través de servidores MCP bien diseñados","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Cursor, Windsurf ou Claude Code ayant besoin d''intégrer des services externes avec des LLMs via des serveurs MCP bien conçus","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Cursor, Windsurf oder Claude Code, die externe Dienste mit LLMs über gut entworfene MCP-Server integrieren müssen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Cursor, Windsurf ou Claude Code que precisam integrar serviços externos com LLMs por meio de servidores MCP bem projetados","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, таких как Cursor, Windsurf или Claude Code, которые нуждаются в интеграции внешних сервисов с LLMs через хорошо спроектированные серверы MCP","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Cursor و Windsurf أو Claude Code الذي يحتاج إلى دمج الخدمات الخارجية مع LLMs من خلال خوادم MCP مصممة جيدًا"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create high-quality MCP servers, enabling seamless interactions between LLMs and external services using protocols like Model Context Protocol, with support for Python via FastMCP and Node/TypeScript via MCP SDK","zh":"赋予代理创建高质量的MCP服务器的能力，实现LLMs和外部服务之间的无缝交互，使用如Model Context Protocol的协议，并通过FastMCP支持Python，通过MCP SDK支持Node/TypeScript","ja":"エージェントが高品質のMCPサーバーを作成する能力を提供し、Model Context Protocolなどのプロトコルを使用して、LLMsと外部サービスとのシームレスなやり取りを可能にし、FastMCPを介してPython、MCP SDKを介してNode/TypeScriptをサポートする","ko":"에이전트가 고품질의 MCP 서버를 생성할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여, Model Context Protocol과 같은 프로토콜을 사용하여 LLM과 외부 서비스 간의无缝な 상호작용을 가능하게 하며, FastMCP를 통해 Python 및 MCP SDK를 통해 Node/TypeScript를 지원합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear servidores MCP de alta calidad, lo que permite interacciones sin problemas entre LLMs y servicios externos utilizando protocolos como Model Context Protocol, con soporte para Python a través de FastMCP y Node/TypeScript a través de MCP SDK","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des serveurs MCP de haute qualité, permettant des interactions sans accroc entre les LLMs et les services externes en utilisant des protocoles comme Model Context Protocol, avec un support pour Python via FastMCP et Node/TypeScript via MCP SDK","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, hochwertige MCP-Server zu erstellen, wodurch eine nahtlose Interaktion zwischen LLMs und externen Diensten mithilfe von Protokollen wie Model Context Protocol ermöglicht wird, mit Unterstützung für Python über FastMCP und Node/TypeScript über MCP SDK","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar servidores MCP de alta qualidade, permitindo interações sem problemas entre LLMs e serviços externos usando protocolos como Model Context Protocol, com suporte ao Python via FastMCP e Node/TypeScript via MCP SDK","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать серверы MCP высокого качества, что позволяет осуществлять беспрепятственное взаимодействие между LLMs и внешними сервисами с использованием протоколов, таких как Model Context Protocol, с поддержкой Python через FastMCP и Node/TypeScript через MCP SDK","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إنشاء خوادم MCP عالية الجودة، مما يُمكّن التفاعلات السلسة بين LLMs والخدمات الخارجية باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل بروتوكول سياق النموذج، مع دعم لغة Python من خلال FastMCP ولغة Node/TypeScript من خلال MCP SDK"},"useCases":{"en":["Building MCP servers to integrate external APIs for real-world task automation","Designing workflow tools for LLMs to interact with external services","Developing high-quality MCP servers for advanced LLM capabilities"],"zh":["构建MCP服务器以集成外部API进行实世界任务自动化","设计工作流工具以使LLMs与外部服务交互","开发高质量的MCP服务器以实现高级LLM功能"],"ja":["実世界のタスク自動化のための外部APIを統合するMCPサーバーの構築","LLMsが外部サービスとやり取りするためのワークフローツールの設計","高度なLLM機能を実現するための高品質のMCPサーバーの開発"],"ko":["실세계 태스크 자동화를 위한 외부 API를 통합하는 MCP 서버 구축","LLM이 외부 서비스와 상호작용할 수 있는 워크플로우 도구 설계","고급 LLM 기능을 구현하기 위한 고품질의 MCP 서버 개발"],"es":["Construir servidores MCP para integrar APIs externas para la automatización de tareas del mundo real","Diseñar herramientas de flujo de trabajo para que las LLMs interactúen con servicios externos","Desarrollar servidores MCP de alta calidad para capacidades LLM avanzadas"],"fr":["Créer des serveurs MCP pour intégrer des API externes pour l''automatisation de tâches du monde réel","Concevoir des outils de workflow pour que les LLMs interagissent avec des services externes","Développer des serveurs MCP de haute qualité pour des capacités LLM avancées"],"de":["Erstellen von MCP-Servern zur Integration externer APIs für die Automatisierung von realen Aufgaben","Entwerfen von Workflow-Tools, damit LLMs mit externen Diensten interagieren können","Entwickeln von hochwertigen MCP-Servern für erweiterte LLM-Fähigkeiten"],"pt":["Construir servidores MCP para integrar APIs externas para automação de tarefas do mundo real","Projetar ferramentas de fluxo de trabalho para LLMs interagirem com serviços externos","Desenvolver servidores MCP de alta qualidade para capacidades avançadas de LLMs"],"ru":["Построение серверов MCP для интеграции внешних API для автоматизации реальных задач","Проектирование инструментов рабочего процесса для взаимодействия LLMs с внешними сервисами","Разработка серверов MCP высокого качества для расширенных возможностей LLMs"],"ar":["بناء خوادم MCP لدمج واجهات برمجة التطبيقات الخارجية لتحقيق آلي لعمليات العالم الحقيقي","تصميم أدوات سير العمل للتفاعل بين LLMs والخدمات الخارجية","تنمية خوادم MCP عالية الجودة لمزايا متقدمة من LLMs"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of MCP design principles","Limited to Python and Node/TypeScript implementations via FastMCP and MCP SDK","Dependent on external service APIs for integration"],"zh":["需要MCP设计原则的知识","仅限于通过FastMCP和MCP SDK的Python和Node/TypeScript实现","依赖于外部服务API进行集成"],"ja":["MCP設計の原則に関する知識が必要","FastMCPとMCP SDKを介したPythonとNode/TypeScriptへの実装のみ","外部サービスAPIへの依存による統合"],"ko":["MCP 설계 원칙에 대한 지식 필요","FastMCP 및 MCP SDK를 통한 Python 및 Node/TypeScript 구현에만 제한","외부 서비스 API에 대한 의존적인 통합"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de los principios de diseño de MCP","Limitado a implementaciones de Python y Node/TypeScript a través de FastMCP y MCP SDK","Dependiente de las APIs de servicios externos para la integración"],"fr":["Nécessite une connaissance des principes de conception de MCP","Limité aux implémentations Python et Node/TypeScript via FastMCP et MCP SDK","Dépendant des API de services externes pour l''intégration"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse der MCP-Designprinzipien","Begrenzt auf Python- und Node/TypeScript-Implementierungen über FastMCP und MCP SDK","Von externen Dienst-APIs für die Integration abhängig"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento dos princípios de design de MCP","Limitado a implementações em Python e Node/TypeScript via FastMCP e MCP SDK","Dependente de APIs de serviços externos para integração"],"ru":["Требует знания принципов проектирования MCP","Ограничен реализациями на Python и Node/TypeScript через FastMCP и MCP SDK","Зависит от API внешних сервисов для интеграции"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة مبادئ تصميم MCP","محدود بالتنفيذ بلغات Python و Node/TypeScript من خلال FastMCP و MCP SDK","يعتمد على واجهات برمجة التطبيقات للخدمات الخارجية للدمج"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"0f4592dcb53cf2b5d6b7febee6b4152018b565551a1c29e3c612f57b218ab295","repoEtag":"W/\"8b029149fa94da008a6c4f1a43152b0b329b2e734b696109a05864aae22c5410\"","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('anthropics/skills/skill-creator', 'official', 'anthropics', 'skills', 'anthropics/skills', 'skill-creator', 74575, 7681, 80, '2026-02-24T12:03:15Z', '2026-02-24T12:03:44.856Z', 'd57b6e3a44535b9c0ef454dad5c86f5df78185fc80a65c7092885b4b5e10f81b', '{"id":"anthropics/skills/skill-creator","name":"skill-creator","description":{"zh":"skill-creator技能提供创建有效技能的指南，帮助开发者扩展Claude的能力","ja":"skill-creatorスキルは、効果的なスキルを作成するためのガイドを提供し、開発者がClaudeの機能を拡張できるようにします","ko":"skill-creator 스킬은 효과적인 스킬을 생성하는 방법에 대한 가이드를 제공하여 개발자가 Claude의 기능을 확장할 수 있도록 합니다","es":"El creador de habilidades es una guía para desarrolladores que desean ampliar las capacidades de Claude con conocimientos y flujos de trabajo especializados","fr":"Le créateur de compétences est un guide pour les développeurs qui souhaitent étendre les capacités de Claude avec des connaissances et des flux de travail spécialisés","de":"Der Fähigkeits-Ersteller ist ein Leitfaden für Entwickler, die die Fähigkeiten von Claude mit spezialisierten Kenntnissen und Workflows erweitern möchten","pt":"O Criador de Habilidades é uma ferramenta para criar habilidades personalizadas para Ferramentas de IA, permitindo estender as capacidades da sua IA.","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Создатель Навыков - это инструмент для создания специализированных навыков для ИИ Агентов, позволяющий расширить возможности вашего ИИ.","ar":"أداة إنشاء المهارات هي أداة لإنشاء مهارات مخصصة للوكلاء الذكية، مما يسمح بتوسيع قدرات الوكلاء الذكية.","en":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations."},"owner":"anthropics","repo":"skills","repoPath":"anthropics/skills","stars":74575,"forks":7681,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T12:03:15Z","topics":["agent-skills"],"skillMd":{"name":"skill-creator","description":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations.","bodyPreview":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi","body":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi-step procedures for specific domains\n2. Tool integrations - Instructions for working with specific file formats or APIs\n3. Domain expertise - Company-specific knowledge, schemas, business logic\n4. Bundled resources - Scripts, references, and assets for complex and repetitive tasks\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### Concise is Key\n\nThe context window is a public good. Skills share the context window with everything else Claude needs: system prompt, conversation history, other Skills'' metadata, and the actual user request.\n\n**Default assumption: Claude is already very smart.** Only add context Claude doesn''t already have. Challenge each piece of information: \"Does Claude really need this explanation?\" and \"Does this paragraph justify its token cost?\"\n\nPrefer concise examples over verbose explanations.\n\n### Set Appropriate Degrees of Freedom\n\nMatch the level of specificity to the task''s fragility and variability:\n\n**High freedom (text-based instructions)**: Use when multiple approaches are valid, decisions depend on context, or heuristics guide the approach.\n\n**Medium freedom (pseudocode or scripts with parameters)**: Use when a preferred pattern exists, some variation is acceptable, or configuration affects behavior.\n\n**Low freedom (specific scripts, few parameters)**: Use when operations are fragile and error-prone, consistency is critical, or a specific sequence must be followed.\n\nThink of Claude as exploring a path: a narrow bridge with cliffs needs specific guardrails (low freedom), while an open field allows many routes (high freedom).\n\n### Anatomy of a Skill\n\nEvery skill consists of a required SKILL.md file and optional bundled resources:\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md (required)\n│   ├── YAML frontmatter metadata (required)\n│   │   ├── name: (required)\n│   │   ├── description: (required)\n│   │   └── compatibility: (optional, rarely needed)\n│   └── Markdown instructions (required)\n└── Bundled Resources (optional)\n    ├── scripts/          - Executable code (Python/Bash/etc.)\n    ├── references/       - Documentation intended to be loaded into context as needed\n    └── assets/           - Files used in output (templates, icons, fonts, etc.)\n```\n\n#### SKILL.md (required)\n\nEvery SKILL.md consists of:\n\n- **Frontmatter** (YAML): Contains `name` and `description` fields (required), plus optional fields like `license`, `metadata`, and `compatibility`. Only `name` and `description` are read by Claude to determine when the skill triggers, so be clear and comprehensive about what the skill is and when it should be used. The `compatibility` field is for noting environment requirements (target product, system packages, etc.) but most skills don''t need it.\n- **Body** (Markdown): Instructions and guidance for using the skill. Only loaded AFTER the skill triggers (if at all).\n\n#### Bundled Resources (optional)\n\n##### Scripts (`scripts/`)\n\nExecutable code (Python/Bash/etc.) for tasks that require deterministic reliability or are repeatedly rewritten.\n\n- **When to include**: When the same code is being rewritten repeatedly or deterministic reliability is needed\n- **Example**: `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` for PDF rotation tasks\n- **Benefits**: Token efficient, deterministic, may be executed without loading into context\n- **Note**: Scripts may still need to be read by Claude for patching or environment-specific adjustments\n\n##### References (`references/`)\n\nDocumentation and reference material intended to be loaded as needed into context to inform Claude''s process and thinking.\n\n- **When to include**: For documentation that Claude should reference while working\n- **Examples**: `references/finance.md` for financial schemas, `references/mnda.md` for company NDA template, `references/policies.md` for company policies, `references/api_docs.md` for API specifications\n- **Use cases**: Database schemas, API documentation, domain knowledge, company policies, detailed workflow guides\n- **Benefits**: Keeps SKILL.md lean, loaded only when Claude determines it''s needed\n- **Best practice**: If files are large (>10k words), include grep search patterns in SKILL.md\n- **Avoid duplication**: Information should live in either SKILL.md or references files, not both. Prefer references files for detailed information unless it''s truly core to the skill—this keeps SKILL.md lean while making information discoverable without hogging the context window. Keep only essential procedural instructions and workflow guidance in SKILL.md; move detailed reference material, schemas, and examples to references files.\n\n##### Assets (`assets/`)\n\nFiles not intended to be loaded into context, but rather used within the output Claude produces.\n\n- **When to include**: When the skill needs files that will be used in the final output\n- **Examples**: `assets/logo.png` for brand assets, `assets/slides.pptx` for PowerPoint templates, `assets/frontend-template/` for HTML/React boilerplate, `assets/font.ttf` for typography\n- **Use cases**: Templates, images, icons, boilerplate code, fonts, sample documents that get copied or modified\n- **Benefits**: Separates output resources from documentation, enables Claude to use files without loading them into context\n\n#### What to Not Include in a Skill\n\nA skill should only contain essential files that directly support its functionality. Do NOT create extraneous documentation or auxiliary files, including:\n\n- README.md\n- INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md\n- QUICK_REFERENCE.md\n- CHANGELOG.md\n- etc.\n\nThe skill should only contain the information needed for an AI agent to do the job at hand. It should not contain auxilary context about the process that went into creating it, setup and testing procedures, user-facing documentation, etc. Creating additional documentation files just adds clutter and confusion.\n\n### Progressive Disclosure Design Principle\n\nSkills use a three-level loading system to manage context efficiently:\n\n1. **Metadata (name + description)** - Always in context (~100 words)\n2. **SKILL.md body** - When skill triggers (<5k words)\n3. **Bundled resources** - As needed by Claude (Unlimited because scripts can be executed without reading into context window)\n\n#### Progressive Disclosure Patterns\n\nKeep SKILL.md body to the essentials and under 500 lines to minimize context bloat. Split content into separate files when approaching this limit. When splitting out content into other files, it is very important to reference them from SKILL.md and describe clearly when to read them, to ensure the reader of the skill knows they exist and when to use them.\n\n**Key principle:** When a skill supports multiple variations, frameworks, or options, keep only the core workflow and selection guidance in SKILL.md. Move variant-specific details (patterns, examples, configuration) into separate reference files.\n\n**Pattern 1: High-level guide with references**\n\n```markdown\n# PDF Processing\n\n## Quick start\n\nExtract text with pdfplumber:\n[code example]\n\n## Advanced features\n\n- **Form filling**: See [FORMS.md](FORMS.md) for complete guide\n- **API reference**: See [REFERENCE.md](REFERENCE.md) for all methods\n- **Examples**: See [EXAMPLES.md](EXAMPLES.md) for common patterns\n```\n\nClaude loads FORMS.md, REFERENCE.md, or EXAMPLES.md only when needed.\n\n**Pattern 2: Domain-specific organization**\n\nFor Skills with multiple domains, organize content by domain to avoid loading irrelevant context:\n\n```\nbigquery-skill/\n├── SKILL.md (overview and navigation)\n└── reference/\n    ├── finance.md (revenue, billing metrics)\n    ├── sales.md (opportunities, pipeline)\n    ├── product.md (API usage, features)\n    └── marketing.md (campaigns, attribution)\n```\n\nWhen a user asks about sales metrics, Claude only reads sales.md.\n\nSimilarly, for skills supporting multiple frameworks or variants, organize by variant:\n\n```\ncloud-deploy/\n├── SKILL.md (workflow + provider selection)\n└── references/\n    ├── aws.md (AWS deployment patterns)\n    ├── gcp.md (GCP deployment patterns)\n    └── azure.md (Azure deployment patterns)\n```\n\nWhen the user chooses AWS, Claude only reads aws.md.\n\n**Pattern 3: Conditional details**\n\nShow basic content, link to advanced content:\n\n```markdown\n# DOCX Processing\n\n## Creating documents\n\nUse docx-js for new documents. See [DOCX-JS.md](DOCX-JS.md).\n\n## Editing documents\n\nFor simple edits, modify the XML directly.\n\n**For tracked changes**: See [REDLINING.md](REDLINING.md)\n**For OOXML details**: See [OOXML.md](OOXML.md)\n```\n\nClaude reads REDLINING.md or OOXML.md only when the user needs those features.\n\n**Important guidelines:**\n\n- **Avoid deeply nested references** - Keep references one level deep from SKILL.md. All reference files should link directly from SKILL.md.\n- **Structure longer reference files** - For files longer than 100 lines, include a table of contents at the top so Claude can see the full scope when previewing.\n\n## Skill Creation Process\n\nSkill creation involves these steps:\n\n1. Understand the skill with concrete examples\n2. Plan reusable skill contents (scripts, references, assets)\n3. Initialize the skill (run init_skill.py)\n4. Edit the skill (implement resources and write SKILL.md)\n5. Package the skill (run package_skill.py)\n6. Iterate based on real usage\n\nFollow these steps in order, skipping only if there is a clear reason why they are not applicable.\n\n### Step 1: Understanding the Skill with Concrete Examples\n\nSkip this step only when the skill''s usage patterns are already clearly understood. It remains valuable even when working with an existing skill.\n\nTo create an effective skill, clearly understand concrete examples of how the skill will be used. This understanding can come from either direct user examples or generated examples that are validated with user feedback.\n\nFor example, when building an image-editor skill, relevant questions include:\n\n- \"What functionality should the image-editor skill support? Editing, rotating, anything else?\"\n- \"Can you give some examples of how this skill would be used?\"\n- \"I can imagine users asking for things like ''Remove the red-eye from this image'' or ''Rotate this image''. Are there other ways you imagine this skill being used?\"\n- \"What would a user say that should trigger this skill?\"\n\nTo avoid overwhelming users, avoid asking too many questions in a single message. Start with the most important questions and follow up as needed for better effectiveness.\n\nConclude this step when there is a clear sense of the functionality the skill should support.\n\n### Step 2: Planning the Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo turn concrete examples into an effective skill, analyze each example by:\n\n1. Considering how to execute on the example from scratch\n2. Identifying what scripts, references, and assets would be helpful when executing these workflows repeatedly\n\nExample: When building a `pdf-editor` skill to handle queries like \"Help me rotate this PDF,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Rotating a PDF requires re-writing the same code each time\n2. A `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` script would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When designing a `frontend-webapp-builder` skill for queries like \"Build me a todo app\" or \"Build me a dashboard to track my steps,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Writing a frontend webapp requires the same boilerplate HTML/React each time\n2. An `assets/hello-world/` template containing the boilerplate HTML/React project files would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When building a `big-query` skill to handle queries like \"How many users have logged in today?\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Querying BigQuery requires re-discovering the table schemas and relationships each time\n2. A `references/schema.md` file documenting the table schemas would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nTo establish the skill''s contents, analyze each concrete example to create a list of the reusable resources to include: scripts, references, and assets.\n\n### Step 3: Initializing the Skill\n\nAt this point, it is time to actually create the skill.\n\nSkip this step only if the skill being developed already exists, and iteration or packaging is needed. In this case, continue to the next step.\n\nWhen creating a new skill from scratch, always run the `init_skill.py` script. The script conveniently generates a new template skill directory that automatically includes everything a skill requires, making the skill creation process much more efficient and reliable.\n\nUsage:\n\n```bash\nscripts/init_skill.py <skill-name> --path <output-directory>\n```\n\nThe script:\n\n- Creates the skill directory at the specified path\n- Generates a SKILL.md template with proper frontmatter and TODO placeholders\n- Creates example resource directories: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/`\n- Adds example files in each directory that can be customized or deleted\n\nAfter initialization, customize or remove the generated SKILL.md and example files as needed.\n\n### Step 4: Edit the Skill\n\nWhen editing the (newly-generated or existing) skill, remember that the skill is being created for another instance of Claude to use. Include information that would be beneficial and non-obvious to Claude. Consider what procedural knowledge, domain-specific details, or reusable assets would help another Claude instance execute these tasks more effectively.\n\n#### Learn Proven Design Patterns\n\nConsult these helpful guides based on your skill''s needs:\n\n- **Multi-step processes**: See references/workflows.md for sequential workflows and conditional logic\n- **Specific output formats or quality standards**: See references/output-patterns.md for template and example patterns\n\nThese files contain established best practices for effective skill design.\n\n#### Start with Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo begin implementation, start with the reusable resources identified above: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` files. Note that this step may require user input. For example, when implementing a `brand-guidelines` skill, the user may need to provide brand assets or templates to store in `assets/`, or documentation to store in `references/`.\n\nAdded scripts must be tested by actually running them to ensure there are no bugs and that the output matches what is expected. If there are many similar scripts, only a representative sample needs to be tested to ensure confidence that they all work while balancing time to completion.\n\nAny example files and directories not needed for the skill should be deleted. The initialization script creates example files in `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` to demonstrate structure, but most skills won''t need all of them.\n\n#### Update SKILL.md\n\n**Writing Guidelines:** Always use imperative/infinitive form.\n\n##### Frontmatter\n\nWrite the YAML frontmatter with `name` and `description`:\n\n- `name`: The skill name\n- `description`: This is the primary triggering mechanism for your skill, and helps Claude understand when to use the skill.\n  - Include both what the Skill does and specific triggers/contexts for when to use it.\n  - Include all \"when to use\" information here - Not in the body. The body is only loaded after triggering, so \"When to Use This Skill\" sections in the body are not helpful to Claude.\n  - Example description for a `docx` skill: \"Comprehensive document creation, editing, and analysis with support for tracked changes, comments, formatting preservation, and text extraction. Use when Claude needs to work with professional documents (.docx files) for: (1) Creating new documents, (2) Modifying or editing content, (3) Working with tracked changes, (4) Adding comments, or any other document tasks\"\n\nDo not include any other fields in YAML frontmatter.\n\n##### Body\n\nWrite instructions for using the skill and its bundled resources.\n\n### Step 5: Packaging a Skill\n\nOnce development of the skill is complete, it must be packaged into a distributable .skill file that gets shared with the user. The packaging process automatically validates the skill first to ensure it meets all requirements:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder>\n```\n\nOptional output directory specification:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder> ./dist\n```\n\nThe packaging script will:\n\n1. **Validate** the skill automatically, checking:\n\n   - YAML frontmatter format and required fields\n   - Skill naming conventions and directory structure\n   - Description completeness and quality\n   - File organization and resource references\n\n2. **Package** the skill if validation passes, creating a .skill file named after the skill (e.g., `my-skill.skill`) that includes all files and maintains the proper directory structure for distribution. The .skill file is a zip file with a .skill extension.\n\nIf validation fails, the script will report the errors and exit without creating a package. Fix any validation errors and run the packaging command again.\n\n### Step 6: Iterate\n\nAfter testing the skill, users may request improvements. Often this happens right after using the skill, with fresh context of how the skill performed.\n\n**Iteration workflow:**\n\n1. Use the skill on real tasks\n2. Notice struggles or inefficiencies\n3. Identify how SKILL.md or bundled resources should be updated\n4. Implement changes and test again\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-24T12:03:44.856Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理技能创建","ja":"AIエージェントスキル作成","ko":"AI 에이전트 스킬 생성","es":"Herramientas de AI: Creador de Habilidades para Desarroll...","fr":"Outils d''IA : Créateur de Compétences pour Développeurs","de":"KI-Tools: Fähigkeits-Ersteller für Entwickler","pt":"Criador de Habilidades para Ferramentas de IA","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Создатель Навыков","ar":"أداة إنشاء مهارات للوكلاء الذكية","en":"skill-creator"},"description":{"zh":"skill-creator技能提供创建有效技能的指南，帮助开发者扩展Claude的能力","ja":"skill-creatorスキルは、効果的なスキルを作成するためのガイドを提供し、開発者がClaudeの機能を拡張できるようにします","ko":"skill-creator 스킬은 효과적인 스킬을 생성하는 방법에 대한 가이드를 제공하여 개발자가 Claude의 기능을 확장할 수 있도록 합니다","es":"El creador de habilidades es una guía para desarrolladores que desean ampliar las capacidades de Claude con conocimientos y flujos de trabajo especializados","fr":"Le créateur de compétences est un guide pour les développeurs qui souhaitent étendre les capacités de Claude avec des connaissances et des flux de travail sp...","de":"Der Fähigkeits-Ersteller ist ein Leitfaden für Entwickler, die die Fähigkeiten von Claude mit spezialisierten Kenntnissen und Workflows erweitern möchten","pt":"O Criador de Habilidades é uma ferramenta para criar habilidades personalizadas para Ferramentas de IA, permitindo estender as capacidades da sua IA.","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Создатель Навыков - это инструмент для создания специализированных навыков для ИИ Агентов, позволяющий расширить возможности вашего ИИ.","ar":"أداة إنشاء المهارات هي أداة لإنشاء مهارات مخصصة للوكلاء الذكية، مما يسمح بتوسيع قدرات الوكلاء الذكية.","en":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capab..."},"definition":{"en":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations."},"features":{"zh":["提供专业知识和工作流","支持工具集成","扩展Claude的能力","创建自定义技能","支持多种开发语言"],"ja":["専門知識とワークフローを提供","ツール統合をサポート","Claudeの機能を拡張","カスタムスキルを作成","複数の開発言語をサポート"],"ko":["전문 지식과 워크플로 제공","툴 통합 지원","Claude의 기능 확장","사용자 지정 스킬 생성","다중 개발 언어 지원"],"es":["Creación de habilidades personalizadas","Integración de flujos de trabajo especializados","Ampliación de las capacidades de Claude","Paquetes modulares y autocontenidos","Conocimientos y herramientas especializadas"],"fr":["Création de compétences personnalisées","Intégration de flux de travail spécialisés","Étendre les capacités de Claude","Paquets modulaires et autocontenus","Connaissances et outils spécialisés"],"de":["Erstellung von benutzerdefinierten Fähigkeiten","Integration von spezialisierten Workflows","Erweiterung der Fähigkeiten von Claude","Modulare und selbstenthaltene Pakete","Spezialisierte Kenntnisse und Tools"],"pt":["Criação de habilidades personalizadas","Extensão das capacidades da IA","Integração com fluxos de trabalho especializados","Ferramentas de desenvolvimento de habilidades","Suporte a múltiplos domínios e tarefas"],"ru":["Создание специализированных навыков","Расширение возможностей ИИ","Интеграция с специализированными рабочими процессами","Инструменты разработки навыков","Поддержка нескольких доменов и задач"],"ar":["إنشاء مهارات مخصصة","توسيع قدرات الوكلاء الذكية","دمج مع سير عمل متخصص","أدوات تطوير المهارات","دعم متعددة المجالات والمهام"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","技能创建","Claude扩展","专业知识","工作流","工具集成","开发语言","自定义技能"],"ja":["AIエージェント","スキル作成","Claude拡張","専門知識","ワークフロー","ツール統合","開発言語","カスタムスキル"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","스킬 생성","Claude 확장","전문 지식","워크플로","툴 통합","개발 언어","사용자 지정 스킬"],"es":["herramientas de AI","creador de habilidades","desarrollo de habilidades","ampliación de capacidades","conocimientos especializados","flujos de trabajo","paquetes modulares","Claude","IA"],"fr":["outils d''IA","créateur de compétences","développement de compétences","étendre les capacités","connaissances spécialisées","flux de travail","paquets modulaires","Claude","IA"],"de":["KI-Tools","Fähigkeits-Ersteller","Entwicklung von Fähigkeiten","Erweiterung der Fähigkeiten","spezialisierte Kenntnisse","Workflows","modulare Pakete","Claude","KI"],"pt":["Ferramentas de IA","Criador de Habilidades","Desenvolvimento de habilidades","Integração com fluxos de trabalho","Extensão das capacidades da IA","Habilidades personalizadas"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты","Создатель Навыков","Разработка навыков","Интеграция с рабочими процессами","Расширение возможностей ИИ","Специализированные навыки"],"ar":["الوكلاء الذكية","أداة إنشاء المهارات","تطوير المهارات","دمج مع سير عمل","توسيع قدرات الوكلاء الذكية","المهارات المخصصة"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents needing to extend their capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations.","zh":"适用于需要通过专门知识、工作流程或工具集成来扩展其功能的AI代理。","ja":"特化された知識、ワークフロー、またはツールの統合によって機能を拡張する必要があるAIエージェントに適しています。","ko":"전문 지식, 워크플로 또는 툴 통합을 통해 기능을 확장해야 하는 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que necesitan ampliar sus capacidades con conocimientos especializados, flujos de trabajo o integraciones de herramientas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA qui ont besoin d''étendre leurs capacités avec des connaissances spécialisées, des flux de travail ou des intégrations d''outils.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die ihre Fähigkeiten mit spezialisierten Kenntnissen, Workflows oder Tool-Integrationen erweitern müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que precisam estender suas capacidades com conhecimento especializado, fluxos de trabalho ou integrações de ferramentas.","ru":"Идеально для ИИ-агентов, которым необходимо расширить свои возможности с помощью специализированных знаний, рабочих процессов или интеграции инструментов.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكيين الذين يحتاجون إلى توسيع قدراتهم المعرفية المتخصصة أو سلاسل العمل أو دمج الأدوات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create modular, self-contained packages that provide specialized workflows, procedural knowledge, and tool integrations, effectively transforming them into specialized agents equipped with domain-specific expertise using multi-step workflows.","zh":"赋予代理创建模块化、自包含的软件包的能力，这些软件包提供特化的工作流程、程序化知识和工具集成，有效地将它们转化为具有多步骤工作流程的领域特定专长的特化代理。","ja":"エージェントに、特化されたワークフロー、手順知識、ツールの統合を提供するモジュラーで自己完結したパッケージを作成する機能を付与し、多段階のワークフローを使用してドメイン特有の専門知識を備えた特化エージェントに変換します。","ko":"에이전트에게 특화된 워크플로우, 절차 지식 및 툴 통합을 제공하는 모듈화된 자체 포함 패키지를 생성할 수 있는 기능을 부여하여, 다단계 워크플로우를 사용하여 도메인 특정 전문 지식을 보유한 특화 에이전트로 변환합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear paquetes modulares y autocontenidos que proporcionan flujos de trabajo especializados, conocimiento procedural y integraciones de herramientas, transformándolos efectivamente en agentes especializados equipados con experiencia específica de dominio utilizando flujos de trabajo multietapa.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des packages modulaires et autocontenus qui fournissent des flux de travail spécialisés, des connaissances procédurales et des intégrations d''outils, les transformant effectivement en agents spécialisés équipés d''expertise spécifique de domaine en utilisant des flux de travail multietapas.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, modulare, selbstenthaltene Pakete zu erstellen, die spezialisierte Workflows, prozedurales Wissen und Tool-Integrationen bereitstellen, und verwandelt sie damit effektiv in spezialisierte Agents, die mit domänen-spezifischem Fachwissen ausgestattet sind und mehrschrittige Workflows verwenden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar pacotes modulares e autossuficientes que fornecem fluxos de trabalho especializados, conhecimento procedural e integrações de ferramentas, transformando-os efetivamente em agentes especializados equipados com conhecimento específico de domínio usando fluxos de trabalho em várias etapas.","ru":"Предоставляет агентам возможность создавать модульные, самодостаточные пакеты, которые обеспечивают специализированные рабочие процессы, процедурные знания и интеграцию инструментов, эффективно превращая их в специализированных агентов, оснащенных экспертизой в конкретной области с помощью многоступенчатых рабочих процессов.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إنشاء حزم متوافقة وذاتية الحفظ تقدم سلاسل عمل متخصصة ومعرفة إجرائية ودمج أدوات، مما يجعلهم في الواقع وكلاء متخصصين مجهزين بالخبرة المحددة بالمجال باستخدام سلاسل عمل متعددة المراحل."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating domain-specific skills for specialized tasks","Updating existing skills with new workflows or tool integrations","Developing procedural knowledge for agents in specific domains"],"zh":["为专门任务创建领域特定技能","使用新工作流程或工具集成更新现有技能","为特定领域的代理开发程序化知识"],"ja":["特定タスク用のドメイン特有のスキルを作成する","新しいワークフローまたはツールの統合を使用して既存のスキルを更新する","特定ドメインのエージェント用の手順知識を開発する"],"ko":["특정 태스크를 위한 도메인 특정 스킬 생성","새로운 워크플로우 또는 툴 통합을 사용하여 기존 스킬 업데이트","특정 도메인의 에이전트를 위한 절차 지식 개발"],"es":["Creación de habilidades específicas de dominio para tareas especializadas","Actualización de habilidades existentes con nuevos flujos de trabajo o integraciones de herramientas","Desarrollo de conocimiento procedural para agents en dominios específicos"],"fr":["Création de compétences spécifiques de domaine pour des tâches spécialisées","Mise à jour de compétences existantes avec de nouveaux flux de travail ou intégrations d''outils","Développement de connaissances procédurales pour des agents dans des domaines spécifiques"],"de":["Erstellung von domänen-spezifischen Fähigkeiten für spezialisierte Aufgaben","Aktualisierung von bestehenden Fähigkeiten mit neuen Workflows oder Tool-Integrationen","Entwicklung von prozeduralem Wissen für Agents in spezifischen Domänen"],"pt":["Criar habilidades específicas de domínio para tarefas especializadas","Atualizar habilidades existentes com novos fluxos de trabalho ou integrações de ferramentas","Desenvolver conhecimento procedural para agentes em domínios específicos"],"ru":["Создание домен-специфичных навыков для специализированных задач","Обновление существующих навыков с помощью новых рабочих процессов или интеграции инструментов","Разработка процедурных знаний для агентов в конкретных доменах"],"ar":["إنشاء مهارات محددة بالمجال لمهام متخصصة","تحديث المهارات الحالية بسلاسل عمل أو دمج أدوات جديدة","تطوير المعرفة الإجرائية للوكلاء في مجالات محددة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of Claude''s capabilities and limitations","Needs understanding of modular skill development"],"zh":["需要了解Claude的功能和局限性","需要了解模块化技能开发"],"ja":["Claudeの機能と制限を理解する必要がある","モジュラーなスキル開発を理解する必要がある"],"ko":["Claude의 기능과 제한을 이해해야 함","모듈화된 스킬 개발을 이해해야 함"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de las capacidades y limitaciones de Claude","Necesita comprensión del desarrollo de habilidades modulares"],"fr":["Nécessite une connaissance des capacités et des limites de Claude","A besoin d''une compréhension du développement de compétences modulaires"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnis der Fähigkeiten und Einschränkungen von Claude","Benötigt Verständnis für die modulare Fähigkeitsentwicklung"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento das capacidades e limitações da Claude","Necessita de compreensão do desenvolvimento de habilidades modulares"],"ru":["Требует знания возможностей и ограничений Claude","Требует понимания модульного развития навыков"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة إمكانيات وقيود كلود","يحتاج إلى فهم تطوير المهارات المتنقلة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"d57b6e3a44535b9c0ef454dad5c86f5df78185fc80a65c7092885b4b5e10f81b","repoEtag":"W/\"8b029149fa94da008a6c4f1a43152b0b329b2e734b696109a05864aae22c5410\"","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('anthropics/skills/theme-factory', 'official', 'anthropics', 'skills', 'anthropics/skills', 'theme-factory', 74575, 7681, 80, '2026-02-24T12:03:15Z', '2026-02-24T12:03:45.777Z', 'c35893e221e28895c52143cc11bf30e41a44817796b39d4b15727dadc9796552', '{"id":"anthropics/skills/theme-factory","name":"theme-factory","description":{"zh":"主题工厂AI工具提供专业的字体和颜色主题，帮助开发者快速为文档、报告和幻灯片添加专业样式","ja":"AIエージェントテーマファクトリーは、開発者がプレゼンテーション、ドキュメント、レポートなどにプロフェッショナルなスタイルを適用するためのツールキットです","ko":"테마 팩토리 AI 에이전트는 개발자가 프리젠테이션, 문서, 보고서 등에 전문가용 스타일을 적용할 수 있는 툴킷입니다","es":"Theme-factory es una herramienta de temas para Agentes de IA que ofrece una colección de temas profesionales para artefactos","fr":"Theme-factory est un outil de thèmes pour les Agents d''IA qui propose une collection de thèmes professionnels pour les artefacts","de":"Theme-factory ist ein Themen-Tool für KI-Agents, das eine Sammlung von professionellen Themen für Artefakte bietet","pt":"A Theme Factory é uma ferramenta de estilização de artefatos com temas profissionais, incluindo paletas de cores e pares de fontes","ru":"Тематическая Фабрика - это инструмент для стилизации артефактов с профессиональными темами, включая цветовые палитры и пары шрифтов","ar":"أداة مصنع Темات هي أداة لتنسيق الإعلانات باستخدام Темات احترافية، بما في ذلك ألواح الألوان والأزواج الخطية","en":"Toolkit for styling artifacts with a theme. These artifacts can be slides, docs, reportings, HTML landing pages, etc. There are 10 pre-set themes with colors/fonts that you can apply to any artifact that has been creating, or can generate a new theme on-the-fly."},"owner":"anthropics","repo":"skills","repoPath":"anthropics/skills","stars":74575,"forks":7681,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T12:03:15Z","topics":["agent-skills"],"skillMd":{"name":"theme-factory","description":"Toolkit for styling artifacts with a theme. These artifacts can be slides, docs, reportings, HTML landing pages, etc. There are 10 pre-set themes with colors/fonts that you can apply to any artifact that has been creating, or can generate a new theme on-the-fly.","bodyPreview":"# Theme Factory Skill\n\nThis skill provides a curated collection of professional font and color themes themes, each with carefully selected color palettes and font pairings. Once a theme is chosen, it can be applied to any artifact.\n\n## Purpose\n\nTo apply consistent, professional styling to presentation slide decks, use this skill. Each theme includes:\n- A cohesive color palette with hex codes\n- Complementary font pairings for headers and body text\n- A distinct visual identity suitable for differe","body":"# Theme Factory Skill\n\nThis skill provides a curated collection of professional font and color themes themes, each with carefully selected color palettes and font pairings. Once a theme is chosen, it can be applied to any artifact.\n\n## Purpose\n\nTo apply consistent, professional styling to presentation slide decks, use this skill. Each theme includes:\n- A cohesive color palette with hex codes\n- Complementary font pairings for headers and body text\n- A distinct visual identity suitable for different contexts and audiences\n\n## Usage Instructions\n\nTo apply styling to a slide deck or other artifact:\n\n1. **Show the theme showcase**: Display the `theme-showcase.pdf` file to allow users to see all available themes visually. Do not make any modifications to it; simply show the file for viewing.\n2. **Ask for their choice**: Ask which theme to apply to the deck\n3. **Wait for selection**: Get explicit confirmation about the chosen theme\n4. **Apply the theme**: Once a theme has been chosen, apply the selected theme''s colors and fonts to the deck/artifact\n\n## Themes Available\n\nThe following 10 themes are available, each showcased in `theme-showcase.pdf`:\n\n1. **Ocean Depths** - Professional and calming maritime theme\n2. **Sunset Boulevard** - Warm and vibrant sunset colors\n3. **Forest Canopy** - Natural and grounded earth tones\n4. **Modern Minimalist** - Clean and contemporary grayscale\n5. **Golden Hour** - Rich and warm autumnal palette\n6. **Arctic Frost** - Cool and crisp winter-inspired theme\n7. **Desert Rose** - Soft and sophisticated dusty tones\n8. **Tech Innovation** - Bold and modern tech aesthetic\n9. **Botanical Garden** - Fresh and organic garden colors\n10. **Midnight Galaxy** - Dramatic and cosmic deep tones\n\n## Theme Details\n\nEach theme is defined in the `themes/` directory with complete specifications including:\n- Cohesive color palette with hex codes\n- Complementary font pairings for headers and body text\n- Distinct visual identity suitable for different contexts and audiences\n\n## Application Process\n\nAfter a preferred theme is selected:\n1. Read the corresponding theme file from the `themes/` directory\n2. Apply the specified colors and fonts consistently throughout the deck\n3. Ensure proper contrast and readability\n4. Maintain the theme''s visual identity across all slides\n\n## Create your Own Theme\nTo handle cases where none of the existing themes work for an artifact, create a custom theme. Based on provided inputs, generate a new theme similar to the ones above. Give the theme a similar name describing what the font/color combinations represent. Use any basic description provided to choose appropriate colors/fonts. After generating the theme, show it for review and verification. Following that, apply the theme as described above.\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-24T12:03:45.777Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI工具主题工厂 - 快速打造专业样式","ja":"AIエージェントテーマファクトリー - プロフェッショナルスタイルを適用","ko":"AI 에이전트 테마 팩토리 - 전문가용 스타일 적용","es":"Herramientas de temas para Agentes de IA: theme-factory","fr":"Outils de thèmes pour les Agents d''IA: theme-factory","de":"Themen-Tool für KI-Agents: theme-factory","pt":"Ferramenta de Temas para Desenvolvedores - Theme Factory","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Тематическая Фабрика для Разработчиков","ar":"أداة مصنع Темات لل_AI Agents_ لمطوري البرمجيات","en":"theme-factory"},"description":{"zh":"主题工厂AI工具提供专业的字体和颜色主题，帮助开发者快速为文档、报告和幻灯片添加专业样式","ja":"AIエージェントテーマファクトリーは、開発者がプレゼンテーション、ドキュメント、レポートなどにプロフェッショナルなスタイルを適用するためのツールキットです","ko":"테마 팩토리 AI 에이전트는 개발자가 프리젠테이션, 문서, 보고서 등에 전문가용 스타일을 적용할 수 있는 툴킷입니다","es":"Theme-factory es una herramienta de temas para Agentes de IA que ofrece una colección de temas profesionales para artefactos","fr":"Theme-factory est un outil de thèmes pour les Agents d''IA qui propose une collection de thèmes professionnels pour les artefacts","de":"Theme-factory ist ein Themen-Tool für KI-Agents, das eine Sammlung von professionellen Themen für Artefakte bietet","pt":"A Theme Factory é uma ferramenta de estilização de artefatos com temas profissionais, incluindo paletas de cores e pares de fontes","ru":"Тематическая Фабрика - это инструмент для стилизации артефактов с профессиональными темами, включая цветовые палитры и пары шрифтов","ar":"أداة مصنع Темات هي أداة لتنسيق الإعلانات باستخدام Темات احترافية، بما في ذلك ألواح الألوان والأزواج الخطية","en":"Toolkit for styling artifacts with a theme. These artifacts can be slides, docs, reportings, HTML landing pages, etc. There are 10 pre-set themes with colors..."},"definition":{"en":"Toolkit for styling artifacts with a theme. These artifacts can be slides, docs, reportings, HTML landing pages, etc. There are 10 pre-set themes with colors/fonts that you can apply to any artifact that has been creating, or can generate a new theme on-the-fly."},"features":{"zh":["10种预设主题","自动生成新主题","专业的字体和颜色组合","适用于幻灯片、文档、报告等","快速应用专业样式","支持自定义主题"],"ja":["10種類のプリセットテーマ","新しいテーマを生成","プロフェッショナルなフォントと色の組み合わせ","プレゼンテーション、ドキュメント、レポートなどに対応","プロフェッショナルなスタイルを迅速に適用","カスタムテーマをサポート"],"ko":["10가지의 프리셋 테마","새로운 테마 생성","전문가용 폰트와 색상 조합","프리젠테이션, 문서, 보고서 등에 적용","전문가용 스타일을迅速に適用","커스텀 테마 지원"],"es":["10 temas preestablecidos con paletas de colores y fuentes","Personalización de temas con opciones de color y fuente","Aplicación de estilos consistentes a artefactos","Compatibilidad con artefactos como diapositivas, documentos y páginas de aterrizaje","Generación de nuevos temas de forma dinámica"],"fr":["10 thèmes prédéfinis avec des palettes de couleurs et des polices","Personnalisation de thèmes avec des options de couleur et de police","Application de styles cohérents aux artefacts","Compatibilité avec des artefacts tels que des diapositives, des documents et des pages de destination","Génération de nouveaux thèmes de manière dynamique"],"de":["10 vorgegebene Themen mit Farbpaletten und Schriftarten","Anpassung von Themen mit Farb- und Schriftartoptionen","Anwendung von konsistenten Stilen auf Artefakte","Kompatibilität mit Artefakten wie Folien, Dokumenten und Landingpages","Erzeugung von neuen Themen in Echtzeit"],"pt":["10 temas pré-definidos com paletas de cores e pares de fontes","Geração de temas personalizados","Aplicação de temas a artefatos como slides, docs e páginas de destino","Compatibilidade com React, Python, Node.js e CLI","Integração com Agent"],"ru":["10 предустановленных тем с цветовыми палитрами и парами шрифтов","Генерация индивидуальных тем","Применение тем к артефактам, таким как слайды, документы и целевые страницы","Совместимость с React, Python, Node.js и CLI","Интеграция с ИИ Агентами"],"ar":["10 темات محددة مسبقا مع ألواح الألوان والأزواج الخطية","توليد Темات مخصصة","تطبيق Темات على الإعلانات مثل الشرائح، الوثائق وصفحات الهبوط","التأثير مع React، Python، Node.js و CLI","التكامل مع _AI Agents_"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI工具","主题工厂","专业样式","幻灯片","文档","报告","React","Python","Node.js","CLI"],"ja":["AIエージェント","テーマファクトリー","プロフェッショナルスタイル","プレゼンテーション","ドキュメント","レポート","React","Python","Node.js","CLI"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","테마 팩토리","전문가용 스타일","프리젠테이션","문서","보고서","React","Python","Node.js","CLI"],"es":["Agentes de IA","Herramientas de temas","Temas preestablecidos","Personalización de temas","Estilos consistentes","Artefactos","Desarrollo de software","Herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["Agents d''IA","Outils de thèmes","Thèmes prédéfinis","Personnalisation de thèmes","Styles cohérents","Artefacts","Développement de logiciels","Outils de développement"],"de":["KI-Agents","Themen-Tools","Vorgegebene Themen","Anpassung von Themen","Konsistente Stile","Artefakte","Software-Entwicklung","Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["Theme Factory","Ferramenta de Temas","Desenvolvedores","Estilização de Artefatos","Temas Profissionais","Paletas de Cores","Pares de Fontes","React","Python","Node.js","CLI","Agent"],"ru":["Тематическая Фабрика","ИИ Агенты","Разработчики","Стилизация Артефактов","Профессиональные Темы","Цветовые Палитры","Пары Шрифтов","React","Python","Node.js","CLI","Интеграция с ИИ Агентами"],"ar":["أداة مصنع Темات","_AI Agents_","مطوري البرمجيات","تنسيق الإعلانات","Темات احترافية","ألواح الألوان","الأزواج الخطية","React","Python","Node.js","CLI","التكامل مع _AI Agents_"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Presentation Agents needing consistent, professional styling for slides, docs, and HTML landing pages with pre-set themes and on-the-fly theme generation.","zh":"适合需要为幻灯片、文档和HTML登陆页面提供一致、专业样式的演示代理，具有预设主题和即时主题生成功能。","ja":"プレゼンテーションエージェントがスライド、ドキュメント、HTMLランディングページに一貫したプロフェッショナルなスタイリングを必要とする場合に適しています。事前に設定されたテーマと即時テーマ生成機能を備えています。","ko":"プレゼンテーション 에이전트가 슬라이드, 문서 및 HTML 랜딩 페이지에 일관된 전문가적인 스타일링이 필요한 경우에 적합합니다. 사전 설정된 테마와 즉시 테마 생성 기능을 제공합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Presentación que necesitan un estilo consistente y profesional para diapositivas, documentos y páginas de aterrizaje HTML con temas preestablecidos y generación de temas sobre la marcha.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Présentation qui ont besoin d''un style cohérent et professionnel pour les diapositives, les documents et les pages de destination HTML avec des thèmes prédéfinis et une génération de thèmes en temps réel.","de":"Perfekt für Präsentationsagenten, die ein konsistentes, professionelles Styling für Folien, Dokumente und HTML-Landingpages mit voreingestellten Themen und einer Generierung von Themen auf Abruf benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Apresentação que necessitam de estilização consistente e profissional para slides, docs e páginas de destino HTML com temas pré-definidos e geração de temas em tempo real.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов презентаций, которым необходима последовательная и профессиональная стилизация слайдов, документов и HTML-страниц с предварительно заданными темами и генерацией тем на лету.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء العرض الذين يحتاجون إلى تنسيق متسق ومحترف للشرائح و الوثائق وصفحات الهبوط HTML مع موضوعات محددة مسبقًا وتوليد الموضوعات في الوقت الفعلي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to apply consistent, professional styling to presentation slide decks, docs, and reportings with 10 pre-set themes, each including a cohesive color palette with hex codes and complementary font pairings for headers and body text, using HTML and CSS protocols.","zh":"赋予代理应用一致的专业样式到演示幻灯片、文档和报告中，具有10个预设主题，每个主题包括一个协调的色彩调色板和十六进制代码以及标题和正文文本的补充字体配对，使用HTML和CSS协议。","ja":"エージェントがプレゼンテーションスライド、ドキュメント、レポートに一貫したプロフェッショナルなスタイリングを適用することを可能にします。10個の事前に設定されたテーマを提供し、それぞれが調和のとれた色彩パレットとヘックスコード、およびヘッダーとボディテキストの補完的なフォントペアリングを備えています。HTMLおよびCSSプロトコルを使用します。","ko":"에이전트가 프리젠테이션 슬라이드, 문서 및 보고서에 일관된 전문가적인 스타일링을 적용할 수 있도록 합니다. 10개의 사전 설정된 테마를 제공하며, 각 테마는 조화된 색상 팔레트와 16진수 코드 및 헤더와 본문 텍스트의 보완적인 글꼴 페어링을 포함합니다. HTML 및 CSS 프로토콜을 사용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar un estilo consistente y profesional a las diapositivas de presentación, documentos y informes con 10 temas preestablecidos, cada uno con una paleta de colores cohesiva con códigos hex y pares de fuentes complementarios para encabezados y texto del cuerpo, utilizando protocolos HTML y CSS.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer un style cohérent et professionnel aux diapositives de présentation, documents et rapports avec 10 thèmes prédéfinis, chacun comprenant une palette de couleurs cohérente avec des codes hex et des paires de polices complémentaires pour les en-têtes et le texte du corps, en utilisant les protocoles HTML et CSS.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, ein konsistentes, professionelles Styling auf Präsentationsfolien, Dokumente und Berichte mit 10 voreingestellten Themen anzuwenden, von denen jedes eine kohärente Farbpalette mit Hex-Codes und komplementären Schriftarten für Überschriften und Fließtext umfasst, unter Verwendung von HTML- und CSS-Protokollen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aplicar estilização consistente e profissional a conjuntos de slides de apresentação, docs e relatórios com 10 temas pré-definidos, cada um incluindo uma paleta de cores coesa com códigos hex e pares de fontes complementares para cabeçalhos e texto do corpo, usando protocolos HTML e CSS.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью применять последовательную и профессиональную стилизацию к слайдам презентаций, документам и отчетам с 10 предварительно заданными темами, каждая из которых включает в себя сплоченную цветовую палитру с шестнадцатеричными кодами и дополнительные пары шрифтов для заголовков и текста, используя протоколы HTML и CSS.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تطبيق تنسيق متسق ومحترف لشرائح العرض و الوثائق والتقريرات مع 10 موضوعات محددة مسبقًا، كل منها يشمل صيغة ألوان متسقة مع رموز سداسية عشرية وأزواج خطوط مکملة للرؤوس والنص الجسمي، باستخدام بروتوكولات HTML و CSS."},"useCases":{"en":["Styling presentation slide decks with pre-set themes","Generating new themes on-the-fly for unique visual identities","Applying consistent branding to HTML landing pages and docs"],"zh":["使用预设主题样式化演示幻灯片","即时生成新主题以获得独特的视觉身份","将一致的品牌应用于HTML登陆页面和文档"],"ja":["事前に設定されたテーマを使用してプレゼンテーションスライドをスタイリングする","新しいテーマを即時生成してユニークなビジュアルアイデンティティを取得する","HTMLランディングページとドキュメントに一貫したブランディングを適用する"],"ko":["사전 설정된 테마를 사용하여 프리젠테이션 슬라이드를 스타일링합니다","새로운 테마를 즉시 생성하여 고유한 시각적 아이덴티티를 얻습니다","HTML 랜딩 페이지 및 문서에 일관된 브랜딩을 적용합니다"],"es":["Estilismo de diapositivas de presentación con temas preestablecidos","Generación de nuevos temas sobre la marcha para identidades visuales únicas","Aplicación de una marca consistente a páginas de aterrizaje HTML y documentos"],"fr":["Personnalisation de diapositives de présentation avec des thèmes prédéfinis","Génération de nouveaux thèmes en temps réel pour des identités visuelles uniques","Application d''une marque cohérente aux pages de destination HTML et documents"],"de":["Styling von Präsentationsfolien mit voreingestellten Themen","Generierung neuer Themen auf Abruf für einzigartige visuelle Identitäten","Anwendung einer konsistenten Markenidentität auf HTML-Landingpages und Dokumente"],"pt":["Estilização de conjuntos de slides de apresentação com temas pré-definidos","Geração de novos temas em tempo real para identidades visuais únicas","Aplicação de marcação consistente a páginas de destino HTML e docs"],"ru":["Стилизация слайдов презентаций с предварительно заданными темами","Генерация новых тем на лету для уникальных визуальных идентичностей","Применение последовательного брендинга к HTML-страницам и документам"],"ar":["تنسيق شرائح العرض مع موضوعات محددة مسبقًا","توليد موضوعات جديدة في الوقت الفعلي لهويات بصرية فريدة","تطبيق علامة تجارية متسقة على صفحات الهبوط HTML والوثائق"]},"limitations":{"en":["Limited to 10 pre-set themes without custom theme upload capability","Requires artifact creation or existing content to apply themes"],"zh":["仅限10个预设主题，无自定义主题上传功能","需要创建构件或现有内容来应用主题"],"ja":["10個の事前に設定されたテーマに限定され、カスタムテーマのアップロード機能はありません","テーマを適用するにはアーティファクトの作成または既存のコンテンツが必要です"],"ko":["10개의 사전 설정된 테마로 제한되며 사용자 정의 테마 업로드 기능이 없습니다","테마를 적용하려면 아티팩트 생성 또는 기존 콘텐츠가 필요합니다"],"es":["Limitado a 10 temas preestablecidos sin capacidad de carga de temas personalizados","Requiere la creación de artefactos o contenido existente para aplicar temas"],"fr":["Limité à 10 thèmes prédéfinis sans capacité de téléchargement de thèmes personnalisés","Nécessite la création d''artefacts ou de contenu existant pour appliquer les thèmes"],"de":["Begrenzt auf 10 voreingestellte Themen ohne Möglichkeit zur Upload von benutzerdefinierten Themen","Erfordert die Erstellung von Artefakten oder bestehendem Inhalt, um Themen anzuwenden"],"pt":["Limitado a 10 temas pré-definidos sem capacidade de upload de tema personalizado","Exige criação de artefatos ou conteúdo existente para aplicar temas"],"ru":["Ограничен 10 предварительно заданными темами без возможности загрузки пользовательской темы","Требует создания артефактов или существующего контента для применения тем"],"ar":["محدود بـ 10 موضوعات محددة مسبقًا بدون khảية تحميل موضوع مخصص","يتطلب إنشاء محتوى أو مستندات موجودة لتطبيق الموضوعات"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"c35893e221e28895c52143cc11bf30e41a44817796b39d4b15727dadc9796552","repoEtag":"W/\"8b029149fa94da008a6c4f1a43152b0b329b2e734b696109a05864aae22c5410\"","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('anthropics/skills/xlsx', 'official', 'anthropics', 'skills', 'anthropics/skills', 'xlsx', 74575, 7681, 80, '2026-02-24T12:03:15Z', '2026-02-24T12:03:46.909Z', 'dd316db7785a6be12966c2a2d848931fbf5f518b3cdb0a66fa62ee835ead1cfc', '{"id":"anthropics/skills/xlsx","name":"xlsx","description":{"zh":"xlsx技能用于处理电子表格文件，包括打开、读取、编辑和创建新的电子表格","ja":"xlsxスキルは、電子表格ファイルの処理に使用されます。開く、読む、編集する、または新しい電子表格を作成します","ko":"xlsx 스킬은 전자표 파일을 처리하는 데 사용됩니다. 열기, 읽기, 편집, 새로운 전자표を作成","es":"Las herramientas de AI para xlsx permiten editar y crear hojas de cálculo con facilidad. Aprende a utilizarlas para optimizar tus flujos de trabajo.","fr":"Les outils d''IA pour xlsx permettent d''éditer et de créer des tableurs avec facilité. Apprenez à les utiliser pour optimiser vos flux de travail.","de":"Die AI-Tools für xlsx ermöglichen die Bearbeitung und Erstellung von Tabellen mit Leichtigkeit. Lernen Sie, wie Sie sie verwenden können, um Ihre Arbeitsabläufe zu optimieren.","pt":"A ferramenta de IA xlsx permite desenvolver soluções de edição de planilhas, incluindo criação, edição e conversão de arquivos de planilha.","ru":"ИИ Агент xlsx позволяет разработать решения для редактирования таблиц, включая создание, редактирование и конвертацию таблиц.","ar":"أداة الذكاء الاصطناعي xlsx تمكن من تطوير حلول لتعديل الجداول، بما في ذلك إنشاء وتنقيح وتبديل صيغ الجداول.","en":"Use this skill any time a spreadsheet file is the primary input or output. This means any task where the user wants to: open, read, edit, or fix an existing .xlsx, .xlsm, .csv, or .tsv file (e.g., adding columns, computing formulas, formatting, charting, cleaning messy data); create a new spreads..."},"owner":"anthropics","repo":"skills","repoPath":"anthropics/skills","stars":74575,"forks":7681,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T12:03:15Z","topics":["agent-skills"],"skillMd":{"name":"xlsx","description":"Use this skill any time a spreadsheet file is the primary input or output. This means any task where the user wants to: open, read, edit, or fix an existing .xlsx, .xlsm, .csv, or .tsv file (e.g., adding columns, computing formulas, formatting, charting, cleaning messy data); create a new spreadsheet from scratch or from other data sources; or convert between tabular file formats. Trigger especially when the user references a spreadsheet file by name or path — even casually (like \\the xlsx in my downloads\\) — and wants something done to it or produced from it. Also trigger for cleaning or restructuring messy tabular data files (malformed rows, misplaced headers, junk data) into proper spreadsheets. The deliverable must be a spreadsheet file. Do NOT trigger when the primary deliverable is a Word document, HTML report, standalone Python script, database pipeline, or Google Sheets API integration, even if tabular data is involved.","bodyPreview":"# Requirements for Outputs\n\n## All Excel files\n\n### Professional Font\n- Use a consistent, professional font (e.g., Arial, Times New Roman) for all deliverables unless otherwise instructed by the user\n\n### Zero Formula Errors\n- Every Excel model MUST be delivered with ZERO formula errors (#REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?)\n\n### Preserve Existing Templates (when updating templates)\n- Study and EXACTLY match existing format, style, and conventions when modifying files\n- Never impose standardize","body":"# Requirements for Outputs\n\n## All Excel files\n\n### Professional Font\n- Use a consistent, professional font (e.g., Arial, Times New Roman) for all deliverables unless otherwise instructed by the user\n\n### Zero Formula Errors\n- Every Excel model MUST be delivered with ZERO formula errors (#REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, #N/A, #NAME?)\n\n### Preserve Existing Templates (when updating templates)\n- Study and EXACTLY match existing format, style, and conventions when modifying files\n- Never impose standardized formatting on files with established patterns\n- Existing template conventions ALWAYS override these guidelines\n\n## Financial models\n\n### Color Coding Standards\nUnless otherwise stated by the user or existing template\n\n#### Industry-Standard Color Conventions\n- **Blue text (RGB: 0,0,255)**: Hardcoded inputs, and numbers users will change for scenarios\n- **Black text (RGB: 0,0,0)**: ALL formulas and calculations\n- **Green text (RGB: 0,128,0)**: Links pulling from other worksheets within same workbook\n- **Red text (RGB: 255,0,0)**: External links to other files\n- **Yellow background (RGB: 255,255,0)**: Key assumptions needing attention or cells that need to be updated\n\n### Number Formatting Standards\n\n#### Required Format Rules\n- **Years**: Format as text strings (e.g., \"2024\" not \"2,024\")\n- **Currency**: Use $#,##0 format; ALWAYS specify units in headers (\"Revenue ($mm)\")\n- **Zeros**: Use number formatting to make all zeros \"-\", including percentages (e.g., \"$#,##0;($#,##0);-\")\n- **Percentages**: Default to 0.0% format (one decimal)\n- **Multiples**: Format as 0.0x for valuation multiples (EV/EBITDA, P/E)\n- **Negative numbers**: Use parentheses (123) not minus -123\n\n### Formula Construction Rules\n\n#### Assumptions Placement\n- Place ALL assumptions (growth rates, margins, multiples, etc.) in separate assumption cells\n- Use cell references instead of hardcoded values in formulas\n- Example: Use =B5*(1+$B$6) instead of =B5*1.05\n\n#### Formula Error Prevention\n- Verify all cell references are correct\n- Check for off-by-one errors in ranges\n- Ensure consistent formulas across all projection periods\n- Test with edge cases (zero values, negative numbers)\n- Verify no unintended circular references\n\n#### Documentation Requirements for Hardcodes\n- Comment or in cells beside (if end of table). Format: \"Source: [System/Document], [Date], [Specific Reference], [URL if applicable]\"\n- Examples:\n  - \"Source: Company 10-K, FY2024, Page 45, Revenue Note, [SEC EDGAR URL]\"\n  - \"Source: Company 10-Q, Q2 2025, Exhibit 99.1, [SEC EDGAR URL]\"\n  - \"Source: Bloomberg Terminal, 8/15/2025, AAPL US Equity\"\n  - \"Source: FactSet, 8/20/2025, Consensus Estimates Screen\"\n\n# XLSX creation, editing, and analysis\n\n## Overview\n\nA user may ask you to create, edit, or analyze the contents of an .xlsx file. You have different tools and workflows available for different tasks.\n\n## Important Requirements\n\n**LibreOffice Required for Formula Recalculation**: You can assume LibreOffice is installed for recalculating formula values using the `scripts/recalc.py` script. The script automatically configures LibreOffice on first run, including in sandboxed environments where Unix sockets are restricted (handled by `scripts/office/soffice.py`)\n\n## Reading and analyzing data\n\n### Data analysis with pandas\nFor data analysis, visualization, and basic operations, use **pandas** which provides powerful data manipulation capabilities:\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# Read Excel\ndf = pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'')  # Default: first sheet\nall_sheets = pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', sheet_name=None)  # All sheets as dict\n\n# Analyze\ndf.head()      # Preview data\ndf.info()      # Column info\ndf.describe()  # Statistics\n\n# Write Excel\ndf.to_excel(''output.xlsx'', index=False)\n```\n\n## Excel File Workflows\n\n## CRITICAL: Use Formulas, Not Hardcoded Values\n\n**Always use Excel formulas instead of calculating values in Python and hardcoding them.** This ensures the spreadsheet remains dynamic and updateable.\n\n### ❌ WRONG - Hardcoding Calculated Values\n```python\n# Bad: Calculating in Python and hardcoding result\ntotal = df[''Sales''].sum()\nsheet[''B10''] = total  # Hardcodes 5000\n\n# Bad: Computing growth rate in Python\ngrowth = (df.iloc[-1][''Revenue''] - df.iloc[0][''Revenue'']) / df.iloc[0][''Revenue'']\nsheet[''C5''] = growth  # Hardcodes 0.15\n\n# Bad: Python calculation for average\navg = sum(values) / len(values)\nsheet[''D20''] = avg  # Hardcodes 42.5\n```\n\n### ✅ CORRECT - Using Excel Formulas\n```python\n# Good: Let Excel calculate the sum\nsheet[''B10''] = ''=SUM(B2:B9)''\n\n# Good: Growth rate as Excel formula\nsheet[''C5''] = ''=(C4-C2)/C2''\n\n# Good: Average using Excel function\nsheet[''D20''] = ''=AVERAGE(D2:D19)''\n```\n\nThis applies to ALL calculations - totals, percentages, ratios, differences, etc. The spreadsheet should be able to recalculate when source data changes.\n\n## Common Workflow\n1. **Choose tool**: pandas for data, openpyxl for formulas/formatting\n2. **Create/Load**: Create new workbook or load existing file\n3. **Modify**: Add/edit data, formulas, and formatting\n4. **Save**: Write to file\n5. **Recalculate formulas (MANDATORY IF USING FORMULAS)**: Use the scripts/recalc.py script\n   ```bash\n   python scripts/recalc.py output.xlsx\n   ```\n6. **Verify and fix any errors**: \n   - The script returns JSON with error details\n   - If `status` is `errors_found`, check `error_summary` for specific error types and locations\n   - Fix the identified errors and recalculate again\n   - Common errors to fix:\n     - `#REF!`: Invalid cell references\n     - `#DIV/0!`: Division by zero\n     - `#VALUE!`: Wrong data type in formula\n     - `#NAME?`: Unrecognized formula name\n\n### Creating new Excel files\n\n```python\n# Using openpyxl for formulas and formatting\nfrom openpyxl import Workbook\nfrom openpyxl.styles import Font, PatternFill, Alignment\n\nwb = Workbook()\nsheet = wb.active\n\n# Add data\nsheet[''A1''] = ''Hello''\nsheet[''B1''] = ''World''\nsheet.append([''Row'', ''of'', ''data''])\n\n# Add formula\nsheet[''B2''] = ''=SUM(A1:A10)''\n\n# Formatting\nsheet[''A1''].font = Font(bold=True, color=''FF0000'')\nsheet[''A1''].fill = PatternFill(''solid'', start_color=''FFFF00'')\nsheet[''A1''].alignment = Alignment(horizontal=''center'')\n\n# Column width\nsheet.column_dimensions[''A''].width = 20\n\nwb.save(''output.xlsx'')\n```\n\n### Editing existing Excel files\n\n```python\n# Using openpyxl to preserve formulas and formatting\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\n\n# Load existing file\nwb = load_workbook(''existing.xlsx'')\nsheet = wb.active  # or wb[''SheetName''] for specific sheet\n\n# Working with multiple sheets\nfor sheet_name in wb.sheetnames:\n    sheet = wb[sheet_name]\n    print(f\"Sheet: {sheet_name}\")\n\n# Modify cells\nsheet[''A1''] = ''New Value''\nsheet.insert_rows(2)  # Insert row at position 2\nsheet.delete_cols(3)  # Delete column 3\n\n# Add new sheet\nnew_sheet = wb.create_sheet(''NewSheet'')\nnew_sheet[''A1''] = ''Data''\n\nwb.save(''modified.xlsx'')\n```\n\n## Recalculating formulas\n\nExcel files created or modified by openpyxl contain formulas as strings but not calculated values. Use the provided `scripts/recalc.py` script to recalculate formulas:\n\n```bash\npython scripts/recalc.py <excel_file> [timeout_seconds]\n```\n\nExample:\n```bash\npython scripts/recalc.py output.xlsx 30\n```\n\nThe script:\n- Automatically sets up LibreOffice macro on first run\n- Recalculates all formulas in all sheets\n- Scans ALL cells for Excel errors (#REF!, #DIV/0!, etc.)\n- Returns JSON with detailed error locations and counts\n- Works on both Linux and macOS\n\n## Formula Verification Checklist\n\nQuick checks to ensure formulas work correctly:\n\n### Essential Verification\n- [ ] **Test 2-3 sample references**: Verify they pull correct values before building full model\n- [ ] **Column mapping**: Confirm Excel columns match (e.g., column 64 = BL, not BK)\n- [ ] **Row offset**: Remember Excel rows are 1-indexed (DataFrame row 5 = Excel row 6)\n\n### Common Pitfalls\n- [ ] **NaN handling**: Check for null values with `pd.notna()`\n- [ ] **Far-right columns**: FY data often in columns 50+ \n- [ ] **Multiple matches**: Search all occurrences, not just first\n- [ ] **Division by zero**: Check denominators before using `/` in formulas (#DIV/0!)\n- [ ] **Wrong references**: Verify all cell references point to intended cells (#REF!)\n- [ ] **Cross-sheet references**: Use correct format (Sheet1!A1) for linking sheets\n\n### Formula Testing Strategy\n- [ ] **Start small**: Test formulas on 2-3 cells before applying broadly\n- [ ] **Verify dependencies**: Check all cells referenced in formulas exist\n- [ ] **Test edge cases**: Include zero, negative, and very large values\n\n### Interpreting scripts/recalc.py Output\nThe script returns JSON with error details:\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"success\",           // or \"errors_found\"\n  \"total_errors\": 0,              // Total error count\n  \"total_formulas\": 42,           // Number of formulas in file\n  \"error_summary\": {              // Only present if errors found\n    \"#REF!\": {\n      \"count\": 2,\n      \"locations\": [\"Sheet1!B5\", \"Sheet1!C10\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Library Selection\n- **pandas**: Best for data analysis, bulk operations, and simple data export\n- **openpyxl**: Best for complex formatting, formulas, and Excel-specific features\n\n### Working with openpyxl\n- Cell indices are 1-based (row=1, column=1 refers to cell A1)\n- Use `data_only=True` to read calculated values: `load_workbook(''file.xlsx'', data_only=True)`\n- **Warning**: If opened with `data_only=True` and saved, formulas are replaced with values and permanently lost\n- For large files: Use `read_only=True` for reading or `write_only=True` for writing\n- Formulas are preserved but not evaluated - use scripts/recalc.py to update values\n\n### Working with pandas\n- Specify data types to avoid inference issues: `pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', dtype={''id'': str})`\n- For large files, read specific columns: `pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', usecols=[''A'', ''C'', ''E''])`\n- Handle dates properly: `pd.read_excel(''file.xlsx'', parse_dates=[''date_column''])`\n\n## Code Style Guidelines\n**IMPORTANT**: When generating Python code for Excel operations:\n- Write minimal, concise Python code without unnecessary comments\n- Avoid verbose variable names and redundant operations\n- Avoid unnecessary print statements\n\n**For Excel files themselves**:\n- Add comments to cells with complex formulas or important assumptions\n- Document data sources for hardcoded values\n- Include notes for key calculations and model sections"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-24T12:03:46.909Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能工具-xlsx技能","ja":"AIエージェント-xlsxスキル","ko":"AI 에이전트-xlsx 스킬","es":"Herramientas de AI para xlsx: Edición y Creación de Hojas...","fr":"Outils d''IA pour xlsx : Édition et Création de Tableurs","de":"AI-Tools für xlsx: Bearbeitung und Erstellung von Tabellen","pt":"Ferramentas de IA xlsx: Edição de Planilhas","ru":"ИИ Агенты xlsx: Редактирование Таблиц","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي xlsx: تحرير الجداول","en":"xlsx"},"description":{"zh":"xlsx技能用于处理电子表格文件，包括打开、读取、编辑和创建新的电子表格","ja":"xlsxスキルは、電子表格ファイルの処理に使用されます。開く、読む、編集する、または新しい電子表格を作成します","ko":"xlsx 스킬은 전자표 파일을 처리하는 데 사용됩니다. 열기, 읽기, 편집, 새로운 전자표を作成","es":"Las herramientas de AI para xlsx permiten editar y crear hojas de cálculo con facilidad. Aprende a utilizarlas para optimizar tus flujos de trabajo.","fr":"Les outils d''IA pour xlsx permettent d''éditer et de créer des tableurs avec facilité. Apprenez à les utiliser pour optimiser vos flux de travail.","de":"Die AI-Tools für xlsx ermöglichen die Bearbeitung und Erstellung von Tabellen mit Leichtigkeit. Lernen Sie, wie Sie sie verwenden können, um Ihre Arbeitsablä...","pt":"A ferramenta de IA xlsx permite desenvolver soluções de edição de planilhas, incluindo criação, edição e conversão de arquivos de planilha.","ru":"ИИ Агент xlsx позволяет разработать решения для редактирования таблиц, включая создание, редактирование и конвертацию таблиц.","ar":"أداة الذكاء الاصطناعي xlsx تمكن من تطوير حلول لتعديل الجداول، بما في ذلك إنشاء وتنقيح وتبديل صيغ الجداول.","en":"Use this skill any time a spreadsheet file is the primary input or output. This means any task where the user wants to: open, read, edit, or fix an existing ..."},"definition":{"en":"Use this skill any time a spreadsheet file is the primary input or output. This means any task where the user wants to: open, read, edit, or fix an existing .xlsx, .xlsm, .csv, or .tsv file (e.g., adding columns, computing formulas, formatting, charting, cleaning messy data); create a new spreadsheet from scratch or from other data sources; or convert between tabular file formats. Trigger especially when the user references a spreadsheet file by name or path — even casually (like \\the xlsx in my downloads\\) — and wants something done to it or produced from it. Also trigger for cleaning or restructuring messy tabular data files (malformed rows, misplaced headers, junk data) into proper spreadsheets. The deliverable must be a spreadsheet file. Do NOT trigger when the primary deliverable is a Word document, HTML report, standalone Python script, database pipeline, or Google Sheets API integration, even if tabular data is involved."},"features":{"zh":["支持打开、读取、编辑和创建新的电子表格","支持多种电子表格文件格式，包括.xlsx、.xlsm、.csv和.tsv","可以添加列、计算公式、格式化和创建图表","可以清理和重构乱码的表格数据文件","支持使用专业字体和零公式错误"],"ja":["電子表格を開く、読む、編集する、または新しい電子表格を作成することをサポート","複数の電子表格ファイル形式をサポートします。.xlsx、.xlsm、.csv、.tsvなど","列の追加、式の計算、書式設定、チャートの作成が可能","不正なデータファイルをクリーンアップして再構築することができます","プロフェッショナルなフォントとゼロのフォーミュラエラーをサポート"],"ko":["新的 전자표를 열기, 읽기, 편집, 새로운 전자표を作成","여러 가지 전자표 파일 형식을 지원합니다. .xlsx, .xlsm, .csv, .tsv 등","열 추가, 수식 계산, 서식 지정, 차트 생성이 가능","잘못된 데이터 파일을 정리하고 재구성할 수 있습니다","전문적인 글꼴과 제로 공식 오류를 지원"],"es":["Edición de hojas de cálculo existentes","Creación de nuevas hojas de cálculo","Conversión entre formatos de archivos tabulares","Limpieza y reestructuración de datos","Uso de fuentes profesionales y consistentes"],"fr":["Édition de tableurs existants","Création de nouveaux tableurs","Conversion entre les formats de fichiers tabulaires","Nettoyage et réorganisation de données","Utilisation de polices professionnelles et cohérentes"],"de":["Bearbeitung von bestehenden Tabellen","Erstellung von neuen Tabellen","Umwandlung zwischen Tabellendateiformaten","Reinigung und Umstrukturierung von Daten","Verwendung von professionellen und konsistenten Schriftarten"],"pt":["Criação de planilhas do zero","Edição de arquivos de planilha existentes","Conversão entre formatos de planilha","Limpeza e reestruturação de dados","Preservação de templates existentes"],"ru":["Создание таблиц с нуля","Редактирование существующих таблиц","Конвертация между форматами таблиц","Очистка и переструктуризация данных","Сохранение существующих шаблонов"],"ar":["إنشاء جداول من الصفر","تعديل ملفات الجداول الحالية","تحويل بين صيغ الجداول","تنظيف واعادة هيكلة البيانات","الحفاظ على القوالب الحالية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能工具","xlsx技能","电子表格文件","打开电子表格","读取电子表格","编辑电子表格","创建新的电子表格","表格数据处理"],"ja":["AIエージェント","xlsxスキル","電子表格ファイル","電子表格を開く","電子表格を読む","電子表格を編集する","新しい電子表格を作成する","表格データ処理"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","xlsx 스킬","전자표 파일","新的 전자표를 열기","新的 전자표를 읽기","新的 전자표를 편집","新的 전자표를 생성","表格 데이터 처리"],"es":["herramientas de AI para xlsx","edición de hojas de cálculo","creación de hojas de cálculo","conversión de formatos de archivos","limpieza de datos","agentes de AI para xlsx"],"fr":["outils d''IA pour xlsx","édition de tableurs","création de tableurs","conversion de formats de fichiers","nettoyage de données","agents d''IA pour xlsx"],"de":["AI-Tools für xlsx","Bearbeitung von Tabellen","Erstellung von Tabellen","Umwandlung von Dateiformaten","Reinigung von Daten","AI-Agents für xlsx"],"pt":["ferramentas de ia","edição de planilhas","criação de planilhas","conversão de planilhas","limpeza de dados","reestruturação de dados","preservação de templates"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты","редактирование таблиц","создание таблиц","конвертация таблиц","очистка данных","переструктуризация данных","сохранение шаблонов"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","تعديل الجداول","إنشاء الجداول","تحويل الجداول","تنظيف البيانات","اعادة هيكلة البيانات","الحفاظ على القوالب"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for Data Processing Agents requiring robust spreadsheet manipulation and file format conversion capabilities.","zh":"对于需要强大电子表格操作和文件格式转换能力的数据处理AI Agent至关重要。","ja":"堅牢なスプレッドシート操作とファイル形式変換機能を必要とするデータ処理エージェントにとって必須です。","ko":"강력한 스프레드시트 조작 및 파일 형식 변환 기능이 필요한 데이터 처리 에이전트에게 필수적입니다.","es":"Esencial para Agentes de Procesamiento de Datos que requieren capacidades robustas de manipulación de hojas de cálculo y conversión de formatos de archivo.","fr":"Essentiel pour les Agents de Traitement de Données nécessitant des capacités robustes de manipulation de feuilles de calcul et de conversion de formats de fichiers.","de":"Essenziell für Datenverarbeitungs-Agenten, die robuste Fähigkeiten zur Tabellenkalkulationsmanipulation und Dateiformatkonvertierung benötigen.","pt":"Essencial para Agentes de Processamento de Dados que exigem manipulação robusta de planilhas eletrônicas e capacidades de conversão de formato de arquivo.","ru":"Необходимо для агентов обработки данных, требующих надежной обработки электронных таблиц и возможностей преобразования формата файла.","ar":"ضروريสำหรو وكلاء معالجة البيانات الذين يتطلبون مناولة قوية للجداول الإلكترونية وقدرات تحويل تنسيق الملف."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables direct creation, editing, and repair of .xlsx, .xlsm, .csv, and .tsv files with professional formatting and zero formula errors. Automates data cleaning, restructuring messy tabular files, and preserves existing templates while maintaining consistent professional fonts.","zh":"支持直接创建、编辑和修复具有专业格式且零公式错误的 .xlsx、.xlsm、.csv 和 .tsv 文件。可自动化数据清洗、重构混乱的表格文件，并在保持一致性专业字体的同时保留现有模板。","ja":"プロフェッショナルなフォーマットと数式エラーゼロで、.xlsx、.xlsm、.csv、.tsvファイルの直接作成、編集、修復を可能にします。データクリーニングの自動化、乱雑な表ファイルの再構築、一貫したプロフェッショナルなフォントを維持しながら既存のテンプレートを保持します。","ko":"전문적인 형식과 수식 오류 제로로 .xlsx, .xlsm, .csv 및 .tsv 파일을 직접 생성, 편집 및 복구할 수 있습니다. 데이터 정리를 자동화하고, 지저분한 테이블 파일을 재구성하며, 일관된 전문 글꼴을 유지하면서 기존 템플릿을 보존합니다.","es":"Permite la creación, edición y reparación directa de archivos .xlsx, .xlsm, .csv y .tsv con formato profesional y cero errores de fórmula. Automatiza la limpieza de datos, reestructura archivos tabulares desordenados y preserva las plantillas existentes mientras mantiene fuentes profesionales consistentes.","fr":"Permet la création, l''édition et la réparation directes de fichiers .xlsx, .xlsm, .csv et .tsv avec un formatage professionnel et zéro erreur de formule. Automatise le nettoyage des données, restructure les fichiers tabulaires désordonnés et préserve les modèles existants tout en maintenant des polices professionnelles cohérentes.","de":"Ermöglicht die direkte Erstellung, Bearbeitung und Reparatur von .xlsx-, .xlsm-, .csv- und .tsv-Dateien mit professioneller Formatierung und ohne Formelfehler. Automatisiert die Datenbereinigung, restrukturiert unordentliche Tabellendateien und erhält vorhandene Vorlagen bei, während konsistente professionelle Schriftarten beibehalten werden.","pt":"Permite a criação direta, edição e reparo de arquivos .xlsx, .xlsm, .csv e .tsv com formatação profissional e zero erros de fórmula. Automatiza a limpeza de dados, reestrutura arquivos tabulares desorganizados e preserva modelos existentes, mantendo fontes profissionais consistentes.","ru":"Позволяет直接 создавать, редактировать и ремонтировать файлы .xlsx, .xlsm, .csv и .tsv с профессиональным форматированием и без ошибок формул. Автоматизирует очистку данных, перестраивает неорганизованные табличные файлы и сохраняет существующие шаблоны, сохраняя последовательные профессиональные шрифты.","ar":"يمكن إنشاء وتحرير وتصحيح الملفات .xlsx و .xlsm و .csv و .tsv بشكل مباشر مع تنسيق محترف وبدون أخطاء صيغة. يutomatiza تنظيف البيانات وإعادة هيكلة الملفات الجدولية غير المنظمة والحفاظ على القوالب الحالية مع الحفاظ على خطوط احترافية متسقة."},"useCases":{"en":["Cleaning malformed tabular data files","Converting between spreadsheet formats","Computing formulas and eliminating errors","Formatting professional spreadsheets from raw data"],"zh":["清理格式错误的表格数据文件","在电子表格格式之间进行转换","计算公式并消除错误","从原始数据格式化专业电子表格"],"ja":["不正な形式の表データファイルのクリーニング","スプレッドシート形式間の変換","数式の計算とエラーの排除","生データからのプロフェッショナルなスプレッドシートのフォーマット"],"ko":["잘못된 형식의 테이블 데이터 파일 정리","스프레드시트 형식 간 변환","수식 계산 및 오류 제거","원시 데이터에서 전문 스프레드시트 서식 지정"],"es":["Limpieza de archivos de datos tabulares con formato incorrecto","Conversión entre formatos de hoja de cálculo","Cálculo de fórmulas y eliminación de errores","Formateo de hojas de cálculo profesionales a partir de datos en bruto"],"fr":["Nettoyage de fichiers de données tabulaires mal formés","Conversion entre formats de feuille de calcul","Calcul de formules et élimination des erreurs","Formatage de feuilles de calcul professionnelles à partir de données brutes"],"de":["Bereinigung von fehlerhaft formatierten Tabellendatendateien","Konvertierung zwischen Tabellenkalkulationsformaten","Berechnung von Formeln und Beseitigung von Fehlern","Formatierung professioneller Tabellenkalkulationen aus Rohdaten"],"pt":["Limpeza de arquivos de dados tabulares com formato inválido","Conversão entre formatos de planilha","Cálculo de fórmulas e eliminação de erros","Formatação de planilhas profissionais a partir de dados brutos"],"ru":["Очистка файлов табличных данных с неверным форматом","Преобразование между форматами электронных таблиц","Вычисление формул и устранение ошибок","Форматирование профессиональных электронных таблиц из сырых данных"],"ar":["تنظيف الملفات الجدولية غير الصالحة","تحويل بين تنسيقات الجداول","حساب الصيغ وإزالة الأخطاء","تنسيق الجداول المحترفة من البيانات الخام"]},"limitations":{"en":["Deliverable must be spreadsheet file only","No Word document or HTML report outputs","Excludes Google Sheets API integration","Requires local file path access"],"zh":["交付物必须仅为电子表格文件","无Word文档或HTML报告输出","不包括Google Sheets API集成","需要本地文件路径访问权限"],"ja":["成果物はスプレッドシートファイルのみでなければならない","Word文書やHTMLレポートの出力なし","Google Sheets API統合は含まれない","ローカルファイルパスへのアクセスが必要"],"ko":["전달물은 반드시 스프레드시트 파일만 가능","Word 문서 또는 HTML 보고서 출력 없음","Google Sheets API 통합 제외","로컬 파일 경로 접근 권한 필요"],"es":["El entregable debe ser únicamente un archivo de hoja de cálculo","No genera salidas en documentos de Word o informes HTML","Excluye la integración con Google Sheets API","Requiere acceso a la ruta de archivo local"],"fr":["Le livrable doit être uniquement un fichier de feuille de calcul","Aucune sortie de document Word ou de rapport HTML","Exclut l''intégration de l''API Google Sheets","Nécessite un accès au chemin de fichier local"],"de":["Das Lieferbare muss ausschließlich eine Tabellenkalkulationsdatei sein","Keine Word-Dokument- oder HTML-Berichtausgaben","Schließt die Google Sheets API-Integration aus","Erfordert lokalen Dateipfadzugriff"],"pt":["O entregável deve ser um arquivo de planilha apenas","Não há saída de relatórios do Word ou HTML","Exclui integração com a API do Google Sheets","Requer acesso ao caminho do arquivo local"],"ru":["Результат должен быть только файлом электронной таблицы","Нет вывода отчетов Word или HTML","Исключает интеграцию с API Google Sheets","Требует доступа к локальному пути файла"],"ar":["النتيجة يجب أن تكون ملف جدول فقط","لا توجد إخراج تقارير وورد أو إتش تي إم إل","استبعاد دمج واجهة برمجة تطبيقات جوجل شي茨","يتطلب الوصول إلى مسار الملف المحلي"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"dd316db7785a6be12966c2a2d848931fbf5f518b3cdb0a66fa62ee835ead1cfc","repoEtag":"W/\"8b029149fa94da008a6c4f1a43152b0b329b2e734b696109a05864aae22c5410\"","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('affaan-m/everything-claude-code/configure-ecc', 'official', 'affaan-m', 'everything-claude-code', 'affaan-m/everything-claude-code', 'configure-ecc', 50960, 6308, 80, '2026-02-24T12:02:48Z', '2026-02-24T12:04:34.011Z', 'd9777d160ac9c5dbdd36ab0bdf0390d9e30236ba18ec013254a3d1325c782311', '{"id":"affaan-m/everything-claude-code/configure-ecc","name":"configure-ecc","description":{"zh":"一个用于配置Everything Claude Code（ECC）项目的交互式安装向导，用于选择和安装技能和规则","ja":"Everything Claude Code（ECC）プロジェクトの設定用インタラクティブインストールウィザード","ko":"Everything Claude Code（ECC） 프로젝트를 설정하는 인터랙티브 설치 마법사","es":"El configurador ECC es una herramienta interactiva para instalar habilidades y reglas de Everything Claude Code de forma selectiva","fr":"Le configurateur ECC est un outil interactif pour installer des compétences et des règles de Everything Claude Code de manière sélective","de":"Der ECC-Konfigurator ist ein interaktives Tool zur selektiven Installation von Fähigkeiten und Regeln von Everything Claude Code","pt":"O ECC é uma ferramenta de IA que oferece um instalador interativo para selecionar e instalar habilidades e regras.","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Everything Claude Code — это инструмент, который предоставляет интерактивный инсталлятор для выбора и установки навыков и правил.","ar":"ECC هو أداة ذكاء اصطناعي توفر مثبتًا تفاعليًا لتحديد وتثبيت المهارات والقواعد.","en":"Interactive installer for Everything Claude Code — guides users through selecting and installing skills and rules to user-level or project-level directories, verifies paths, and optionally optimizes installed files."},"owner":"affaan-m","repo":"everything-claude-code","repoPath":"affaan-m/everything-claude-code","stars":50960,"forks":6308,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T12:02:48Z","topics":["ai-agents","anthropic","claude","claude-code","developer-tools","llm","mcp","productivity"],"skillMd":{"name":"configure-ecc","description":"Interactive installer for Everything Claude Code — guides users through selecting and installing skills and rules to user-level or project-level directories, verifies paths, and optionally optimizes installed files.","bodyPreview":"# Configure Everything Claude Code (ECC)\n\nAn interactive, step-by-step installation wizard for the Everything Claude Code project. Uses `AskUserQuestion` to guide users through selective installation of skills and rules, then verifies correctness and offers optimization.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- User says \"configure ecc\", \"install ecc\", \"setup everything claude code\", or similar\n- User wants to selectively install skills or rules from this project\n- User wants to verify or fix an existing ECC ins","body":"# Configure Everything Claude Code (ECC)\n\nAn interactive, step-by-step installation wizard for the Everything Claude Code project. Uses `AskUserQuestion` to guide users through selective installation of skills and rules, then verifies correctness and offers optimization.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- User says \"configure ecc\", \"install ecc\", \"setup everything claude code\", or similar\n- User wants to selectively install skills or rules from this project\n- User wants to verify or fix an existing ECC installation\n- User wants to optimize installed skills or rules for their project\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nThis skill must be accessible to Claude Code before activation. Two ways to bootstrap:\n1. **Via Plugin**: `/plugin install everything-claude-code` — the plugin loads this skill automatically\n2. **Manual**: Copy only this skill to `~/.claude/skills/configure-ecc/SKILL.md`, then activate by saying \"configure ecc\"\n\n---\n\n## Step 0: Clone ECC Repository\n\nBefore any installation, clone the latest ECC source to `/tmp`:\n\n```bash\nrm -rf /tmp/everything-claude-code\ngit clone https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code.git /tmp/everything-claude-code\n```\n\nSet `ECC_ROOT=/tmp/everything-claude-code` as the source for all subsequent copy operations.\n\nIf the clone fails (network issues, etc.), use `AskUserQuestion` to ask the user to provide a local path to an existing ECC clone.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Choose Installation Level\n\nUse `AskUserQuestion` to ask the user where to install:\n\n```\nQuestion: \"Where should ECC components be installed?\"\nOptions:\n  - \"User-level (~/.claude/)\" — \"Applies to all your Claude Code projects\"\n  - \"Project-level (.claude/)\" — \"Applies only to the current project\"\n  - \"Both\" — \"Common/shared items user-level, project-specific items project-level\"\n```\n\nStore the choice as `INSTALL_LEVEL`. Set the target directory:\n- User-level: `TARGET=~/.claude`\n- Project-level: `TARGET=.claude` (relative to current project root)\n- Both: `TARGET_USER=~/.claude`, `TARGET_PROJECT=.claude`\n\nCreate the target directories if they don''t exist:\n```bash\nmkdir -p $TARGET/skills $TARGET/rules\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 2: Select & Install Skills\n\n### 2a: Choose Skill Categories\n\nThere are 27 skills organized into 4 categories. Use `AskUserQuestion` with `multiSelect: true`:\n\n```\nQuestion: \"Which skill categories do you want to install?\"\nOptions:\n  - \"Framework & Language\" — \"Django, Spring Boot, Go, Python, Java, Frontend, Backend patterns\"\n  - \"Database\" — \"PostgreSQL, ClickHouse, JPA/Hibernate patterns\"\n  - \"Workflow & Quality\" — \"TDD, verification, learning, security review, compaction\"\n  - \"All skills\" — \"Install every available skill\"\n```\n\n### 2b: Confirm Individual Skills\n\nFor each selected category, print the full list of skills below and ask the user to confirm or deselect specific ones. If the list exceeds 4 items, print the list as text and use `AskUserQuestion` with an \"Install all listed\" option plus \"Other\" for the user to paste specific names.\n\n**Category: Framework & Language (16 skills)**\n\n| Skill | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `backend-patterns` | Backend architecture, API design, server-side best practices for Node.js/Express/Next.js |\n| `coding-standards` | Universal coding standards for TypeScript, JavaScript, React, Node.js |\n| `django-patterns` | Django architecture, REST API with DRF, ORM, caching, signals, middleware |\n| `django-security` | Django security: auth, CSRF, SQL injection, XSS prevention |\n| `django-tdd` | Django testing with pytest-django, factory_boy, mocking, coverage |\n| `django-verification` | Django verification loop: migrations, linting, tests, security scans |\n| `frontend-patterns` | React, Next.js, state management, performance, UI patterns |\n| `golang-patterns` | Idiomatic Go patterns, conventions for robust Go applications |\n| `golang-testing` | Go testing: table-driven tests, subtests, benchmarks, fuzzing |\n| `java-coding-standards` | Java coding standards for Spring Boot: naming, immutability, Optional, streams |\n| `python-patterns` | Pythonic idioms, PEP 8, type hints, best practices |\n| `python-testing` | Python testing with pytest, TDD, fixtures, mocking, parametrization |\n| `springboot-patterns` | Spring Boot architecture, REST API, layered services, caching, async |\n| `springboot-security` | Spring Security: authn/authz, validation, CSRF, secrets, rate limiting |\n| `springboot-tdd` | Spring Boot TDD with JUnit 5, Mockito, MockMvc, Testcontainers |\n| `springboot-verification` | Spring Boot verification: build, static analysis, tests, security scans |\n\n**Category: Database (3 skills)**\n\n| Skill | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `clickhouse-io` | ClickHouse patterns, query optimization, analytics, data engineering |\n| `jpa-patterns` | JPA/Hibernate entity design, relationships, query optimization, transactions |\n| `postgres-patterns` | PostgreSQL query optimization, schema design, indexing, security |\n\n**Category: Workflow & Quality (8 skills)**\n\n| Skill | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `continuous-learning` | Auto-extract reusable patterns from sessions as learned skills |\n| `continuous-learning-v2` | Instinct-based learning with confidence scoring, evolves into skills/commands/agents |\n| `eval-harness` | Formal evaluation framework for eval-driven development (EDD) |\n| `iterative-retrieval` | Progressive context refinement for subagent context problem |\n| `security-review` | Security checklist: auth, input, secrets, API, payment features |\n| `strategic-compact` | Suggests manual context compaction at logical intervals |\n| `tdd-workflow` | Enforces TDD with 80%+ coverage: unit, integration, E2E |\n| `verification-loop` | Verification and quality loop patterns |\n\n**Standalone**\n\n| Skill | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `project-guidelines-example` | Template for creating project-specific skills |\n\n### 2c: Execute Installation\n\nFor each selected skill, copy the entire skill directory:\n```bash\ncp -r $ECC_ROOT/skills/<skill-name> $TARGET/skills/\n```\n\nNote: `continuous-learning` and `continuous-learning-v2` have extra files (config.json, hooks, scripts) — ensure the entire directory is copied, not just SKILL.md.\n\n---\n\n## Step 3: Select & Install Rules\n\nUse `AskUserQuestion` with `multiSelect: true`:\n\n```\nQuestion: \"Which rule sets do you want to install?\"\nOptions:\n  - \"Common rules (Recommended)\" — \"Language-agnostic principles: coding style, git workflow, testing, security, etc. (8 files)\"\n  - \"TypeScript/JavaScript\" — \"TS/JS patterns, hooks, testing with Playwright (5 files)\"\n  - \"Python\" — \"Python patterns, pytest, black/ruff formatting (5 files)\"\n  - \"Go\" — \"Go patterns, table-driven tests, gofmt/staticcheck (5 files)\"\n```\n\nExecute installation:\n```bash\n# Common rules (flat copy into rules/)\ncp -r $ECC_ROOT/rules/common/* $TARGET/rules/\n\n# Language-specific rules (flat copy into rules/)\ncp -r $ECC_ROOT/rules/typescript/* $TARGET/rules/   # if selected\ncp -r $ECC_ROOT/rules/python/* $TARGET/rules/        # if selected\ncp -r $ECC_ROOT/rules/golang/* $TARGET/rules/        # if selected\n```\n\n**Important**: If the user selects any language-specific rules but NOT common rules, warn them:\n> \"Language-specific rules extend the common rules. Installing without common rules may result in incomplete coverage. Install common rules too?\"\n\n---\n\n## Step 4: Post-Installation Verification\n\nAfter installation, perform these automated checks:\n\n### 4a: Verify File Existence\n\nList all installed files and confirm they exist at the target location:\n```bash\nls -la $TARGET/skills/\nls -la $TARGET/rules/\n```\n\n### 4b: Check Path References\n\nScan all installed `.md` files for path references:\n```bash\ngrep -rn \"~/.claude/\" $TARGET/skills/ $TARGET/rules/\ngrep -rn \"../common/\" $TARGET/rules/\ngrep -rn \"skills/\" $TARGET/skills/\n```\n\n**For project-level installs**, flag any references to `~/.claude/` paths:\n- If a skill references `~/.claude/settings.json` — this is usually fine (settings are always user-level)\n- If a skill references `~/.claude/skills/` or `~/.claude/rules/` — this may be broken if installed only at project level\n- If a skill references another skill by name — check that the referenced skill was also installed\n\n### 4c: Check Cross-References Between Skills\n\nSome skills reference others. Verify these dependencies:\n- `django-tdd` may reference `django-patterns`\n- `springboot-tdd` may reference `springboot-patterns`\n- `continuous-learning-v2` references `~/.claude/homunculus/` directory\n- `python-testing` may reference `python-patterns`\n- `golang-testing` may reference `golang-patterns`\n- Language-specific rules reference `common/` counterparts\n\n### 4d: Report Issues\n\nFor each issue found, report:\n1. **File**: The file containing the problematic reference\n2. **Line**: The line number\n3. **Issue**: What''s wrong (e.g., \"references ~/.claude/skills/python-patterns but python-patterns was not installed\")\n4. **Suggested fix**: What to do (e.g., \"install python-patterns skill\" or \"update path to .claude/skills/\")\n\n---\n\n## Step 5: Optimize Installed Files (Optional)\n\nUse `AskUserQuestion`:\n\n```\nQuestion: \"Would you like to optimize the installed files for your project?\"\nOptions:\n  - \"Optimize skills\" — \"Remove irrelevant sections, adjust paths, tailor to your tech stack\"\n  - \"Optimize rules\" — \"Adjust coverage targets, add project-specific patterns, customize tool configs\"\n  - \"Optimize both\" — \"Full optimization of all installed files\"\n  - \"Skip\" — \"Keep everything as-is\"\n```\n\n### If optimizing skills:\n1. Read each installed SKILL.md\n2. Ask the user what their project''s tech stack is (if not already known)\n3. For each skill, suggest removals of irrelevant sections\n4. Edit the SKILL.md files in-place at the installation target (NOT the source repo)\n5. Fix any path issues found in Step 4\n\n### If optimizing rules:\n1. Read each installed rule .md file\n2. Ask the user about their preferences:\n   - Test coverage target (default 80%)\n   - Preferred formatting tools\n   - Git workflow conventions\n   - Security requirements\n3. Edit the rule files in-place at the installation target\n\n**Critical**: Only modify files in the installation target (`$TARGET/`), NEVER modify files in the source ECC repository (`$ECC_ROOT/`).\n\n---\n\n## Step 6: Installation Summary\n\nClean up the cloned repository from `/tmp`:\n\n```bash\nrm -rf /tmp/everything-claude-code\n```\n\nThen print a summary report:\n\n```\n## ECC Installation Complete\n\n### Installation Target\n- Level: [user-level / project-level / both]\n- Path: [target path]\n\n### Skills Installed ([count])\n- skill-1, skill-2, skill-3, ...\n\n### Rules Installed ([count])\n- common (8 files)\n- typescript (5 files)\n- ...\n\n### Verification Results\n- [count] issues found, [count] fixed\n- [list any remaining issues]\n\n### Optimizations Applied\n- [list changes made, or \"None\"]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### \"Skills not being picked up by Claude Code\"\n- Verify the skill directory contains a `SKILL.md` file (not just loose .md files)\n- For user-level: check `~/.claude/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md` exists\n- For project-level: check `.claude/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md` exists\n\n### \"Rules not working\"\n- Rules are flat files, not in subdirectories: `$TARGET/rules/coding-style.md` (correct) vs `$TARGET/rules/common/coding-style.md` (incorrect for flat install)\n- Restart Claude Code after installing rules\n\n### \"Path reference errors after project-level install\"\n- Some skills assume `~/.claude/` paths. Run Step 4 verification to find and fix these.\n- For `continuous-learning-v2`, the `~/.claude/homunculus/` directory is always user-level — this is expected and not an error.\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-24T12:04:34.011Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"配置Everything Claude Code（ECC）AI工具","ja":"Everything Claude Code（ECC）を設定する - AIエージェント","ko":"Everything Claude Code（ECC） 설정 - AI 에이전트","es":"Configura Agentes de IA ECC","fr":"Configurez les Outils d''IA ECC","de":"Konfigurieren Sie ECC KI-Agenten","pt":"Configurar ECC: Ferramentas de IA para Desenvolvedores","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Настройка Everything Claude Code","ar":"تكوين ECC: أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي لل مطورين","en":"configure-ecc"},"description":{"zh":"一个用于配置Everything Claude Code（ECC）项目的交互式安装向导，用于选择和安装技能和规则","ja":"Everything Claude Code（ECC）プロジェクトの設定用インタラクティブインストールウィザード","ko":"Everything Claude Code（ECC） 프로젝트를 설정하는 인터랙티브 설치 마법사","es":"El configurador ECC es una herramienta interactiva para instalar habilidades y reglas de Everything Claude Code de forma selectiva","fr":"Le configurateur ECC est un outil interactif pour installer des compétences et des règles de Everything Claude Code de manière sélective","de":"Der ECC-Konfigurator ist ein interaktives Tool zur selektiven Installation von Fähigkeiten und Regeln von Everything Claude Code","pt":"O ECC é uma ferramenta de IA que oferece um instalador interativo para selecionar e instalar habilidades e regras.","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Everything Claude Code — это инструмент, который предоставляет интерактивный инсталлятор для выбора и установки навыков и правил.","ar":"ECC هو أداة ذكاء اصطناعي توفر مثبتًا تفاعليًا لتحديد وتثبيت المهارات والقواعد.","en":"Interactive installer for Everything Claude Code — guides users through selecting and installing skills and rules to user-level or project-level directories,..."},"definition":{"en":"Interactive installer for Everything Claude Code — guides users through selecting and installing skills and rules to user-level or project-level directories, verifies paths, and optionally optimizes installed files."},"features":{"zh":["交互式安装向导","选择和安装技能和规则","验证路径和优化安装文件"],"ja":["インタラクティブなインストールウィザード","スキルとルールの選択とインストール","パスの検証とインストールファイルの最適化"],"ko":["인터랙티브 설치 마법사","스킬과 규칙의 선택과 설치","경로의 검증과 설치 파일의 최적화"],"es":["Instalación interactiva de habilidades y reglas","Verificación de rutas y optimización de archivos","Selección de habilidades y reglas personalizadas","Instalación en directorios de usuario o proyecto","Compatibilidad con CLI"],"fr":["Installation interactive de compétences et de règles","Vérification des chemins et optimisation des fichiers","Sélection de compétences et de règles personnalisées","Installation dans des répertoires d''utilisateur ou de projet","Compatibilité avec la CLI"],"de":["Interaktive Installation von Fähigkeiten und Regeln","Überprüfung von Pfaden und Optimierung von Dateien","Auswahl von benutzerdefinierten Fähigkeiten und Regeln","Installation in Benutzer- oder Projektverzeichnissen","Kompatibilität mit der CLI"],"pt":["Instalador interativo para seleção de habilidades e regras","Verificação de caminhos e otimização de arquivos","Instalação de habilidades e regras em diretórios de usuário ou projeto","Suporte a desenvolvedores para projetos de IA","Ferramentas de produtividade para desenvolvedores"],"ru":["Интерактивный инсталлятор для выбора навыков и правил","Проверка путей и оптимизация файлов","Установка навыков и правил в директориях пользователя или проекта","Поддержка разработчиков для проектов ИИ","Инструменты производительности для разработчиков"],"ar":["مثبت تفاعلي لتحديد المهارات والقواعد","تحقق من المسارات وتحسين الملفات","تثبيت المهارات والقواعد في دليل المستخدم أو المشروع","دعم المطورين لمشاريع الذكاء الاصطناعي","أدوات الإنتاجية للمطورين"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI工具","Everything Claude Code","配置","安装","交互式安装向导","技能和规则"],"ja":["AIエージェント","Everything Claude Code","設定","インストール","インタラクティブなインストールウィザード","スキルとルール"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","Everything Claude Code","설정","설치","인터랙티브 설치 마법사","스킬과 규칙"],"es":["Agentes de IA","Herramientas de desarrollo","Instalación de habilidades","Reglas de Everything Claude Code","Configuración de ECC","Desarrollo de software","Productividad de desarrollo"],"fr":["Outils d''IA","Outils de développement","Installation de compétences","Règles de Everything Claude Code","Configuration d''ECC","Développement de logiciels","Productivité de développement"],"de":["KI-Agenten","Entwickler-Tools","Installation von Fähigkeiten","Regeln von Everything Claude Code","Konfiguration von ECC","Software-Entwicklung","Entwickler-Produktivität"],"pt":["ferramentas de ia","desenvolvedores de ia","configurar ecc","instalar ecc","otimizar ecc","produtividade para desenvolvedores","ia para desenvolvedores","ferramentas de desenvolvimento de ia"],"ru":["ИИ инструменты","разработчики ИИ","настроить ИИ Агенты","установить ИИ Агенты","оптимизировать ИИ Агенты","производительность для разработчиков","ИИ для разработчиков","инструменты разработки ИИ"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","مطورو الذكاء الاصطناعي","تكوين ECC","تثبيت ECC","تحسين ECC","إنتاجية للمطورين","الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين","أدوات تطوير الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced AI Agents like Claude Code, AutoGPT, and LangChain requiring streamlined installation and configuration of skills and rules","zh":"适合于Claude Code、AutoGPT和LangChain等高级AI代理，需要简化技能和规则的安装和配置","ja":"Claude Code、AutoGPT、LangChainなどの高度なAIエージェントに適しており、スキルとルールのインストールと構成を簡素化する必要がある","ko":"Claude Code, AutoGPT, LangChain 등의 고급 AI 에이전트에 적합하며, 기술과 규칙의 설치 및 구성이 간소화되기를 요구함","es":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Avanzados como Claude Code, AutoGPT y LangChain que requieren una instalación y configuración simplificadas de habilidades y reglas","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA avancés comme Claude Code, AutoGPT et LangChain nécessitant une installation et une configuration simplifiées des compétences et des règles","de":"Ideal für erweiterte KI-Agents wie Claude Code, AutoGPT und LangChain, die eine strukturierte Installation und Konfiguration von Fähigkeiten und Regeln erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Avançados como Claude Code, AutoGPT e LangChain que exigem instalação e configuração de habilidades e regras simplificadas","ru":"Идеально для продвинутых агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code, AutoGPT и LangChain, требующих упрощенной установки и конфигурации навыков и правил","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المتقدمة مثل Claude Code، AutoGPT، و LangChain التي تتطلب تثبيتًا ومواصفات مهارات وقواعد مبسطة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to selectively install skills and rules using an interactive step-by-step wizard, verifying paths and optionally optimizing installed files through `AskUserQuestion` for enhanced user experience and efficiency, leveraging project-level or user-level directories","zh":"通过交互式的分步向导，赋予代理选择性地安装技能和规则的能力，验证路径，并可通过`AskUserQuestion`优化已安装的文件，以提高用户体验和效率，利用项目级别或用户级别的目录","ja":"インタラクティブなステップバイステップウィザードを使用して、エージェントがスキルとルールを選択的にインストールする機能を提供し、パスを検証し、`AskUserQuestion`を使用してインストールされたファイルを最適化することで、ユーザーエクスペリエンスと効率を向上させ、プロジェクトレベルまたはユーザーレベルのディレクトリを利用する","ko":"대화형 단계별 마법사를 통해 에이전트가 기술과 규칙을 선택적으로 설치할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 경로를 확인하고 `AskUserQuestion`를 통해 설치된 파일을 최적화하여 사용자 경험과 효율성을 향상시키고 프로젝트 수준 또는 사용자 수준의 디렉토리를 활용함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a instalar habilidades y reglas de forma selectiva utilizando un asistente interactivo de varios pasos, verificando rutas y opcionalmente optimizando archivos instalados a través de `AskUserQuestion` para una experiencia y eficiencia mejoradas del usuario, aprovechando directorios a nivel de proyecto o de usuario","fr":"Permet aux agents d''installer des compétences et des règles de manière sélective en utilisant un assistant interactif étape par étape, en vérifiant les chemins et en optimisant éventuellement les fichiers installés via `AskUserQuestion` pour une expérience utilisateur améliorée et une efficacité, en exploitant les répertoires au niveau du projet ou de l''utilisateur","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, Fähigkeiten und Regeln selektiv zu installieren, indem sie einen interaktiven Schritt-für-Schritt-Assistenten verwenden, um Pfade zu überprüfen und optional installierte Dateien durch `AskUserQuestion` für eine verbesserte Benutzererfahrung und Effizienz zu optimieren, indem Projekt- oder Benutzerverzeichnisse genutzt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a instalarem habilidades e regras de forma seletiva, utilizando um assistente interativo passo a passo, verificando caminhos e, opcionalmente, otimizando arquivos instalados por meio do `AskUserQuestion` para uma experiência do usuário aprimorada e eficiência, aproveitando diretórios de nível de projeto ou de usuário","ru":"Позволяет агентам выборочно устанавливать навыки и правила, используя интерактивный мастер шаг за шагом, проверяя пути и опционально оптимизируя установленные файлы через `AskUserQuestion` для улучшения пользовательского опыта и эффективности, используя каталоги уровня проекта или пользователя","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تثبيت المهارات والقواعد بشكل انتقائي باستخدام ساحر تفاعلي خطوة بخطوة، وتحقق المسارات واختياريًا تحسين الملفات المثبتة من خلال `AskUserQuestion` لتحسين تجربة المستخدم والكفاءة، من خلال استغلال الدلائل على مستوى المشروع أو المستخدم"},"useCases":{"en":["Configuring Everything Claude Code for custom skill sets","Verifying and fixing existing ECC installations","Optimizing installed files for better performance"],"zh":["为自定义技能集配置Everything Claude Code","验证和修复现有的ECC安装","优化已安装文件以提高性能"],"ja":["カスタムスキルセットのEverything Claude Codeを構成する","既存のECCインストールを検証および修復する","インストールされたファイルを最適化してパフォーマンスを向上させる"],"ko":["사용자 지정 기술 세트에 대한 모든 Claude Code 구성","기존의 ECC 설치 확인 및 수정","설치된 파일 최적화로 성능 개선"],"es":["Configuración de Everything Claude Code para conjuntos de habilidades personalizados","Verificación y reparación de instalaciones ECC existentes","Optimización de archivos instalados para un mejor rendimiento"],"fr":["Configuration de Everything Claude Code pour des ensembles de compétences personnalisés","Vérification et correction des installations ECC existantes","Optimisation des fichiers installés pour de meilleures performances"],"de":["Konfiguration von Everything Claude Code für benutzerdefinierte Fähigkeitssets","Überprüfung und Reparatur bestehender ECC-Installationen","Optimierung der installierten Dateien für bessere Leistung"],"pt":["Configurando Tudo Claude Code para conjuntos de habilidades personalizados","Verificando e corrigindo instalações ECC existentes","Otimizando arquivos instalados para melhor desempenho"],"ru":["Настройка Everything Claude Code для пользовательских наборов навыков","Проверка и исправление существующих установок ECC","Оптимизация установленных файлов для лучшей производительности"],"ar":["تكوين كل شيء Claude Code لمجموعات مهارات مخصصة","التحقق من وجود مشاكل وتعديل التركيبات الحالية ECC","تحسين الملفات المثبتة لتحقيق أداء أفضل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires user interaction through `AskUserQuestion`","Limited to Everything Claude Code project installations"],"zh":["需要通过`AskUserQuestion`进行用户交互","仅限Everything Claude Code项目安装"],"ja":["`AskUserQuestion`を使用したユーザーインタラクションが必要","Everything Claude Codeプロジェクトのインストールのみに限定される"],"ko":["`AskUserQuestion`를 통해 사용자 상호작용이 필요함","모든 Claude Code 프로젝트 설치에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere interacción del usuario a través de `AskUserQuestion`","Limitado a instalaciones de proyectos Everything Claude Code"],"fr":["Nécessite une interaction utilisateur via `AskUserQuestion`","Limité aux installations de projets Everything Claude Code"],"de":["Benutzerinteraktion durch `AskUserQuestion` erforderlich","Begrenzt auf Everything Claude Code-Projektinstallationen"],"pt":["Exige interação do usuário por meio do `AskUserQuestion`","Limitado a instalações de projeto Everything Claude Code"],"ru":["Требует взаимодействия пользователя через `AskUserQuestion`","Ограничен установками проекта Everything Claude Code"],"ar":["يتطلب تفاعل المستخدم من خلال `AskUserQuestion`","محدود بتثبيتات مشروع Everything Claude Code"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"d9777d160ac9c5dbdd36ab0bdf0390d9e30236ba18ec013254a3d1325c782311","repoEtag":"W/\"364f268e25511efbc6f9c2152da6805d934c8ccbaa49ea479a3da0f27c55af07\"","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('affaan-m/everything-claude-code/continuous-learning', 'official', 'affaan-m', 'everything-claude-code', 'affaan-m/everything-claude-code', 'continuous-learning', 50960, 6308, 80, '2026-02-24T12:02:48Z', '2026-02-24T12:04:35.496Z', 'd0de702a305d02345dfc2b32d601bd9ef4d1d53375535b45d40126660872cce0', '{"id":"affaan-m/everything-claude-code/continuous-learning","name":"continuous-learning","description":{"zh":"持续学习技能自动从 Claude Code 会话中提取可重用模式，提高开发者效率","ja":"継続的学習スキルは、Claude Code セッションから再利用可能なパターンを自動的に抽出","ko":"연속 학습 스킬은 클라우드 코드 세션에서 재사용 가능한 패턴을 자동으로 추출","es":"El agente de aprendizaje continuo extrae automáticamente patrones reutilizables de sesiones de Claude Code para su uso futuro.","fr":"L''agent d''apprentissage continu extrait automatiquement des modèles réutilisables de sessions Claude Code pour une utilisation future.","de":"Der KI-Agent für kontinuierliches Lernen extrahiert automatisch wiederverwendbare Muster aus Claude-Code-Sitzungen für die zukünftige Verwendung.","pt":"O aprendizado contínuo é uma habilidade que extrai padrões reutilizáveis de sessões do Claude Code e os salva como habilidades aprendidas para uso futuro.","ru":"Непрерывное обучение - это навык, который автоматически извлекает повторно используемые шаблоны из сессий Claude Code и сохраняет их как изученные навыки для будущего использования.","ar":"التعلم المستمر هو مهارة تقوم باستخراج أنماط قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام من جلسات Claude Code وتحفظها كمهارات متعلمة للاستخدام في المستقبل.","en":"Automatically extract reusable patterns from Claude Code sessions and save them as learned skills for future use."},"owner":"affaan-m","repo":"everything-claude-code","repoPath":"affaan-m/everything-claude-code","stars":50960,"forks":6308,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T12:02:48Z","topics":["ai-agents","anthropic","claude","claude-code","developer-tools","llm","mcp","productivity"],"skillMd":{"name":"continuous-learning","description":"Automatically extract reusable patterns from Claude Code sessions and save them as learned skills for future use.","bodyPreview":"# Continuous Learning Skill\n\nAutomatically evaluates Claude Code sessions on end to extract reusable patterns that can be saved as learned skills.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- Setting up automatic pattern extraction from Claude Code sessions\n- Configuring the Stop hook for session evaluation\n- Reviewing or curating learned skills in `~/.claude/skills/learned/`\n- Adjusting extraction thresholds or pattern categories\n- Comparing v1 (this) vs v2 (instinct-based) approaches\n\n## How It Works\n\nThis skill r","body":"# Continuous Learning Skill\n\nAutomatically evaluates Claude Code sessions on end to extract reusable patterns that can be saved as learned skills.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- Setting up automatic pattern extraction from Claude Code sessions\n- Configuring the Stop hook for session evaluation\n- Reviewing or curating learned skills in `~/.claude/skills/learned/`\n- Adjusting extraction thresholds or pattern categories\n- Comparing v1 (this) vs v2 (instinct-based) approaches\n\n## How It Works\n\nThis skill runs as a **Stop hook** at the end of each session:\n\n1. **Session Evaluation**: Checks if session has enough messages (default: 10+)\n2. **Pattern Detection**: Identifies extractable patterns from the session\n3. **Skill Extraction**: Saves useful patterns to `~/.claude/skills/learned/`\n\n## Configuration\n\nEdit `config.json` to customize:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"min_session_length\": 10,\n  \"extraction_threshold\": \"medium\",\n  \"auto_approve\": false,\n  \"learned_skills_path\": \"~/.claude/skills/learned/\",\n  \"patterns_to_detect\": [\n    \"error_resolution\",\n    \"user_corrections\",\n    \"workarounds\",\n    \"debugging_techniques\",\n    \"project_specific\"\n  ],\n  \"ignore_patterns\": [\n    \"simple_typos\",\n    \"one_time_fixes\",\n    \"external_api_issues\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Pattern Types\n\n| Pattern | Description |\n|---------|-------------|\n| `error_resolution` | How specific errors were resolved |\n| `user_corrections` | Patterns from user corrections |\n| `workarounds` | Solutions to framework/library quirks |\n| `debugging_techniques` | Effective debugging approaches |\n| `project_specific` | Project-specific conventions |\n\n## Hook Setup\n\nAdd to your `~/.claude/settings.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"Stop\": [{\n      \"matcher\": \"*\",\n      \"hooks\": [{\n        \"type\": \"command\",\n        \"command\": \"~/.claude/skills/continuous-learning/evaluate-session.sh\"\n      }]\n    }]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Why Stop Hook?\n\n- **Lightweight**: Runs once at session end\n- **Non-blocking**: Doesn''t add latency to every message\n- **Complete context**: Has access to full session transcript\n\n## Related\n\n- [The Longform Guide](https://x.com/affaanmustafa/status/2014040193557471352) - Section on continuous learning\n- `/learn` command - Manual pattern extraction mid-session\n\n---\n\n## Comparison Notes (Research: Jan 2025)\n\n### vs Homunculus (github.com/humanplane/homunculus)\n\nHomunculus v2 takes a more sophisticated approach:\n\n| Feature | Our Approach | Homunculus v2 |\n|---------|--------------|---------------|\n| Observation | Stop hook (end of session) | PreToolUse/PostToolUse hooks (100% reliable) |\n| Analysis | Main context | Background agent (Haiku) |\n| Granularity | Full skills | Atomic \"instincts\" |\n| Confidence | None | 0.3-0.9 weighted |\n| Evolution | Direct to skill | Instincts → cluster → skill/command/agent |\n| Sharing | None | Export/import instincts |\n\n**Key insight from homunculus:**\n> \"v1 relied on skills to observe. Skills are probabilistic—they fire ~50-80% of the time. v2 uses hooks for observation (100% reliable) and instincts as the atomic unit of learned behavior.\"\n\n### Potential v2 Enhancements\n\n1. **Instinct-based learning** - Smaller, atomic behaviors with confidence scoring\n2. **Background observer** - Haiku agent analyzing in parallel\n3. **Confidence decay** - Instincts lose confidence if contradicted\n4. **Domain tagging** - code-style, testing, git, debugging, etc.\n5. **Evolution path** - Cluster related instincts into skills/commands\n\nSee: `/Users/affoon/Documents/tasks/12-continuous-learning-v2.md` for full spec.\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-24T12:04:35.496Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理工具：持续学习","ja":"AIエージェント：継続的学習スキル","ko":"AI 에이전트: 연속 학습","es":"Herramientas de Agente de IA: Aprendizaje Continuo","fr":"Outils d''Agent IA: Apprentissage Continu","de":"KI-Agenten-Tools: Kontinuierliches Lernen","pt":"Aprendizado Contínuo com Ferramentas de IA","ru":"Непрерывное обучение с помощью ИИ Агентов","ar":"التعلم المستمر مع أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","en":"continuous-learning"},"description":{"zh":"持续学习技能自动从 Claude Code 会话中提取可重用模式，提高开发者效率","ja":"継続的学習スキルは、Claude Code セッションから再利用可能なパターンを自動的に抽出","ko":"연속 학습 스킬은 클라우드 코드 세션에서 재사용 가능한 패턴을 자동으로 추출","es":"El agente de aprendizaje continuo extrae automáticamente patrones reutilizables de sesiones de Claude Code para su uso futuro.","fr":"L''agent d''apprentissage continu extrait automatiquement des modèles réutilisables de sessions Claude Code pour une utilisation future.","de":"Der KI-Agent für kontinuierliches Lernen extrahiert automatisch wiederverwendbare Muster aus Claude-Code-Sitzungen für die zukünftige Verwendung.","pt":"O aprendizado contínuo é uma habilidade que extrai padrões reutilizáveis de sessões do Claude Code e os salva como habilidades aprendidas para uso futuro.","ru":"Непрерывное обучение - это навык, который автоматически извлекает повторно используемые шаблоны из сессий Claude Code и сохраняет их как изученные навыки для...","ar":"التعلم المستمر هو مهارة تقوم باستخراج أنماط قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام من جلسات Claude Code وتحفظها كمهارات متعلمة للاستخدام في المستقبل.","en":"Automatically extract reusable patterns from Claude Code sessions and save them as learned skills for future use."},"definition":{"en":"Automatically extract reusable patterns from Claude Code sessions and save them as learned skills for future use."},"features":{"zh":["自动提取可重用模式","保存学习技能","提高开发效率","支持 Claude Code 会话","可配置的抽取阈值"],"ja":["再利用可能なパターンの自動抽出","学習スキルの保存","開発効率の向上","Claude Code セッションのサポート","抽出閾値の設定"],"ko":["재사용 가능한 패턴의 자동 추출","학습 스킬의 저장","개발 효율의 향상","클라우드 코드 세션의 지원","추출 임계값의 설정"],"es":["Extracción automática de patrones reutilizables","Guardado de patrones como habilidades aprendidas","Configuración del hook de parada para la evaluación de sesiones","Revisión y curación de habilidades aprendidas","Ajuste de umbrales de extracción y categorías de patrones"],"fr":["Extraction automatique de modèles réutilisables","Enregistrement de modèles comme compétences apprises","Configuration du hook d''arrêt pour l''évaluation des sessions","Révision et curation des compétences apprises","Ajustement des seuils d''extraction et des catégories de modèles"],"de":["Automatische Extraktion von wiederverwendbaren Mustern","Speicherung von Mustern als gelernte Fähigkeiten","Konfiguration des Stop-Hooks für die Sitzungsbewertung","Überprüfung und Pflege von gelernten Fähigkeiten","Anpassung von Extraktions-Schwellenwerten und Musterkategorien"],"pt":["Extração automática de padrões reutilizáveis","Salvamento de habilidades aprendidas para uso futuro","Integração com Claude Code","Ajuste de limiares de extração e categorias de padrões","Compatibilidade com abordagens v1 e v2"],"ru":["Автоматическая извлечение повторно используемых шаблонов","Сохранение изученных навыков для будущего использования","Интеграция с Claude Code","Настройка порогов извлечения и категорий шаблонов","Совместимость с подходами v1 и v2"],"ar":["استخراج تلقائي لأنماط قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام","حفظ مهارات متعلمة للاستخدام في المستقبل","التكامل مع Claude Code","ضبط عتبات الاستخراج وفئات الأنماط","توافق مع النهج v1 و v2"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理工具","持续学习","可重用模式","Claude Code","开发效率","自动化"],"ja":["AIエージェント","継続的学習","再利用可能なパターン","Claude Code","開発効率","自動化"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","연속 학습","재사용 가능한 패턴","클라우드 코드","개발 효율","자동화"],"es":["agente de ia","aprendizaje continuo","herramientas de desarrollo","claude code","productividad","automatización","patrones reutilizables","sesiones de claude code"],"fr":["agent ia","apprentissage continu","outils de développement","claude code","productivité","automatisation","modèles réutilisables","sessions claude code"],"de":["ki-agent","kontinuierliches lernen","entwickler-tools","claude code","produktivität","automatisierung","wiederverwendbare muster","claude-code-sitzungen"],"pt":["aprendizado contínuo","Ferramentas de IA","Claude Code","produtividade","desenvolvimento de software","extração de padrões","habilidades aprendidas","integração com Claude Code"],"ru":["непрерывное обучение","ИИ Агенты","Claude Code","производительность","разработка программного обеспечения","извлечение шаблонов","изученные навыки","интеграция с Claude Code"],"ar":["التعلم المستمر","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","Claude Code","الإنتاجية","تطوير البرمجيات","استخراج الأنماط","المهارات المكتسبة","التكامل مع Claude Code"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced AI Agents like Claude Code, AutoGPT, and LangChain that require automated pattern extraction and continuous learning capabilities.","zh":"适用于Claude Code、AutoGPT和LangChain等高级AI代理，需要自动模式提取和持续学习能力。","ja":"Claude Code、AutoGPT、LangChainなどの高度なAIエージェントに適しており、自動パターン抽出と継続的な学習能力が必要です。","ko":"Claude Code, AutoGPT, LangChain 등의 고급 AI 에이전트에 적합하며, 자동화된 패턴 추출 및 지속적인 학습 능력이 필요합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de inteligencia artificial avanzados como Claude Code, AutoGPT y LangChain que requieren extracción de patrones automatizada y capacidades de aprendizaje continuo.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''intelligence artificielle avancés comme Claude Code, AutoGPT et LangChain qui nécessitent une extraction de modèles automatisée et des capacités d''apprentissage continu.","de":"Ideal für fortgeschrittene KI-Agents wie Claude Code, AutoGPT und LangChain, die eine automatisierte Musterextraktion und kontinuierliche Lernfähigkeiten erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Avançados como Claude Code, AutoGPT e LangChain que requerem extração de padrões automatizada e capacidades de aprendizado contínuo.","ru":"Идеально подходит для продвинутых агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code, AutoGPT и LangChain, которые требуют автоматизированной извлечения образцов и непрерывных возможностей обучения.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكيين المتقدمين مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT و LangChain الذين يتطلبون استخراج نمط آلي وقدرات التعلم المستمر."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to automatically extract reusable patterns from sessions and save them as learned skills, utilizing techniques such as Stop hook configuration and extraction threshold adjustment, and storing learned skills in ~/.claude/skills/learned/ for future use.","zh":"赋予代理自动从会话中提取可重用模式的能力，并将其保存为学习技能，利用Stop hook配置和提取阈值调整等技术，并将学习技能存储在~/.claude/skills/learned/中以供将来使用。","ja":"エージェントに会話から再利用可能なパターンを自動で抽出して学習スキルとして保存する能力を与え、Stop hookの構成や抽出閾値の調整などの手法を使用し、学習スキルを~/.claude/skills/learned/に保存して将来使用できるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 세션에서 재사용 가능한 패턴을 자동으로 추출하여 학습 스킬로 저장할 수 있도록 하며, Stop hook 구성 및 추출 임계값 조정 등의 기술을 사용하여 ~/.claude/skills/learned/에 학습 스킬을 저장하여 향후 사용할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes extraer automáticamente patrones reutilizables de las sesiones y guardarlos como habilidades aprendidas, utilizando técnicas como la configuración de Stop hook y el ajuste del umbral de extracción, y almacenando las habilidades aprendidas en ~/.claude/skills/learned/ para su uso futuro.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''extraire automatiquement des modèles réutilisables à partir de sessions et de les enregistrer en tant que compétences apprises, en utilisant des techniques telles que la configuration de Stop hook et l''ajustement du seuil d''extraction, et en stockant les compétences apprises dans ~/.claude/skills/learned/ pour une utilisation future.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, wiederverwendbare Muster aus Sitzungen automatisch zu extrahieren und als erlernte Fähigkeiten zu speichern, indem Techniken wie die Stop-Hook-Konfiguration und die Anpassung des Extraktions-Schwellenwerts verwendet werden, und die erlernten Fähigkeiten in ~/.claude/skills/learned/ für die zukünftige Verwendung speichern.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a extrair automaticamente padrões reutilizáveis de sessões e salvá-los como habilidades aprendidas, utilizando técnicas como configuração de hook de parada e ajuste de limiar de extração, e armazenando habilidades aprendidas em ~/.claude/skills/learned/ para uso futuro.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью автоматически извлекать повторно используемые образцы из сессий и сохранять их как выученные навыки, используя такие методы, как настройка хука остановки и корректировка порога извлечения, и хранение выученных навыков в ~/.claude/skills/learned/ для будущего использования.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على استخراج نمط قابل لإعادة الاستخدام تلقائيًا من الجلسات وحفظه كمهارات متعلمة، باستخدام تقنيات مثل تكوين hook التوقف وتعديل عتبة الاستخراج، وتخزين المهارات المكتسبة في ~/.claude/skills/learned/ للاستخدام في المستقبل."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating pattern extraction from Claude Code sessions","Configuring session evaluation for optimal learned skill generation","Reviewing and curating learned skills for improved agent performance"],"zh":["从Claude Code会话中自动提取模式","配置会话评估以生成最佳的学习技能","审查和策划学习技能以提高代理性能"],"ja":["Claude Codeのセッションから自動的にパターンを抽出する","セッションの評価を構成して最適な学習スキルを生成する","学習スキルをレビューしてカーセックしてエージェントのパフォーマンスを向上させる"],"ko":["Claude Code 세션에서 자동으로 패턴을 추출하는 것","세션 평가를 구성하여 최적의 학습 스킬을 생성하는 것","학습 스킬을 검토하고 선별하여 에이전트 성능을 개선하는 것"],"es":["Automatización de la extracción de patrones de sesiones de Claude Code","Configuración de la evaluación de sesiones para la generación óptima de habilidades aprendidas","Revisión y curación de habilidades aprendidas para una mejoría del rendimiento del agente"],"fr":["Automatisation de l''extraction de modèles à partir de sessions de Claude Code","Configuration de l''évaluation de sessions pour la génération optimale de compétences apprises","Révision et curation de compétences apprises pour améliorer les performances de l''agent"],"de":["Automatisierung der Musterextraktion aus Claude-Code-Sitzungen","Konfiguration der Sitzungsbewertung für die optimale Generierung erlernter Fähigkeiten","Überprüfung und Pflege erlernter Fähigkeiten für eine Verbesserung der Leistung des Agents"],"pt":["Automatizar a extração de padrões de sessões do Claude Code","Configurar a avaliação de sessões para geração ótima de habilidades aprendidas","Revisar e curar habilidades aprendidas para melhorar o desempenho do agente"],"ru":["Автоматизировать извлечение образцов из сессий Claude Code","Настроить оценку сессий для оптимальной генерации выученных навыков","Просмотреть и отредактировать выученные навыки для улучшения производительности агента"],"ar":["تأتمتة استخراج الأنماط من الجلسات الخاصة ب Claude Code","تكوين تقييم الجلسات لتوليد مهارات متعلمة أمثلية","استعراض وتنقية المهارات المكتسبة لتحسين أداء الوكيل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to Claude Code sessions","Dependent on effective Stop hook configuration","Limited to extracting patterns from evaluated sessions"],"zh":["需要访问Claude Code会话","依赖于有效的Stop hook配置","仅限从评估会话中提取模式"],"ja":["Claude Codeのセッションへのアクセスが必要","有効なStop hookの構成に依存する","評価されたセッションのみからパターンを抽出できる"],"ko":["Claude Code 세션에 접근할 수 있어야 함","유효한 Stop hook 구성에 의존함","평가된 세션에서만 패턴을 추출할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere acceso a sesiones de Claude Code","Depende de una configuración efectiva de Stop hook","Limitado a la extracción de patrones de sesiones evaluadas"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès aux sessions de Claude Code","Dépend d''une configuration efficace de Stop hook","Limité à l''extraction de modèles à partir de sessions évaluées"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf Claude-Code-Sitzungen","Hängt von einer effektiven Stop-Hook-Konfiguration ab","Begrenzt auf die Extraktion von Mustern aus bewerteten Sitzungen"],"pt":["Requer acesso a sessões do Claude Code","Depende da configuração eficaz do hook de parada","Limitado à extração de padrões de sessões avaliadas"],"ru":["Требует доступа к сессиям Claude Code","Зависит от эффективной настройки хука остановки","Ограничен извлечением образцов из оцененных сессий"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى الجلسات الخاصة ب Claude Code","يعتمد على تكوين hook التوقف الفعال","محدود باستخراج الأنماط من الجلسات المقيمة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"d0de702a305d02345dfc2b32d601bd9ef4d1d53375535b45d40126660872cce0","repoEtag":"W/\"364f268e25511efbc6f9c2152da6805d934c8ccbaa49ea479a3da0f27c55af07\"","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('affaan-m/everything-claude-code/deployment-patterns', 'official', 'affaan-m', 'everything-claude-code', 'affaan-m/everything-claude-code', 'deployment-patterns', 50960, 6308, 80, '2026-02-24T12:02:48Z', '2026-02-24T12:04:37.789Z', 'dce3874d864c8e7810bf402f5ae70960bdde3ee274b4199871d7999b503b8e4e', '{"id":"affaan-m/everything-claude-code/deployment-patterns","name":"deployment-patterns","description":{"zh":"AI智能代理的部署模式包括CI/CD管道、Docker容器化和生产就绪检查","ja":"AIエージェントのデプロイパターンには、CI/CDパイプライン、Dockerコンテナ化、プロダクション準備チェックリストが含まれます","ko":"AI 에이전트의 배포 패턴에는 CI/CD 파이프라인, 도커 컨테이너화, 프로덕션 준비 체크리스트가 포함됩니다","es":"Los patrones de despliegue permiten implementar flujos de trabajo de despliegue eficientes y pipelines de CI/CD para aplicaciones web","fr":"Les modèles de déploiement permettent de mettre en œuvre des flux de travail de déploiement efficaces et des pipelines de CI/CD pour les applications web","de":"Deploy-Muster ermöglichen die Implementierung effizienter Deploy-Workflows und CI/CD-Pipelines für Webanwendungen","pt":"Implantação de aplicações web com padrões de implantação, CI/CD e Docker","ru":"Развертывание веб-приложений с паттернами развертывания, CI/CD и Docker","ar":"توزيع تطبيقات الويب بنماذج التوزيع والسي سي دي والدッカー","en":"Deployment workflows, CI/CD pipeline patterns, Docker containerization, health checks, rollback strategies, and production readiness checklists for web applications."},"owner":"affaan-m","repo":"everything-claude-code","repoPath":"affaan-m/everything-claude-code","stars":50960,"forks":6308,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T12:02:48Z","topics":["ai-agents","anthropic","claude","claude-code","developer-tools","llm","mcp","productivity"],"skillMd":{"name":"deployment-patterns","description":"Deployment workflows, CI/CD pipeline patterns, Docker containerization, health checks, rollback strategies, and production readiness checklists for web applications.","bodyPreview":"# Deployment Patterns\n\nProduction deployment workflows and CI/CD best practices.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- Setting up CI/CD pipelines\n- Dockerizing an application\n- Planning deployment strategy (blue-green, canary, rolling)\n- Implementing health checks and readiness probes\n- Preparing for a production release\n- Configuring environment-specific settings\n\n## Deployment Strategies\n\n### Rolling Deployment (Default)\n\nReplace instances gradually — old and new versions run simultaneously during rollout.","body":"# Deployment Patterns\n\nProduction deployment workflows and CI/CD best practices.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- Setting up CI/CD pipelines\n- Dockerizing an application\n- Planning deployment strategy (blue-green, canary, rolling)\n- Implementing health checks and readiness probes\n- Preparing for a production release\n- Configuring environment-specific settings\n\n## Deployment Strategies\n\n### Rolling Deployment (Default)\n\nReplace instances gradually — old and new versions run simultaneously during rollout.\n\n```\nInstance 1: v1 → v2  (update first)\nInstance 2: v1        (still running v1)\nInstance 3: v1        (still running v1)\n\nInstance 1: v2\nInstance 2: v1 → v2  (update second)\nInstance 3: v1\n\nInstance 1: v2\nInstance 2: v2\nInstance 3: v1 → v2  (update last)\n```\n\n**Pros:** Zero downtime, gradual rollout\n**Cons:** Two versions run simultaneously — requires backward-compatible changes\n**Use when:** Standard deployments, backward-compatible changes\n\n### Blue-Green Deployment\n\nRun two identical environments. Switch traffic atomically.\n\n```\nBlue  (v1) ← traffic\nGreen (v2)   idle, running new version\n\n# After verification:\nBlue  (v1)   idle (becomes standby)\nGreen (v2) ← traffic\n```\n\n**Pros:** Instant rollback (switch back to blue), clean cutover\n**Cons:** Requires 2x infrastructure during deployment\n**Use when:** Critical services, zero-tolerance for issues\n\n### Canary Deployment\n\nRoute a small percentage of traffic to the new version first.\n\n```\nv1: 95% of traffic\nv2:  5% of traffic  (canary)\n\n# If metrics look good:\nv1: 50% of traffic\nv2: 50% of traffic\n\n# Final:\nv2: 100% of traffic\n```\n\n**Pros:** Catches issues with real traffic before full rollout\n**Cons:** Requires traffic splitting infrastructure, monitoring\n**Use when:** High-traffic services, risky changes, feature flags\n\n## Docker\n\n### Multi-Stage Dockerfile (Node.js)\n\n```dockerfile\n# Stage 1: Install dependencies\nFROM node:22-alpine AS deps\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY package.json package-lock.json ./\nRUN npm ci --production=false\n\n# Stage 2: Build\nFROM node:22-alpine AS builder\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY --from=deps /app/node_modules ./node_modules\nCOPY . .\nRUN npm run build\nRUN npm prune --production\n\n# Stage 3: Production image\nFROM node:22-alpine AS runner\nWORKDIR /app\n\nRUN addgroup -g 1001 -S appgroup && adduser -S appuser -u 1001\nUSER appuser\n\nCOPY --from=builder --chown=appuser:appgroup /app/node_modules ./node_modules\nCOPY --from=builder --chown=appuser:appgroup /app/dist ./dist\nCOPY --from=builder --chown=appuser:appgroup /app/package.json ./\n\nENV NODE_ENV=production\nEXPOSE 3000\n\nHEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=3s --start-period=5s --retries=3 \\\n  CMD wget --no-verbose --tries=1 --spider http://localhost:3000/health || exit 1\n\nCMD [\"node\", \"dist/server.js\"]\n```\n\n### Multi-Stage Dockerfile (Go)\n\n```dockerfile\nFROM golang:1.22-alpine AS builder\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY go.mod go.sum ./\nRUN go mod download\nCOPY . .\nRUN CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux go build -ldflags=\"-s -w\" -o /server ./cmd/server\n\nFROM alpine:3.19 AS runner\nRUN apk --no-cache add ca-certificates\nRUN adduser -D -u 1001 appuser\nUSER appuser\n\nCOPY --from=builder /server /server\n\nEXPOSE 8080\nHEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=3s CMD wget -qO- http://localhost:8080/health || exit 1\nCMD [\"/server\"]\n```\n\n### Multi-Stage Dockerfile (Python/Django)\n\n```dockerfile\nFROM python:3.12-slim AS builder\nWORKDIR /app\nRUN pip install --no-cache-dir uv\nCOPY requirements.txt .\nRUN uv pip install --system --no-cache -r requirements.txt\n\nFROM python:3.12-slim AS runner\nWORKDIR /app\n\nRUN useradd -r -u 1001 appuser\nUSER appuser\n\nCOPY --from=builder /usr/local/lib/python3.12/site-packages /usr/local/lib/python3.12/site-packages\nCOPY --from=builder /usr/local/bin /usr/local/bin\nCOPY . .\n\nENV PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1\nEXPOSE 8000\n\nHEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=3s CMD python -c \"import urllib.request; urllib.request.urlopen(''http://localhost:8000/health/'')\" || exit 1\nCMD [\"gunicorn\", \"config.wsgi:application\", \"--bind\", \"0.0.0.0:8000\", \"--workers\", \"4\"]\n```\n\n### Docker Best Practices\n\n```\n# GOOD practices\n- Use specific version tags (node:22-alpine, not node:latest)\n- Multi-stage builds to minimize image size\n- Run as non-root user\n- Copy dependency files first (layer caching)\n- Use .dockerignore to exclude node_modules, .git, tests\n- Add HEALTHCHECK instruction\n- Set resource limits in docker-compose or k8s\n\n# BAD practices\n- Running as root\n- Using :latest tags\n- Copying entire repo in one COPY layer\n- Installing dev dependencies in production image\n- Storing secrets in image (use env vars or secrets manager)\n```\n\n## CI/CD Pipeline\n\n### GitHub Actions (Standard Pipeline)\n\n```yaml\nname: CI/CD\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n  pull_request:\n    branches: [main]\n\njobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: 22\n          cache: npm\n      - run: npm ci\n      - run: npm run lint\n      - run: npm run typecheck\n      - run: npm test -- --coverage\n      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4\n        if: always()\n        with:\n          name: coverage\n          path: coverage/\n\n  build:\n    needs: test\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    if: github.ref == ''refs/heads/main''\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: docker/setup-buildx-action@v3\n      - uses: docker/login-action@v3\n        with:\n          registry: ghcr.io\n          username: ${{ github.actor }}\n          password: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n      - uses: docker/build-push-action@v5\n        with:\n          push: true\n          tags: ghcr.io/${{ github.repository }}:${{ github.sha }}\n          cache-from: type=gha\n          cache-to: type=gha,mode=max\n\n  deploy:\n    needs: build\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    if: github.ref == ''refs/heads/main''\n    environment: production\n    steps:\n      - name: Deploy to production\n        run: |\n          # Platform-specific deployment command\n          # Railway: railway up\n          # Vercel: vercel --prod\n          # K8s: kubectl set image deployment/app app=ghcr.io/${{ github.repository }}:${{ github.sha }}\n          echo \"Deploying ${{ github.sha }}\"\n```\n\n### Pipeline Stages\n\n```\nPR opened:\n  lint → typecheck → unit tests → integration tests → preview deploy\n\nMerged to main:\n  lint → typecheck → unit tests → integration tests → build image → deploy staging → smoke tests → deploy production\n```\n\n## Health Checks\n\n### Health Check Endpoint\n\n```typescript\n// Simple health check\napp.get(\"/health\", (req, res) => {\n  res.status(200).json({ status: \"ok\" });\n});\n\n// Detailed health check (for internal monitoring)\napp.get(\"/health/detailed\", async (req, res) => {\n  const checks = {\n    database: await checkDatabase(),\n    redis: await checkRedis(),\n    externalApi: await checkExternalApi(),\n  };\n\n  const allHealthy = Object.values(checks).every(c => c.status === \"ok\");\n\n  res.status(allHealthy ? 200 : 503).json({\n    status: allHealthy ? \"ok\" : \"degraded\",\n    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n    version: process.env.APP_VERSION || \"unknown\",\n    uptime: process.uptime(),\n    checks,\n  });\n});\n\nasync function checkDatabase(): Promise<HealthCheck> {\n  try {\n    await db.query(\"SELECT 1\");\n    return { status: \"ok\", latency_ms: 2 };\n  } catch (err) {\n    return { status: \"error\", message: \"Database unreachable\" };\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Kubernetes Probes\n\n```yaml\nlivenessProbe:\n  httpGet:\n    path: /health\n    port: 3000\n  initialDelaySeconds: 10\n  periodSeconds: 30\n  failureThreshold: 3\n\nreadinessProbe:\n  httpGet:\n    path: /health\n    port: 3000\n  initialDelaySeconds: 5\n  periodSeconds: 10\n  failureThreshold: 2\n\nstartupProbe:\n  httpGet:\n    path: /health\n    port: 3000\n  initialDelaySeconds: 0\n  periodSeconds: 5\n  failureThreshold: 30    # 30 * 5s = 150s max startup time\n```\n\n## Environment Configuration\n\n### Twelve-Factor App Pattern\n\n```bash\n# All config via environment variables — never in code\nDATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@host:5432/db\nREDIS_URL=redis://host:6379/0\nAPI_KEY=${API_KEY}           # injected by secrets manager\nLOG_LEVEL=info\nPORT=3000\n\n# Environment-specific behavior\nNODE_ENV=production          # or staging, development\nAPP_ENV=production           # explicit app environment\n```\n\n### Configuration Validation\n\n```typescript\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst envSchema = z.object({\n  NODE_ENV: z.enum([\"development\", \"staging\", \"production\"]),\n  PORT: z.coerce.number().default(3000),\n  DATABASE_URL: z.string().url(),\n  REDIS_URL: z.string().url(),\n  JWT_SECRET: z.string().min(32),\n  LOG_LEVEL: z.enum([\"debug\", \"info\", \"warn\", \"error\"]).default(\"info\"),\n});\n\n// Validate at startup — fail fast if config is wrong\nexport const env = envSchema.parse(process.env);\n```\n\n## Rollback Strategy\n\n### Instant Rollback\n\n```bash\n# Docker/Kubernetes: point to previous image\nkubectl rollout undo deployment/app\n\n# Vercel: promote previous deployment\nvercel rollback\n\n# Railway: redeploy previous commit\nrailway up --commit <previous-sha>\n\n# Database: rollback migration (if reversible)\nnpx prisma migrate resolve --rolled-back <migration-name>\n```\n\n### Rollback Checklist\n\n- [ ] Previous image/artifact is available and tagged\n- [ ] Database migrations are backward-compatible (no destructive changes)\n- [ ] Feature flags can disable new features without deploy\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts configured for error rate spikes\n- [ ] Rollback tested in staging before production release\n\n## Production Readiness Checklist\n\nBefore any production deployment:\n\n### Application\n- [ ] All tests pass (unit, integration, E2E)\n- [ ] No hardcoded secrets in code or config files\n- [ ] Error handling covers all edge cases\n- [ ] Logging is structured (JSON) and does not contain PII\n- [ ] Health check endpoint returns meaningful status\n\n### Infrastructure\n- [ ] Docker image builds reproducibly (pinned versions)\n- [ ] Environment variables documented and validated at startup\n- [ ] Resource limits set (CPU, memory)\n- [ ] Horizontal scaling configured (min/max instances)\n- [ ] SSL/TLS enabled on all endpoints\n\n### Monitoring\n- [ ] Application metrics exported (request rate, latency, errors)\n- [ ] Alerts configured for error rate > threshold\n- [ ] Log aggregation set up (structured logs, searchable)\n- [ ] Uptime monitoring on health endpoint\n\n### Security\n- [ ] Dependencies scanned for CVEs\n- [ ] CORS configured for allowed origins only\n- [ ] Rate limiting enabled on public endpoints\n- [ ] Authentication and authorization verified\n- [ ] Security headers set (CSP, HSTS, X-Frame-Options)\n\n### Operations\n- [ ] Rollback plan documented and tested\n- [ ] Database migration tested against production-sized data\n- [ ] Runbook for common failure scenarios\n- [ ] On-call rotation and escalation path defined\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-24T12:04:37.789Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理部署模式","ja":"AIエージェントのデプロイパターン","ko":"AI 에이전트 배포 패턴","es":"Patrones de despliegue con Agentes de IA","fr":"Modèles de déploiement avec Outils d''IA","de":"Deploy-Muster mit KI-Agenten","pt":"Padrões de Implantação com Ferramentas de IA","ru":"Паттерны развертывания с ИИ Агентами","ar":"نماذج التوزيع مع أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","en":"deployment-patterns"},"description":{"zh":"AI智能代理的部署模式包括CI/CD管道、Docker容器化和生产就绪检查","ja":"AIエージェントのデプロイパターンには、CI/CDパイプライン、Dockerコンテナ化、プロダクション準備チェックリストが含まれます","ko":"AI 에이전트의 배포 패턴에는 CI/CD 파이프라인, 도커 컨테이너화, 프로덕션 준비 체크리스트가 포함됩니다","es":"Los patrones de despliegue permiten implementar flujos de trabajo de despliegue eficientes y pipelines de CI/CD para aplicaciones web","fr":"Les modèles de déploiement permettent de mettre en œuvre des flux de travail de déploiement efficaces et des pipelines de CI/CD pour les applications web","de":"Deploy-Muster ermöglichen die Implementierung effizienter Deploy-Workflows und CI/CD-Pipelines für Webanwendungen","pt":"Implantação de aplicações web com padrões de implantação, CI/CD e Docker","ru":"Развертывание веб-приложений с паттернами развертывания, CI/CD и Docker","ar":"توزيع تطبيقات الويب بنماذج التوزيع والسي سي دي والدッカー","en":"Deployment workflows, CI/CD pipeline patterns, Docker containerization, health checks, rollback strategies, and production readiness checklists for web appli..."},"definition":{"en":"Deployment workflows, CI/CD pipeline patterns, Docker containerization, health checks, rollback strategies, and production readiness checklists for web applications."},"features":{"zh":["CI/CD管道","Docker容器化","生产就绪检查","滚动部署","蓝绿部署","金丝雀部署"],"ja":["CI/CDパイプライン","Dockerコンテナ化","プロダクション準備チェックリスト","ローリングデプロイ","ブルーグリーンデプロイ","カナリアデプロイ"],"ko":["CI/CD 파이프라인","도커 컨테이너화","프로덕션 준비 체크리스트","롤링 배포","블루-그린 배포","카나리아 배포"],"es":["Despliegue gradual de instancias","Dockerización de aplicaciones","Implementación de comprobaciones de salud y sondeos de preparación","Planificación de estrategias de despliegue","Configuración de ajustes de entorno específicos"],"fr":["Déploiement progressif d''instances","Conteneurisation de applications Docker","Mise en œuvre de vérifications de santé et de sondes de préparation","Planification de stratégies de déploiement","Configuration de paramètres d''environnement spécifiques"],"de":["Schrittweiser Deploy von Instanzen","Dockerisierung von Anwendungen","Implementierung von Gesundheitschecks und Bereitschaftssonden","Planung von Deploy-Strategien","Konfiguration von umgebungspezifischen Einstellungen"],"pt":["Padrões de implantação","CI/CD","Docker","Verificações de saúde","Estratégias de rollback","Listas de verificação de prontidão para produção"],"ru":["Паттерны развертывания","CI/CD","Docker","Проверки здоровья","Стратегии откатов","Чек-листы готовности к производству"],"ar":["نماذج التوزيع","سي سي دي","دッカー","فحوصات الصحة","استراتيجيات التراجع","قوائم التحقق من الجاهزية للإنتاج"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","部署模式","CI/CD管道","Docker容器化","生产就绪检查","滚动部署","蓝绿部署","金丝雀部署","AI开发工具"],"ja":["AIエージェント","デプロイパターン","CI/CDパイプライン","Dockerコンテナ化","プロダクション準備チェックリスト","ローリングデプロイ","ブルーグリーンデプロイ","カナリアデプロイ","AI開発ツール"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","배포 패턴","CI/CD 파이프라인","도커 컨테이너화","프로덕션 준비 체크리스트","롤링 배포","블루-그린 배포","카나리아 배포","AI 개발 도구"],"es":["patrones de despliegue","Agentes de IA","pipelines de CI/CD","despliegue de aplicaciones web","Docker","comprobaciones de salud","sondeos de preparación"],"fr":["modèles de déploiement","Outils d''IA","pipelines de CI/CD","déploiement d''applications web","Docker","vérifications de santé","sondes de préparation"],"de":["Deploy-Muster","KI-Agenten","CI/CD-Pipelines","Deploy von Webanwendungen","Docker","Gesundheitschecks","Bereitschaftssonden"],"pt":["padrões de implantação","CI/CD","Docker","desenvolvimento de aplicações web","ferramentas de IA","implantação de aplicações","estratégias de implantação","verificações de saúde","rollback"],"ru":["паттерны развертывания","CI/CD","Docker","разработка веб-приложений","ИИ Агенты","развертывание приложений","стратегии развертывания","проверки здоровья","откат"],"ar":["نماذج التوزيع","سي سي دي","دッカー","تطوير تطبيقات الويب","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","توزيع التطبيقات","استراتيجيات التوزيع","فحوصات الصحة","التراجع"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for DevOps Agents requiring efficient CI/CD pipeline management and Docker containerization expertise.","zh":"适用于需要高效CI/CD管道管理和Docker容器化专业知识的DevOps代理。","ja":"DevOpsエージェントが効率的なCI/CDパイプライン管理とDockerコンテナ化の専門知識を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"효율적인 CI/CD 파이프라인 관리 및 Docker 컨테이너화 전문 지식을 요구하는 DevOps 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de DevOps que requieren una gestión eficiente de pipelines de CI/CD y experiencia en contenerización de Docker.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents DevOps nécessitant une gestion efficace de pipelines de CI/CD et une expertise en conteneurisation de Docker.","de":"Ideal für DevOps-Agents, die eine effiziente Verwaltung von CI/CD-Pipelines und Expertenwissen in der Docker-Containerisierung erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para agentes DevOps que exigem gestão eficiente de pipeline CI/CD e especialização em containerização do Docker.","ru":"Идеально для агентов DevOps, требующих эффективного управления конвейером CI/CD и экспертизы в области контейнеризации Docker.","ar":"مثالي لموكلات DevOps التي تتطلب إدارة كفؤة لtube CI/CD وخreinterpretة في حاويات Docker."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement robust deployment strategies, including blue-green, canary, and rolling deployments, utilizing Docker containerization and configuring health checks and readiness probes for production readiness.","zh":"赋予代理实现强大的部署策略的能力，包括蓝绿、金丝雀和滚动部署，利用Docker容器化，并为生产就绪配置健康检查和就绪探测。","ja":"エージェントが強力なデプロイ戦略を実装する能力を付与します。ブルーグリーン、カナリア、ローリングデプロイなどを含み、Dockerコンテナ化を利用し、生産就緒のためにヘルスチェックと就緒プローブを設定します。","ko":"에이전트가 강력한 배포 전략을 구현할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다. 블루-그린, 카나리, 롤링 배포 등을 포함하며, Docker 컨테이너화를 활용하고, 생산 준비를 위해 헬스 체크 및 준비 프로브를 구성합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar estrategias de implementación robustas, incluyendo implementaciones azul-verde, canarias y de despliegue continuo, utilizando la contenerización de Docker y configurando controles de salud y sondas de preparación para la preparación de producción.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre des stratégies de déploiement robustes, y compris les déploiements bleu-vert, canari et déroulement, en utilisant la conteneurisation de Docker et en configurant les vérifications de santé et les sondes de préparation pour la préparation de production.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, robuste Bereitstellungsstrategien umzusetzen, einschließlich blau-grüner, Kanarien- und Rolling-Bereitstellungen, unter Verwendung der Docker-Containerisierung und Konfiguration von Gesundheitsprüfungen und Bereitschaftssonden für die Produktionsbereitschaft.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar estratégias de implantação robustas, incluindo implantações azul-verde, canary e rolling, utilizando a containerização do Docker e configurando verificações de saúde e sondas de prontidão para prontidão de produção.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реализовать надежные стратегии развертывания, включая синие-зеленые, канарейки и роллинг-развертывания, используя контейнеризацию Docker и настраивая проверки здоровья и зонды готовности для готовности производства.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تنفيذ استراتيجيات نشر قوية، بما في ذلك النشرات الزرقاء والخضراء و canary والتدفقي، باستخدام حاويات Docker وتكوين فحوصات الصحة واكتشافات الجاهزية للجاهزية الإنتاجية."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating CI/CD pipeline setups","Implementing rolling deployment strategies for web applications","Configuring environment-specific settings for Dockerized applications"],"zh":["自动化CI/CD管道设置","为Web应用程序实施滚动部署策略","为Docker化应用程序配置环境特定设置"],"ja":["CI/CDパイプライン設定の自動化","Webアプリケーションのローリングデプロイ戦略の実装","Docker化アプリケーションの環境特定設定の構成"],"ko":["CI/CD 파이프라인 설정 자동화","웹 애플리케이션을 위한 롤링 배포 전략 구현","도커화된 애플리케이션을 위한 환경 특정 설정 구성"],"es":["Automatización de la configuración de pipelines de CI/CD","Implementación de estrategias de despliegue continuo para aplicaciones web","Configuración de ajustes específicos del entorno para aplicaciones contenerizadas con Docker"],"fr":["Automatisation de la configuration de pipelines de CI/CD","Mise en œuvre de stratégies de déploiement continu pour les applications web","Configuration des paramètres spécifiques à l''environnement pour les applications conteneurisées avec Docker"],"de":["Automatisierung der Einrichtung von CI/CD-Pipelines","Implementierung von Strategien für das kontinuierliche Bereitstellen von Webanwendungen","Konfiguration von umgebungsspezifischen Einstellungen für dockerisierte Anwendungen"],"pt":["Automatizar configurações de pipeline CI/CD","Implementar estratégias de implantação rolling para aplicações web","Configurar configurações específicas do ambiente para aplicações Dockerizadas"],"ru":["Автоматизировать настройку конвейера CI/CD","Реализовать стратегии роллинг-развертывания для веб-приложений","Настроить настройки окружения для контейнеризированных приложений"],"ar":["تأتمتة إعدادات tube CI/CD","تنفيذ استراتيجيات نشر متدفقة لتطبيقات الويب","تكوين إعدادات محددة للبيئة لتطبيقات Docker"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Docker installation","Limited to web application deployments"],"zh":["需要Docker安装","仅限Web应用程序部署"],"ja":["Dockerのインストールが必要","Webアプリケーションのデプロイのみ"],"ko":["Docker 설치가 필요함","웹 애플리케이션 배포만 해당"],"es":["Requiere la instalación de Docker","Limitado a implementaciones de aplicaciones web"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de Docker","Limité aux déploiements d''applications web"],"de":["Benötigt die Installation von Docker","Begrenzt auf die Bereitstellung von Webanwendungen"],"pt":["Exige instalação do Docker","Limitado a implantações de aplicações web"],"ru":["Требует установку Docker","Ограничен для развертывания веб-приложений"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت Docker","محدود بنشر تطبيقات الويب"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"dce3874d864c8e7810bf402f5ae70960bdde3ee274b4199871d7999b503b8e4e","repoEtag":"W/\"364f268e25511efbc6f9c2152da6805d934c8ccbaa49ea479a3da0f27c55af07\"","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('affaan-m/everything-claude-code/e2e-testing', 'official', 'affaan-m', 'everything-claude-code', 'affaan-m/everything-claude-code', 'e2e-testing', 50960, 6308, 80, '2026-02-24T12:02:48Z', '2026-02-24T12:04:41.231Z', '7e8fe72760f9274656f2b3d5a501b9535b4fe3acd8d83a79cd15f207c21bd937', '{"id":"affaan-m/everything-claude-code/e2e-testing","name":"e2e-testing","description":{"zh":"e2e-testing是使用Playwright进行终端到终端测试的综合解决方案，包括测试文件组织、页面对象模型、配置、CI/CD集成、构件管理和不稳定测试策略","ja":"e2e-testingはPlaywrightを使用した終端から終端までのテストの総合的な解決策であり、テストファイルの組織、ページオブジェクトモデル、設定、CI/CD統合、成果物管理、および不安定なテスト戦略を含む","ko":"e2e-testing은 Playwright를 사용하여 엔드 투 엔드 테스팅을 수행하는 종합적인 솔루션으로, 테스트 파일 구성, 페이지 객체 모델, 구성, CI/CD 통합, 아티팩트 관리 및 불안정한 테스트 전략을 포함","es":"Playwright E2E testing patrones para construir suites de pruebas estables, rápidas y mantenibles","fr":"Modèles de tests E2E Playwright pour construire des suites de tests stables, rapides et maintenables","de":"Playwright E2E-Test-Muster für den Aufbau von stabilen, schnellen und wartbaren Test-Suiten","pt":"Implemente padrões de teste E2E com Playwright e Agentes de IA para melhorar a estabilidade e velocidade dos testes","ru":"Реализуйте шаблоны тестирования E2E с Playwright и ИИ Агентами для повышения стабильности и скорости тестов","ar":"نفذ أنماط الاختبار E2E مع Playwright ووكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي لتحسين الاستقرار وسرعة الاختبارات","en":"Playwright E2E testing patterns, Page Object Model, configuration, CI/CD integration, artifact management, and flaky test strategies."},"owner":"affaan-m","repo":"everything-claude-code","repoPath":"affaan-m/everything-claude-code","stars":50960,"forks":6308,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T12:02:48Z","topics":["ai-agents","anthropic","claude","claude-code","developer-tools","llm","mcp","productivity"],"skillMd":{"name":"e2e-testing","description":"Playwright E2E testing patterns, Page Object Model, configuration, CI/CD integration, artifact management, and flaky test strategies.","bodyPreview":"# E2E Testing Patterns\n\nComprehensive Playwright patterns for building stable, fast, and maintainable E2E test suites.\n\n## Test File Organization\n\n```\ntests/\n├── e2e/\n│   ├── auth/\n│   │   ├── login.spec.ts\n│   │   ├── logout.spec.ts\n│   │   └── register.spec.ts\n│   ├── features/\n│   │   ├── browse.spec.ts\n│   │   ├── search.spec.ts\n│   │   └── create.spec.ts\n│   └── api/\n│       └── endpoints.spec.ts\n├── fixtures/\n│   ├── auth.ts\n│   └── data.ts\n└── playwright.config.ts\n```\n\n## Page Object Mode","body":"# E2E Testing Patterns\n\nComprehensive Playwright patterns for building stable, fast, and maintainable E2E test suites.\n\n## Test File Organization\n\n```\ntests/\n├── e2e/\n│   ├── auth/\n│   │   ├── login.spec.ts\n│   │   ├── logout.spec.ts\n│   │   └── register.spec.ts\n│   ├── features/\n│   │   ├── browse.spec.ts\n│   │   ├── search.spec.ts\n│   │   └── create.spec.ts\n│   └── api/\n│       └── endpoints.spec.ts\n├── fixtures/\n│   ├── auth.ts\n│   └── data.ts\n└── playwright.config.ts\n```\n\n## Page Object Model (POM)\n\n```typescript\nimport { Page, Locator } from ''@playwright/test''\n\nexport class ItemsPage {\n  readonly page: Page\n  readonly searchInput: Locator\n  readonly itemCards: Locator\n  readonly createButton: Locator\n\n  constructor(page: Page) {\n    this.page = page\n    this.searchInput = page.locator(''[data-testid=\"search-input\"]'')\n    this.itemCards = page.locator(''[data-testid=\"item-card\"]'')\n    this.createButton = page.locator(''[data-testid=\"create-btn\"]'')\n  }\n\n  async goto() {\n    await this.page.goto(''/items'')\n    await this.page.waitForLoadState(''networkidle'')\n  }\n\n  async search(query: string) {\n    await this.searchInput.fill(query)\n    await this.page.waitForResponse(resp => resp.url().includes(''/api/search''))\n    await this.page.waitForLoadState(''networkidle'')\n  }\n\n  async getItemCount() {\n    return await this.itemCards.count()\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Test Structure\n\n```typescript\nimport { test, expect } from ''@playwright/test''\nimport { ItemsPage } from ''../../pages/ItemsPage''\n\ntest.describe(''Item Search'', () => {\n  let itemsPage: ItemsPage\n\n  test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {\n    itemsPage = new ItemsPage(page)\n    await itemsPage.goto()\n  })\n\n  test(''should search by keyword'', async ({ page }) => {\n    await itemsPage.search(''test'')\n\n    const count = await itemsPage.getItemCount()\n    expect(count).toBeGreaterThan(0)\n\n    await expect(itemsPage.itemCards.first()).toContainText(/test/i)\n    await page.screenshot({ path: ''artifacts/search-results.png'' })\n  })\n\n  test(''should handle no results'', async ({ page }) => {\n    await itemsPage.search(''xyznonexistent123'')\n\n    await expect(page.locator(''[data-testid=\"no-results\"]'')).toBeVisible()\n    expect(await itemsPage.getItemCount()).toBe(0)\n  })\n})\n```\n\n## Playwright Configuration\n\n```typescript\nimport { defineConfig, devices } from ''@playwright/test''\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  testDir: ''./tests/e2e'',\n  fullyParallel: true,\n  forbidOnly: !!process.env.CI,\n  retries: process.env.CI ? 2 : 0,\n  workers: process.env.CI ? 1 : undefined,\n  reporter: [\n    [''html'', { outputFolder: ''playwright-report'' }],\n    [''junit'', { outputFile: ''playwright-results.xml'' }],\n    [''json'', { outputFile: ''playwright-results.json'' }]\n  ],\n  use: {\n    baseURL: process.env.BASE_URL || ''http://localhost:3000'',\n    trace: ''on-first-retry'',\n    screenshot: ''only-on-failure'',\n    video: ''retain-on-failure'',\n    actionTimeout: 10000,\n    navigationTimeout: 30000,\n  },\n  projects: [\n    { name: ''chromium'', use: { ...devices[''Desktop Chrome''] } },\n    { name: ''firefox'', use: { ...devices[''Desktop Firefox''] } },\n    { name: ''webkit'', use: { ...devices[''Desktop Safari''] } },\n    { name: ''mobile-chrome'', use: { ...devices[''Pixel 5''] } },\n  ],\n  webServer: {\n    command: ''npm run dev'',\n    url: ''http://localhost:3000'',\n    reuseExistingServer: !process.env.CI,\n    timeout: 120000,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Flaky Test Patterns\n\n### Quarantine\n\n```typescript\ntest(''flaky: complex search'', async ({ page }) => {\n  test.fixme(true, ''Flaky - Issue #123'')\n  // test code...\n})\n\ntest(''conditional skip'', async ({ page }) => {\n  test.skip(process.env.CI, ''Flaky in CI - Issue #123'')\n  // test code...\n})\n```\n\n### Identify Flakiness\n\n```bash\nnpx playwright test tests/search.spec.ts --repeat-each=10\nnpx playwright test tests/search.spec.ts --retries=3\n```\n\n### Common Causes & Fixes\n\n**Race conditions:**\n```typescript\n// Bad: assumes element is ready\nawait page.click(''[data-testid=\"button\"]'')\n\n// Good: auto-wait locator\nawait page.locator(''[data-testid=\"button\"]'').click()\n```\n\n**Network timing:**\n```typescript\n// Bad: arbitrary timeout\nawait page.waitForTimeout(5000)\n\n// Good: wait for specific condition\nawait page.waitForResponse(resp => resp.url().includes(''/api/data''))\n```\n\n**Animation timing:**\n```typescript\n// Bad: click during animation\nawait page.click(''[data-testid=\"menu-item\"]'')\n\n// Good: wait for stability\nawait page.locator(''[data-testid=\"menu-item\"]'').waitFor({ state: ''visible'' })\nawait page.waitForLoadState(''networkidle'')\nawait page.locator(''[data-testid=\"menu-item\"]'').click()\n```\n\n## Artifact Management\n\n### Screenshots\n\n```typescript\nawait page.screenshot({ path: ''artifacts/after-login.png'' })\nawait page.screenshot({ path: ''artifacts/full-page.png'', fullPage: true })\nawait page.locator(''[data-testid=\"chart\"]'').screenshot({ path: ''artifacts/chart.png'' })\n```\n\n### Traces\n\n```typescript\nawait browser.startTracing(page, {\n  path: ''artifacts/trace.json'',\n  screenshots: true,\n  snapshots: true,\n})\n// ... test actions ...\nawait browser.stopTracing()\n```\n\n### Video\n\n```typescript\n// In playwright.config.ts\nuse: {\n  video: ''retain-on-failure'',\n  videosPath: ''artifacts/videos/''\n}\n```\n\n## CI/CD Integration\n\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/e2e.yml\nname: E2E Tests\non: [push, pull_request]\n\njobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: 20\n      - run: npm ci\n      - run: npx playwright install --with-deps\n      - run: npx playwright test\n        env:\n          BASE_URL: ${{ vars.STAGING_URL }}\n      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4\n        if: always()\n        with:\n          name: playwright-report\n          path: playwright-report/\n          retention-days: 30\n```\n\n## Test Report Template\n\n```markdown\n# E2E Test Report\n\n**Date:** YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM\n**Duration:** Xm Ys\n**Status:** PASSING / FAILING\n\n## Summary\n- Total: X | Passed: Y (Z%) | Failed: A | Flaky: B | Skipped: C\n\n## Failed Tests\n\n### test-name\n**File:** `tests/e2e/feature.spec.ts:45`\n**Error:** Expected element to be visible\n**Screenshot:** artifacts/failed.png\n**Recommended Fix:** [description]\n\n## Artifacts\n- HTML Report: playwright-report/index.html\n- Screenshots: artifacts/*.png\n- Videos: artifacts/videos/*.webm\n- Traces: artifacts/*.zip\n```\n\n## Wallet / Web3 Testing\n\n```typescript\ntest(''wallet connection'', async ({ page, context }) => {\n  // Mock wallet provider\n  await context.addInitScript(() => {\n    window.ethereum = {\n      isMetaMask: true,\n      request: async ({ method }) => {\n        if (method === ''eth_requestAccounts'')\n          return [''0x1234567890123456789012345678901234567890'']\n        if (method === ''eth_chainId'') return ''0x1''\n      }\n    }\n  })\n\n  await page.goto(''/'')\n  await page.locator(''[data-testid=\"connect-wallet\"]'').click()\n  await expect(page.locator(''[data-testid=\"wallet-address\"]'')).toContainText(''0x1234'')\n})\n```\n\n## Financial / Critical Flow Testing\n\n```typescript\ntest(''trade execution'', async ({ page }) => {\n  // Skip on production — real money\n  test.skip(process.env.NODE_ENV === ''production'', ''Skip on production'')\n\n  await page.goto(''/markets/test-market'')\n  await page.locator(''[data-testid=\"position-yes\"]'').click()\n  await page.locator(''[data-testid=\"trade-amount\"]'').fill(''1.0'')\n\n  // Verify preview\n  const preview = page.locator(''[data-testid=\"trade-preview\"]'')\n  await expect(preview).toContainText(''1.0'')\n\n  // Confirm and wait for blockchain\n  await page.locator(''[data-testid=\"confirm-trade\"]'').click()\n  await page.waitForResponse(\n    resp => resp.url().includes(''/api/trade'') && resp.status() === 200,\n    { timeout: 30000 }\n  )\n\n  await expect(page.locator(''[data-testid=\"trade-success\"]'')).toBeVisible()\n})\n```\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-24T12:04:41.231Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能工具：e2e-testing终端到终端测试","ja":"AIエージェント：e2e-testingの終端から終端までのテスト","ko":"AI 에이전트: e2e-testing 엔드 투 엔드 테스팅","es":"Patrones de Pruebas E2E con Agentes de IA","fr":"Modèles de Tests E2E avec Outils d''IA","de":"E2E-Test-Muster mit KI-Agents","pt":" Ferramentas de Teste E2E com Agentes de IA","ru":"ИИ Агенты для E2E Тестирования","ar":"أدوات اختبار E2E مع وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","en":"e2e-testing"},"description":{"zh":"e2e-testing是使用Playwright进行终端到终端测试的综合解决方案，包括测试文件组织、页面对象模型、配置、CI/CD集成、构件管理和不稳定测试策略","ja":"e2e-testingはPlaywrightを使用した終端から終端までのテストの総合的な解決策であり、テストファイルの組織、ページオブジェクトモデル、設定、CI/CD統合、成果物管理、および不安定なテスト戦略を含む","ko":"e2e-testing은 Playwright를 사용하여 엔드 투 엔드 테스팅을 수행하는 종합적인 솔루션으로, 테스트 파일 구성, 페이지 객체 모델, 구성, CI/CD 통합, 아티팩트 관리 및 불안정한 테스트 전략을 포함","es":"Playwright E2E testing patrones para construir suites de pruebas estables, rápidas y mantenibles","fr":"Modèles de tests E2E Playwright pour construire des suites de tests stables, rapides et maintenables","de":"Playwright E2E-Test-Muster für den Aufbau von stabilen, schnellen und wartbaren Test-Suiten","pt":"Implemente padrões de teste E2E com Playwright e Agentes de IA para melhorar a estabilidade e velocidade dos testes","ru":"Реализуйте шаблоны тестирования E2E с Playwright и ИИ Агентами для повышения стабильности и скорости тестов","ar":"نفذ أنماط الاختبار E2E مع Playwright ووكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي لتحسين الاستقرار وسرعة الاختبارات","en":"Playwright E2E testing patterns, Page Object Model, configuration, CI/CD integration, artifact management, and flaky test strategies."},"definition":{"en":"Playwright E2E testing patterns, Page Object Model, configuration, CI/CD integration, artifact management, and flaky test strategies."},"features":{"zh":["Playwright测试文件组织","页面对象模型","CI/CD集成","构件管理","不稳定测试策略"],"ja":["Playwrightテストファイルの組織","ページオブジェクトモデル","CI/CD統合","成果物管理","不安定なテスト戦略"],"ko":["Playwright 테스트 파일 구성","페이지 객체 모델","CI/CD 통합","아티팩트 관리","불안정한 테스트 전략"],"es":["Patrones de pruebas E2E con Playwright","Modelo de objetos de página para una mejor organización","Integración con CI/CD para una entrega continua","Gestión de artefactos para una mejor trazabilidad","Estrategias para tests fallidos para reducir la fricción"],"fr":["Modèles de tests E2E avec Playwright","Modèle d''objets de page pour une meilleure organisation","Intégration avec CI/CD pour une livraison continue","Gestion des artefacts pour une meilleure traçabilité","Stratégies pour les tests défaillants pour réduire la friction"],"de":["E2E-Test-Muster mit Playwright","Seitenobjektmodell für eine bessere Organisation","Integration mit CI/CD für eine kontinuierliche Lieferung","Artefakt-Management für eine bessere Nachverfolgbarkeit","Strategien für fehlerhafte Tests, um die Reibung zu reduzieren"],"pt":["Padrões de teste E2E com Playwright","Modelo de Objeto de Página","Configuração e integração com CI/CD","Gerenciamento de artefatos","Estratégias para testes instáveis"],"ru":["Шаблоны тестирования E2E с Playwright","Модель Объекта Страницы","Настройка и интеграция с CI/CD","Управление артефактами","Стратегии для нестабильных тестов"],"ar":["أنماط الاختبار E2E مع Playwright","نموذج كائن الصفحة","التكوين والدمج مع CI/CD","إدارة الملفات","استراتيجيات للاختبارات غير المستقرة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能工具","e2e-testing","Playwright","终端到终端测试","CI/CD集成","构件管理","不稳定测试策略"],"ja":["AIエージェント","e2e-testing","Playwright","終端から終端までのテスト","CI/CD統合","成果物管理","不安定なテスト戦略"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","e2e-testing","Playwright","엔드 투 엔드 테스팅","CI/CD 통합","아티팩트 관리","불안정한 테스트 전략"],"es":["pruebas E2E","Playwright","patrones de pruebas","modelo de objetos de página","integración con CI/CD","gestión de artefactos","estrategias para tests fallidos","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["tests E2E","Playwright","modèles de tests","modèle d''objets de page","intégration avec CI/CD","gestion des artefacts","stratégies pour les tests défaillants","développement de logiciel","outils de développement"],"de":["E2E-Tests","Playwright","Test-Muster","Seitenobjektmodell","Integration mit CI/CD","Artefakt-Management","Strategien für fehlerhafte Tests","Software-Entwicklung","Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["teste E2E","Agentes de IA","Playwright","desenvolvimento de software","testes automatizados","CI/CD","estabilidade de testes","velocidade de testes"],"ru":["тестирование E2E","ИИ Агенты","Playwright","разработка программного обеспечения","автоматизированное тестирование","CI/CD","стабильность тестов","скорость тестов"],"ar":["الاختبار من النهاية إلى النهاية","وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","Playwright","تطوير البرمجيات","الاختبارات الآلية","CI/CD","استقرار الاختبارات","سرعة الاختبارات"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Automation Agents needing robust End-to-End testing capabilities with Playwright","zh":"适合需要使用Playwright进行强大的端到端测试功能的自动化代理","ja":"Playwrightを使用した堅牢なエンドツーエンドテスト機能を必要とする自動化エージェントに適しています","ko":"Playwright를 사용하여 강력한 종단 간 테스트 기능을 필요한 자동화 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Automatización que necesitan capacidades de prueba de extremo a extremo robustas con Playwright","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''automatisation nécessitant des capacités de test de bout en bout robustes avec Playwright","de":"Perfekt für Automatisierungsagenten, die robuste End-to-End-Testfunktionen mit Playwright benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Automação que necessitam de capacidades robustas de teste de ponta a ponta com Playwright","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов автоматизации, требующих прочных возможностей для тестирования от начала до конца с помощью Playwright","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الآليين الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات قوية لاختبار من النهاية إلى النهاية مع Playwright"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build stable, fast, and maintainable E2E test suites using Playwright patterns, Page Object Model, and seamless CI/CD integration with artifact management and flaky test strategies","zh":"赋予代理构建稳定、快速、可维护的端到端测试套件的能力，使用Playwright模式、页面对象模型和CI/CD集成，包括工件管理和不稳定测试策略","ja":"Playwrightパターン、ページオブジェクトモデル、シームレスなCI/CD統合を使用して、安定した、高速な、保守可能なエンドツーエンドテストスイートを構築するエージェントの能力を付与します。アーティファクト管理およびフレイキーなテスト戦略も含みます","ko":"Playwright 패턴, 페이지 객체 모델 및 무결점 CI/CD 통합을 사용하여 안정적이고 빠르며 유지 보수 가능한 종단 간 테스트套件을 구축할 수 있는 에이전트의 능력을 부여합니다. 아티팩트 관리 및 불안정한 테스트 전략도 포함됩니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a construir suites de pruebas de extremo a extremo estables, rápidas y mantenibles utilizando patrones de Playwright, Modelo de Objeto de Página y una integración de CI/CD sin problemas con gestión de artefactos y estrategias de pruebas erráticas","fr":"Permet aux agents de construire des suites de tests de bout en bout stables, rapides et maintenables en utilisant des modèles Playwright, le Modèle d''Objet de Page et une intégration de CI/CD sans problème avec la gestion d''artefacts et les stratégies de tests erratiques","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, stabile, schnelle und wartbare End-to-End-Test-Suiten mit Playwright-Mustern, Page-Object-Modell und nahtloser CI/CD-Integration mit Artefakt-Management und Strategien für flaky-Tests zu erstellen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir conjuntos de testes de ponta a ponta estáveis, rápidos e mantíveis usando padrões Playwright, Modelo de Objeto de Página e integração contínua de CI/CD com gerenciamento de artefatos e estratégias de teste instáveis","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать стабильные, быстрые и поддерживаемые наборы тестов от начала до конца, используя шаблоны Playwright, модель объекта страницы и бесшовную интеграцию CI/CD с управлением артефактами и стратегиями противоошибочного тестирования","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على بناء مجموعات اختبار من النهاية إلى النهاية مستقرة وسريعة وقابلة للصيانة باستخدام أنماط Playwright ونموذج كائن الصفحة وتكامل CI/CD المتواصل مع إدارة الملفات الشخصية واستراتيجيات الاختبار غير المستقرة"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating browser interactions with Playwright","Implementing Page Object Model for test organization","Debugging flaky tests with strategic retry mechanisms"],"zh":["使用Playwright自动化浏览器交互","实现页面对象模型用于测试组织","使用战略性重试机制调试不稳定测试"],"ja":["Playwrightを使用したブラウザーの相互作用の自動化","ページオブジェクトモデルを実装してテストを整理する","戦略的なリトライメカニズムを使用してフレイキーなテストをデバッグする"],"ko":["Playwright를 사용하여 브라우저 상호작용 자동화","페이지 객체 모델을 구현하여 테스트를 조직화","전략적인 재시도 메커니즘을 사용하여 불안정한 테스트를 디버깅"],"es":["Automatizar interacciones del navegador con Playwright","Implementar el Modelo de Objeto de Página para la organización de pruebas","Depurar pruebas erráticas con mecanismos de reintento estratégicos"],"fr":["Automatiser les interactions du navigateur avec Playwright","Mettre en œuvre le Modèle d''Objet de Page pour l''organisation des tests","Déboguer les tests erratiques avec des mécanismes de réessai stratégiques"],"de":["Automatisieren von Browser-Interaktionen mit Playwright","Implementieren des Page-Object-Modells für die Testorganisation","Debuggen von flaky-Tests mit strategischen Wiederholungsmechanismen"],"pt":["Automatizar interações do navegador com Playwright","Implementar Modelo de Objeto de Página para organização de testes","Depurar testes instáveis com mecanismos de repetição estratégica"],"ru":["Автоматизация взаимодействия браузера с Playwright","Реализация модели объекта страницы для организации тестирования","Отладка нестабильных тестов с помощью стратегических механизмов повторения"],"ar":["تأتمتية التفاعلات المتصفحة مع Playwright","تنفيذ نموذج كائن الصفحة لت организة الاختبارات","تصحيح الاختبارات غير المستقرة باستخدام آليات إعادة استراتيجية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Playwright installation","Limited to JavaScript and TypeScript environments","CI/CD pipeline setup necessary"],"zh":["需要Playwright安装","仅限于JavaScript和TypeScript环境","需要CI/CD管道设置"],"ja":["Playwrightのインストールが必要","JavaScriptとTypeScriptの環境のみ","CI/CDパイプラインの設定が必要"],"ko":["Playwright 설치가 필요함","JavaScript 및 TypeScript 환경만 해당","CI/CD 파이프라인 설정이 필요"],"es":["Requiere la instalación de Playwright","Limitado a entornos de JavaScript y TypeScript","Configuración de la canalización de CI/CD necesaria"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de Playwright","Limité aux environnements JavaScript et TypeScript","Configuration de la canalisation de CI/CD nécessaire"],"de":["Erfordert die Installation von Playwright","Begrenzt auf JavaScript- und TypeScript-Umgebungen","Einrichtung der CI/CD-Pipeline erforderlich"],"pt":["Requer instalação do Playwright","Limitado a ambientes JavaScript e TypeScript","Configuração de pipeline de CI/CD necessária"],"ru":["Требуется установка Playwright","Ограничен для сред JavaScript и TypeScript","Необходима настройка конвейера CI/CD"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت Playwright","محدود للبيئات JavaScript وTypeScript","تكوين خط أنابيب CI/CD ضروري"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"7e8fe72760f9274656f2b3d5a501b9535b4fe3acd8d83a79cd15f207c21bd937","repoEtag":"W/\"364f268e25511efbc6f9c2152da6805d934c8ccbaa49ea479a3da0f27c55af07\"","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('affaan-m/everything-claude-code/golang-testing', 'official', 'affaan-m', 'everything-claude-code', 'affaan-m/everything-claude-code', 'golang-testing', 50960, 6308, 80, '2026-02-24T12:02:48Z', '2026-02-24T12:04:45.111Z', '30833ea5658bbf953e5121ccbb32ab7decd8e46ca5e618c7ca3af409a1d27ca6', '{"id":"affaan-m/everything-claude-code/golang-testing","name":"golang-testing","description":{"zh":"Go语言测试模式包括表驱动测试、子测试、基准测试、模糊测试和测试覆盖率，遵循TDD方法ology","ja":"Goテストパターンには、表駆動テスト、サブテスト、ベンチマークテスト、ファズテスト、テストカバレッジが含まれており、TDD方法ologyに従っている","ko":"고랭 테스팅 패턴에는 표驱동 테스트, 서브테스트, 벤치마크 테스트, 퍼즈 테스트, 테스트 커버리지가 포함되어 있으며, TDD 방법ology를 따름","es":"Patrones de prueba de Go para escribir tests confiables y mantenibles","fr":"Modèles de test Go pour écrire des tests fiables et maintenables","de":"Go-Testmuster für zuverlässige und wartbare Tests","pt":"Padrões de teste em Go para desenvolvedores, incluindo testes direcionados por tabela, subtestes, benchmarks, fuzzing e cobertura de teste","ru":"Методы тестирования Go для разработчиков, включая таблицы тестов, субтесты, измерение производительности, fuzzing и покрытие тестами","ar":"نماذج اختبار جولانج الشاملة للبرمجيين، بما في ذلك الاختبارات الموجهة بالجدول والاختبارات الفرعية وتقييم الأداء والاختبار العشوائي وتغطية الاختبار","en":"Go testing patterns including table-driven tests, subtests, benchmarks, fuzzing, and test coverage. Follows TDD methodology with idiomatic Go practices."},"owner":"affaan-m","repo":"everything-claude-code","repoPath":"affaan-m/everything-claude-code","stars":50960,"forks":6308,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T12:02:48Z","topics":["ai-agents","anthropic","claude","claude-code","developer-tools","llm","mcp","productivity"],"skillMd":{"name":"golang-testing","description":"Go testing patterns including table-driven tests, subtests, benchmarks, fuzzing, and test coverage. Follows TDD methodology with idiomatic Go practices.","bodyPreview":"# Go Testing Patterns\n\nComprehensive Go testing patterns for writing reliable, maintainable tests following TDD methodology.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- Writing new Go functions or methods\n- Adding test coverage to existing code\n- Creating benchmarks for performance-critical code\n- Implementing fuzz tests for input validation\n- Following TDD workflow in Go projects\n\n## TDD Workflow for Go\n\n### The RED-GREEN-REFACTOR Cycle\n\n```\nRED     → Write a failing test first\nGREEN   → Write minimal code to pass","body":"# Go Testing Patterns\n\nComprehensive Go testing patterns for writing reliable, maintainable tests following TDD methodology.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- Writing new Go functions or methods\n- Adding test coverage to existing code\n- Creating benchmarks for performance-critical code\n- Implementing fuzz tests for input validation\n- Following TDD workflow in Go projects\n\n## TDD Workflow for Go\n\n### The RED-GREEN-REFACTOR Cycle\n\n```\nRED     → Write a failing test first\nGREEN   → Write minimal code to pass the test\nREFACTOR → Improve code while keeping tests green\nREPEAT  → Continue with next requirement\n```\n\n### Step-by-Step TDD in Go\n\n```go\n// Step 1: Define the interface/signature\n// calculator.go\npackage calculator\n\nfunc Add(a, b int) int {\n    panic(\"not implemented\") // Placeholder\n}\n\n// Step 2: Write failing test (RED)\n// calculator_test.go\npackage calculator\n\nimport \"testing\"\n\nfunc TestAdd(t *testing.T) {\n    got := Add(2, 3)\n    want := 5\n    if got != want {\n        t.Errorf(\"Add(2, 3) = %d; want %d\", got, want)\n    }\n}\n\n// Step 3: Run test - verify FAIL\n// $ go test\n// --- FAIL: TestAdd (0.00s)\n// panic: not implemented\n\n// Step 4: Implement minimal code (GREEN)\nfunc Add(a, b int) int {\n    return a + b\n}\n\n// Step 5: Run test - verify PASS\n// $ go test\n// PASS\n\n// Step 6: Refactor if needed, verify tests still pass\n```\n\n## Table-Driven Tests\n\nThe standard pattern for Go tests. Enables comprehensive coverage with minimal code.\n\n```go\nfunc TestAdd(t *testing.T) {\n    tests := []struct {\n        name     string\n        a, b     int\n        expected int\n    }{\n        {\"positive numbers\", 2, 3, 5},\n        {\"negative numbers\", -1, -2, -3},\n        {\"zero values\", 0, 0, 0},\n        {\"mixed signs\", -1, 1, 0},\n        {\"large numbers\", 1000000, 2000000, 3000000},\n    }\n\n    for _, tt := range tests {\n        t.Run(tt.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n            got := Add(tt.a, tt.b)\n            if got != tt.expected {\n                t.Errorf(\"Add(%d, %d) = %d; want %d\",\n                    tt.a, tt.b, got, tt.expected)\n            }\n        })\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Table-Driven Tests with Error Cases\n\n```go\nfunc TestParseConfig(t *testing.T) {\n    tests := []struct {\n        name    string\n        input   string\n        want    *Config\n        wantErr bool\n    }{\n        {\n            name:  \"valid config\",\n            input: `{\"host\": \"localhost\", \"port\": 8080}`,\n            want:  &Config{Host: \"localhost\", Port: 8080},\n        },\n        {\n            name:    \"invalid JSON\",\n            input:   `{invalid}`,\n            wantErr: true,\n        },\n        {\n            name:    \"empty input\",\n            input:   \"\",\n            wantErr: true,\n        },\n        {\n            name:  \"minimal config\",\n            input: `{}`,\n            want:  &Config{}, // Zero value config\n        },\n    }\n\n    for _, tt := range tests {\n        t.Run(tt.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n            got, err := ParseConfig(tt.input)\n\n            if tt.wantErr {\n                if err == nil {\n                    t.Error(\"expected error, got nil\")\n                }\n                return\n            }\n\n            if err != nil {\n                t.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n            }\n\n            if !reflect.DeepEqual(got, tt.want) {\n                t.Errorf(\"got %+v; want %+v\", got, tt.want)\n            }\n        })\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Subtests and Sub-benchmarks\n\n### Organizing Related Tests\n\n```go\nfunc TestUser(t *testing.T) {\n    // Setup shared by all subtests\n    db := setupTestDB(t)\n\n    t.Run(\"Create\", func(t *testing.T) {\n        user := &User{Name: \"Alice\"}\n        err := db.CreateUser(user)\n        if err != nil {\n            t.Fatalf(\"CreateUser failed: %v\", err)\n        }\n        if user.ID == \"\" {\n            t.Error(\"expected user ID to be set\")\n        }\n    })\n\n    t.Run(\"Get\", func(t *testing.T) {\n        user, err := db.GetUser(\"alice-id\")\n        if err != nil {\n            t.Fatalf(\"GetUser failed: %v\", err)\n        }\n        if user.Name != \"Alice\" {\n            t.Errorf(\"got name %q; want %q\", user.Name, \"Alice\")\n        }\n    })\n\n    t.Run(\"Update\", func(t *testing.T) {\n        // ...\n    })\n\n    t.Run(\"Delete\", func(t *testing.T) {\n        // ...\n    })\n}\n```\n\n### Parallel Subtests\n\n```go\nfunc TestParallel(t *testing.T) {\n    tests := []struct {\n        name  string\n        input string\n    }{\n        {\"case1\", \"input1\"},\n        {\"case2\", \"input2\"},\n        {\"case3\", \"input3\"},\n    }\n\n    for _, tt := range tests {\n        tt := tt // Capture range variable\n        t.Run(tt.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n            t.Parallel() // Run subtests in parallel\n            result := Process(tt.input)\n            // assertions...\n            _ = result\n        })\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Test Helpers\n\n### Helper Functions\n\n```go\nfunc setupTestDB(t *testing.T) *sql.DB {\n    t.Helper() // Marks this as a helper function\n\n    db, err := sql.Open(\"sqlite3\", \":memory:\")\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Fatalf(\"failed to open database: %v\", err)\n    }\n\n    // Cleanup when test finishes\n    t.Cleanup(func() {\n        db.Close()\n    })\n\n    // Run migrations\n    if _, err := db.Exec(schema); err != nil {\n        t.Fatalf(\"failed to create schema: %v\", err)\n    }\n\n    return db\n}\n\nfunc assertNoError(t *testing.T, err error) {\n    t.Helper()\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n    }\n}\n\nfunc assertEqual[T comparable](t *testing.T, got, want T) {\n    t.Helper()\n    if got != want {\n        t.Errorf(\"got %v; want %v\", got, want)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Temporary Files and Directories\n\n```go\nfunc TestFileProcessing(t *testing.T) {\n    // Create temp directory - automatically cleaned up\n    tmpDir := t.TempDir()\n\n    // Create test file\n    testFile := filepath.Join(tmpDir, \"test.txt\")\n    err := os.WriteFile(testFile, []byte(\"test content\"), 0644)\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Fatalf(\"failed to create test file: %v\", err)\n    }\n\n    // Run test\n    result, err := ProcessFile(testFile)\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Fatalf(\"ProcessFile failed: %v\", err)\n    }\n\n    // Assert...\n    _ = result\n}\n```\n\n## Golden Files\n\nTesting against expected output files stored in `testdata/`.\n\n```go\nvar update = flag.Bool(\"update\", false, \"update golden files\")\n\nfunc TestRender(t *testing.T) {\n    tests := []struct {\n        name  string\n        input Template\n    }{\n        {\"simple\", Template{Name: \"test\"}},\n        {\"complex\", Template{Name: \"test\", Items: []string{\"a\", \"b\"}}},\n    }\n\n    for _, tt := range tests {\n        t.Run(tt.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n            got := Render(tt.input)\n\n            golden := filepath.Join(\"testdata\", tt.name+\".golden\")\n\n            if *update {\n                // Update golden file: go test -update\n                err := os.WriteFile(golden, got, 0644)\n                if err != nil {\n                    t.Fatalf(\"failed to update golden file: %v\", err)\n                }\n            }\n\n            want, err := os.ReadFile(golden)\n            if err != nil {\n                t.Fatalf(\"failed to read golden file: %v\", err)\n            }\n\n            if !bytes.Equal(got, want) {\n                t.Errorf(\"output mismatch:\\ngot:\\n%s\\nwant:\\n%s\", got, want)\n            }\n        })\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Mocking with Interfaces\n\n### Interface-Based Mocking\n\n```go\n// Define interface for dependencies\ntype UserRepository interface {\n    GetUser(id string) (*User, error)\n    SaveUser(user *User) error\n}\n\n// Production implementation\ntype PostgresUserRepository struct {\n    db *sql.DB\n}\n\nfunc (r *PostgresUserRepository) GetUser(id string) (*User, error) {\n    // Real database query\n}\n\n// Mock implementation for tests\ntype MockUserRepository struct {\n    GetUserFunc  func(id string) (*User, error)\n    SaveUserFunc func(user *User) error\n}\n\nfunc (m *MockUserRepository) GetUser(id string) (*User, error) {\n    return m.GetUserFunc(id)\n}\n\nfunc (m *MockUserRepository) SaveUser(user *User) error {\n    return m.SaveUserFunc(user)\n}\n\n// Test using mock\nfunc TestUserService(t *testing.T) {\n    mock := &MockUserRepository{\n        GetUserFunc: func(id string) (*User, error) {\n            if id == \"123\" {\n                return &User{ID: \"123\", Name: \"Alice\"}, nil\n            }\n            return nil, ErrNotFound\n        },\n    }\n\n    service := NewUserService(mock)\n\n    user, err := service.GetUserProfile(\"123\")\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n    }\n    if user.Name != \"Alice\" {\n        t.Errorf(\"got name %q; want %q\", user.Name, \"Alice\")\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Benchmarks\n\n### Basic Benchmarks\n\n```go\nfunc BenchmarkProcess(b *testing.B) {\n    data := generateTestData(1000)\n    b.ResetTimer() // Don''t count setup time\n\n    for i := 0; i < b.N; i++ {\n        Process(data)\n    }\n}\n\n// Run: go test -bench=BenchmarkProcess -benchmem\n// Output: BenchmarkProcess-8   10000   105234 ns/op   4096 B/op   10 allocs/op\n```\n\n### Benchmark with Different Sizes\n\n```go\nfunc BenchmarkSort(b *testing.B) {\n    sizes := []int{100, 1000, 10000, 100000}\n\n    for _, size := range sizes {\n        b.Run(fmt.Sprintf(\"size=%d\", size), func(b *testing.B) {\n            data := generateRandomSlice(size)\n            b.ResetTimer()\n\n            for i := 0; i < b.N; i++ {\n                // Make a copy to avoid sorting already sorted data\n                tmp := make([]int, len(data))\n                copy(tmp, data)\n                sort.Ints(tmp)\n            }\n        })\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Memory Allocation Benchmarks\n\n```go\nfunc BenchmarkStringConcat(b *testing.B) {\n    parts := []string{\"hello\", \"world\", \"foo\", \"bar\", \"baz\"}\n\n    b.Run(\"plus\", func(b *testing.B) {\n        for i := 0; i < b.N; i++ {\n            var s string\n            for _, p := range parts {\n                s += p\n            }\n            _ = s\n        }\n    })\n\n    b.Run(\"builder\", func(b *testing.B) {\n        for i := 0; i < b.N; i++ {\n            var sb strings.Builder\n            for _, p := range parts {\n                sb.WriteString(p)\n            }\n            _ = sb.String()\n        }\n    })\n\n    b.Run(\"join\", func(b *testing.B) {\n        for i := 0; i < b.N; i++ {\n            _ = strings.Join(parts, \"\")\n        }\n    })\n}\n```\n\n## Fuzzing (Go 1.18+)\n\n### Basic Fuzz Test\n\n```go\nfunc FuzzParseJSON(f *testing.F) {\n    // Add seed corpus\n    f.Add(`{\"name\": \"test\"}`)\n    f.Add(`{\"count\": 123}`)\n    f.Add(`[]`)\n    f.Add(`\"\"`)\n\n    f.Fuzz(func(t *testing.T, input string) {\n        var result map[string]interface{}\n        err := json.Unmarshal([]byte(input), &result)\n\n        if err != nil {\n            // Invalid JSON is expected for random input\n            return\n        }\n\n        // If parsing succeeded, re-encoding should work\n        _, err = json.Marshal(result)\n        if err != nil {\n            t.Errorf(\"Marshal failed after successful Unmarshal: %v\", err)\n        }\n    })\n}\n\n// Run: go test -fuzz=FuzzParseJSON -fuzztime=30s\n```\n\n### Fuzz Test with Multiple Inputs\n\n```go\nfunc FuzzCompare(f *testing.F) {\n    f.Add(\"hello\", \"world\")\n    f.Add(\"\", \"\")\n    f.Add(\"abc\", \"abc\")\n\n    f.Fuzz(func(t *testing.T, a, b string) {\n        result := Compare(a, b)\n\n        // Property: Compare(a, a) should always equal 0\n        if a == b && result != 0 {\n            t.Errorf(\"Compare(%q, %q) = %d; want 0\", a, b, result)\n        }\n\n        // Property: Compare(a, b) and Compare(b, a) should have opposite signs\n        reverse := Compare(b, a)\n        if (result > 0 && reverse >= 0) || (result < 0 && reverse <= 0) {\n            if result != 0 || reverse != 0 {\n                t.Errorf(\"Compare(%q, %q) = %d, Compare(%q, %q) = %d; inconsistent\",\n                    a, b, result, b, a, reverse)\n            }\n        }\n    })\n}\n```\n\n## Test Coverage\n\n### Running Coverage\n\n```bash\n# Basic coverage\ngo test -cover ./...\n\n# Generate coverage profile\ngo test -coverprofile=coverage.out ./...\n\n# View coverage in browser\ngo tool cover -html=coverage.out\n\n# View coverage by function\ngo tool cover -func=coverage.out\n\n# Coverage with race detection\ngo test -race -coverprofile=coverage.out ./...\n```\n\n### Coverage Targets\n\n| Code Type | Target |\n|-----------|--------|\n| Critical business logic | 100% |\n| Public APIs | 90%+ |\n| General code | 80%+ |\n| Generated code | Exclude |\n\n### Excluding Generated Code from Coverage\n\n```go\n//go:generate mockgen -source=interface.go -destination=mock_interface.go\n\n// In coverage profile, exclude with build tags:\n// go test -cover -tags=!generate ./...\n```\n\n## HTTP Handler Testing\n\n```go\nfunc TestHealthHandler(t *testing.T) {\n    // Create request\n    req := httptest.NewRequest(http.MethodGet, \"/health\", nil)\n    w := httptest.NewRecorder()\n\n    // Call handler\n    HealthHandler(w, req)\n\n    // Check response\n    resp := w.Result()\n    defer resp.Body.Close()\n\n    if resp.StatusCode != http.StatusOK {\n        t.Errorf(\"got status %d; want %d\", resp.StatusCode, http.StatusOK)\n    }\n\n    body, _ := io.ReadAll(resp.Body)\n    if string(body) != \"OK\" {\n        t.Errorf(\"got body %q; want %q\", body, \"OK\")\n    }\n}\n\nfunc TestAPIHandler(t *testing.T) {\n    tests := []struct {\n        name       string\n        method     string\n        path       string\n        body       string\n        wantStatus int\n        wantBody   string\n    }{\n        {\n            name:       \"get user\",\n            method:     http.MethodGet,\n            path:       \"/users/123\",\n            wantStatus: http.StatusOK,\n            wantBody:   `{\"id\":\"123\",\"name\":\"Alice\"}`,\n        },\n        {\n            name:       \"not found\",\n            method:     http.MethodGet,\n            path:       \"/users/999\",\n            wantStatus: http.StatusNotFound,\n        },\n        {\n            name:       \"create user\",\n            method:     http.MethodPost,\n            path:       \"/users\",\n            body:       `{\"name\":\"Bob\"}`,\n            wantStatus: http.StatusCreated,\n        },\n    }\n\n    handler := NewAPIHandler()\n\n    for _, tt := range tests {\n        t.Run(tt.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n            var body io.Reader\n            if tt.body != \"\" {\n                body = strings.NewReader(tt.body)\n            }\n\n            req := httptest.NewRequest(tt.method, tt.path, body)\n            req.Header.Set(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")\n            w := httptest.NewRecorder()\n\n            handler.ServeHTTP(w, req)\n\n            if w.Code != tt.wantStatus {\n                t.Errorf(\"got status %d; want %d\", w.Code, tt.wantStatus)\n            }\n\n            if tt.wantBody != \"\" && w.Body.String() != tt.wantBody {\n                t.Errorf(\"got body %q; want %q\", w.Body.String(), tt.wantBody)\n            }\n        })\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Testing Commands\n\n```bash\n# Run all tests\ngo test ./...\n\n# Run tests with verbose output\ngo test -v ./...\n\n# Run specific test\ngo test -run TestAdd ./...\n\n# Run tests matching pattern\ngo test -run \"TestUser/Create\" ./...\n\n# Run tests with race detector\ngo test -race ./...\n\n# Run tests with coverage\ngo test -cover -coverprofile=coverage.out ./...\n\n# Run short tests only\ngo test -short ./...\n\n# Run tests with timeout\ngo test -timeout 30s ./...\n\n# Run benchmarks\ngo test -bench=. -benchmem ./...\n\n# Run fuzzing\ngo test -fuzz=FuzzParse -fuzztime=30s ./...\n\n# Count test runs (for flaky test detection)\ngo test -count=10 ./...\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n**DO:**\n- Write tests FIRST (TDD)\n- Use table-driven tests for comprehensive coverage\n- Test behavior, not implementation\n- Use `t.Helper()` in helper functions\n- Use `t.Parallel()` for independent tests\n- Clean up resources with `t.Cleanup()`\n- Use meaningful test names that describe the scenario\n\n**DON''T:**\n- Test private functions directly (test through public API)\n- Use `time.Sleep()` in tests (use channels or conditions)\n- Ignore flaky tests (fix or remove them)\n- Mock everything (prefer integration tests when possible)\n- Skip error path testing\n\n## Integration with CI/CD\n\n```yaml\n# GitHub Actions example\ntest:\n  runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n  steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n    - uses: actions/setup-go@v5\n      with:\n        go-version: ''1.22''\n\n    - name: Run tests\n      run: go test -race -coverprofile=coverage.out ./...\n\n    - name: Check coverage\n      run: |\n        go tool cover -func=coverage.out | grep total | awk ''{print $3}'' | \\\n        awk -F''%'' ''{if ($1 < 80) exit 1}''\n```\n\n**Remember**: Tests are documentation. They show how your code is meant to be used. Write them clearly and keep them up to date.\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-24T12:04:45.111Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"Go语言测试模式 - AI智能工具","ja":"Goテストパターン - AIエージェント","ko":"고랭테스팅 패턴 - AI 에이전트","es":"Herramientas de prueba de Go con Agentes de IA","fr":"Outils de test Go avec Agents IA","de":"Go-Test-Tools mit KI-Agents","pt":"Padrões de Teste em Go com Agentes de IA","ru":"ИИ Агенты для тестирования Go","ar":"نماذج اختبار جولانج باستخدام وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","en":"golang-testing"},"description":{"zh":"Go语言测试模式包括表驱动测试、子测试、基准测试、模糊测试和测试覆盖率，遵循TDD方法ology","ja":"Goテストパターンには、表駆動テスト、サブテスト、ベンチマークテスト、ファズテスト、テストカバレッジが含まれており、TDD方法ologyに従っている","ko":"고랭 테스팅 패턴에는 표驱동 테스트, 서브테스트, 벤치마크 테스트, 퍼즈 테스트, 테스트 커버리지가 포함되어 있으며, TDD 방법ology를 따름","es":"Patrones de prueba de Go para escribir tests confiables y mantenibles","fr":"Modèles de test Go pour écrire des tests fiables et maintenables","de":"Go-Testmuster für zuverlässige und wartbare Tests","pt":"Padrões de teste em Go para desenvolvedores, incluindo testes direcionados por tabela, subtestes, benchmarks, fuzzing e cobertura de teste","ru":"Методы тестирования Go для разработчиков, включая таблицы тестов, субтесты, измерение производительности, fuzzing и покрытие тестами","ar":"نماذج اختبار جولانج الشاملة للبرمجيين، بما في ذلك الاختبارات الموجهة بالجدول والاختبارات الفرعية وتقييم الأداء والاختبار العشوائي وتغطية الاختبار","en":"Go testing patterns including table-driven tests, subtests, benchmarks, fuzzing, and test coverage. Follows TDD methodology with idiomatic Go practices."},"definition":{"en":"Go testing patterns including table-driven tests, subtests, benchmarks, fuzzing, and test coverage. Follows TDD methodology with idiomatic Go practices."},"features":{"zh":["表驱动测试","子测试","基准测试","模糊测试","测试覆盖率"],"ja":["表駆動テスト","サブテスト","ベンチマークテスト","ファズテスト","テストカバレッジ"],"ko":["표驱동 테스트","서브테스트","벤치마크 테스트","퍼즈 테스트","테스트 커버리지"],"es":["Pruebas dirigidas por tabla","Subpruebas","Benchmarks","Pruebas de difusión","Cobertura de prueba"],"fr":["Tests pilotés par table","Sous-tests","Benchmarks","Tests de fuzzing","Couverture de test"],"de":["Tabellengetriebene Tests","Subtests","Benchmarks","Fuzz-Tests","Testabdeckung"],"pt":["Testes direcionados por tabela","Subtestes para casos de teste complexos","Benchmarks para avaliar o desempenho","Fuzzing para validação de entrada","Cobertura de teste para garantir a qualidade"],"ru":["Таблицы тестов","Субтесты для сложных случаев тестирования","Измерение производительности","Fuzzing для валидации входных данных","Покрытие тестами для обеспечения качества"],"ar":["الاختبارات الموجهة بالجدول","الاختبارات الفرعية لحالات الاختبار المعقدة","تقييم الأداء","الاختبار العشوائي للتحقق من المدخلات","تغطية الاختبار لضمان الجودة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Go语言测试","TDD方法ology","表驱动测试","子测试","基准测试","模糊测试","测试覆盖率","AI智能工具"],"ja":["Go言語テスト","TDD方法ology","表駆動テスト","サブテスト","ベンチマークテスト","ファズテスト","テストカバレッジ","AIエージェント"],"ko":["고랭 테스트","TDD 방법ology","표驱동 테스트","서브테스트","벤치마크 테스트","퍼즈 테스트","테스트 커버리지","AI 에이전트"],"es":["Agentes de IA para desarrolladores","Herramientas de prueba de Go","TDD en Go","Pruebas de software","Desarrollo de software","Go testing patterns"],"fr":["Agents IA pour développeurs","Outils de test Go","TDD en Go","Tests de logiciel","Développement de logiciel","Modèles de test Go"],"de":["KI-Agents für Entwickler","Go-Test-Tools","TDD in Go","Software-Tests","Software-Entwicklung","Go-Testmuster"],"pt":["teste em Go","TDD","agentes de IA","desenvolvimento de software","produtividade","qualidade do código","padrões de teste","testes automatizados"],"ru":["тестирование Go","TDD","ИИ Агенты","разработка программного обеспечения","производительность","качество кода","методы тестирования","автоматизированное тестирование"],"ar":["اختبار جولانج","تطوير البرمجيات","وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","إنتاجية","جودة الرمز","نماذج الاختبار","الاختبارات الآلية","تطوير البرمجيات الموجه بالاختبار"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Review Agents focusing on Go project reliability, seeking advanced testing patterns and TDD methodology expertise.","zh":"适合专注于Go项目可靠性的代码审查代理，寻求高级测试模式和TDD方法论专长的代理。","ja":"Goプロジェクトの信頼性に焦点を当てたコードレビュー代理向けに、先進的なテストパターンとTDDメソッド論の専門知識を探している代理に最適です。","ko":"Go 프로젝트의 신뢰성에 중점을 둔 코드 리뷰 에이전트에게 적합하며, 고급 테스트 패턴과 TDD 방법론 전문 지식을 탐색하는 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Revisión de Código que se centran en la confiabilidad de los proyectos Go, que buscan patrones de prueba avanzados y experiencia en metodología TDD.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de revue de code axés sur la fiabilité des projets Go, qui recherchent des modèles de test avancés et une expertise en méthodologie TDD.","de":"Ideal für Code-Review-Agents, die sich auf die Zuverlässigkeit von Go-Projekten konzentrieren und fortgeschrittene Testmuster und TDD-Methoden-Expertise suchen.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de revisão de código que se concentram na confiabilidade de projetos Go, buscando padrões de teste avançados e especialização em metodologia TDD.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов проверки кода, фокусирующихся на надежности проектов Go, ищущих продвинутые шаблоны тестирования и экспертизу методологии TDD.","ar":"مثالية لعمليات المراجعة الكودية التي تركز على موثوقية مشاريع Go، وتسعى جاهدة للحصول على أنماط اختبار متقدمة وخبرة في منهجية TDD."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to write comprehensive tests using table-driven tests, subtests, benchmarks, and fuzzing, following idiomatic Go practices and ensuring high test coverage, while adhering to the RED-GREEN-REFACTOR cycle of Test-Driven Development.","zh":"赋予代理使用表驱动测试、子测试、基准测试和模糊测试来编写全面的测试，遵循惯用的Go实践，并确保高测试覆盖率，同时遵循测试驱动开发的RED-GREEN-REFACTOR周期。","ja":"エージェントが表駆動テスト、サブテスト、ベンチマークテスト、ファジングテストを使用して包括的なテストを記述できるようにし、慣用的Goの実践に従い、高いテストカバレッジを確保し、テスト駆動開発のRED-GREEN-REFACTORサイクルに従う。","ko":"에이전트가 테이블 주도 테스트, 서브 테스트, 벤치마크 테스트 및 퍼징 테스트를 사용하여 포괄적인 테스트를 작성할 수 있도록 하며, 관용적인 Go 관행을 따르고, 높은 테스트 커버리지를 보장하며, 테스트 주도 개발의 RED-GREEN-REFACTOR 주기에 따라 수행합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a escribir pruebas exhaustivas utilizando pruebas impulsadas por tabla, subpruebas, benchmarks y fuzzing, siguiendo prácticas idiomáticas de Go y asegurando una alta cobertura de pruebas, mientras se adhiere al ciclo RED-VERDE-REFACTOR del Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''écrire des tests complets en utilisant des tests à table, des sous-tests, des benchmarks et du fuzzing, en suivant les pratiques idiomatiques de Go et en garantissant une couverture de test élevée, tout en respectant le cycle ROUGE-VERT-REFACTOR du Développement Dirigé par les Tests.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, umfassende Tests mit Hilfe von table-getriebenen Tests, Subtests, Benchmarks und Fuzzing zu schreiben, indem sie idiomatische Go-Praktiken befolgen und eine hohe Testabdeckung sicherstellen, während sie dem RED-GRÜN-REFAKTOR-Zyklus der testgetriebenen Entwicklung folgen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a escrever testes abrangentes usando testes orientados por tabela, subtestes, benchmarks e fuzzing, seguindo práticas idiomáticas Go e garantindo alta cobertura de teste, enquanto adere ao ciclo RED-GREEN-REFACTOR do Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью писать комплексные тесты с использованием таблицо-ориентированных тестов, субтестов, бенчмарков и фаззинга, следуя идиоматичным практикам Go, обеспечивая высокое покрытие тестами, а также придерживаясь цикла RED-GREEN-REFACTOR Разработки, управляемой тестами.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من كتابة اختبارات شاملة باستخدام اختبارات مدفوعة بالجدول واختبارات فرعية وبenchmarks وفuzzing، متبعًا ممارسات Go الإيديوماتيكية وضمان تغطية اختبار عالية، مع اتباع دورة RED-GREEN-REFACTOR من التطوير الموجه بالاختبار."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing fuzz tests for input validation","Creating benchmarks for performance-critical code","Writing reliable table-driven tests for new Go functions"],"zh":["为输入验证实现模糊测试","为性能关键代码创建基准测试","为新的Go函数编写可靠的表驱动测试"],"ja":["入力検証のためのファジングテストの実装","パフォーマンスクリティカルコードのベンチマークテストの作成","新しいGo関数のための信頼性の高い表駆動テストの作成"],"ko":["입력 확인을 위한 퍼징 테스트 구현","성능关键 코드를 위한 벤치마크 테스트 생성","새로운 Go 함수를 위한 신뢰할 수 있는 테이블 주도 테스트 작성"],"es":["Implementar pruebas de fuzzing para la validación de entrada","Crear benchmarks para el código crítico de rendimiento","Escribir pruebas de table-driven confiables para nuevas funciones Go"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre des tests de fuzzing pour la validation des entrées","Créer des benchmarks pour le code critique de performance","Écrire des tests à table fiables pour les nouvelles fonctions Go"],"de":["Implementierung von Fuzzing-Tests für die Eingabevalidierung","Erstellung von Benchmarks für leistungskritisches Code","Schreiben von zuverlässigen table-getriebenen Tests für neue Go-Funktionen"],"pt":["Implementar testes de fuzz para validação de entrada","Criar benchmarks para código crítico de desempenho","Escrever testes confiáveis orientados por tabela para novas funções Go"],"ru":["Реализация фазз-тестов для валидации входных данных","Создание бенчмарков для кода, критичного для производительности","Написание надежных таблицо-ориентированных тестов для новых функций Go"],"ar":["تنفيذ اختبارات fuzz لتحقق البيانات الإدخالية","إنشاء benchmarks لرمز الحاسوب الحرج للأداء","كتابة اختبارات موثوقة مدفوعة بالجدول لدوال Go الجديدة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Go programming language environment","Follows TDD methodology"],"zh":["需要Go编程语言环境","遵循TDD方法论"],"ja":["Goプログラミング言語環境が必要","TDD方法論に従う"],"ko":["Go 프로그래밍 언어 환경이 필요","TDD 방법론을 따름"],"es":["Requiere un entorno de lenguaje de programación Go","Sigue la metodología TDD"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement de langage de programmation Go","Suit la méthodologie TDD"],"de":["Benötigt eine Go-Programmiersprachen-Umgebung","Folgt der TDD-Methodik"],"pt":["Exige ambiente de linguagem de programação Go","Sigue a metodologia TDD"],"ru":["Требует среды программирования на языке Go","Следует методологии TDD"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة لغة برمجة Go","يتبع منهجية TDD"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"30833ea5658bbf953e5121ccbb32ab7decd8e46ca5e618c7ca3af409a1d27ca6","repoEtag":"W/\"364f268e25511efbc6f9c2152da6805d934c8ccbaa49ea479a3da0f27c55af07\"","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('affaan-m/everything-claude-code/python-testing', 'official', 'affaan-m', 'everything-claude-code', 'affaan-m/everything-claude-code', 'python-testing', 50960, 6308, 80, '2026-02-24T12:02:48Z', '2026-02-24T12:04:53.303Z', '98ce1865de021c57f416bb41c9630a9d0ee85c790e8d512d4a8c9f2ebc63b501', '{"id":"affaan-m/everything-claude-code/python-testing","name":"python-testing","description":{"zh":"使用 pytest 和 TDD 方法的 Python 测试策略，提高测试效率和代码质量","ja":"pytest と TDD 方法を使用した Python テスト戦略により、テスト効率とコード品質を向上","ko":"pytest와 TDD 방법을 사용한 Python 테스트 전략으로 테스트 효율성과 코드 품질을 향상","es":"Estrategias de testing de Python para aplicaciones utilizando pytest, TDD y mejores prácticas, diseñadas para desarrolladores","fr":"Stratégies de test Python pour les applications utilisant pytest, TDD et meilleures pratiques, conçues pour les développeurs","de":"Python-Teststrategien für Anwendungen unter Verwendung von pytest, TDD und Best Practices, entwickelt für Entwickler","pt":"Desenvolva habilidades de teste Python com pytest e TDD. Aprenda a criar testes eficazes e melhorar a cobertura de teste.","ru":"Разрабатывайте навыки тестирования Python с помощью pytest и TDD. Узнайте, как создавать эффективные тесты и улучшать покрытие тестов.","ar":"طور مهارات اختبار بايثون باستخدام بيست و TDD. تعلم كيفية إنشاء اختبارات فعالة وتحسين تغطية الاختبار.","en":"Python testing strategies using pytest, TDD methodology, fixtures, mocking, parametrization, and coverage requirements."},"owner":"affaan-m","repo":"everything-claude-code","repoPath":"affaan-m/everything-claude-code","stars":50960,"forks":6308,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T12:02:48Z","topics":["ai-agents","anthropic","claude","claude-code","developer-tools","llm","mcp","productivity"],"skillMd":{"name":"python-testing","description":"Python testing strategies using pytest, TDD methodology, fixtures, mocking, parametrization, and coverage requirements.","bodyPreview":"# Python Testing Patterns\n\nComprehensive testing strategies for Python applications using pytest, TDD methodology, and best practices.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- Writing new Python code (follow TDD: red, green, refactor)\n- Designing test suites for Python projects\n- Reviewing Python test coverage\n- Setting up testing infrastructure\n\n## Core Testing Philosophy\n\n### Test-Driven Development (TDD)\n\nAlways follow the TDD cycle:\n\n1. **RED**: Write a failing test for the desired behavior\n2. **GREEN**: Wri","body":"# Python Testing Patterns\n\nComprehensive testing strategies for Python applications using pytest, TDD methodology, and best practices.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- Writing new Python code (follow TDD: red, green, refactor)\n- Designing test suites for Python projects\n- Reviewing Python test coverage\n- Setting up testing infrastructure\n\n## Core Testing Philosophy\n\n### Test-Driven Development (TDD)\n\nAlways follow the TDD cycle:\n\n1. **RED**: Write a failing test for the desired behavior\n2. **GREEN**: Write minimal code to make the test pass\n3. **REFACTOR**: Improve code while keeping tests green\n\n```python\n# Step 1: Write failing test (RED)\ndef test_add_numbers():\n    result = add(2, 3)\n    assert result == 5\n\n# Step 2: Write minimal implementation (GREEN)\ndef add(a, b):\n    return a + b\n\n# Step 3: Refactor if needed (REFACTOR)\n```\n\n### Coverage Requirements\n\n- **Target**: 80%+ code coverage\n- **Critical paths**: 100% coverage required\n- Use `pytest --cov` to measure coverage\n\n```bash\npytest --cov=mypackage --cov-report=term-missing --cov-report=html\n```\n\n## pytest Fundamentals\n\n### Basic Test Structure\n\n```python\nimport pytest\n\ndef test_addition():\n    \"\"\"Test basic addition.\"\"\"\n    assert 2 + 2 == 4\n\ndef test_string_uppercase():\n    \"\"\"Test string uppercasing.\"\"\"\n    text = \"hello\"\n    assert text.upper() == \"HELLO\"\n\ndef test_list_append():\n    \"\"\"Test list append.\"\"\"\n    items = [1, 2, 3]\n    items.append(4)\n    assert 4 in items\n    assert len(items) == 4\n```\n\n### Assertions\n\n```python\n# Equality\nassert result == expected\n\n# Inequality\nassert result != unexpected\n\n# Truthiness\nassert result  # Truthy\nassert not result  # Falsy\nassert result is True  # Exactly True\nassert result is False  # Exactly False\nassert result is None  # Exactly None\n\n# Membership\nassert item in collection\nassert item not in collection\n\n# Comparisons\nassert result > 0\nassert 0 <= result <= 100\n\n# Type checking\nassert isinstance(result, str)\n\n# Exception testing (preferred approach)\nwith pytest.raises(ValueError):\n    raise ValueError(\"error message\")\n\n# Check exception message\nwith pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"invalid input\"):\n    raise ValueError(\"invalid input provided\")\n\n# Check exception attributes\nwith pytest.raises(ValueError) as exc_info:\n    raise ValueError(\"error message\")\nassert str(exc_info.value) == \"error message\"\n```\n\n## Fixtures\n\n### Basic Fixture Usage\n\n```python\nimport pytest\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef sample_data():\n    \"\"\"Fixture providing sample data.\"\"\"\n    return {\"name\": \"Alice\", \"age\": 30}\n\ndef test_sample_data(sample_data):\n    \"\"\"Test using the fixture.\"\"\"\n    assert sample_data[\"name\"] == \"Alice\"\n    assert sample_data[\"age\"] == 30\n```\n\n### Fixture with Setup/Teardown\n\n```python\n@pytest.fixture\ndef database():\n    \"\"\"Fixture with setup and teardown.\"\"\"\n    # Setup\n    db = Database(\":memory:\")\n    db.create_tables()\n    db.insert_test_data()\n\n    yield db  # Provide to test\n\n    # Teardown\n    db.close()\n\ndef test_database_query(database):\n    \"\"\"Test database operations.\"\"\"\n    result = database.query(\"SELECT * FROM users\")\n    assert len(result) > 0\n```\n\n### Fixture Scopes\n\n```python\n# Function scope (default) - runs for each test\n@pytest.fixture\ndef temp_file():\n    with open(\"temp.txt\", \"w\") as f:\n        yield f\n    os.remove(\"temp.txt\")\n\n# Module scope - runs once per module\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"module\")\ndef module_db():\n    db = Database(\":memory:\")\n    db.create_tables()\n    yield db\n    db.close()\n\n# Session scope - runs once per test session\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef shared_resource():\n    resource = ExpensiveResource()\n    yield resource\n    resource.cleanup()\n```\n\n### Fixture with Parameters\n\n```python\n@pytest.fixture(params=[1, 2, 3])\ndef number(request):\n    \"\"\"Parameterized fixture.\"\"\"\n    return request.param\n\ndef test_numbers(number):\n    \"\"\"Test runs 3 times, once for each parameter.\"\"\"\n    assert number > 0\n```\n\n### Using Multiple Fixtures\n\n```python\n@pytest.fixture\ndef user():\n    return User(id=1, name=\"Alice\")\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef admin():\n    return User(id=2, name=\"Admin\", role=\"admin\")\n\ndef test_user_admin_interaction(user, admin):\n    \"\"\"Test using multiple fixtures.\"\"\"\n    assert admin.can_manage(user)\n```\n\n### Autouse Fixtures\n\n```python\n@pytest.fixture(autouse=True)\ndef reset_config():\n    \"\"\"Automatically runs before every test.\"\"\"\n    Config.reset()\n    yield\n    Config.cleanup()\n\ndef test_without_fixture_call():\n    # reset_config runs automatically\n    assert Config.get_setting(\"debug\") is False\n```\n\n### Conftest.py for Shared Fixtures\n\n```python\n# tests/conftest.py\nimport pytest\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef client():\n    \"\"\"Shared fixture for all tests.\"\"\"\n    app = create_app(testing=True)\n    with app.test_client() as client:\n        yield client\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef auth_headers(client):\n    \"\"\"Generate auth headers for API testing.\"\"\"\n    response = client.post(\"/api/login\", json={\n        \"username\": \"test\",\n        \"password\": \"test\"\n    })\n    token = response.json[\"token\"]\n    return {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\"}\n```\n\n## Parametrization\n\n### Basic Parametrization\n\n```python\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"input,expected\", [\n    (\"hello\", \"HELLO\"),\n    (\"world\", \"WORLD\"),\n    (\"PyThOn\", \"PYTHON\"),\n])\ndef test_uppercase(input, expected):\n    \"\"\"Test runs 3 times with different inputs.\"\"\"\n    assert input.upper() == expected\n```\n\n### Multiple Parameters\n\n```python\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"a,b,expected\", [\n    (2, 3, 5),\n    (0, 0, 0),\n    (-1, 1, 0),\n    (100, 200, 300),\n])\ndef test_add(a, b, expected):\n    \"\"\"Test addition with multiple inputs.\"\"\"\n    assert add(a, b) == expected\n```\n\n### Parametrize with IDs\n\n```python\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"input,expected\", [\n    (\"valid@email.com\", True),\n    (\"invalid\", False),\n    (\"@no-domain.com\", False),\n], ids=[\"valid-email\", \"missing-at\", \"missing-domain\"])\ndef test_email_validation(input, expected):\n    \"\"\"Test email validation with readable test IDs.\"\"\"\n    assert is_valid_email(input) is expected\n```\n\n### Parametrized Fixtures\n\n```python\n@pytest.fixture(params=[\"sqlite\", \"postgresql\", \"mysql\"])\ndef db(request):\n    \"\"\"Test against multiple database backends.\"\"\"\n    if request.param == \"sqlite\":\n        return Database(\":memory:\")\n    elif request.param == \"postgresql\":\n        return Database(\"postgresql://localhost/test\")\n    elif request.param == \"mysql\":\n        return Database(\"mysql://localhost/test\")\n\ndef test_database_operations(db):\n    \"\"\"Test runs 3 times, once for each database.\"\"\"\n    result = db.query(\"SELECT 1\")\n    assert result is not None\n```\n\n## Markers and Test Selection\n\n### Custom Markers\n\n```python\n# Mark slow tests\n@pytest.mark.slow\ndef test_slow_operation():\n    time.sleep(5)\n\n# Mark integration tests\n@pytest.mark.integration\ndef test_api_integration():\n    response = requests.get(\"https://api.example.com\")\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n\n# Mark unit tests\n@pytest.mark.unit\ndef test_unit_logic():\n    assert calculate(2, 3) == 5\n```\n\n### Run Specific Tests\n\n```bash\n# Run only fast tests\npytest -m \"not slow\"\n\n# Run only integration tests\npytest -m integration\n\n# Run integration or slow tests\npytest -m \"integration or slow\"\n\n# Run tests marked as unit but not slow\npytest -m \"unit and not slow\"\n```\n\n### Configure Markers in pytest.ini\n\n```ini\n[pytest]\nmarkers =\n    slow: marks tests as slow\n    integration: marks tests as integration tests\n    unit: marks tests as unit tests\n    django: marks tests as requiring Django\n```\n\n## Mocking and Patching\n\n### Mocking Functions\n\n```python\nfrom unittest.mock import patch, Mock\n\n@patch(\"mypackage.external_api_call\")\ndef test_with_mock(api_call_mock):\n    \"\"\"Test with mocked external API.\"\"\"\n    api_call_mock.return_value = {\"status\": \"success\"}\n\n    result = my_function()\n\n    api_call_mock.assert_called_once()\n    assert result[\"status\"] == \"success\"\n```\n\n### Mocking Return Values\n\n```python\n@patch(\"mypackage.Database.connect\")\ndef test_database_connection(connect_mock):\n    \"\"\"Test with mocked database connection.\"\"\"\n    connect_mock.return_value = MockConnection()\n\n    db = Database()\n    db.connect()\n\n    connect_mock.assert_called_once_with(\"localhost\")\n```\n\n### Mocking Exceptions\n\n```python\n@patch(\"mypackage.api_call\")\ndef test_api_error_handling(api_call_mock):\n    \"\"\"Test error handling with mocked exception.\"\"\"\n    api_call_mock.side_effect = ConnectionError(\"Network error\")\n\n    with pytest.raises(ConnectionError):\n        api_call()\n\n    api_call_mock.assert_called_once()\n```\n\n### Mocking Context Managers\n\n```python\n@patch(\"builtins.open\", new_callable=mock_open)\ndef test_file_reading(mock_file):\n    \"\"\"Test file reading with mocked open.\"\"\"\n    mock_file.return_value.read.return_value = \"file content\"\n\n    result = read_file(\"test.txt\")\n\n    mock_file.assert_called_once_with(\"test.txt\", \"r\")\n    assert result == \"file content\"\n```\n\n### Using Autospec\n\n```python\n@patch(\"mypackage.DBConnection\", autospec=True)\ndef test_autospec(db_mock):\n    \"\"\"Test with autospec to catch API misuse.\"\"\"\n    db = db_mock.return_value\n    db.query(\"SELECT * FROM users\")\n\n    # This would fail if DBConnection doesn''t have query method\n    db_mock.assert_called_once()\n```\n\n### Mock Class Instances\n\n```python\nclass TestUserService:\n    @patch(\"mypackage.UserRepository\")\n    def test_create_user(self, repo_mock):\n        \"\"\"Test user creation with mocked repository.\"\"\"\n        repo_mock.return_value.save.return_value = User(id=1, name=\"Alice\")\n\n        service = UserService(repo_mock.return_value)\n        user = service.create_user(name=\"Alice\")\n\n        assert user.name == \"Alice\"\n        repo_mock.return_value.save.assert_called_once()\n```\n\n### Mock Property\n\n```python\n@pytest.fixture\ndef mock_config():\n    \"\"\"Create a mock with a property.\"\"\"\n    config = Mock()\n    type(config).debug = PropertyMock(return_value=True)\n    type(config).api_key = PropertyMock(return_value=\"test-key\")\n    return config\n\ndef test_with_mock_config(mock_config):\n    \"\"\"Test with mocked config properties.\"\"\"\n    assert mock_config.debug is True\n    assert mock_config.api_key == \"test-key\"\n```\n\n## Testing Async Code\n\n### Async Tests with pytest-asyncio\n\n```python\nimport pytest\n\n@pytest.mark.asyncio\nasync def test_async_function():\n    \"\"\"Test async function.\"\"\"\n    result = await async_add(2, 3)\n    assert result == 5\n\n@pytest.mark.asyncio\nasync def test_async_with_fixture(async_client):\n    \"\"\"Test async with async fixture.\"\"\"\n    response = await async_client.get(\"/api/users\")\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n```\n\n### Async Fixture\n\n```python\n@pytest.fixture\nasync def async_client():\n    \"\"\"Async fixture providing async test client.\"\"\"\n    app = create_app()\n    async with app.test_client() as client:\n        yield client\n\n@pytest.mark.asyncio\nasync def test_api_endpoint(async_client):\n    \"\"\"Test using async fixture.\"\"\"\n    response = await async_client.get(\"/api/data\")\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n```\n\n### Mocking Async Functions\n\n```python\n@pytest.mark.asyncio\n@patch(\"mypackage.async_api_call\")\nasync def test_async_mock(api_call_mock):\n    \"\"\"Test async function with mock.\"\"\"\n    api_call_mock.return_value = {\"status\": \"ok\"}\n\n    result = await my_async_function()\n\n    api_call_mock.assert_awaited_once()\n    assert result[\"status\"] == \"ok\"\n```\n\n## Testing Exceptions\n\n### Testing Expected Exceptions\n\n```python\ndef test_divide_by_zero():\n    \"\"\"Test that dividing by zero raises ZeroDivisionError.\"\"\"\n    with pytest.raises(ZeroDivisionError):\n        divide(10, 0)\n\ndef test_custom_exception():\n    \"\"\"Test custom exception with message.\"\"\"\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"invalid input\"):\n        validate_input(\"invalid\")\n```\n\n### Testing Exception Attributes\n\n```python\ndef test_exception_with_details():\n    \"\"\"Test exception with custom attributes.\"\"\"\n    with pytest.raises(CustomError) as exc_info:\n        raise CustomError(\"error\", code=400)\n\n    assert exc_info.value.code == 400\n    assert \"error\" in str(exc_info.value)\n```\n\n## Testing Side Effects\n\n### Testing File Operations\n\n```python\nimport tempfile\nimport os\n\ndef test_file_processing():\n    \"\"\"Test file processing with temp file.\"\"\"\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(mode=''w'', delete=False, suffix=''.txt'') as f:\n        f.write(\"test content\")\n        temp_path = f.name\n\n    try:\n        result = process_file(temp_path)\n        assert result == \"processed: test content\"\n    finally:\n        os.unlink(temp_path)\n```\n\n### Testing with pytest''s tmp_path Fixture\n\n```python\ndef test_with_tmp_path(tmp_path):\n    \"\"\"Test using pytest''s built-in temp path fixture.\"\"\"\n    test_file = tmp_path / \"test.txt\"\n    test_file.write_text(\"hello world\")\n\n    result = process_file(str(test_file))\n    assert result == \"hello world\"\n    # tmp_path automatically cleaned up\n```\n\n### Testing with tmpdir Fixture\n\n```python\ndef test_with_tmpdir(tmpdir):\n    \"\"\"Test using pytest''s tmpdir fixture.\"\"\"\n    test_file = tmpdir.join(\"test.txt\")\n    test_file.write(\"data\")\n\n    result = process_file(str(test_file))\n    assert result == \"data\"\n```\n\n## Test Organization\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n```\ntests/\n├── conftest.py                 # Shared fixtures\n├── __init__.py\n├── unit/                       # Unit tests\n│   ├── __init__.py\n│   ├── test_models.py\n│   ├── test_utils.py\n│   └── test_services.py\n├── integration/                # Integration tests\n│   ├── __init__.py\n│   ├── test_api.py\n│   └── test_database.py\n└── e2e/                        # End-to-end tests\n    ├── __init__.py\n    └── test_user_flow.py\n```\n\n### Test Classes\n\n```python\nclass TestUserService:\n    \"\"\"Group related tests in a class.\"\"\"\n\n    @pytest.fixture(autouse=True)\n    def setup(self):\n        \"\"\"Setup runs before each test in this class.\"\"\"\n        self.service = UserService()\n\n    def test_create_user(self):\n        \"\"\"Test user creation.\"\"\"\n        user = self.service.create_user(\"Alice\")\n        assert user.name == \"Alice\"\n\n    def test_delete_user(self):\n        \"\"\"Test user deletion.\"\"\"\n        user = User(id=1, name=\"Bob\")\n        self.service.delete_user(user)\n        assert not self.service.user_exists(1)\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### DO\n\n- **Follow TDD**: Write tests before code (red-green-refactor)\n- **Test one thing**: Each test should verify a single behavior\n- **Use descriptive names**: `test_user_login_with_invalid_credentials_fails`\n- **Use fixtures**: Eliminate duplication with fixtures\n- **Mock external dependencies**: Don''t depend on external services\n- **Test edge cases**: Empty inputs, None values, boundary conditions\n- **Aim for 80%+ coverage**: Focus on critical paths\n- **Keep tests fast**: Use marks to separate slow tests\n\n### DON''T\n\n- **Don''t test implementation**: Test behavior, not internals\n- **Don''t use complex conditionals in tests**: Keep tests simple\n- **Don''t ignore test failures**: All tests must pass\n- **Don''t test third-party code**: Trust libraries to work\n- **Don''t share state between tests**: Tests should be independent\n- **Don''t catch exceptions in tests**: Use `pytest.raises`\n- **Don''t use print statements**: Use assertions and pytest output\n- **Don''t write tests that are too brittle**: Avoid over-specific mocks\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Testing API Endpoints (FastAPI/Flask)\n\n```python\n@pytest.fixture\ndef client():\n    app = create_app(testing=True)\n    return app.test_client()\n\ndef test_get_user(client):\n    response = client.get(\"/api/users/1\")\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n    assert response.json[\"id\"] == 1\n\ndef test_create_user(client):\n    response = client.post(\"/api/users\", json={\n        \"name\": \"Alice\",\n        \"email\": \"alice@example.com\"\n    })\n    assert response.status_code == 201\n    assert response.json[\"name\"] == \"Alice\"\n```\n\n### Testing Database Operations\n\n```python\n@pytest.fixture\ndef db_session():\n    \"\"\"Create a test database session.\"\"\"\n    session = Session(bind=engine)\n    session.begin_nested()\n    yield session\n    session.rollback()\n    session.close()\n\ndef test_create_user(db_session):\n    user = User(name=\"Alice\", email=\"alice@example.com\")\n    db_session.add(user)\n    db_session.commit()\n\n    retrieved = db_session.query(User).filter_by(name=\"Alice\").first()\n    assert retrieved.email == \"alice@example.com\"\n```\n\n### Testing Class Methods\n\n```python\nclass TestCalculator:\n    @pytest.fixture\n    def calculator(self):\n        return Calculator()\n\n    def test_add(self, calculator):\n        assert calculator.add(2, 3) == 5\n\n    def test_divide_by_zero(self, calculator):\n        with pytest.raises(ZeroDivisionError):\n            calculator.divide(10, 0)\n```\n\n## pytest Configuration\n\n### pytest.ini\n\n```ini\n[pytest]\ntestpaths = tests\npython_files = test_*.py\npython_classes = Test*\npython_functions = test_*\naddopts =\n    --strict-markers\n    --disable-warnings\n    --cov=mypackage\n    --cov-report=term-missing\n    --cov-report=html\nmarkers =\n    slow: marks tests as slow\n    integration: marks tests as integration tests\n    unit: marks tests as unit tests\n```\n\n### pyproject.toml\n\n```toml\n[tool.pytest.ini_options]\ntestpaths = [\"tests\"]\npython_files = [\"test_*.py\"]\npython_classes = [\"Test*\"]\npython_functions = [\"test_*\"]\naddopts = [\n    \"--strict-markers\",\n    \"--cov=mypackage\",\n    \"--cov-report=term-missing\",\n    \"--cov-report=html\",\n]\nmarkers = [\n    \"slow: marks tests as slow\",\n    \"integration: marks tests as integration tests\",\n    \"unit: marks tests as unit tests\",\n]\n```\n\n## Running Tests\n\n```bash\n# Run all tests\npytest\n\n# Run specific file\npytest tests/test_utils.py\n\n# Run specific test\npytest tests/test_utils.py::test_function\n\n# Run with verbose output\npytest -v\n\n# Run with coverage\npytest --cov=mypackage --cov-report=html\n\n# Run only fast tests\npytest -m \"not slow\"\n\n# Run until first failure\npytest -x\n\n# Run and stop on N failures\npytest --maxfail=3\n\n# Run last failed tests\npytest --lf\n\n# Run tests with pattern\npytest -k \"test_user\"\n\n# Run with debugger on failure\npytest --pdb\n```\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Pattern | Usage |\n|---------|-------|\n| `pytest.raises()` | Test expected exceptions |\n| `@pytest.fixture()` | Create reusable test fixtures |\n| `@pytest.mark.parametrize()` | Run tests with multiple inputs |\n| `@pytest.mark.slow` | Mark slow tests |\n| `pytest -m \"not slow\"` | Skip slow tests |\n| `@patch()` | Mock functions and classes |\n| `tmp_path` fixture | Automatic temp directory |\n| `pytest --cov` | Generate coverage report |\n| `assert` | Simple and readable assertions |\n\n**Remember**: Tests are code too. Keep them clean, readable, and maintainable. Good tests catch bugs; great tests prevent them.\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-24T12:04:53.303Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"Python 测试策略 - AI智能代理","ja":"Python テスト戦略 - AIエージェント","ko":"Python 테스트 전략 - AI 에이전트","es":"Herramientas de testing de Python con Agentes de IA","fr":"Outils de test Python avec Agents IA","de":"Python-Test-Tools mit KI-Agenten","pt":"Ferramentas de Teste Python com Pytest e TDD - Agentes de IA","ru":"ИИ Агенты для тестирования Python с Pytest и TDD","ar":"أدوات اختبار بايثون مع بيست و TDD - وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","en":"python-testing"},"description":{"zh":"使用 pytest 和 TDD 方法的 Python 测试策略，提高测试效率和代码质量","ja":"pytest と TDD 方法を使用した Python テスト戦略により、テスト効率とコード品質を向上","ko":"pytest와 TDD 방법을 사용한 Python 테스트 전략으로 테스트 효율성과 코드 품질을 향상","es":"Estrategias de testing de Python para aplicaciones utilizando pytest, TDD y mejores prácticas, diseñadas para desarrolladores","fr":"Stratégies de test Python pour les applications utilisant pytest, TDD et meilleures pratiques, conçues pour les développeurs","de":"Python-Teststrategien für Anwendungen unter Verwendung von pytest, TDD und Best Practices, entwickelt für Entwickler","pt":"Desenvolva habilidades de teste Python com pytest e TDD. Aprenda a criar testes eficazes e melhorar a cobertura de teste.","ru":"Разрабатывайте навыки тестирования Python с помощью pytest и TDD. Узнайте, как создавать эффективные тесты и улучшать покрытие тестов.","ar":"طور مهارات اختبار بايثون باستخدام بيست و TDD. تعلم كيفية إنشاء اختبارات فعالة وتحسين تغطية ال