安全性和功能的 Stripe API 版本升级","将服务器端 SDK 迁移到最新的 Stripe API 版本","更新 Stripe.js 和移动 SDK 以改善支付处理"],"ja":["セキュリティと機能の向上のための Stripe API バージョンのアップグレード","サーバーサイドの SDK を最新の Stripe API バージョンに移行","Stripe.js とモバイル SDK を更新して決済処理を改善"],"ko":["보안 및 기능 개선을 위한 Stripe API 버전 업그레이드","서버 측 SDK를 최신 Stripe API 버전으로 마이그레이션","결제 처리 개선을 위한 Stripe.js 및 모바일 SDK 업데이트"],"es":["Actualización de versiones de API de Stripe para mejorar la seguridad y las características","Migración de SDK del lado del servidor a la última versión de la API de Stripe","Actualización de Stripe.js y SDK móviles para mejorar el procesamiento de pagos"],"fr":["Mise à jour des versions d''API Stripe pour améliorer la sécurité et les fonctionnalités","Migration des SDK côté serveur vers la dernière version de l''API Stripe","Mise à jour de Stripe.js et des SDK mobiles pour améliorer le traitement des paiements"],"de":["Aktualisieren von Stripe-API-Versionen für verbesserte Sicherheit und Funktionen","Migration von Server-seitigen SDKs auf die neueste Stripe-API-Version","Aktualisieren von Stripe.js und mobilen SDKs für verbessertes Zahlungsverarbeitung"],"pt":["Atualizar versões da API do Stripe para segurança e recursos aprimorados","Migrar SDKs no lado do servidor para a versão mais recente da API do Stripe","Atualizar Stripe.js e SDKs móveis para processamento de pagamentos aprimorado"],"ru":["Обновление версий API Stripe для повышения безопасности и функций","Миграция SDK на стороне сервера на последнюю версию API Stripe","Обновление Stripe.js и мобильных SDK для улучшения обработки платежей"],"ar":["تحديث إصدارات API Stripe لتحسين الأمان والميزات","نقل SDKs على جانب الخادم إلى أحدث إصدار من API Stripe","تحديث Stripe.js و SDKs المتنقلة لتحسين معالجة الدفع"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of Stripe API versioning and SDK management","Stripe account and API keys necessary for implementation"],"zh":["需要了解 Stripe API 版本和 SDK 管理的知识","需要 Stripe 账户和 API 密钥来实现"],"ja":["Stripe API バージョニングと SDK 管理の知識が必要","実装には Stripe アカウントと API キーが必要"],"ko":["Stripe API 버전 및 SDK 관리에 대한 지식 필요","구현을 위해 Stripe 계정 및 API 키가 필요"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de la versiones de API de Stripe y administración de SDK","Cuenta de Stripe y claves de API necesarias para la implementación"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances sur les versions d''API Stripe et la gestion de SDK","Compte Stripe et clés d''API nécessaires pour la mise en œuvre"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse über Stripe-API-Versionen und SDK-Verwaltung","Stripe-Konto und API-Schlüssel erforderlich für die Implementierung"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento de versionamento de API do Stripe e gerenciamento de SDK","Conta do Stripe e chaves de API necessárias para implementação"],"ru":["Требует знания версионности API Stripe и управления SDK","Требуется учетная запись Stripe и ключи API для реализации"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة إصدار API Stripe وإدارة SDK","حساب Stripe ومفاتيح API ضرورية للتطبيق"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"32f409610b34809799eba26a6c2a162fda1375f3ae27c1de5d5ff27b7c8b769b","repoEtag":"W/\"5ee601b6d9ce462bc4233d19d0ff766141297146df7a423c734bf7ea3ea80018\"","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('huggingface/skills/hugging-face-tool-builder', 'official', 'huggingface', 'skills', 'huggingface/skills', 'hugging-face-tool-builder', 2623, 186, 80, '2026-02-23T01:07:27Z', '2026-02-23T01:07:33.931Z', 'ad8ea7af44a94503c52859696c1828046688ceb71fda4361725fcd64e7aeaa82', '{"id":"huggingface/skills/hugging-face-tool-builder","name":"hugging-face-tool-builder","description":{"zh":"Hugging Face API工具构建器允许您创建可重用的命令行脚本和工具，用于获取、增强和处理数据","ja":"Hugging Face APIツールビルダーは、データの取得、強化、処理のために再利用可能なコマンドラインスクリプトとツールを作成することを可能にします","ko":"Hugging Face API 툴 빌더는 데이터의 가져오기, 강화, 처리를 위해 재사용 가능한 명령어 줄 스크립트와 툴을 생성할 수 있도록 합니다","es":"El constructor de herramientas de Hugging Face permite crear scripts reutilizables para utilizar la API de Hugging Face y automatizar tareas","fr":"Le constructeur d''outils Hugging Face permet de créer des scripts réutilisables pour utiliser l''API Hugging Face et automatiser des tâches","de":"Der Hugging Face-Tool-Builder ermöglicht die Erstellung wiederverwendbarer Skripte, um die Hugging Face-API zu nutzen und Aufgaben zu automatisieren","pt":"O Hugging Face Tool Builder permite criar scripts reutilizáveis para usar a API Hugging Face, facilitando a automação de tarefas","ru":"Hugging Face Tool Builder позволяет создавать повторно используемые скрипты для работы с API Hugging Face, что упрощает автоматизацию задач","ar":"يسمح Hugging Face Tool Builder بإنشاء scripts قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام لاستخدام واجهة برمجة تطبيقات Hugging Face، مما يسهل автоматيزация المهام","en":"Use this skill when the user wants to build tool/scripts or achieve a task where using data from the Hugging Face API would help. This is especially useful when chaining or combining API calls or the task will be repeated/automated. This Skill creates a reusable script to fetch, enrich or process..."},"owner":"huggingface","repo":"skills","repoPath":"huggingface/skills","stars":2623,"forks":186,"updatedAt":"2026-02-23T01:07:27Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"hugging-face-tool-builder","description":"Use this skill when the user wants to build tool/scripts or achieve a task where using data from the Hugging Face API would help. This is especially useful when chaining or combining API calls or the task will be repeated/automated. This Skill creates a reusable script to fetch, enrich or process data.","bodyPreview":"# Hugging Face API Tool Builder\n\nYour purpose is now is to create reusable command line scripts and utilities for using the Hugging Face API, allowing chaining, piping and intermediate processing where helpful. You can access the API directly, as well as use the `hf` command line tool. Model and Dataset cards can be accessed from repositories directly.\n\n## Script Rules\n\nMake sure to follow these rules:\n - Scripts must take a `--help` command line argument to describe their inputs and outputs\n -","body":"# Hugging Face API Tool Builder\n\nYour purpose is now is to create reusable command line scripts and utilities for using the Hugging Face API, allowing chaining, piping and intermediate processing where helpful. You can access the API directly, as well as use the `hf` command line tool. Model and Dataset cards can be accessed from repositories directly.\n\n## Script Rules\n\nMake sure to follow these rules:\n - Scripts must take a `--help` command line argument to describe their inputs and outputs\n - Non-destructive scripts should be tested before handing over to the User\n - Shell scripts are preferred, but use Python or TSX if complexity or user need requires it.\n - IMPORTANT: Use the `HF_TOKEN` environment variable as an Authorization header. For example: `curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer ${HF_TOKEN}\" https://huggingface.co/api/`. This provides higher rate limits and appropriate authorization for data access.\n - Investigate the shape of the API results before commiting to a final design; make use of piping and chaining where composability would be an advantage - prefer simple solutions where possible.\n - Share usage examples once complete.\n\nBe sure to confirm User preferences where there are questions or clarifications needed.\n\n## Sample Scripts\n\nPaths below are relative to this skill directory.\n\nReference examples:\n- `references/hf_model_papers_auth.sh` — uses `HF_TOKEN` automatically and chains trending → model metadata → model card parsing with fallbacks; it demonstrates multi-step API usage plus auth hygiene for gated/private content.\n- `references/find_models_by_paper.sh` — optional `HF_TOKEN` usage via `--token`, consistent authenticated search, and a retry path when arXiv-prefixed searches are too narrow; it shows resilient query strategy and clear user-facing help.\n- `references/hf_model_card_frontmatter.sh` — uses the `hf` CLI to download model cards, extracts YAML frontmatter, and emits NDJSON summaries (license, pipeline tag, tags, gated prompt flag) for easy filtering.\n\nBaseline examples (ultra-simple, minimal logic, raw JSON output with `HF_TOKEN` header):\n- `references/baseline_hf_api.sh` — bash\n- `references/baseline_hf_api.py` — python\n- `references/baseline_hf_api.tsx` — typescript executable\n\nComposable utility (stdin → NDJSON):\n- `references/hf_enrich_models.sh` — reads model IDs from stdin, fetches metadata per ID, emits one JSON object per line for streaming pipelines.\n\nComposability through piping (shell-friendly JSON output):\n- `references/baseline_hf_api.sh 25 | jq -r ''.[].id'' | references/hf_enrich_models.sh | jq -s ''sort_by(.downloads) | reverse | .[:10]''`\n- `references/baseline_hf_api.sh 50 | jq ''[.[] | {id, downloads}] | sort_by(.downloads) | reverse | .[:10]''`\n- `printf ''%s\\n'' openai/gpt-oss-120b meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3.1-8B | references/hf_model_card_frontmatter.sh | jq -s ''map({id, license, has_extra_gated_prompt})''`\n\n## High Level Endpoints\n\nThe following are the main API endpoints available at `https://huggingface.co`\n\n```\n/api/datasets\n/api/models\n/api/spaces\n/api/collections\n/api/daily_papers\n/api/notifications\n/api/settings\n/api/whoami-v2\n/api/trending\n/oauth/userinfo\n```\n\n## Accessing the API\n\nThe API is documented with the OpenAPI standard at `https://huggingface.co/.well-known/openapi.json`.\n\n**IMPORTANT:** DO NOT ATTEMPT to read `https://huggingface.co/.well-known/openapi.json` directly as it is too large to process. \n\n**IMPORTANT** Use `jq` to query and extract relevant parts. For example, \n\n Command to Get All 160 Endpoints\n\n```bash\ncurl -s \"https://huggingface.co/.well-known/openapi.json\" | jq ''.paths | keys | sort''\n```\n\nModel Search Endpoint Details\n\n```bash\ncurl -s \"https://huggingface.co/.well-known/openapi.json\" | jq ''.paths[\"/api/models\"]''\n```\n\nYou can also query endpoints to see the shape of the data. When doing so constrain results to low numbers to make them easy to process, yet representative.\n\n## Using the HF command line tool\n\nThe `hf` command line tool gives you further access to Hugging Face repository content and infrastructure. \n\n```bash\n❯ hf --help\nUsage: hf [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...\n\n  Hugging Face Hub CLI\n\nOptions:\n  --help                Show this message and exit.\n\nCommands:\n  auth                 Manage authentication (login, logout, etc.).\n  cache                Manage local cache directory.\n  download             Download files from the Hub.\n  endpoints            Manage Hugging Face Inference Endpoints.\n  env                  Print information about the environment.\n  jobs                 Run and manage Jobs on the Hub.\n  repo                 Manage repos on the Hub.\n  repo-files           Manage files in a repo on the Hub.\n  upload               Upload a file or a folder to the Hub.\n  upload-large-folder  Upload a large folder to the Hub.\n  version              Print information about the hf version.\n```\n\nThe `hf` CLI command has replaced the now deprecated `huggingface_hub` CLI command.\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-23T01:07:33.931Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI工具构建器 - Hugging Face API 工具","ja":"AIエージェント - Hugging Face API ツールビルダー","ko":"AI 에이전트 - Hugging Face API 툴 빌더","es":"Herramientas de AI: Constructor de herramientas de Huggin...","fr":"Outils d''IA: Constructeur d''outils Hugging Face","de":"KI-Tools: Hugging Face-Tool-Builder","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: Hugging Face Tool Builder","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Hugging Face Tool Builder","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: Hugging Face Tool Builder","en":"hugging-face-tool-builder"},"description":{"zh":"Hugging Face API工具构建器允许您创建可重用的命令行脚本和工具，用于获取、增强和处理数据","ja":"Hugging Face APIツールビルダーは、データの取得、強化、処理のために再利用可能なコマンドラインスクリプトとツールを作成することを可能にします","ko":"Hugging Face API 툴 빌더는 데이터의 가져오기, 강화, 처리를 위해 재사용 가능한 명령어 줄 스크립트와 툴을 생성할 수 있도록 합니다","es":"El constructor de herramientas de Hugging Face permite crear scripts reutilizables para utilizar la API de Hugging Face y automatizar tareas","fr":"Le constructeur d''outils Hugging Face permet de créer des scripts réutilisables pour utiliser l''API Hugging Face et automatiser des tâches","de":"Der Hugging Face-Tool-Builder ermöglicht die Erstellung wiederverwendbarer Skripte, um die Hugging Face-API zu nutzen und Aufgaben zu automatisieren","pt":"O Hugging Face Tool Builder permite criar scripts reutilizáveis para usar a API Hugging Face, facilitando a automação de tarefas","ru":"Hugging Face Tool Builder позволяет создавать повторно используемые скрипты для работы с API Hugging Face, что упрощает автоматизацию задач","ar":"يسمح Hugging Face Tool Builder بإنشاء scripts قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام لاستخدام واجهة برمجة تطبيقات Hugging Face، مما يسهل автоматيزация المهام","en":"Use this skill when the user wants to build tool/scripts or achieve a task where using data from the Hugging Face API would help. This is especially useful w..."},"definition":{"en":"Use this skill when the user wants to build tool/scripts or achieve a task where using data from the Hugging Face API would help. This is especially useful when chaining or combining API calls or the task will be repeated/automated. This Skill creates a reusable script to fetch, enrich or process data."},"features":{"zh":["支持Hugging Face API的直接访问","支持hf命令行工具","支持模型和数据集卡片的访问","支持脚本的重用和组合","支持数据的获取、增强和处理"],"ja":["Hugging Face APIへの直接アクセスをサポート","hfコマンドラインツールをサポート","モデルとデータセットカードへのアクセスをサポート","スクリプトの再利用と組み合わせをサポート","データの取得、強化、処理をサポート"],"ko":["Hugging Face APIへの 직접 접근을 지원","hf 명령어 줄 툴을 지원","모델과 데이터셋 카드への 접근을 지원","스크립트의 재사용과 조합을 지원","데이터의 가져오기, 강화, 처리를 지원"],"es":["Crea scripts reutilizables para la API de Hugging Face","Permite la automatización de tareas","Soporta la línea de comandos `hf`","Acceso a tarjetas de modelos y conjuntos de datos","Permite el procesamiento de datos intermedio","Soporta la chaining y el piping"],"fr":["Crée des scripts réutilisables pour l''API Hugging Face","Permet l''automatisation de tâches","Prend en charge la ligne de commande `hf`","Accès aux cartes de modèles et de jeux de données","Permet le traitement de données intermédiaires","Prend en charge la chaîne et le piping"],"de":["Erstellt wiederverwendbare Skripte für die Hugging Face-API","Ermöglicht die Automatisierung von Aufgaben","Unterstützt die Kommandozeile `hf`","Zugriff auf Modell- und Datensatz-Karten","Ermöglicht die Zwischenverarbeitung von Daten","Unterstützt die Verkettung und den Piping"],"pt":["Criação de scripts reutilizáveis","Acesso direto à API Hugging Face","Uso do comando `hf`","Acesso a cartões de modelos e conjuntos de dados","Processamento intermediário"],"ru":["Создание повторно используемых скриптов","Прямой доступ к API Hugging Face","Использование команды `hf`","Доступ к карточкам моделей и наборов данных","Промежуточная обработка"],"ar":["إنشاء scripts قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام","الدخول المباشر إلى واجهة برمجة تطبيقات Hugging Face","استخدام الأمر `hf`","الدخول إلى بطاقات النماذج ومجموعات البيانات","المعالجة الوسيطة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI工具","Hugging Face API","命令行脚本","数据获取","数据增强","数据处理","hf命令行工具","模型和数据集卡片"],"ja":["AIエージェント","Hugging Face API","コマンドラインスクリプト","データの取得","データの強化","データの処理","hfコマンドラインツール","モデルとデータセットカード"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","Hugging Face API","명령어 줄 스크립트","데이터의 가져오기","데이터의 강화","데이터의 처리","hf 명령어 줄 툴","모델과 데이터셋 카드"],"es":["Herramientas de AI","Constructor de herramientas de Hugging Face","API de Hugging Face","Automatización de tareas","Skripting","Línea de comandos","Procesamiento de datos","Inteligencia artificial"],"fr":["Outils d''IA","Constructeur d''outils Hugging Face","API Hugging Face","Automatisation de tâches","Scripting","Ligne de commande","Traitement de données","Intelligence artificielle"],"de":["KI-Tools","Hugging Face-Tool-Builder","Hugging Face-API","Automatisierung von Aufgaben","Skripting","Kommandozeile","Datenverarbeitung","Künstliche Intelligenz"],"pt":["Hugging Face Tool Builder","Ferramentas de IA","API Hugging Face","Scripts reutilizáveis","Automação de tarefas","Desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["Hugging Face Tool Builder","ИИ Агенты","API Hugging Face","Повторно используемые скрипты","Автоматизация задач","Разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["Hugging Face Tool Builder","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","واجهة برمجة تطبيقات Hugging Face","scripts قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام","تأتيير المهام","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents needing automated data processing and enrichment using the Hugging Face API","zh":"适合需要使用 Hugging Face API 进行自动化数据处理和增强的 AI Agents","ja":"Hugging Face API を使用した自動化されたデータ処理およびエンリッチメントが必要な AI エージェントに適しています","ko":"Hugging Face API를 사용하여 자동화된 데이터 처리 및 강화가 필요한 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que necesitan procesamiento y enriquecimiento de datos automatizados utilizando la Hugging Face API","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA ayant besoin d''un traitement et d''un enrichissement de données automatisés à l''aide de la Hugging Face API","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die automatisierte Datenverarbeitung und -anreicherung unter Verwendung der Hugging Face API benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que necessitam de processamento e enriquecimento de dados automatizados usando a Hugging Face API","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, которым требуется автоматизированная обработка и обогащение данных с использованием Hugging Face API","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يحتاجون إلى معالجة البيانات وتحسينها آليًا باستخدام واجهة برمجة تطبيقات Hugging Face"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create reusable command line scripts and utilities for fetching, enriching, or processing data from the Hugging Face API, utilizing the `hf` command line tool and supporting chaining, piping, and intermediate processing, while accessing model and dataset cards from repositories directly","zh":"赋予代理创建可重用命令行脚本和实用程序的能力，以从 Hugging Face API 中获取、增强或处理数据，利用 `hf` 命令行工具并支持链式、管道和中间处理，同时直接从存储库访问模型和数据集卡","ja":"Hugging Face API からデータを取得、エンリッチメント、または処理するための再利用可能なコマンドラインスクリプトおよびユーティリティを作成する機能をエージェントに与え、`hf` コマンドラインツールを使用し、チェーン、パイプ、 intermediate 処理をサポートしながら、リポジトリから直接モデルおよびデータセットカードにアクセスします","ko":"Hugging Face API에서 데이터를 가져오거나 강화 또는 처리하기 위한 재사용 가능한 명령줄 스크립트 및 유틸리티를 생성할 수 있는 기능을 에이전트에 부여하여 `hf` 명령줄 도구를 사용하고 체인, 파이프 및 중간 처리를 지원하며 리포지토리에서 직접 모델 및 데이터셋 카드를 액세스합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear scripts de línea de comandos reutilizables y utilidades para recuperar, enriquecer o procesar datos de la Hugging Face API, utilizando la herramienta de línea de comandos `hf` y admitiendo encadenamiento, tuberías y procesamiento intermedio, mientras accede a tarjetas de modelo y conjunto de datos de los repositorios directamente","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des scripts de ligne de commande réutilisables et des utilitaires pour récupérer, enrichir ou traiter des données de la Hugging Face API, en utilisant l''outil de ligne de commande `hf` et en prenant en charge la chaîne, la tuyauterie et le traitement intermédiaire, tout en accédant aux cartes de modèle et de jeu de données à partir de référentiels directement","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, wiederverwendbare Befehlszeilen-Skripte und -Utilities für das Abrufen, Anreichern oder Verarbeiten von Daten aus der Hugging Face API zu erstellen, indem es das Befehlszeilen-Tool `hf` verwendet und die Verkettung, Pipelining und Zwischenverarbeitung unterstützt, während es direkt auf Modell- und Datensatz-Karten aus den Repositories zugreift","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar scripts de linha de comando reutilizáveis e utilitários para buscar, enriquecer ou processar dados da Hugging Face API, utilizando a ferramenta de linha de comando `hf` e suportando encadeamento, tubulação e processamento intermediário, ao mesmo tempo em que acessa cartões de modelo e conjunto de dados de repositórios diretamente","ru":"Предоставляет агентам возможность создавать многократно используемые скрипты командной строки и утилиты для получения, обогащения или обработки данных из Hugging Face API, используя инструмент командной строки `hf` и поддерживая цепочечную обработку, потоковую обработку и промежуточную обработку, а также доступ к карточкам модели и наборов данных из репозиториев напрямую","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إنشاء سكريبتات سطر الأوامر القابلة لإعادة الاستخدام وأدوات لاسترجاع البيانات أو تعزيزها أو معالجتها من واجهة برمجة تطبيقات Hugging Face، باستخدام أداة سطر الأوامر `hf` ودعم السلاسل والأنابيب والمعالجة الوسيطية، مع الوصول إلى بطاقات النموذج وجموع البيانات من 存储 مباشرة"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating data enrichment tasks using Hugging Face models","Generating reusable scripts for fetching dataset cards","Creating custom utilities for processing data from the Hugging Face API"],"zh":["使用 Hugging Face 模型自动执行数据增强任务","生成可重用脚本以获取数据集卡","创建自定义实用程序以从 Hugging Face API 处理数据"],"ja":["Hugging Face モデルを使用したデータエンリッチメントタスクの自動化","データセットカードを取得する再利用可能なスクリプトの生成","Hugging Face API からデータを処理するためのカスタムユーティリティの作成"],"ko":["Hugging Face 모델을 사용하여 데이터 강화 작업을 자동화하는こと","데이터셋 카드를 가져오는 재사용 가능한 스크립트를 생성하는こと","Hugging Face API에서 데이터를 처리하기 위한 사용자 지정 유틸리티를 만드는こと"],"es":["Automatizar tareas de enriquecimiento de datos utilizando modelos de Hugging Face","Generar scripts reutilizables para recuperar tarjetas de conjunto de datos","Crear utilidades personalizadas para procesar datos de la Hugging Face API"],"fr":["Automatiser les tâches d''enrichissement de données à l''aide de modèles Hugging Face","Générer des scripts réutilisables pour récupérer des cartes de jeu de données","Créer des utilitaires personnalisés pour traiter des données de la Hugging Face API"],"de":["Automatisierung von Datenanreicherungsaufgaben unter Verwendung von Hugging Face-Modellen","Erstellen wiederverwendbarer Skripte zum Abrufen von Datensatz-Karten","Erstellen benutzerdefinierter Utilities zum Verarbeiten von Daten aus der Hugging Face API"],"pt":["Automatizar tarefas de enriquecimento de dados usando modelos Hugging Face","Gerar scripts reutilizáveis para buscar cartões de conjunto de dados","Criar utilitários personalizados para processar dados da Hugging Face API"],"ru":["Автоматизировать задачи обогащения данных с использованием моделей Hugging Face","Генерировать многократно используемые скрипты для получения карточек наборов данных","Создавать пользовательские утилиты для обработки данных из Hugging Face API"],"ar":["تأتمتة مهام تحسين البيانات باستخدام نماذج واجهة برمجة تطبيقات Hugging Face","генерировать سكريبتات قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام لاسترجاع بطاقات مجموعة البيانات","إنشاء أدوات مخصصة لمعالجة البيانات من واجهة برمجة تطبيقات Hugging Face"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Hugging Face API access","Must follow script rules, including implementing a `--help` command line argument"],"zh":["需要 Hugging Face API 访问","必须遵循脚本规则，包括实现 `--help` 命令行参数"],"ja":["Hugging Face API へのアクセスが必要","スクリプトのルールに従う必要があり、`--help` コマンドライン引数の実装が含まれます"],"ko":["Hugging Face API에 대한 액세스가 필요합니다","스크립트 규칙을 따라야 하며 `--help` 명령줄 인수를 구현해야 함"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la Hugging Face API","Debe seguir las reglas de script, incluyendo la implementación de un argumento de línea de comandos `--help`"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à la Hugging Face API","Doit suivre les règles de script, y compris la mise en œuvre d''un argument de ligne de commande `--help`"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die Hugging Face API","Muss den Skriptregeln folgen, einschließlich der Implementierung eines Befehlszeilenarguments `--help`"],"pt":["Requer acesso à Hugging Face API","Deve seguir as regras de script, incluindo a implementação de um argumento de linha de comando `--help`"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к Hugging Face API","Должно соблюдать правила скрипта, включая реализацию аргумента командной строки `--help`"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى واجهة برمجة تطبيقات Hugging Face","يجب اتباع قواعد السكريبت، بما في ذلك تنفيذ حجة سطر الأوامر `--help`"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"ad8ea7af44a94503c52859696c1828046688ceb71fda4361725fcd64e7aeaa82","repoEtag":"W/\"d4d9459564f81c1ff31ac7f0c8bef3b09fd0bddb85b49126293f0deb1bf630b8\"","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('google-labs-code/stitch-skills/stitch-loop', 'official', 'google-labs-code', 'stitch-skills', 'google-labs-code/stitch-skills', 'stitch-loop', 1902, 219, 80, '2026-02-22T23:11:02Z', '2026-02-23T01:07:34.632Z', 'db146c4fff2a52e8bae41fdf717cddbf7a075b913c4d0d82180441b9cb84c90a', '{"id":"google-labs-code/stitch-skills/stitch-loop","name":"stitch-loop","description":{"zh":"Stitch Loop模式是一种自主的网站开发模式，使用Stitch工具生成页面并集成到网站中","ja":"Stitch Loopパターンは、Stitchツールを使用してページを生成し、Webサイトに統合する自主的なWebサイト開発モードです","ko":"스티치 루프 패턴은 스티치 툴을 사용하여 페이지를 생성하고 웹사이트에 통합하는 자율적인 웹사이트 개발 모드입니다","es":"Stitch Loop es un patrón de desarrollo web autónomo que utiliza un sistema de ''baton'' para generar páginas con Stitch. Permite la creación continua de sitios web a través de iteraciones autónomas","fr":"Stitch Loop est un modèle de développement web autonome qui utilise un système de ''baton'' pour générer des pages avec Stitch. Il permet la création continue de sites web à travers des itérations autonomes","de":"Stitch Loop ist ein Muster für autonomes Webdevelopment, das ein ''Baton''-System verwendet, um Seiten mit Stitch zu generieren. Es ermöglicht die kontinuierliche Erstellung von Webseiten durch autonome Iterationen","pt":"O stitch-loop é um padrão de loop de construção de sites autônomo que permite o desenvolvimento contínuo de sites com Stitch","ru":"Stitch-loop - это шаблон автономного цикла создания сайтов, который позволяет обеспечить непрерывное развитие сайтов с помощью Stitch","ar":"stitch-loop هو نمط لتعلم بناء مواقع الويب التطوري التي تمكن من تطوير المواقع بشكل مستمر باستخدام Stitch","en":"Teaches agents to iteratively build websites using Stitch with an autonomous baton-passing loop pattern"},"owner":"google-labs-code","repo":"stitch-skills","repoPath":"google-labs-code/stitch-skills","stars":1902,"forks":219,"updatedAt":"2026-02-22T23:11:02Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"stitch-loop","description":"Teaches agents to iteratively build websites using Stitch with an autonomous baton-passing loop pattern","bodyPreview":"# Stitch Build Loop\n\nYou are an **autonomous frontend builder** participating in an iterative site-building loop. Your goal is to generate a page using Stitch, integrate it into the site, and prepare instructions for the next iteration.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Build Loop pattern enables continuous, autonomous website development through a \"baton\" system. Each iteration:\n1. Reads the current task from a baton file (`next-prompt.md`)\n2. Generates a page using Stitch MCP tools\n3. Integrates the page into","body":"# Stitch Build Loop\n\nYou are an **autonomous frontend builder** participating in an iterative site-building loop. Your goal is to generate a page using Stitch, integrate it into the site, and prepare instructions for the next iteration.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Build Loop pattern enables continuous, autonomous website development through a \"baton\" system. Each iteration:\n1. Reads the current task from a baton file (`next-prompt.md`)\n2. Generates a page using Stitch MCP tools\n3. Integrates the page into the site structure\n4. Writes the next task to the baton file for the next iteration\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n**Required:**\n- Access to the Stitch MCP Server\n- A Stitch project (existing or will be created)\n- A `DESIGN.md` file (generate one using the `design-md` skill if needed)\n- A `SITE.md` file documenting the site vision and roadmap\n\n**Optional:**\n- Chrome DevTools MCP Server — enables visual verification of generated pages\n\n## The Baton System\n\nThe `next-prompt.md` file acts as a relay baton between iterations:\n\n```markdown\n---\npage: about\n---\nA page describing how jules.top tracking works.\n\n**DESIGN SYSTEM (REQUIRED):**\n[Copy from DESIGN.md Section 6]\n\n**Page Structure:**\n1. Header with navigation\n2. Explanation of tracking methodology\n3. Footer with links\n```\n\n**Critical rules:**\n- The `page` field in YAML frontmatter determines the output filename\n- The prompt content must include the design system block from `DESIGN.md`\n- You MUST update this file before completing your work to continue the loop\n\n## Execution Protocol\n\n### Step 1: Read the Baton\n\nParse `next-prompt.md` to extract:\n- **Page name** from the `page` frontmatter field\n- **Prompt content** from the markdown body\n\n### Step 2: Consult Context Files\n\nBefore generating, read these files:\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `SITE.md` | Site vision, **Stitch Project ID**, existing pages (sitemap), roadmap |\n| `DESIGN.md` | Required visual style for Stitch prompts |\n\n**Important checks:**\n- Section 4 (Sitemap) — Do NOT recreate pages that already exist\n- Section 5 (Roadmap) — Pick tasks from here if backlog exists\n- Section 6 (Creative Freedom) — Ideas for new pages if roadmap is empty\n\n### Step 3: Generate with Stitch\n\nUse the Stitch MCP tools to generate the page:\n\n1. **Discover namespace**: Run `list_tools` to find the Stitch MCP prefix\n2. **Get or create project**: \n   - If `stitch.json` exists, use the `projectId` from it\n   - Otherwise, call `[prefix]:create_project` and save the ID to `stitch.json`\n3. **Generate screen**: Call `[prefix]:generate_screen_from_text` with:\n   - `projectId`: The project ID\n   - `prompt`: The full prompt from the baton (including design system block)\n   - `deviceType`: `DESKTOP` (or as specified)\n4. **Retrieve assets**: Call `[prefix]:get_screen` to get:\n   - `htmlCode.downloadUrl` — Download and save as `queue/{page}.html`\n   - `screenshot.downloadUrl` — Download and save as `queue/{page}.png`\n\n### Step 4: Integrate into Site\n\n1. Move generated HTML from `queue/{page}.html` to `site/public/{page}.html`\n2. Fix any asset paths to be relative to the public folder\n3. Update navigation:\n   - Find existing placeholder links (e.g., `href=\"#\"`) and wire them to the new page\n   - Add the new page to the global navigation if appropriate\n4. Ensure consistent headers/footers across all pages\n\n### Step 4.5: Visual Verification (Optional)\n\nIf the **Chrome DevTools MCP Server** is available, verify the generated page:\n\n1. **Check availability**: Run `list_tools` to see if `chrome*` tools are present\n2. **Start dev server**: Use Bash to start a local server (e.g., `npx serve site/public`)\n3. **Navigate to page**: Call `[chrome_prefix]:navigate` to open `http://localhost:3000/{page}.html`\n4. **Capture screenshot**: Call `[chrome_prefix]:screenshot` to capture the rendered page\n5. **Visual comparison**: Compare against the Stitch screenshot (`queue/{page}.png`) for fidelity\n6. **Stop server**: Terminate the dev server process\n\n> **Note:** This step is optional. If Chrome DevTools MCP is not installed, skip to Step 5.\n\n### Step 5: Update Site Documentation\n\nModify `SITE.md`:\n- Add the new page to Section 4 (Sitemap) with `[x]`\n- Remove any idea you consumed from Section 6 (Creative Freedom)\n- Update Section 5 (Roadmap) if you completed a backlog item\n\n### Step 6: Prepare the Next Baton (Critical)\n\n**You MUST update `next-prompt.md` before completing.** This keeps the loop alive.\n\n1. **Decide the next page**: \n   - Check `SITE.md` Section 5 (Roadmap) for pending items\n   - If empty, pick from Section 6 (Creative Freedom)\n   - Or invent something new that fits the site vision\n2. **Write the baton** with proper YAML frontmatter:\n\n```markdown\n---\npage: achievements\n---\nA competitive achievements page showing developer badges and milestones.\n\n**DESIGN SYSTEM (REQUIRED):**\n[Copy the entire design system block from DESIGN.md]\n\n**Page Structure:**\n1. Header with title and navigation\n2. Badge grid showing unlocked/locked states\n3. Progress bars for milestone tracking\n```\n\n## File Structure Reference\n\n```\nproject/\n├── next-prompt.md      # The baton — current task\n├── stitch.json         # Stitch project ID (persist this!)\n├── DESIGN.md           # Visual design system (from design-md skill)\n├── SITE.md             # Site vision, sitemap, roadmap\n├── queue/              # Staging area for Stitch output\n│   ├── {page}.html\n│   └── {page}.png\n└── site/public/        # Production pages\n    ├── index.html\n    └── {page}.html\n```\n\n## Orchestration Options\n\nThe loop can be driven by different orchestration layers:\n\n| Method | How it works |\n|--------|--------------|\n| **CI/CD** | GitHub Actions triggers on `next-prompt.md` changes |\n| **Human-in-loop** | Developer reviews each iteration before continuing |\n| **Agent chains** | One agent dispatches to another (e.g., Jules API) |\n| **Manual** | Developer runs the agent repeatedly with the same repo |\n\nThe skill is orchestration-agnostic — focus on the pattern, not the trigger mechanism.\n\n## Design System Integration\n\nThis skill works best with the `design-md` skill:\n\n1. **First time setup**: Generate `DESIGN.md` using the `design-md` skill from an existing Stitch screen\n2. **Every iteration**: Copy Section 6 (\"Design System Notes for Stitch Generation\") into your baton prompt\n3. **Consistency**: All generated pages will share the same visual language\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n- ❌ Forgetting to update `next-prompt.md` (breaks the loop)\n- ❌ Recreating a page that already exists in the sitemap\n- ❌ Not including the design system block in the prompt\n- ❌ Leaving placeholder links (`href=\"#\"`) instead of wiring real navigation\n- ❌ Forgetting to persist `stitch.json` after creating a new project\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n| Issue | Solution |\n|-------|----------|\n| Stitch generation fails | Check that the prompt includes the design system block |\n| Inconsistent styles | Ensure DESIGN.md is up-to-date and copied correctly |\n| Loop stalls | Verify `next-prompt.md` was updated with valid frontmatter |\n| Navigation broken | Check all internal links use correct relative paths |\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-23T01:07:34.632Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理Stitch Loop模式","ja":"AIエージェントのStitch Loopパターン","ko":"AI 에이전트 스티치 루프 패턴","es":"Herramientas de AI: Stitch Loop para Desarrolladores","fr":"Outils d''IA: Stitch Loop pour les Développeurs","de":"KI-Tools: Stitch Loop für Entwickler","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: Stitch Loop para Desenvolvedores","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Stitch Loop для Автоматизации Сайтов","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: stitch-loop للتعلم التطويري","en":"stitch-loop"},"description":{"zh":"Stitch Loop模式是一种自主的网站开发模式，使用Stitch工具生成页面并集成到网站中","ja":"Stitch Loopパターンは、Stitchツールを使用してページを生成し、Webサイトに統合する自主的なWebサイト開発モードです","ko":"스티치 루프 패턴은 스티치 툴을 사용하여 페이지를 생성하고 웹사이트에 통합하는 자율적인 웹사이트 개발 모드입니다","es":"Stitch Loop es un patrón de desarrollo web autónomo que utiliza un sistema de ''baton'' para generar páginas con Stitch. Permite la creación continua de sitios...","fr":"Stitch Loop est un modèle de développement web autonome qui utilise un système de ''baton'' pour générer des pages avec Stitch. Il permet la création continue ...","de":"Stitch Loop ist ein Muster für autonomes Webdevelopment, das ein ''Baton''-System verwendet, um Seiten mit Stitch zu generieren. Es ermöglicht die kontinuierli...","pt":"O stitch-loop é um padrão de loop de construção de sites autônomo que permite o desenvolvimento contínuo de sites com Stitch","ru":"Stitch-loop - это шаблон автономного цикла создания сайтов, который позволяет обеспечить непрерывное развитие сайтов с помощью Stitch","ar":"stitch-loop هو نمط لتعلم بناء مواقع الويب التطوري التي تمكن من تطوير المواقع بشكل مستمر باستخدام Stitch","en":"Teaches agents to iteratively build websites using Stitch with an autonomous baton-passing loop pattern"},"definition":{"en":"Teaches agents to iteratively build websites using Stitch with an autonomous baton-passing loop pattern"},"features":{"zh":["自主的网站开发","使用Stitch工具生成页面","页面集成到网站中","持续的开发循环","提高开发效率"],"ja":["自主的なWebサイト開発","Stitchツールを使用したページの生成","ページのWebサイトへの統合","継続的な開発サイクル","開発効率の向上"],"ko":["자율적인 웹사이트 개발","스티치 툴을 사용한 페이지 생성","페이지의 웹사이트 통합","지속적인 개발 사이클","개발 효율성 향상"],"es":["Desarrollo web autónomo","Sistema de ''baton'' para generar páginas","Integración con Stitch","Creación continua de sitios web","Iteraciones autónomas"],"fr":["Développement web autonome","Système de ''baton'' pour générer des pages","Intégration avec Stitch","Création continue de sites web","Itérations autonomes"],"de":["Autonomes Webdevelopment","''Baton''-System für die Generierung von Seiten","Integration mit Stitch","Kontinuierliche Erstellung von Webseiten","Autonome Iterationen"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento contínuo de sites com Stitch","Padrão de loop de construção de sites autônomo","Integração com ferramentas MCP","Geração de páginas com Stitch","Preparação de instruções para a próxima iteração"],"ru":["Непрерывное развитие сайтов с помощью Stitch","Шаблон автономного цикла создания сайтов","Интеграция с инструментами MCP","Генерация страниц с помощью Stitch","Подготовка инструкций для следующей итерации"],"ar":["التطوير المستمر للمواقع باستخدام Stitch","نمط لتعلم بناء مواقع الويب التطوري","التكامل مع أدوات MCP","توليد صفحات باستخدام Stitch","إعداد تعليمات للتعلم التطوري التالي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","Stitch Loop模式","自主网站开发","Stitch工具","网站开发效率","持续开发循环"],"ja":["AIエージェント","Stitch Loopパターン","自主的なWebサイト開発","Stitchツール","Webサイト開発効率","継続的な開発サイクル"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","스티치 루프 패턴","자율적인 웹사이트 개발","스티치 툴","웹사이트 개발 효율성","지속적인 개발 사이클"],"es":["Stitch Loop","desarrollo web autónomo","herramientas de AI","sistema de baton","generación de páginas","integración con Stitch","creación de sitios web","desarrollo de software","tecnologías web"],"fr":["Stitch Loop","développement web autonome","outils d''IA","système de baton","génération de pages","intégration avec Stitch","création de sites web","développement de logiciels","technologies web"],"de":["Stitch Loop","autonomes Webdevelopment","KI-Tools","Baton-System","Seitengenerierung","Integration mit Stitch","Erstellung von Webseiten","Softwareentwicklung","Webtechnologien"],"pt":["stitch-loop","desenvolvimento de sites","ferramentas de IA","Stitch","MCP","loop de construção de sites","desenvolvedores de frontend"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты","stitch-loop","создание сайтов","Stitch","MCP","автономный цикл создания сайтов","разработчики frontend"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","stitch-loop","بناء مواقع الويب","Stitch","MCP","نمط لتعلم بناء مواقع الويب التطوري","مطورين التطوير الأمامي"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Autonomous Frontend Builder Agents needing iterative website development capabilities using Stitch with a baton-passing loop pattern","zh":"非常适合需要使用Stitch进行迭代网站开发的Autonomous Frontend Builder Agents，采用baton-passing循环模式","ja":"Stitchを使用してイテレーティブなWebサイト開発を必要とするAutonomous Frontend Builder Agentsに最適です。バトンパス循環パターンを使用します","ko":"Stitch를 사용하여 반복적인 웹사이트 개발 기능이 필요한 자율적 프론트엔드 빌더 에이전트에게 적합합니다. baton-passing 루프 패턴을 사용합니다","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Constructor de Frontend Autónomo que necesitan capacidades de desarrollo de sitios web iterativos utilizando Stitch con un patrón de bucle de paso de testigo","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Construction de Frontend Autonome nécessitant des capacités de développement de site Web itératif en utilisant Stitch avec un modèle de boucle de passage de bâton","de":"Perfekt für autonome Frontend-Builder-Agents, die iterative Website-Entwicklungsfähigkeiten mit Stitch und einem Staffelübernahmemuster benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Construtores de Frontend Autônomos que necessitam de capacidades de desenvolvimento de sites iterativos usando Stitch com um padrão de loop de passagem de bastão","ru":"Идеально для автономных агентов по построению frontend, которым необходимы итеративные возможности разработки сайтов с помощью Stitch и шаблона передачи эстафеты","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الأمامية البناء المستقلة التي تحتاج إلى القدرات التطويرية الموقع الإيتراتيف باستخدام خياطة مع نمط حلقة تمرير العصا"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate pages using Stitch MCP tools, integrate them into sites, and prepare instructions for the next iteration via a baton file system, leveraging Markdown files like ''next-prompt.md'' for continuous development","zh":"赋予代理生成页面的能力，使用Stitch MCP工具，将其集成到网站中，并通过baton文件系统为下一次迭代准备说明，利用如''next-prompt.md''的Markdown文件实现持续开发","ja":"エージェントにStitch MCPツールを使用してページを生成し、サイトに統合し、バトンファイルシステムを使用して次のイテレーションの説明を準備する機能を提供します。''next-prompt.md''のようなMarkdownファイルを使用して継続的な開発を実現します","ko":"에이전트가 Stitch MCP 도구를 사용하여 페이지를 생성하고 사이트에 통합하며 baton 파일 시스템을 사용하여 다음 반복에 대한 지침을 준비할 수 있는 기능을 제공합니다. ''next-prompt.md''와 같은 Markdown 파일을 사용하여 지속적인 개발을 구현합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar páginas utilizando las herramientas Stitch MCP, integrarlas en sitios y preparar instrucciones para la siguiente iteración a través de un sistema de archivos de testigo, aprovechando archivos Markdown como ''next-prompt.md'' para el desarrollo continuo","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des pages en utilisant les outils Stitch MCP, de les intégrer dans des sites et de préparer des instructions pour l''itération suivante via un système de fichiers de bâton, en exploitant des fichiers Markdown tels que ''next-prompt.md'' pour le développement continu","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Seiten mit den Stitch-MCP-Tools zu generieren, sie in Websites zu integrieren und Anweisungen für die nächste Iteration über ein Staffelübergabedateisystem vorzubereiten, wobei Markdown-Dateien wie ''next-prompt.md'' für die kontinuierliche Entwicklung genutzt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar páginas usando as ferramentas Stitch MCP, integrá-las em sites e preparar instruções para a próxima iteração via um sistema de arquivos de bastão, aproveitando arquivos Markdown como ''next-prompt.md'' para desenvolvimento contínuo","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать страницы с помощью инструментов Stitch MCP, интегрировать их в сайты и готовить инструкции для следующей итерации через систему файлов эстафеты, используя файлы Markdown, такие как ''next-prompt.md'', для непрерывной разработки","ar":"يتمكن الوكلاء من إنشاء صفحات باستخدام أدوات خياطة إم سي بي، وتكاملها مع المواقع، وإعداد الإرشادات للتعاقب التالي من خلال نظام ملفات العصا، واستخدام ملفات ماركداون مثل ''next-prompt.md'' من أجل التطوير المستمر"},"useCases":{"en":["Generating pages using Stitch MCP tools","Integrating pages into existing websites","Preparing instructions for subsequent iterations via baton files"],"zh":["使用Stitch MCP工具生成页面","将页面集成到现有网站中","通过baton文件为后续迭代准备说明"],"ja":["Stitch MCPツールを使用してページを生成する","ページを既存のWebサイトに統合する","バトンファイルを使用して後のイテレーションの説明を準備する"],"ko":["Stitch MCP 도구를 사용하여 페이지를 생성하는 것","페이지를 기존 웹사이트에 통합하는 것","baton 파일을 사용하여 이후 반복에 대한 지침을 준비하는 것"],"es":["Generar páginas utilizando las herramientas Stitch MCP","Integrar páginas en sitios web existentes","Preparar instrucciones para iteraciones posteriores a través de archivos de testigo"],"fr":["Générer des pages en utilisant les outils Stitch MCP","Intégrer des pages dans des sites Web existants","Préparer des instructions pour les itérations suivantes via des fichiers de bâton"],"de":["Seiten mit den Stitch-MCP-Tools generieren","Seiten in bestehende Websites integrieren","Anweisungen für nachfolgende Iterationen über Staffelübergabedateien vorbereiten"],"pt":["Geração de páginas usando as ferramentas Stitch MCP","Integração de páginas em sites existentes","Preparação de instruções para iterações subsequentes via arquivos de bastão"],"ru":["Генерация страниц с помощью инструментов Stitch MCP","Интеграция страниц в существующие сайты","Подготовка инструкций для последующих итераций через файлы эстафеты"],"ar":["إنشاء صفحات باستخدام أدوات خياطة إم سي بي","دمج الصفحات مع المواقع الحالية","إعداد الإرشادات للتعاقبات التالية من خلال ملفات العصا"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Stitch MCP tools access","Dependent on baton file system for iteration management"],"zh":["需要Stitch MCP工具的访问权限","依赖于baton文件系统进行迭代管理"],"ja":["Stitch MCPツールへのアクセスが必要","バトンファイルシステムに依存してイテレーション管理を行う"],"ko":["Stitch MCP 도구에 대한 액세스 권한이 필요함","baton 파일 시스템에 의존하여 반복 관리를 수행함"],"es":["Requiere acceso a las herramientas Stitch MCP","Dependiente del sistema de archivos de testigo para la gestión de iteraciones"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès aux outils Stitch MCP","Dépendant du système de fichiers de bâton pour la gestion des itérations"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die Stitch-MCP-Tools","Von der Staffelübergabedatei für die Iterationsverwaltung abhängig"],"pt":["Requer acesso às ferramentas Stitch MCP","Dependente do sistema de arquivos de bastão para gerenciamento de iterações"],"ru":["Требует доступа к инструментам Stitch MCP","Зависит от системы файлов эстафеты для управления итерациями"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى أدوات خياطة إم سي بي","يعتمد على نظام ملفات العصا لإدارة التعاقبات"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"db146c4fff2a52e8bae41fdf717cddbf7a075b913c4d0d82180441b9cb84c90a","repoEtag":"W/\"97396f88dec05911887e095e3b912a4db53ced027333efd2abb67102273debbc\"","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('cloudflare/skills/workers-best-practices', 'official', 'cloudflare', 'skills', 'cloudflare/skills', 'workers-best-practices', 341, 32, 80, '2026-02-23T00:27:49Z', '2026-02-23T01:07:35.525Z', '099432ff265ff6080327ef0b392c118b835d2a5bda98a7de07e1afd115ed6458', '{"id":"cloudflare/skills/workers-best-practices","name":"workers-best-practices","description":{"zh":"Cloudflare Workers 代码审查和优化，使用最新的最佳实践和API文档","ja":"Cloudflare Workers コードのレビューと最適化、最新のベストプラクティスとAPIドキュメントを使用","ko":"클라우드플레어 워커즈 코드 리뷰 및 최적화, 최신 베스트 프랙티스 및 API 문서 사용","es":"workers-best-practices es una herramienta de AI que revisa y autoriza código de Cloudflare Workers según las mejores prácticas de producción.","fr":"workers-best-practices est un outil IA qui examine et valide le code des Workers de Cloudflare selon les meilleures pratiques de production.","de":"workers-best-practices ist ein KI-Tool, das Cloudflare-Workers-Code nach Produktionsbest-Praktiken überprüft und autorisiert.","pt":"O skill workers-best-practices ajuda a garantir a qualidade e a segurança do código de Workers, fornecendo as melhores práticas para escrita e revisão","ru":"Навык workers-best-practices помогает обеспечить качество и безопасность кода Workers, предоставляя лучшие практики для написания и проверки","ar":"مهارة workers-best-practices تساعد على ضمان جودة وأمان код العاملين، بتوفير أفضل الممارسات للكتابة والمراجعة","en":"Reviews and authors Cloudflare Workers code against production best practices. Load when writing new Workers, reviewing Worker code, configuring wrangler.jsonc, or checking for common Workers anti-patterns (streaming, floating promises, global state, secrets, bindings, observability). Biases towa..."},"owner":"cloudflare","repo":"skills","repoPath":"cloudflare/skills","stars":341,"forks":32,"updatedAt":"2026-02-23T00:27:49Z","topics":["agents","cloudflare","skills","workers"],"skillMd":{"name":"workers-best-practices","description":"Reviews and authors Cloudflare Workers code against production best practices. Load when writing new Workers, reviewing Worker code, configuring wrangler.jsonc, or checking for common Workers anti-patterns (streaming, floating promises, global state, secrets, bindings, observability). Biases towards retrieval from Cloudflare docs over pre-trained knowledge.","bodyPreview":"Your knowledge of Cloudflare Workers APIs, types, and configuration may be outdated. **Prefer retrieval over pre-training** for any Workers code task — writing or reviewing.\n\n## Retrieval Sources\n\nFetch the **latest** versions before writing or reviewing Workers code. Do not rely on baked-in knowledge for API signatures, config fields, or binding shapes.\n\n| Source | How to retrieve | Use for |\n|--------|----------------|---------|\n| Workers best practices | Fetch `https://developers.cloudflare.c","body":"Your knowledge of Cloudflare Workers APIs, types, and configuration may be outdated. **Prefer retrieval over pre-training** for any Workers code task — writing or reviewing.\n\n## Retrieval Sources\n\nFetch the **latest** versions before writing or reviewing Workers code. Do not rely on baked-in knowledge for API signatures, config fields, or binding shapes.\n\n| Source | How to retrieve | Use for |\n|--------|----------------|---------|\n| Workers best practices | Fetch `https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/best-practices/workers-best-practices/` | Canonical rules, patterns, anti-patterns |\n| Workers types | See `references/review.md` for retrieval steps | API signatures, handler types, binding types |\n| Wrangler config schema | `node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json` | Config fields, binding shapes, allowed values |\n| Cloudflare docs | Search tool or `https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/` | API reference, compatibility dates/flags |\n\n## FIRST: Fetch Latest References\n\nBefore reviewing or writing Workers code, retrieve the current best practices page and relevant type definitions. If the project''s `node_modules` has an older version, **prefer the latest published version**.\n\n```bash\n# Fetch latest workers types\nmkdir -p /tmp/workers-types-latest && \\\n  npm pack @cloudflare/workers-types --pack-destination /tmp/workers-types-latest && \\\n  tar -xzf /tmp/workers-types-latest/cloudflare-workers-types-*.tgz -C /tmp/workers-types-latest\n# Types at /tmp/workers-types-latest/package/index.d.ts\n```\n\n## Reference Documentation\n\n- `references/rules.md` — all best practice rules with code examples and anti-patterns\n- `references/review.md` — type validation, config validation, binding access patterns, review process\n\n## Rules Quick Reference\n\n### Configuration\n\n| Rule | Summary |\n|------|---------|\n| Compatibility date | Set `compatibility_date` to today on new projects; update periodically on existing ones |\n| nodejs_compat | Enable the `nodejs_compat` flag — many libraries depend on Node.js built-ins |\n| wrangler types | Run `wrangler types` to generate `Env` — never hand-write binding interfaces |\n| Secrets | Use `wrangler secret put`, never hardcode secrets in config or source |\n| wrangler.jsonc | Use JSONC config for non-secret settings — newer features are JSON-only |\n\n### Request & Response Handling\n\n| Rule | Summary |\n|------|---------|\n| Streaming | Stream large/unknown payloads — never `await response.text()` on unbounded data |\n| waitUntil | Use `ctx.waitUntil()` for post-response work; do not destructure `ctx` |\n\n### Architecture\n\n| Rule | Summary |\n|------|---------|\n| Bindings over REST | Use in-process bindings (KV, R2, D1, Queues) — not the Cloudflare REST API |\n| Queues & Workflows | Move async/background work off the critical path |\n| Service bindings | Use service bindings for Worker-to-Worker calls — not public HTTP |\n| Hyperdrive | Always use Hyperdrive for external PostgreSQL/MySQL connections |\n\n### Observability\n\n| Rule | Summary |\n|------|---------|\n| Logs & Traces | Enable `observability` in config with `head_sampling_rate`; use structured JSON logging |\n\n### Code Patterns\n\n| Rule | Summary |\n|------|---------|\n| No global request state | Never store request-scoped data in module-level variables |\n| Floating promises | Every Promise must be `await`ed, `return`ed, `void`ed, or passed to `ctx.waitUntil()` |\n\n### Security\n\n| Rule | Summary |\n|------|---------|\n| Web Crypto | Use `crypto.randomUUID()` / `crypto.getRandomValues()` — never `Math.random()` for security |\n| No passThroughOnException | Use explicit try/catch with structured error responses |\n\n## Anti-Patterns to Flag\n\n| Anti-pattern | Why it matters |\n|-------------|----------------|\n| `await response.text()` on unbounded data | Memory exhaustion — 128 MB limit |\n| Hardcoded secrets in source or config | Credential leak via version control |\n| `Math.random()` for tokens/IDs | Predictable, not cryptographically secure |\n| Bare `fetch()` without `await` or `waitUntil` | Floating promise — dropped result, swallowed error |\n| Module-level mutable variables for request state | Cross-request data leaks, stale state, I/O errors |\n| Cloudflare REST API from inside a Worker | Unnecessary network hop, auth overhead, added latency |\n| `ctx.passThroughOnException()` as error handling | Hides bugs, makes debugging impossible |\n| Hand-written `Env` interface | Drifts from actual wrangler config bindings |\n| Direct string comparison for secret values | Timing side-channel — use `crypto.subtle.timingSafeEqual` |\n| Destructuring `ctx` (`const { waitUntil } = ctx`) | Loses `this` binding — throws \"Illegal invocation\" at runtime |\n| `any` on `Env` or handler params | Defeats type safety for all binding access |\n| `as unknown as T` double-cast | Hides real type incompatibilities — fix the design |\n| `implements` on platform base classes (instead of `extends`) | Legacy — loses `this.ctx`, `this.env`. Applies to DurableObject, WorkerEntrypoint, Workflow |\n| `env.X` inside platform base class | Should be `this.env.X` in classes extending DurableObject, WorkerEntrypoint, etc. |\n\n## Review Workflow\n\n1. **Retrieve** — fetch latest best practices page, workers types, and wrangler schema\n2. **Read full files** — not just diffs; context matters for binding access patterns\n3. **Check types** — binding access, handler signatures, no `any`, no unsafe casts (see `references/review.md`)\n4. **Check config** — compatibility_date, nodejs_compat, observability, secrets, binding-code consistency\n5. **Check patterns** — streaming, floating promises, global state, serialization boundaries\n6. **Check security** — crypto usage, secret handling, timing-safe comparisons, error handling\n7. **Validate with tools** — `npx tsc --noEmit`, lint for `no-floating-promises`\n8. **Reference rules** — see `references/rules.md` for each rule''s correct pattern\n\n## Scope\n\nThis skill covers Workers-specific best practices and code review. For related topics:\n\n- **Durable Objects**: load the `durable-objects` skill\n- **Workflows**: see [Rules of Workflows](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/rules-of-workflows/)\n- **Wrangler CLI commands**: load the `wrangler` skill\n\n## Principles\n\n- **Be certain.** Retrieve before flagging. If unsure about an API, config field, or pattern, fetch the docs first.\n- **Provide evidence.** Reference line numbers, tool output, or docs links.\n- **Focus on what developers will copy.** Workers code in examples and docs gets pasted into production.\n- **Correctness over completeness.** A concise example that works beats a comprehensive one with errors.\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-23T01:07:35.525Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理：Cloudflare Workers 最佳实践","ja":"AIエージェント：Cloudflare Workers ベストプラクティス","ko":"AI 에이전트: 클라우드플레어 워커즈 최적화","es":"Herramientas de AI: workers-best-practices para Desarroll...","fr":"Outils IA : workers-best-practices pour les Développeurs","de":"KI-Tools: workers-best-practices für Entwickler","pt":"Ferramentas de IA para Melhores Práticas de Workers","ru":"ИИ Агенты для Лучших Практик Workers","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي لأفضل الممارسات للعاملين","en":"workers-best-practices"},"description":{"zh":"Cloudflare Workers 代码审查和优化，使用最新的最佳实践和API文档","ja":"Cloudflare Workers コードのレビューと最適化、最新のベストプラクティスとAPIドキュメントを使用","ko":"클라우드플레어 워커즈 코드 리뷰 및 최적화, 최신 베스트 프랙티스 및 API 문서 사용","es":"workers-best-practices es una herramienta de AI que revisa y autoriza código de Cloudflare Workers según las mejores prácticas de producción.","fr":"workers-best-practices est un outil IA qui examine et valide le code des Workers de Cloudflare selon les meilleures pratiques de production.","de":"workers-best-practices ist ein KI-Tool, das Cloudflare-Workers-Code nach Produktionsbest-Praktiken überprüft und autorisiert.","pt":"O skill workers-best-practices ajuda a garantir a qualidade e a segurança do código de Workers, fornecendo as melhores práticas para escrita e revisão","ru":"Навык workers-best-practices помогает обеспечить качество и безопасность кода Workers, предоставляя лучшие практики для написания и проверки","ar":"مهارة workers-best-practices تساعد على ضمان جودة وأمان код العاملين، بتوفير أفضل الممارسات للكتابة والمراجعة","en":"Reviews and authors Cloudflare Workers code against production best practices. Load when writing new Workers, reviewing Worker code, configuring wrangler.jso..."},"definition":{"en":"Reviews and authors Cloudflare Workers code against production best practices. Load when writing new Workers, reviewing Worker code, configuring wrangler.jsonc, or checking for common Workers anti-patterns (streaming, floating promises, global state, secrets, bindings, observability). Biases towards retrieval from Cloudflare docs over pre-trained knowledge."},"features":{"zh":["代码审查和优化","使用最新的API文档","检测常见的反模式","支持配置wrangler.jsonc","提高代码质量和性能"],"ja":["コードのレビューと最適化","最新のAPIドキュメントを使用","一般的なアンチパターンの検出","wrangler.jsoncの設定をサポート","コード品質とパフォーマンスの向上"],"ko":["코드 리뷰 및 최적화","최신 API 문서 사용","일반적인 안티패턴 감지","wrangler.jsonc 설정 지원","코드 품질 및 성능 개선"],"es":["Revisión de código de Cloudflare Workers","Autorización de código según mejores prácticas de producción","Integración con Cloudflare Docs","Detección de patrones anti-Workers comunes","Optimización de rendimiento y seguridad"],"fr":["Examen de code des Workers de Cloudflare","Validation de code selon les meilleures pratiques de production","Intégration avec Cloudflare Docs","Détection de modèles anti-Workers courants","Optimisation des performances et de la sécurité"],"de":["Überprüfung von Cloudflare-Workers-Code","Autorisierung von Code nach Produktionsbest-Praktiken","Integration mit Cloudflare Docs","Erkennung von gängigen Anti-Workers-Mustern","Optimierung von Leistung und Sicherheit"],"pt":["Análise de código de Workers","Verificação de segurança","Melhores práticas para escrita e revisão","Integração com a documentação da Cloudflare","Suporte à configuração do wrangler.jsonc"],"ru":["Анализ кода Workers","Проверка безопасности","Лучшие практики для написания и проверки","Интеграция с документацией Cloudflare","Поддержка конфигурации wrangler.jsonc"],"ar":["تحليل код العاملين","فحص الأمان","أفضل الممارسات للكتابة والمراجعة","التكامل مع وثائق كلاود فلير","دعم تكوين wrangler.jsonc"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Cloudflare Workers","AI智能代理","代码审查","代码优化","API文档","wrangler.jsonc"],"ja":["Cloudflare Workers","AIエージェント","コードのレビュー","コードの最適化","APIドキュメント","wrangler.jsonc"],"ko":["클라우드플레어 워커즈","AI 에이전트","코드 리뷰","코드 최적화","API 문서","wrangler.jsonc"],"es":["herramientas de AI","Cloudflare Workers","mejores prácticas de producción","desarrollo de software","optimización de código","seguridad de código"],"fr":["outils IA","Workers de Cloudflare","meilleures pratiques de production","développement de logiciels","optimisation de code","sécurité de code"],"de":["KI-Tools","Cloudflare Workers","Produktionsbest-Praktiken","Software-Entwicklung","Code-Optimierung","Code-Sicherheit"],"pt":["ferramentas de ia para desenvolvedores","melhores práticas para workers","segurança de código","cloudflare workers","wrangler jsonc","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["ии агенты для разработчиков","лучшие практики для workers","безопасность кода","cloudflare workers","wrangler jsonc","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين","أفضل الممارسات للعاملين","أمان الكود","كلاود فلير العاملين","wrangler jsonc","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Cloudflare-focused AI Agents needing expertise in Workers code review and best practices implementation.","zh":"适用于需要在 Workers 代码审查和最佳实践实施方面具有专长的 Cloudflare 专注的 AI Agent。","ja":"Cloudflare に焦点を当てた AI エージェントが Workers コードのレビューとベストプラクティスの実装に関する専門知識を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"Cloudflare에 중점을 둔 AI 에이전트가 Workers 코드 리뷰 및 최선의 실践 구현에 대한 전문 지식을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de inteligencia artificial de Cloudflare que necesitan experiencia en revisión de código de Workers y implementación de mejores prácticas.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''intelligence artificielle de Cloudflare qui ont besoin d''expertise dans la révision de code de Workers et la mise en œuvre de meilleures pratiques.","de":"Ideal für Cloudflare-AI-Agents, die Erfahrung in der Überprüfung von Workers-Code und der Implementierung von Best Practices benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA focados em Cloudflare que necessitam de especialização em revisão de código de Workers e implementação de melhores práticas.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, ориентированных на Cloudflare, которым требуется экспертиза в области обзора кода Workers и реализации лучших практик.","ar":"مثالي لعميلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يركزون على Cloudflare و الذين يحتاجون إلى الخبرة في مراجعة رمز Workers وتنفيذ أفضل الممارسات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to review and author Cloudflare Workers code against production best practices, leveraging retrieval from Cloudflare docs for the latest API signatures, config fields, and binding shapes, and checking for anti-patterns like streaming, floating promises, and global state.","zh":"赋予代理审查和编写 Cloudflare Workers 代码的能力，以便于生产中的最佳实践，利用从 Cloudflare 文档中检索最新的 API 签名、配置字段和绑定形状，并检查诸如流媒体、浮动承诺和全局状态等反模式。","ja":"エージェントに、Cloudflare Workers コードをレビューし、ベストプラクティスに従ってコードを書く能力を付与し、Cloudflare ドキュメントから最新の API シグネチャ、構成フィールド、バインディング シェイプを取得し、ストリーミング、浮動プロミス、グローバル状態などのアンチパターンをチェックします。","ko":"에이전트가 생산 환경에서 최선의 실践을 준수하도록 Cloudflare Workers 코드를 검토하고 작성할 수 있는 능력을 부여하고, Cloudflare 문서에서 최신 API 서명, 구성 필드 및 바인딩 형태를 가져와 스트리밍, 浮動 프로미스, 전역 상태와 같은 반 패턴을 확인합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes revisar y crear código de Cloudflare Workers contra las mejores prácticas de producción, aprovechando la recuperación de la documentación de Cloudflare para las últimas firmas de API, campos de configuración y formas de enlace, y comprobando anti-patrones como streaming, promesas flotantes y estado global.","fr":"Permet aux agents de réviser et de créer du code de Cloudflare Workers contre les meilleures pratiques de production, en exploitant la récupération de la documentation de Cloudflare pour les dernières signatures d''API, les champs de configuration et les formes de liaison, et en vérifiant les anti-patrons tels que le streaming, les promesses flottantes et l''état global.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Cloudflare-Workers-Code gegen Produktionsbest-Practices zu überprüfen und zu verfassen, indem es die Abrufung der Cloudflare-Dokumentation für die neuesten API-Signaturen, Konfigurationsfelder und Bindungsformen nutzt und Anti-Muster wie Streaming, schwimmende Versprechen und globalen Zustand überprüft.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a revisar e criar código de Cloudflare Workers contra as melhores práticas de produção, aproveitando a recuperação dos documentos da Cloudflare para as assinaturas de API mais recentes, campos de configuração e formas de ligação, e verificando anti-padrões como streaming, promessas flutuantes e estado global.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проверять и создавать код Cloudflare Workers в соответствии с лучшими практиками производства, используя получение документов Cloudflare для последних подписей API, полей конфигурации и форм привязки, а также проверку анти-шаблонов, таких как потоковая передача, плавающие обещания и глобальное состояние.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من مراجعة ونشر رمز Cloudflare Workers ضد أفضل الممارسات الإنتاجية، واستخدام استرجاع وثائق Cloudflare لأحدث التوقيعات API، وحقول التكوين، واشكال الربط، وفحص أنماط مضادة مثل البث، والوعود العائمة، والحالة العالمية."},"useCases":{"en":["Reviewing Worker code for adherence to best practices","Configuring wrangler.jsonc for optimal Workers performance","Detecting common Workers anti-patterns such as secrets, bindings, and observability issues"],"zh":["审查 Worker 代码以确保遵守最佳实践","配置 wrangler.jsonc 以实现 Workers 的最佳性能","检测常见的 Workers 反模式，例如机密、绑定和可观察性问题"],"ja":["ベストプラクティスに従った Worker コードのレビュー","wrangler.jsonc の構成による Workers のパフォーマンスの最適化","シークレット、バインディング、観測可能性の問題などの一般的な Workers のアンチパターンの検出"],"ko":["최선의 실践을 준수하도록 워커 코드를 검토하는 것","wrangler.jsonc를 구성하여 워커의 최적의 성능을 달성하는 것","비밀, 바인딩, 관측 가능성 문제와 같은 일반적인 워커의 반 패턴을 감지하는 것"],"es":["Revisar el código de Worker para el cumplimiento de las mejores prácticas","Configurar wrangler.jsonc para un rendimiento óptimo de Workers","Detectar anti-patrones comunes de Workers como secretos, enlaces y problemas de observabilidad"],"fr":["Réviser le code de Worker pour le respect des meilleures pratiques","Configurer wrangler.jsonc pour une performance optimale de Workers","Déceler les anti-patrons courants de Workers tels que les secrets, les liens et les problèmes d''observabilité"],"de":["Überprüfen des Worker-Codes auf Einhaltung von Best-Practices","Konfigurieren von wrangler.jsonc für optimale Workers-Leistung","Erkennen von häufigen Workers-Anti-Mustern wie Geheimnissen, Bindungen und Beobachtbarkeitsproblemen"],"pt":["Revisar o código do Worker para aderência às melhores práticas","Configurar o wrangler.jsonc para o desempenho ótimo dos Workers","Detectar anti-padrões comuns dos Workers, como segredos, ligações e problemas de observabilidade"],"ru":["Проверка кода Worker на соблюдение лучших практик","Настройка wrangler.jsonc для оптимальной производительности Workers","Обнаружение общих анти-шаблонов Workers, таких как секреты, привязки и проблемы наблюдаемости"],"ar":["مراجعة رمز Worker لتطبيق أفضل الممارسات","تكوين wrangler.jsonc لأداء Workers الأمثل","كشف أنماط مضادة شائعة في Workers، مثل الأسرار والربط وقضايا المراقبة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires internet access for retrieval of latest Cloudflare Workers documentation","Biases towards Cloudflare documentation over pre-trained knowledge","Specific to Cloudflare Workers, not applicable to other serverless platforms"],"zh":["需要互联网访问以检索最新的 Cloudflare Workers 文档","偏向 Cloudflare 文档而非预先训练的知识","仅适用于 Cloudflare Workers，不适用于其他无服务器平台"],"ja":["最新の Cloudflare Workers ドキュメントの取得のためにインターネットアクセスが必要","事前にトレーニングされた知識よりも Cloudflare ドキュメントを優先する","Cloudflare Workers 専用であり、他のサーバーレス プラットフォームには適用されない"],"ko":["최신 Cloudflare Workers 문서를 가져오기 위해 인터넷 액세스가 필요함","사전 교육된 지식보다 Cloudflare 문서를 우선함","Cloudflare Workers에만 적용되며, 다른 서버리스 플랫폼에는 적용되지 않음"],"es":["Requiere acceso a Internet para la recuperación de la documentación más reciente de Cloudflare Workers","Sesgo hacia la documentación de Cloudflare sobre el conocimiento preentrenado","Específico para Cloudflare Workers, no aplicable a otras plataformas sin servidor"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à Internet pour la récupération de la documentation la plus récente de Cloudflare Workers","Biais vers la documentation de Cloudflare plutôt que vers les connaissances préentraînées","Spécifique à Cloudflare Workers, non applicable à d''autres plateformes sans serveur"],"de":["Benötigt Internetzugang für die Abrufung der neuesten Cloudflare-Workers-Dokumentation","Voreingenommen gegenüber der Cloudflare-Dokumentation gegenüber dem vorgefertigten Wissen","Spezifisch für Cloudflare-Workers, nicht anwendbar auf andere serverlose Plattformen"],"pt":["Requer acesso à internet para recuperação da documentação mais recente do Cloudflare Workers","Tende a favorecer a documentação da Cloudflare em detrimento do conhecimento pré-treinado","Específico para Cloudflare Workers, não se aplica a outras plataformas sem servidor"],"ru":["Требует доступа к интернету для получения последней документации Cloudflare Workers","Имеет偏ление в сторону документации Cloudflare по сравнению с предварительно обученным знанием","Конкретно предназначен для Cloudflare Workers, не применим к другим безсерверным платформам"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى الإنترنت لاسترجاع أحدث وثائق Cloudflare Workers","يميل إلى التوجيه نحو وثائق Cloudflare على حساب المعرفة المسبقة","محدد لعميلاء Cloudflare Workers، لا ينطبق على منصات خادمة أخرى"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"099432ff265ff6080327ef0b392c118b835d2a5bda98a7de07e1afd115ed6458","repoEtag":"W/\"d80154fd9ed8586078af8bf4b067aaef85c0af6b0931f4dceda13fbdd08d77f7\"","qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('cloudflare/skills/wrangler', 'official', 'cloudflare', 'skills', 'cloudflare/skills', 'wrangler', 341, 32, 80, '2026-02-23T00:27:49Z', '2026-02-23T01:07:35.605Z', 'b1192e4c6701de164c48f44bb9cf6ccba92070ae2873c8beca00a6aadc64b750', '{"id":"cloudflare/skills/wrangler","name":"wrangler","description":{"zh":"Wrangler是Cloudflare Workers的CLI工具，用于部署、开发和管理Workers和相关资源","ja":"WranglerはCloudflare WorkersのCLIツールで、Workersと関連リソースのデプロイ、開発、管理に使用されます","ko":"Wrangler는 Cloudflare Workers의 CLI 도구로서 Workers와 관련 리소스의 배포, 개발, 관리에 사용됩니다","es":"Wrangler CLI es una herramienta de línea de comandos para Cloudflare Workers que facilita el deploy, desarrollo y manejo de Workers y recursos asociados.","fr":"Wrangler CLI est un outil de ligne de commande pour Cloudflare Workers qui facilite le déploiement, le développement et la gestion de Workers et ressources associées.","de":"Wrangler CLI ist ein Kommandozeilen-Tool für Cloudflare Workers, das die Bereitstellung, Entwicklung und Verwaltung von Workers und zugehörigen Ressourcen erleichtert.","pt":"O Wrangler CLI é uma ferramenta para deploy, desenvolvimento e gerenciamento de Cloudflare Workers e recursos associados","ru":"Wrangler CLI - это инструмент для развертывания, разработки и управления Cloudflare Workers и связанных ресурсов","ar":"Wrangler CLI هو أداة لتنفيذ وتطوير وإدارة Cloudflare Workers والموارد المرتبطة بها","en":"Cloudflare Workers CLI for deploying, developing, and managing Workers, KV, R2, D1, Vectorize, Hyperdrive, Workers AI, Containers, Queues, Workflows, Pipelines, and Secrets Store. Load before running wrangler commands to ensure correct syntax and best practices."},"owner":"cloudflare","repo":"skills","repoPath":"cloudflare/skills","stars":341,"forks":32,"updatedAt":"2026-02-23T00:27:49Z","topics":["agents","cloudflare","skills","workers"],"skillMd":{"name":"wrangler","description":"Cloudflare Workers CLI for deploying, developing, and managing Workers, KV, R2, D1, Vectorize, Hyperdrive, Workers AI, Containers, Queues, Workflows, Pipelines, and Secrets Store. Load before running wrangler commands to ensure correct syntax and best practices.","bodyPreview":"# Wrangler CLI\n\nDeploy, develop, and manage Cloudflare Workers and associated resources.\n\n## FIRST: Verify Wrangler Installation\n\n```bash\nwrangler --version  # Requires v4.x+\n```\n\nIf not installed:\n```bash\nnpm install -D wrangler@latest\n```\n\n## Key Guidelines\n\n- **Use `wrangler.jsonc`**: Prefer JSON config over TOML. Newer features are JSON-only.\n- **Set `compatibility_date`**: Use a recent date (within 30 days). Check https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/compatibility-dates/","body":"# Wrangler CLI\n\nDeploy, develop, and manage Cloudflare Workers and associated resources.\n\n## FIRST: Verify Wrangler Installation\n\n```bash\nwrangler --version  # Requires v4.x+\n```\n\nIf not installed:\n```bash\nnpm install -D wrangler@latest\n```\n\n## Key Guidelines\n\n- **Use `wrangler.jsonc`**: Prefer JSON config over TOML. Newer features are JSON-only.\n- **Set `compatibility_date`**: Use a recent date (within 30 days). Check https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/compatibility-dates/\n- **Generate types after config changes**: Run `wrangler types` to update TypeScript bindings.\n- **Local dev defaults to local storage**: Bindings use local simulation unless `remote: true`.\n- **Validate config before deploy**: Run `wrangler check` to catch errors early.\n- **Use environments for staging/prod**: Define `env.staging` and `env.production` in config.\n\n## Quick Start: New Worker\n\n```bash\n# Initialize new project\nnpx wrangler init my-worker\n\n# Or with a framework\nnpx create-cloudflare@latest my-app\n```\n\n## Quick Reference: Core Commands\n\n| Task | Command |\n|------|---------|\n| Start local dev server | `wrangler dev` |\n| Deploy to Cloudflare | `wrangler deploy` |\n| Deploy dry run | `wrangler deploy --dry-run` |\n| Generate TypeScript types | `wrangler types` |\n| Validate configuration | `wrangler check` |\n| View live logs | `wrangler tail` |\n| Delete Worker | `wrangler delete` |\n| Auth status | `wrangler whoami` |\n\n---\n\n## Configuration (wrangler.jsonc)\n\n### Minimal Config\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"./node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json\",\n  \"name\": \"my-worker\",\n  \"main\": \"src/index.ts\",\n  \"compatibility_date\": \"2026-01-01\"\n}\n```\n\n### Full Config with Bindings\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"./node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json\",\n  \"name\": \"my-worker\",\n  \"main\": \"src/index.ts\",\n  \"compatibility_date\": \"2026-01-01\",\n  \"compatibility_flags\": [\"nodejs_compat_v2\"],\n\n  // Environment variables\n  \"vars\": {\n    \"ENVIRONMENT\": \"production\"\n  },\n\n  // KV Namespace\n  \"kv_namespaces\": [\n    { \"binding\": \"KV\", \"id\": \"<KV_NAMESPACE_ID>\" }\n  ],\n\n  // R2 Bucket\n  \"r2_buckets\": [\n    { \"binding\": \"BUCKET\", \"bucket_name\": \"my-bucket\" }\n  ],\n\n  // D1 Database\n  \"d1_databases\": [\n    { \"binding\": \"DB\", \"database_name\": \"my-db\", \"database_id\": \"<DB_ID>\" }\n  ],\n\n  // Workers AI (always remote)\n  \"ai\": { \"binding\": \"AI\" },\n\n  // Vectorize\n  \"vectorize\": [\n    { \"binding\": \"VECTOR_INDEX\", \"index_name\": \"my-index\" }\n  ],\n\n  // Hyperdrive\n  \"hyperdrive\": [\n    { \"binding\": \"HYPERDRIVE\", \"id\": \"<HYPERDRIVE_ID>\" }\n  ],\n\n  // Durable Objects\n  \"durable_objects\": {\n    \"bindings\": [\n      { \"name\": \"COUNTER\", \"class_name\": \"Counter\" }\n    ]\n  },\n\n  // Cron triggers\n  \"triggers\": {\n    \"crons\": [\"0 * * * *\"]\n  },\n\n  // Environments\n  \"env\": {\n    \"staging\": {\n      \"name\": \"my-worker-staging\",\n      \"vars\": { \"ENVIRONMENT\": \"staging\" }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Generate Types from Config\n\n```bash\n# Generate worker-configuration.d.ts\nwrangler types\n\n# Custom output path\nwrangler types ./src/env.d.ts\n\n# Check types are up to date (CI)\nwrangler types --check\n```\n\n---\n\n## Local Development\n\n### Start Dev Server\n\n```bash\n# Local mode (default) - uses local storage simulation\nwrangler dev\n\n# With specific environment\nwrangler dev --env staging\n\n# Force local-only (disable remote bindings)\nwrangler dev --local\n\n# Remote mode - runs on Cloudflare edge (legacy)\nwrangler dev --remote\n\n# Custom port\nwrangler dev --port 8787\n\n# Live reload for HTML changes\nwrangler dev --live-reload\n\n# Test scheduled/cron handlers\nwrangler dev --test-scheduled\n# Then visit: http://localhost:8787/__scheduled\n```\n\n### Remote Bindings for Local Dev\n\nUse `remote: true` in binding config to connect to real resources while running locally:\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"r2_buckets\": [\n    { \"binding\": \"BUCKET\", \"bucket_name\": \"my-bucket\", \"remote\": true }\n  ],\n  \"ai\": { \"binding\": \"AI\", \"remote\": true },\n  \"vectorize\": [\n    { \"binding\": \"INDEX\", \"index_name\": \"my-index\", \"remote\": true }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Recommended remote bindings**: AI (required), Vectorize, Browser Rendering, mTLS, Images.\n\n### Local Secrets\n\nCreate `.dev.vars` for local development secrets:\n\n```\nAPI_KEY=local-dev-key\nDATABASE_URL=postgres://localhost:5432/dev\n```\n\n---\n\n## Deployment\n\n### Deploy Worker\n\n```bash\n# Deploy to production\nwrangler deploy\n\n# Deploy specific environment\nwrangler deploy --env staging\n\n# Dry run (validate without deploying)\nwrangler deploy --dry-run\n\n# Keep dashboard-set variables\nwrangler deploy --keep-vars\n\n# Minify code\nwrangler deploy --minify\n```\n\n### Manage Secrets\n\n```bash\n# Set secret interactively\nwrangler secret put API_KEY\n\n# Set from stdin\necho \"secret-value\" | wrangler secret put API_KEY\n\n# List secrets\nwrangler secret list\n\n# Delete secret\nwrangler secret delete API_KEY\n\n# Bulk secrets from JSON file\nwrangler secret bulk secrets.json\n```\n\n### Versions and Rollback\n\n```bash\n# List recent versions\nwrangler versions list\n\n# View specific version\nwrangler versions view <VERSION_ID>\n\n# Rollback to previous version\nwrangler rollback\n\n# Rollback to specific version\nwrangler rollback <VERSION_ID>\n```\n\n---\n\n## KV (Key-Value Store)\n\n### Manage Namespaces\n\n```bash\n# Create namespace\nwrangler kv namespace create MY_KV\n\n# List namespaces\nwrangler kv namespace list\n\n# Delete namespace\nwrangler kv namespace delete --namespace-id <ID>\n```\n\n### Manage Keys\n\n```bash\n# Put value\nwrangler kv key put --namespace-id <ID> \"key\" \"value\"\n\n# Put with expiration (seconds)\nwrangler kv key put --namespace-id <ID> \"key\" \"value\" --expiration-ttl 3600\n\n# Get value\nwrangler kv key get --namespace-id <ID> \"key\"\n\n# List keys\nwrangler kv key list --namespace-id <ID>\n\n# Delete key\nwrangler kv key delete --namespace-id <ID> \"key\"\n\n# Bulk put from JSON\nwrangler kv bulk put --namespace-id <ID> data.json\n```\n\n### Config Binding\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"kv_namespaces\": [\n    { \"binding\": \"CACHE\", \"id\": \"<NAMESPACE_ID>\" }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## R2 (Object Storage)\n\n### Manage Buckets\n\n```bash\n# Create bucket\nwrangler r2 bucket create my-bucket\n\n# Create with location hint\nwrangler r2 bucket create my-bucket --location wnam\n\n# List buckets\nwrangler r2 bucket list\n\n# Get bucket info\nwrangler r2 bucket info my-bucket\n\n# Delete bucket\nwrangler r2 bucket delete my-bucket\n```\n\n### Manage Objects\n\n```bash\n# Upload object\nwrangler r2 object put my-bucket/path/file.txt --file ./local-file.txt\n\n# Download object\nwrangler r2 object get my-bucket/path/file.txt\n\n# Delete object\nwrangler r2 object delete my-bucket/path/file.txt\n```\n\n### Config Binding\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"r2_buckets\": [\n    { \"binding\": \"ASSETS\", \"bucket_name\": \"my-bucket\" }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## D1 (SQL Database)\n\n### Manage Databases\n\n```bash\n# Create database\nwrangler d1 create my-database\n\n# Create with location\nwrangler d1 create my-database --location wnam\n\n# List databases\nwrangler d1 list\n\n# Get database info\nwrangler d1 info my-database\n\n# Delete database\nwrangler d1 delete my-database\n```\n\n### Execute SQL\n\n```bash\n# Execute SQL command (remote)\nwrangler d1 execute my-database --remote --command \"SELECT * FROM users\"\n\n# Execute SQL file (remote)\nwrangler d1 execute my-database --remote --file ./schema.sql\n\n# Execute locally\nwrangler d1 execute my-database --local --command \"SELECT * FROM users\"\n```\n\n### Migrations\n\n```bash\n# Create migration\nwrangler d1 migrations create my-database create_users_table\n\n# List pending migrations\nwrangler d1 migrations list my-database --local\n\n# Apply migrations locally\nwrangler d1 migrations apply my-database --local\n\n# Apply migrations to remote\nwrangler d1 migrations apply my-database --remote\n```\n\n### Export/Backup\n\n```bash\n# Export schema and data\nwrangler d1 export my-database --remote --output backup.sql\n\n# Export schema only\nwrangler d1 export my-database --remote --output schema.sql --no-data\n```\n\n### Config Binding\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"d1_databases\": [\n    {\n      \"binding\": \"DB\",\n      \"database_name\": \"my-database\",\n      \"database_id\": \"<DATABASE_ID>\",\n      \"migrations_dir\": \"./migrations\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Vectorize (Vector Database)\n\n### Manage Indexes\n\n```bash\n# Create index with dimensions\nwrangler vectorize create my-index --dimensions 768 --metric cosine\n\n# Create with preset (auto-configures dimensions/metric)\nwrangler vectorize create my-index --preset @cf/baai/bge-base-en-v1.5\n\n# List indexes\nwrangler vectorize list\n\n# Get index info\nwrangler vectorize get my-index\n\n# Delete index\nwrangler vectorize delete my-index\n```\n\n### Manage Vectors\n\n```bash\n# Insert vectors from NDJSON file\nwrangler vectorize insert my-index --file vectors.ndjson\n\n# Query vectors\nwrangler vectorize query my-index --vector \"[0.1, 0.2, ...]\" --top-k 10\n```\n\n### Config Binding\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"vectorize\": [\n    { \"binding\": \"SEARCH_INDEX\", \"index_name\": \"my-index\" }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Hyperdrive (Database Accelerator)\n\n### Manage Configs\n\n```bash\n# Create config\nwrangler hyperdrive create my-hyperdrive \\\n  --connection-string \"postgres://user:pass@host:5432/database\"\n\n# List configs\nwrangler hyperdrive list\n\n# Get config details\nwrangler hyperdrive get <HYPERDRIVE_ID>\n\n# Update config\nwrangler hyperdrive update <HYPERDRIVE_ID> --origin-password \"new-password\"\n\n# Delete config\nwrangler hyperdrive delete <HYPERDRIVE_ID>\n```\n\n### Config Binding\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"compatibility_flags\": [\"nodejs_compat_v2\"],\n  \"hyperdrive\": [\n    { \"binding\": \"HYPERDRIVE\", \"id\": \"<HYPERDRIVE_ID>\" }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Workers AI\n\n### List Models\n\n```bash\n# List available models\nwrangler ai models\n\n# List finetunes\nwrangler ai finetune list\n```\n\n### Config Binding\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"ai\": { \"binding\": \"AI\" }\n}\n```\n\n**Note**: Workers AI always runs remotely and incurs usage charges even in local dev.\n\n---\n\n## Queues\n\n### Manage Queues\n\n```bash\n# Create queue\nwrangler queues create my-queue\n\n# List queues\nwrangler queues list\n\n# Delete queue\nwrangler queues delete my-queue\n\n# Add consumer to queue\nwrangler queues consumer add my-queue my-worker\n\n# Remove consumer\nwrangler queues consumer remove my-queue my-worker\n```\n\n### Config Binding\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"queues\": {\n    \"producers\": [\n      { \"binding\": \"MY_QUEUE\", \"queue\": \"my-queue\" }\n    ],\n    \"consumers\": [\n      {\n        \"queue\": \"my-queue\",\n        \"max_batch_size\": 10,\n        \"max_batch_timeout\": 30\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Containers\n\n### Build and Push Images\n\n```bash\n# Build container image\nwrangler containers build -t my-app:latest .\n\n# Build and push in one command\nwrangler containers build -t my-app:latest . --push\n\n# Push existing image to Cloudflare registry\nwrangler containers push my-app:latest\n```\n\n### Manage Containers\n\n```bash\n# List containers\nwrangler containers list\n\n# Get container info\nwrangler containers info <CONTAINER_ID>\n\n# Delete container\nwrangler containers delete <CONTAINER_ID>\n```\n\n### Manage Images\n\n```bash\n# List images in registry\nwrangler containers images list\n\n# Delete image\nwrangler containers images delete my-app:latest\n```\n\n### Manage External Registries\n\n```bash\n# List configured registries\nwrangler containers registries list\n\n# Configure external registry (e.g., ECR)\nwrangler containers registries configure <DOMAIN> \\\n  --public-credential <AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID>\n\n# Delete registry configuration\nwrangler containers registries delete <DOMAIN>\n```\n\n---\n\n## Workflows\n\n### Manage Workflows\n\n```bash\n# List workflows\nwrangler workflows list\n\n# Describe workflow\nwrangler workflows describe my-workflow\n\n# Trigger workflow instance\nwrangler workflows trigger my-workflow\n\n# Trigger with parameters\nwrangler workflows trigger my-workflow --params ''{\"key\": \"value\"}''\n\n# Delete workflow\nwrangler workflows delete my-workflow\n```\n\n### Manage Workflow Instances\n\n```bash\n# List instances\nwrangler workflows instances list my-workflow\n\n# Describe instance\nwrangler workflows instances describe my-workflow <INSTANCE_ID>\n\n# Terminate instance\nwrangler workflows instances terminate my-workflow <INSTANCE_ID>\n```\n\n### Config Binding\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"workflows\": [\n    {\n      \"binding\": \"MY_WORKFLOW\",\n      \"name\": \"my-workflow\",\n      \"class_name\": \"MyWorkflow\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Pipelines\n\n### Manage Pipelines\n\n```bash\n# Create pipeline\nwrangler pipelines create my-pipeline --r2 my-bucket\n\n# List pipelines\nwrangler pipelines list\n\n# Show pipeline details\nwrangler pipelines show my-pipeline\n\n# Update pipeline\nwrangler pipelines update my-pipeline --batch-max-mb 100\n\n# Delete pipeline\nwrangler pipelines delete my-pipeline\n```\n\n### Config Binding\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"pipelines\": [\n    { \"binding\": \"MY_PIPELINE\", \"pipeline\": \"my-pipeline\" }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Secrets Store\n\n### Manage Stores\n\n```bash\n# Create store\nwrangler secrets-store store create my-store\n\n# List stores\nwrangler secrets-store store list\n\n# Delete store\nwrangler secrets-store store delete <STORE_ID>\n```\n\n### Manage Secrets in Store\n\n```bash\n# Add secret to store\nwrangler secrets-store secret put <STORE_ID> my-secret\n\n# List secrets in store\nwrangler secrets-store secret list <STORE_ID>\n\n# Get secret\nwrangler secrets-store secret get <STORE_ID> my-secret\n\n# Delete secret from store\nwrangler secrets-store secret delete <STORE_ID> my-secret\n```\n\n### Config Binding\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"secrets_store_secrets\": [\n    {\n      \"binding\": \"MY_SECRET\",\n      \"store_id\": \"<STORE_ID>\",\n      \"secret_name\": \"my-secret\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Pages (Frontend Deployment)\n\n```bash\n# Create Pages project\nwrangler pages project create my-site\n\n# Deploy directory to Pages\nwrangler pages deploy ./dist\n\n# Deploy with specific branch\nwrangler pages deploy ./dist --branch main\n\n# List deployments\nwrangler pages deployment list --project-name my-site\n```\n\n---\n\n## Observability\n\n### Tail Logs\n\n```bash\n# Stream live logs\nwrangler tail\n\n# Tail specific Worker\nwrangler tail my-worker\n\n# Filter by status\nwrangler tail --status error\n\n# Filter by search term\nwrangler tail --search \"error\"\n\n# JSON output\nwrangler tail --format json\n```\n\n### Config Logging\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"observability\": {\n    \"enabled\": true,\n    \"head_sampling_rate\": 1\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Testing\n\n### Local Testing with Vitest\n\n```bash\nnpm install -D @cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers vitest\n```\n\n`vitest.config.ts`:\n```typescript\nimport { defineWorkersConfig } from \"@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers/config\";\n\nexport default defineWorkersConfig({\n  test: {\n    poolOptions: {\n      workers: {\n        wrangler: { configPath: \"./wrangler.jsonc\" },\n      },\n    },\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Test Scheduled Events\n\n```bash\n# Enable in dev\nwrangler dev --test-scheduled\n\n# Trigger via HTTP\ncurl http://localhost:8787/__scheduled\n```\n\n---\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Common Issues\n\n| Issue | Solution |\n|-------|----------|\n| `command not found: wrangler` | Install: `npm install -D wrangler` |\n| Auth errors | Run `wrangler login` |\n| Config validation errors | Run `wrangler check` |\n| Type errors after config change | Run `wrangler types` |\n| Local storage not persisting | Check `.wrangler/state` directory |\n| Binding undefined in Worker | Verify binding name matches config exactly |\n\n### Debug Commands\n\n```bash\n# Check auth status\nwrangler whoami\n\n# Validate config\nwrangler check\n\n# View config schema\nwrangler docs configuration\n```\n\n---\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Version control `wrangler.jsonc`**: Treat as source of truth for Worker config.\n2. **Use automatic provisioning**: Omit resource IDs for auto-creation on deploy.\n3. **Run `wrangler types` in CI**: Add to build step to catch binding mismatches.\n4. **Use environments**: Separate staging/production with `env.staging`, `env.production`.\n5. **Set `compatibility_date`**: Update quarterly to get new runtime features.\n6. **Use `.dev.vars` for local secrets**: Never commit secrets to config.\n7. **Test locally first**: `wrangler dev` with local bindings before deploying.\n8. **Use `--dry-run` before major deploys**: Validate changes without deployment.\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-23T01:07:35.605Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI代理Wrangler：Cloudflare Workers的CLI工具","ja":"AIエージェントWrangler：Cloudflare WorkersのCLIツール","ko":"AI 에이전트 Wrangler: Cloudflare Workers의 CLI 도구","es":"Herramientas de AI: Wrangler CLI para Cloudflare Workers","fr":"Outils d''IA: Wrangler CLI pour Cloudflare Workers","de":"KI-Tools: Wrangler CLI für Cloudflare Workers","pt":"Ferramentas de Agente de Inteligência Artificial: Wrangle...","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Wrangler CLI для Cloudflare Workers","ar":"أدوات الإیجنت الذكية: Wrangler CLI","en":"wrangler"},"description":{"zh":"Wrangler是Cloudflare Workers的CLI工具，用于部署、开发和管理Workers和相关资源","ja":"WranglerはCloudflare WorkersのCLIツールで、Workersと関連リソースのデプロイ、開発、管理に使用されます","ko":"Wrangler는 Cloudflare Workers의 CLI 도구로서 Workers와 관련 리소스의 배포, 개발, 관리에 사용됩니다","es":"Wrangler CLI es una herramienta de línea de comandos para Cloudflare Workers que facilita el deploy, desarrollo y manejo de Workers y recursos asociados.","fr":"Wrangler CLI est un outil de ligne de commande pour Cloudflare Workers qui facilite le déploiement, le développement et la gestion de Workers et ressources a...","de":"Wrangler CLI ist ein Kommandozeilen-Tool für Cloudflare Workers, das die Bereitstellung, Entwicklung und Verwaltung von Workers und zugehörigen Ressourcen er...","pt":"O Wrangler CLI é uma ferramenta para deploy, desenvolvimento e gerenciamento de Cloudflare Workers e recursos associados","ru":"Wrangler CLI - это инструмент для развертывания, разработки и управления Cloudflare Workers и связанных ресурсов","ar":"Wrangler CLI هو أداة لتنفيذ وتطوير وإدارة Cloudflare Workers والموارد المرتبطة بها","en":"Cloudflare Workers CLI for deploying, developing, and managing Workers, KV, R2, D1, Vectorize, Hyperdrive, Workers AI, Containers, Queues, Workflows, Pipelin..."},"definition":{"en":"Cloudflare Workers CLI for deploying, developing, and managing Workers, KV, R2, D1, Vectorize, Hyperdrive, Workers AI, Containers, Queues, Workflows, Pipelines, and Secrets Store. Load before running wrangler commands to ensure correct syntax and best practices."},"features":{"zh":["支持Cloudflare Workers的部署、开发和管理","支持KV、R2、D1、Vectorize、Hyperdrive、Workers AI、Containers、Queues、Workflows、Pipelines和Secrets Store","使用wrangler.jsonc配置文件","设置compatibility_date以确保兼容性"],"ja":["Cloudflare Workersのデプロイ、開発、管理をサポート","KV、R2、D1、Vectorize、Hyperdrive、Workers AI、Containers、Queues、Workflows、PipelinesとSecrets Storeをサポート","wrangler.jsonc構成ファイルを使用","compatibility_dateを設定して互換性を確保"],"ko":["Cloudflare Workers의 배포, 개발, 관리를 지원","KV, R2, D1, Vectorize, Hyperdrive, Workers AI, Containers, Queues, Workflows, Pipelines 및 Secrets Store를 지원","wrangler.jsonc 구성 파일을 사용","compatibility_date를 설정하여 호환성을 보장"],"es":["Deploy y desarrollo de Cloudflare Workers","Gestión de recursos asociados como KV, R2 y D1","Compatibilidad con Vectorize, Hyperdrive y Workers AI","Soporte para contenedores, colas, flujos de trabajo y pipelines","Almacenamiento seguro de secretos con Secrets Store"],"fr":["Déploiement et développement de Cloudflare Workers","Gestion des ressources associées telles que KV, R2 et D1","Compatibilité avec Vectorize, Hyperdrive et Workers AI","Prise en charge des conteneurs, des files d''attente, des flux de travail et des pipelines","Stockage sécurisé des secrets avec Secrets Store"],"de":["Bereitstellung und Entwicklung von Cloudflare Workers","Verwaltung von zugehörigen Ressourcen wie KV, R2 und D1","Kompatibilität mit Vectorize, Hyperdrive und Workers AI","Unterstützung für Container, Queues, Workflows und Pipelines","Sicheres Speichern von Geheimnissen mit Secrets Store"],"pt":["Deploy de Cloudflare Workers","Desenvolvimento de Workers","Gerenciamento de recursos associados","Uso de configuração JSON","Definição de data de compatibilidade"],"ru":["Развертывание Cloudflare Workers","Разработка Workers","Управление связанными ресурсами","Использование конфигурации JSON","Определение даты совместимости"],"ar":["تنفيذ Cloudflare Workers","تطوير Workers","إدارة الموارد المرتبطة","استخدام التهيئة JSON","تحديد تاريخ التوافق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI代理","Cloudflare Workers","CLI工具","Wrangler","部署","开发","管理","KV","R2","D1"],"ja":["AIエージェント","Cloudflare Workers","CLIツール","Wrangler","デプロイ","開発","管理","KV","R2","D1"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","Cloudflare Workers","CLI 도구","Wrangler","배포","개발","관리","KV","R2","D1"],"es":["Herramientas de AI","Wrangler CLI","Cloudflare Workers","Desarrollo de Workers","Gestión de recursos","CLI para Cloudflare"],"fr":["Outils d''IA","Wrangler CLI","Cloudflare Workers","Développement de Workers","Gestion des ressources","CLI pour Cloudflare"],"de":["KI-Tools","Wrangler CLI","Cloudflare Workers","Entwicklung von Workers","Verwaltung von Ressourcen","CLI für Cloudflare"],"pt":["Agente de Inteligência Artificial","Wrangler CLI","Cloudflare Workers","Desenvolvimento de Workers","Gerenciamento de recursos","Configuração JSON","Data de compatibilidade"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты","Wrangler CLI","Cloudflare Workers","Разработка Workers","Управление ресурсами","Конфигурация JSON","Дата совместимости"],"ar":["أدوات الإیجنت الذكية","Wrangler CLI","Cloudflare Workers","تطوير Workers","إدارة الموارد","تهيئة JSON","تاريخ التوافق"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Cloudflare-focused AI Agents requiring streamlined Workers deployment and management.","zh":"适用于需要简化Workers部署和管理的Cloudflare专用AI代理。","ja":"Cloudflareに特化したAIエージェントがWorkerの展開と管理を簡素化する場合に適しています。","ko":"Cloudflare에 특화된 AI 에이전트가 Worker 배포 및 관리를 간소화하는 경우 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de inteligencia artificial de Cloudflare que requieren una implementación y administración de Workers optimizadas.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''intelligence artificielle de Cloudflare nécessitant un déploiement et une gestion de Workers rationalisés.","de":"Ideal für Cloudflare-fokussierte KI-Agents, die eine optimierte Workers-Bereitstellung und -Verwaltung erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de IA do Cloudflare que exigem implantação e gerenciamento de Workers otimizados.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ Cloudflare, требующих оптимизированного развер