 rationalisées basées sur les modifications du code.","de":"Ideal für Next.js Agents, die optimierte Dokumentationsaktualisierungen basierend auf Codeänderungen benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Next.js que requerem atualizações de documentação simplificadas com base em alterações de código.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Next.js, требующих упрощенных обновлений документации на основе изменений кода.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء Next.js الذين يتطلبون تحديثات موثقة مبسطة بناءً على تغييرات التعليمات البرمجية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to synchronize documentation with code updates using git diff, mapping changed source files to documentation paths, and validating updates with pnpm lint, ensuring documentation completeness and accuracy for MDX files and API references.","zh":"使 Agent 能够使用 git diff 将文档与代码更新同步，将更改的源文件映射到文档路径，并使用 pnpm lint 验证更新，确保 MDX 文件和 API 参考的文档完整性和准确性。","ja":"git diff を使用してコード更新とドキュメントを同期し、変更されたソースファイルをドキュメントパスにマッピングし、pnpm lint で更新を検証することで、MDX ファイルと API リファレンスのドキュメントの完全性と正確性を保証するように Agent を強化します。","ko":"git diff를 사용하여 코드 업데이트와 문서를 동기화하고, 변경된 소스 파일을 문서 경로에 매핑하며, pnpm lint로 업데이트를 검증하여 MDX 파일 및 API 참조에 대한 문서의 완전성과 정확성을 보장하도록 Agent에 권한을 부여합니다.","es":"Empodera a los agents para sincronizar la documentación con las actualizaciones de código usando git diff, mapeando archivos fuente modificados a rutas de documentación, y validando las actualizaciones con pnpm lint, asegurando la integridad y precisión de la documentación para archivos MDX y referencias API.","fr":"Permet aux agents de synchroniser la documentation avec les mises à jour du code en utilisant git diff, en mappant les fichiers source modifiés aux chemins de documentation, et en validant les mises à jour avec pnpm lint, garantissant l''exhaustivité et la précision de la documentation pour les fichiers MDX et les références d''API.","de":"Ermöglicht Agents, die Dokumentation mit Code-Updates mithilfe von git diff zu synchronisieren, indem geänderte Quelldateien Dokumentationspfaden zugeordnet werden und Updates mit pnpm lint validiert werden, wodurch die Vollständigkeit und Genauigkeit der Dokumentation für MDX-Dateien und API-Referenzen sichergestellt wird.","pt":"Capacita os agentes a sincronizar a documentação com atualizações de código usando git diff, mapeando arquivos fonte alterados para caminhos de documentação e validando atualizações com pnpm lint, garantindo integridade e precisão da documentação para arquivos MDX e referências de API.","ru":"Позволяет агентам синхронизировать документацию с обновлениями кода с использованием git diff, сопоставляя измененные исходные файлы с путями документации и проверяя обновления с помощью pnpm lint, обеспечивая полноту и точность документации для файлов MDX и ссылок на API.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من مزامنة الوثائق مع تحديثات التعليمات البرمجية باستخدام git diff، وتخطيط ملفات المصدر المتغيرة إلى مسارات الوثائق، والتحقق من صحة التحديثات باستخدام pnpm lint، مما يضمن اكتمال ودقة الوثائق لملفات MDX ومراجع API."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating documentation updates for new features","Reviewing documentation completeness for PRs","Scaffolding documentation for new code changes","Validating documentation formatting with pnpm lint"],"zh":["为新功能自动化文档更新","为 PR 审查文档完整性","为新代码变更搭建文档框架","使用 pnpm lint 验证文档格式"],"ja":["新機能のためのドキュメント更新の自動化","PR のためのドキュメント完全性のレビュー","新しいコード変更のためのドキュメントのスキャフォールディング","pnpm lint を使用したドキュメントフォーマットの検証"],"ko":["새로운 기능에 대한 문서 업데이트 자동화","PR에 대한 문서 완전성 검토","새로운 코드 변경에 대한 문서 스캐폴딩","pnpm lint를 사용한 문서 형식 검증"],"es":["Automatizar las actualizaciones de documentación para nuevas features","Revisar la integridad de la documentación para los PRs","Scaffolding de documentación para nuevos cambios de código","Validar el formato de la documentación con pnpm lint"],"fr":["Automatiser les mises à jour de la documentation pour les nouvelles features","Examiner l''exhaustivité de la documentation pour les PRs","Scaffolding de la documentation pour les nouveaux changements de code","Valider le formatage de la documentation avec pnpm lint"],"de":["Automatisieren von Dokumentationsupdates für neue Features","Überprüfen der Dokumentationsvollständigkeit für PRs","Scaffolding der Dokumentation für neue Codeänderungen","Validieren der Dokumentationsformatierung mit pnpm lint"],"pt":["Automatizando atualizações de documentação para novos recursos","Revisando a integridade da documentação para PRs","Estruturando documentação para novas alterações de código","Validando formatação de documentação com pnpm lint"],"ru":["Автоматизация обновлений документации для новых функций","Проверка полноты документации для пул-реквестов (PR)","Создание каркаса документации для новых изменений кода","Проверка форматирования документации с помощью pnpm lint"],"ar":["أتمتة تحديثات الوثائق للميزات الجديدة","مراجعة اكتمال الوثائق لطلبات السحب (PRs)","إعداد هيكل الوثائق لتغييرات التعليمات البرمجية الجديدة","التحقق من تنسيق الوثائق باستخدام pnpm lint"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires git repository access","Designed for Next.js documentation only","Needs pnpm installed for linting"],"zh":["需要 git 仓库访问权限","仅专为 Next.js 文档设计","需要安装 pnpm 以进行 lint 操作"],"ja":["git リポジトリへのアクセスが必要","Next.js ドキュメント専用に設計","lint 処理のために pnpm のインストールが必要"],"ko":["git 저장소 액세스 권한 필요","Next.js 문서 전용으로 설계됨","linting을 위해 pnpm 설치 필요"],"es":["Requiere acceso a un repositorio git","Diseñado únicamente para documentación de Next.js","Necesita pnpm instalado para el linting"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au repository git","Conçu uniquement pour la documentation Next.js","Nécessite pnpm installé pour le linting"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf ein git-Repository","Nur für Next.js-Dokumentation konzipiert","Erfordert die Installation von pnpm für Linting"],"pt":["Requer acesso a repositório git","Projetado apenas para documentação Next.js","Necessita do pnpm instalado para linting"],"ru":["Требует доступ к репозиторию git","Предназначен только для документации Next.js","Требует установки pnpm для линтинга"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى مستودع git","مصمم لوثائق Next.js فقط","يحتاج إلى تثبيت pnpm للتدقيق (linting)"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"0f46c6e76a222cfa4008d16cdb1dfa37c413901db2b304a49cce829ef4c7ad71","repoEtag":"W/\"1e771a77abb3975cfbad0c789af1c3b089fbc40eb93052ab794eb54ec6fcc469\"","qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('facebook/react/feature-flags', 'official', 'facebook', 'react', 'facebook/react', 'feature-flags', 243274, 50614, 65, '2026-02-22T23:26:11Z', '2026-02-23T01:08:22.555Z', 'b82f8ab67ebed3a34d71cb9f4ed7a0f94ab6129d23c171443ba10fef3f92adc1', '{"id":"facebook/react/feature-flags","name":"feature-flags","description":{"zh":"React功能标志用于管理和调试React应用的功能，包括@gate语法和渠道特定测试故障","ja":"React機能フラグは、Reactアプリケーションの機能を管理およびデバッグするために使用されます。@gate構文やチャネル固有のテスト障害が含まれます","ko":"리액트 기능 플래그는 리액트 애플리케이션의 기능을 관리하고 디버깅하는 데 사용됩니다. @gate 구문과 채널 특정 테스트 장애가 포함됩니다","es":"Feature-flags para React es una herramienta para pruebas y depuración de funciones","fr":"Les feature-flags pour React sont un outil pour les tests et le débogage de fonctions","de":"Feature-Flags für React sind ein Tool für Tests und Fehlerbehebung","pt":"Feature flags são uma técnica para gerenciar recursos em aplicações React. Ela permite ativar ou desativar recursos com base em condições específicas.","ru":"Фишки флагов - это техника для управления функциями в приложениях React. Она позволяет включать или выключать функции на основе определенных условий.","ar":"ميزات الراية هي تقنية لإدارة الميزات في تطبيقات الري액ت. تسمح بتفعيل أو تعطيل الميزات بناءً على ظروف محددة.","en":"Use when feature flag tests fail, flags need updating, understanding @gate pragmas, debugging channel-specific test failures, or adding new flags to React."},"owner":"facebook","repo":"react","repoPath":"facebook/react","stars":243274,"forks":50614,"updatedAt":"2026-02-22T23:26:11Z","topics":["declarative","frontend","javascript","library","react","ui"],"skillMd":{"name":"feature-flags","description":"Use when feature flag tests fail, flags need updating, understanding @gate pragmas, debugging channel-specific test failures, or adding new flags to React.","bodyPreview":"# React Feature Flags\n\n## Flag Files\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `packages/shared/ReactFeatureFlags.js` | Default flags (canary), `__EXPERIMENTAL__` overrides |\n| `packages/shared/forks/ReactFeatureFlags.www.js` | www channel, `__VARIANT__` overrides |\n| `packages/shared/forks/ReactFeatureFlags.native-fb.js` | React Native, `__VARIANT__` overrides |\n| `packages/shared/forks/ReactFeatureFlags.test-renderer.js` | Test renderer |\n\n## Gating Tests\n\n### `@gate` pragma (test-level)\n\nUse w","body":"# React Feature Flags\n\n## Flag Files\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `packages/shared/ReactFeatureFlags.js` | Default flags (canary), `__EXPERIMENTAL__` overrides |\n| `packages/shared/forks/ReactFeatureFlags.www.js` | www channel, `__VARIANT__` overrides |\n| `packages/shared/forks/ReactFeatureFlags.native-fb.js` | React Native, `__VARIANT__` overrides |\n| `packages/shared/forks/ReactFeatureFlags.test-renderer.js` | Test renderer |\n\n## Gating Tests\n\n### `@gate` pragma (test-level)\n\nUse when the feature is completely unavailable without the flag:\n\n```javascript\n// @gate enableViewTransition\nit(''supports view transitions'', () => {\n  // This test only runs when enableViewTransition is true\n  // and is SKIPPED (not failed) when false\n});\n```\n\n### `gate()` inline (assertion-level)\n\nUse when the feature exists but behavior differs based on flag:\n\n```javascript\nit(''renders component'', async () => {\n  await act(() => root.render(<App />));\n\n  if (gate(flags => flags.enableNewBehavior)) {\n    expect(container.textContent).toBe(''new output'');\n  } else {\n    expect(container.textContent).toBe(''legacy output'');\n  }\n});\n```\n\n## Adding a New Flag\n\n1. Add to `ReactFeatureFlags.js` with default value\n2. Add to each fork file (`*.www.js`, `*.native-fb.js`, etc.)\n3. If it should vary in www/RN, set to `__VARIANT__` in the fork file\n4. Gate tests with `@gate flagName` or inline `gate()`\n\n## Checking Flag States\n\nUse `/flags` to view states across channels. See the `flags` skill for full command options.\n\n## `__VARIANT__` Flags (GKs)\n\nFlags set to `__VARIANT__` simulate gatekeepers - tested twice (true and false):\n\n```bash\n/test www <pattern>              # __VARIANT__ = true\n/test www variant false <pattern> # __VARIANT__ = false\n```\n\n## Debugging Channel-Specific Failures\n\n1. Run `/flags --diff <channel1> <channel2>` to compare values\n2. Check `@gate` conditions - test may be gated to specific channels\n3. Run `/test <channel> <pattern>` to isolate the failure\n4. Verify flag exists in all fork files if newly added\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n- **Forgetting both variants** - Always test `www` AND `www variant false` for `__VARIANT__` flags\n- **Using @gate for behavior differences** - Use inline `gate()` if both paths should run\n- **Missing fork files** - New flags must be added to ALL fork files, not just the main one\n- **Wrong gate syntax** - It''s `gate(flags => flags.name)`, not `gate(''name'')`\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-23T01:08:22.555Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能工具：React功能标志","ja":"AIエージェント：React機能フラグ","ko":"AI 에이전트: 리액트 기능 플래그","es":"Herramientas de feature-flags para React","fr":"Outils de feature-flags pour React","de":"Feature-Flags-Tools für React","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: Feature Flags para React","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Фишки флагов для React","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: ميزات الراية للري액ت","en":"feature-flags"},"description":{"zh":"React功能标志用于管理和调试React应用的功能，包括@gate语法和渠道特定测试故障","ja":"React機能フラグは、Reactアプリケーションの機能を管理およびデバッグするために使用されます。@gate構文やチャネル固有のテスト障害が含まれます","ko":"리액트 기능 플래그는 리액트 애플리케이션의 기능을 관리하고 디버깅하는 데 사용됩니다. @gate 구문과 채널 특정 테스트 장애가 포함됩니다","es":"Feature-flags para React es una herramienta para pruebas y depuración de funciones","fr":"Les feature-flags pour React sont un outil pour les tests et le débogage de fonctions","de":"Feature-Flags für React sind ein Tool für Tests und Fehlerbehebung","pt":"Feature flags são uma técnica para gerenciar recursos em aplicações React. Ela permite ativar ou desativar recursos com base em condições específicas.","ru":"Фишки флагов - это техника для управления функциями в приложениях React. Она позволяет включать или выключать функции на основе определенных условий.","ar":"ميزات الراية هي تقنية لإدارة الميزات في تطبيقات الري액ت. تسمح بتفعيل أو تعطيل الميزات بناءً على ظروف محددة.","en":"Use when feature flag tests fail, flags need updating, understanding @gate pragmas, debugging channel-specific test failures, or adding new flags to React."},"definition":{"en":"Use when feature flag tests fail, flags need updating, understanding @gate pragmas, debugging channel-specific test failures, or adding new flags to React."},"features":{"zh":["使用@gate语法","管理React应用的功能","调试渠道特定测试故障","支持React Native和Test Renderer","使用__EXPERIMENTAL__和__VARIANT__覆盖"],"ja":["@gate構文の使用","Reactアプリケーションの機能の管理","チャネル固有のテスト障害のデバッグ","React NativeとTest Rendererのサポート","__EXPERIMENTAL__と__VARIANT__のオーバーライド"],"ko":["@gate 구문의 사용","리액트 애플리케이션의 기능 관리","채널 특정 테스트 장애의 디버깅","리액트 네이티브와 테스트 렌더러의 지원","__EXPERIMENTAL__와 __VARIANT__의 오버라이드"],"es":["Uso de @gate pragma para pruebas","Actualización de flags","Depuración de fallos de canal específicos","Adición de nuevos flags a React","Uso de archivos de flags para configuración"],"fr":["Utilisation de @gate pragma pour les tests","Mise à jour des flags","Débogage des échecs de canal spécifiques","Ajout de nouveaux flags à React","Utilisation de fichiers de flags pour la configuration"],"de":["Verwendung von @gate-Pragma für Tests","Aktualisierung von Flags","Fehlerbehebung bei kanal-spezifischen Fehlern","Hinzufügen neuer Flags zu React","Verwendung von Flag-Dateien für die Konfiguration"],"pt":["Arquivos de flags para gerenciar recursos","Testes de gateway para validar a lógica de negócios","Suporte a múltiplos canais e variantes","Integração com bibliotecas de frontend","Depuração de falhas de teste de canal específico"],"ru":["Файлы флагов для управления функциями","Тесты шлюза для проверки логики бизнеса","Поддержка нескольких каналов и вариантов","Интеграция с библиотеками frontend","Отладка ошибок теста канала"],"ar":["ملفات الراية لإدارة الميزات","أختبارات البوابة لتأكيد المنطق التجاري","دعم قنوات متعددة ومتغيرات","التكامل مع مكتبات واجهة المستخدم","تصحيح أخطاء اختبار القناة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["React功能标志","AI智能工具","React调试","功能管理","渠道特定测试","React Native","Test Renderer","JavaScript"],"ja":["React機能フラグ","AIエージェント","Reactデバッグ","機能管理","チャネル固有のテスト","React Native","Test Renderer","JavaScript"],"ko":["리액트 기능 플래그","AI 에이전트","리액트 디버깅","기능 관리","채널 특정 테스트","리액트 네이티브","테스트 렌더러","JavaScript"],"es":["feature-flags","React","pruebas","depuración","flags","canal específico","actualización de flags","nuevos flags"],"fr":["feature-flags","React","tests","débogage","flags","canal spécifique","mise à jour des flags","nouveaux flags"],"de":["Feature-Flags","React","Tests","Fehlerbehebung","Flags","kanal-spezifisch","Aktualisierung von Flags","neue Flags"],"pt":["feature flags","react","frontend","bibliotecas de frontend","testes de gateway","depuração de erros","canais específicos","variantes","gerenciamento de recursos"],"ru":["фишки флагов","react","frontend","библиотеки frontend","тесты шлюза","отладка ошибок","каналы","варианты","управление функциями"],"ar":["ميزات الراية","ري액ت","واجهة المستخدم","مكتبات واجهة المستخدم","أختبارات البوابة","تصحيح أخطاء","قنوات محددة","متغيرات","إدارة الميزات"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for React Development Agents needing advanced feature flag management capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级功能标志管理功能的React开发代理。","ja":"React開発エージェントが高度な機能フラグ管理機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 기능 플래그 관리 기능이 필요한 React 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo de React que necesitan capacidades de administración de indicadores de características avanzadas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement React nécessitant des capacités de gestion de drapeaux de fonctionnalités avancées.","de":"Perfekt für React-Entwicklungsagenten, die erweiterte Funktionsschaltflaggen-Verwaltungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento React que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de gerenciamento de feature flags.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки React, которым требуются расширенные возможности управления функциональными флагами.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء تطوير React الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات متقدمة لإدارة علم الميزات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage and debug React feature flags using @gate pragmas, updating flags, and understanding channel-specific test failures, leveraging files like ReactFeatureFlags.js and ReactFeatureFlags.www.js.","zh":"赋予代理管理和调试React功能标志的能力，使用@gate语法，更新标志，并了解特定频道的测试失败，利用文件如ReactFeatureFlags.js和ReactFeatureFlags.www.js。","ja":"エージェントがReactの機能フラグを管理およびデバッグする能力を提供します。@gate文法、フラグの更新、特定のチャネルのテストの失敗の理解を使用し、ReactFeatureFlags.jsやReactFeatureFlags.www.jsなどのファイルを活用します。","ko":"에이전트가 React 기능 플래그를 관리하고 디버깅할 수 있는 기능을 제공합니다. @gate 구문을 사용하여 플래그를 업데이트하고 특정 채널의 테스트 실패를 이해하며, ReactFeatureFlags.js와 ReactFeatureFlags.www.js 같은 파일을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a administrar y depurar los indicadores de características de React utilizando @gate pragmas, actualizando indicadores y comprendiendo fallos de prueba específicos del canal, aprovechando archivos como ReactFeatureFlags.js y ReactFeatureFlags.www.js.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer et de déboguer les drapeaux de fonctionnalités React en utilisant des @gate pragmas, en mettant à jour les drapeaux et en comprenant les défaillances de test spécifiques au canal, en exploitant des fichiers tels que ReactFeatureFlags.js et ReactFeatureFlags.www.js.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, React-Funktionsschaltflagen zu verwalten und zu debuggen, indem @gate-Pragmas verwendet werden, Schaltflagen aktualisiert werden und kanalspezifische Testfehler verstanden werden, indem Dateien wie ReactFeatureFlags.js und ReactFeatureFlags.www.js genutzt werden.","pt":"Capacita os agentes a gerenciar e depurar feature flags do React usando pragmas @gate, atualizar flags e compreender falhas de teste específicas do canal, aproveitando arquivos como ReactFeatureFlags.js e ReactFeatureFlags.www.js.","ru":"Позволяет агентам управлять и отлаживать функциональные флаги React с использованием прагм @gate, обновлять флаги и понимать сбои тестов для конкретных каналов, используя такие файлы, как ReactFeatureFlags.js и ReactFeatureFlags.www.js.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من إدارة وتصحيح أعلام ميزات React باستخدام التوجيهات البرمجية @gate، وتحديث الأعلام، وفهم حالات فشل الاختبارات الخاصة بالقناة، والاستفادة من ملفات مثل ReactFeatureFlags.js و ReactFeatureFlags.www.js."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging channel-specific test failures in React Native and www channels","Updating and managing default flags and __EXPERIMENTAL__ overrides in ReactFeatureFlags.js","Adding new flags to React applications using @gate pragmas","Resolving test failures by understanding and utilizing __VARIANT__ overrides"],"zh":["在React Native和www频道中调试特定频道的测试失败","在ReactFeatureFlags.js中更新和管理默认标志和__EXPERIMENTAL__重写","使用@gate语法向React应用程序添加新标志","通过了解和利用__VARIANT__重写来解决测试失败"],"ja":["React Nativeおよびwwwチャネルの特定のチャネルのテストの失敗をデバッグする","ReactFeatureFlags.js内のデフォルトのフラグおよび__EXPERIMENTAL__のオーバーライドを更新および管理する","@gate文法を使用してReactアプリケーションに新しいフラグを追加する","__VARIANT__のオーバーライドを理解および活用してテストの失敗を解決する"],"ko":["React Native와 www 채널에서 특정 채널의 테스트 실패를 디버깅하는 것","ReactFeatureFlags.js에서 기본 플래그와 __EXPERIMENTAL__ 오버라이드를 업데이트하고 관리하는 것","@gate 구문을 사용하여 React 애플리케이션에 새로운 플래그를 추가하는 것","__VARIANT__ 오버라이드를 이해하고 활용하여 테스트 실패를 해결하는 것"],"es":["Depuración de fallos de prueba específicos del canal en canales React Native y www","Actualización y administración de indicadores predeterminados y anulaciones __EXPERIMENTAL__ en ReactFeatureFlags.js","Adición de nuevos indicadores a aplicaciones React utilizando @gate pragmas","Resolución de fallos de prueba mediante la comprensión y utilización de anulaciones __VARIANT__"],"fr":["Débogage des défaillances de test spécifiques au canal dans les canaux React Native et www","Mise à jour et gestion des drapeaux par défaut et des substitutions __EXPERIMENTAL__ dans ReactFeatureFlags.js","Ajout de nouveaux drapeaux aux applications React en utilisant des @gate pragmas","Résolution des défaillances de test en comprenant et en utilisant les substitutions __VARIANT__"],"de":["Debuggen kanalspezifischer Testfehler in React Native- und www-Kanälen","Aktualisieren und Verwalten von Standard-Schaltflagen und __EXPERIMENTAL__-Überschreibungen in ReactFeatureFlags.js","Hinzufügen neuer Schaltflagen zu React-Anwendungen unter Verwendung von @gate-Pragmas","Beheben von Testfehlern durch Verständnis und Nutzung von __VARIANT__-Überschreibungen"],"pt":["Depuração de falhas de teste específicas do canal nos canais React Native e www","Atualização e gerenciamento de flags padrão e substituições __EXPERIMENTAL__ no ReactFeatureFlags.js","Adição de novas flags a aplicações React usando pragmas @gate","Resolução de falhas de teste através da compreensão e utilização de substituições __VARIANT__"],"ru":["Отладка сбоев тестов для конкретных каналов в каналах React Native и www","Обновление и управление флагами по умолчанию и экспериментальными переопределениями __EXPERIMENTAL__ в ReactFeatureFlags.js","Добавление новых флагов в приложения React с использованием прагм @gate","Устранение сбоев тестов путем понимания и использования переопределений __VARIANT__"],"ar":["تصحيح حالات فشل الاختبارات الخاصة بالقناة في قنوات React Native و www","تحديث وإدارة الأعلام الافتراضية وتجاوزات __EXPERIMENTAL__ في ملف ReactFeatureFlags.js","إضافة أعلام جديدة لتطبيقات React باستخدام التوجيهات البرمجية @gate","حل حالات فشل الاختبارات من خلال فهم واستخدام تجاوزات __VARIANT__"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of React and feature flag management","Specific to React ecosystem, not applicable to other frameworks","Needs access to React project files and configuration"],"zh":["需要了解React和功能标志管理","仅适用于React生态系统，不适用于其他框架","需要访问React项目文件和配置"],"ja":["Reactおよび機能フラグ管理の知識が必要","Reactエコシステムのみに特有で、他のフレームワークには適用できない","Reactプロジェクトのファイルおよび設定へのアクセスが必要"],"ko":["React와 기능 플래그 관리에 대한 지식이 필요함","React 생태계에만 특화되어 있으며, 다른 프레임워크에는 적용할 수 없음","React 프로젝트 파일 및 설정에 대한 액세스가 필요함"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de React y administración de indicadores de características","Específico del ecosistema React, no aplicable a otros frameworks","Necesita acceso a archivos y configuración del proyecto React"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances en React et en gestion de drapeaux de fonctionnalités","Spécifique à l''écosystème React, non applicable à d''autres frameworks","Nécessite un accès aux fichiers et à la configuration du projet React"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse von React und Funktions-Schaltflaggen-Verwaltung","Spezifisch für das React-Ökosystem, nicht anwendbar auf andere Frameworks","Benötigt Zugriff auf React-Projektdateien und -Konfiguration"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento de React e gerenciamento de feature flags","Específico para o ecossistema React, não é aplicável a outros frameworks","Necessita de acesso aos arquivos e configuração do projeto React"],"ru":["Требует знания React и управления функциональными флагами","Специфично для экосистемы React, не применимо к другим фреймворкам","Требует доступа к файлам и конфигурации проекта React"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة بـ React وإدارة علم الميزات","مخصص لبيئة React ولا ينطبق على أطر عمل أخرى","يحتاج إلى الوصول إلى ملفات وتكوين مشروع React"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"b82f8ab67ebed3a34d71cb9f4ed7a0f94ab6129d23c171443ba10fef3f92adc1","repoEtag":"W/\"760a59871b4a4077e06a22aacf6f520d97df70e5d97d558f7c60e2050ca096b9\"","qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('callstackincubator/agent-skills/upgrading-react-native', 'official', 'callstackincubator', 'agent-skills', 'callstackincubator/agent-skills', 'upgrading-react-native', 922, 51, 60, '2026-02-24T07:45:20Z', '2026-02-24T12:10:19.258Z', 'd8100fa8d5d42b4176bebc940be651444bd6734073e400313519f422a1fb6f13', '{"id":"callstackincubator/agent-skills/upgrading-react-native","name":"upgrading-react-native","description":{"zh":"升级React Native的AI工具提供了升级工作流，包括更新模板、依赖项和常见陷阱","ja":"React NativeアップグレードのAIエージェントは、アップグレードワークフローを提供し、テンプレートの更新、依存関係の更新、一般的な落とし穴を含む","ko":"React Native 업그레이드 AI 에이전트는 업그레이드 워크플로우를 제공하며, 템플릿 업데이트와 종속성 업데이트 및 일반적인 함정 등을 포함","es":"Actualiza React Native con nuestra guía de herramientas de IA, que cubre el flujo de trabajo de actualización completo.","fr":"Mettez à jour React Native avec notre guide d''outils d''IA, qui couvre le flux de travail de mise à jour complet.","de":"Aktualisieren Sie React Native mit unserer Anleitung zu KI-Tools, die den kompletten Aktualisierungs-Workflow abdeckt.","pt":"O guia de upgrade do React Native cobre o fluxo de trabalho de atualização completo, incluindo modelos atualizados e dependências","ru":"Руководство по обновлению React Native охватывает полный процесс обновления, включая обновленные шаблоны и зависимости","ar":"دليل ترقية React Native يغطي عملية الترقية الكاملة، بما في ذلك القوالب واعتمادات محدثة","en":"React Native upgrade workflow covering updated templates, dependencies, and common pitfalls. Use when migrating a React Native app to a newer release."},"owner":"callstackincubator","repo":"agent-skills","repoPath":"callstackincubator/agent-skills","stars":922,"forks":51,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T07:45:20Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"upgrading-react-native","description":"React Native upgrade workflow covering updated templates, dependencies, and common pitfalls. Use when migrating a React Native app to a newer release.","tags":"react-native, upgrade, upgrade-helper, npm, changelog, cocoapods, ios, android","bodyPreview":"# Upgrading React Native\n\n## Overview\n\nCovers the full React Native upgrade workflow: template diffs via Upgrade Helper, dependency updates, Expo SDK steps, and common pitfalls.\n\n## When to Apply\n\nReference these guidelines when:\n- Moving a React Native app to a newer version\n- Reconciling native config changes from Upgrade Helper\n- Validating release notes for breaking changes\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| File | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| [upgrading-react-native.md][upgrading-react-native","body":"# Upgrading React Native\n\n## Overview\n\nCovers the full React Native upgrade workflow: template diffs via Upgrade Helper, dependency updates, Expo SDK steps, and common pitfalls.\n\n## When to Apply\n\nReference these guidelines when:\n- Moving a React Native app to a newer version\n- Reconciling native config changes from Upgrade Helper\n- Validating release notes for breaking changes\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| File | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| [upgrading-react-native.md][upgrading-react-native] | Router: choose the right upgrade path |\n| [upgrade-helper-core.md][upgrade-helper-core] | Core Upgrade Helper workflow and reliability gates |\n| [upgrading-dependencies.md][upgrading-dependencies] | Dependency compatibility checks and migration planning |\n| [react.md][react] | React and React 19 upgrade alignment rules |\n| [expo-sdk-upgrade.md][expo-sdk-upgrade] | Expo SDK-specific upgrade layer (conditional) |\n| [upgrade-verification.md][upgrade-verification] | Manual post-upgrade verification checklist |\n| [monorepo-singlerepo-targeting.md][monorepo-singlerepo-targeting] | Monorepo and single-repo app targeting and command scoping |\n\n## Problem → Skill Mapping\n\n| Problem | Start With |\n|---------|------------|\n| Need to upgrade React Native | [upgrade-helper-core.md][upgrade-helper-core] |\n| Need dependency risk triage and migration options | [upgrading-dependencies.md][upgrading-dependencies] |\n| Need React/React 19 package alignment | [react.md][react] |\n| Need workflow routing first | [upgrading-react-native.md][upgrading-react-native] |\n| Need Expo SDK-specific steps | [expo-sdk-upgrade.md][expo-sdk-upgrade] |\n| Need manual regression validation | [upgrade-verification.md][upgrade-verification] |\n| Need repo/app command scoping | [monorepo-singlerepo-targeting.md][monorepo-singlerepo-targeting] |\n\n[upgrading-react-native]: references/upgrading-react-native.md\n[upgrade-helper-core]: references/upgrade-helper-core.md\n[upgrading-dependencies]: references/upgrading-dependencies.md\n[react]: references/react.md\n[expo-sdk-upgrade]: references/expo-sdk-upgrade.md\n[upgrade-verification]: references/upgrade-verification.md\n[monorepo-singlerepo-targeting]: references/monorepo-singlerepo-targeting.md\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-24T12:10:19.258Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"升级React Native的AI工具","ja":"React NativeアップグレードのAIエージェント","ko":"React Native 업그레이드 AI 에이전트","es":"Herramientas de IA para Actualizar React Native","fr":"Outils d''IA pour Mettre à Jour React Native","de":"KI-Tools zum Updaten von React Native","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: Upgrading React Native","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Обновление React Native","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: ترقية React Native","en":"upgrading-react-native"},"description":{"zh":"升级React Native的AI工具提供了升级工作流，包括更新模板、依赖项和常见陷阱","ja":"React NativeアップグレードのAIエージェントは、アップグレードワークフローを提供し、テンプレートの更新、依存関係の更新、一般的な落とし穴を含む","ko":"React Native 업그레이드 AI 에이전트는 업그레이드 워크플로우를 제공하며, 템플릿 업데이트와 종속성 업데이트 및 일반적인 함정 등을 포함","es":"Actualiza React Native con nuestra guía de herramientas de IA, que cubre el flujo de trabajo de actualización completo.","fr":"Mettez à jour React Native avec notre guide d''outils d''IA, qui couvre le flux de travail de mise à jour complet.","de":"Aktualisieren Sie React Native mit unserer Anleitung zu KI-Tools, die den kompletten Aktualisierungs-Workflow abdeckt.","pt":"O guia de upgrade do React Native cobre o fluxo de trabalho de atualização completo, incluindo modelos atualizados e dependências","ru":"Руководство по обновлению React Native охватывает полный процесс обновления, включая обновленные шаблоны и зависимости","ar":"دليل ترقية React Native يغطي عملية الترقية الكاملة، بما في ذلك القوالب واعتمادات محدثة","en":"React Native upgrade workflow covering updated templates, dependencies, and common pitfalls. Use when migrating a React Native app to a newer release."},"definition":{"en":"React Native upgrade workflow covering updated templates, dependencies, and common pitfalls. Use when migrating a React Native app to a newer release."},"features":{"zh":["升级工作流","更新模板","依赖项更新","常见陷阱","Expo SDK步骤","Upgrade Helper集成"],"ja":["アップグレードワークフロー","テンプレートの更新","依存関係の更新","一般的な落とし穴","Expo SDKステップ","Upgrade Helperの統合"],"ko":["업그레이드 워크플로우","템플릿 업데이트","종속성 업데이트","일반적인 함정","Expo SDKステップ","Upgrade Helper 통합"],"es":["Flujo de trabajo de actualización completo","Actualizaciones de dependencias y plantillas","Paso a paso para evitar errores comunes","Validación de notas de lanzamiento para cambios importantes","Integración con Expo SDK"],"fr":["Flux de travail de mise à jour complet","Mises à jour des dépendances et des modèles","Étapes pour éviter les erreurs courantes","Validation des notes de version pour les changements importants","Intégration avec Expo SDK"],"de":["Kompletter Aktualisierungs-Workflow","Aktualisierungen von Abhängigkeiten und Vorlagen","Schritt-für-Schritt-Anleitung zur Vermeidung von häufigen Fehlern","Validierung von Versionshinweisen für wichtige Änderungen","Integration mit Expo SDK"],"pt":["Atualização de modelos via Upgrade Helper","Atualização de dependências","Passos para o SDK do Expo","Pitfalls comuns"],"ru":["Обновление шаблонов с помощью Upgrade Helper","Обновление зависимостей","Шаги для SDK Expo","Распространенные ошибки"],"ar":["تحديث القوالب عبر Upgrade Helper","تحديث الاعتمادات","خطوات SDK Expo","الأخطاء الشائعة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["React Native升级","AI工具","升级工作流","依赖项更新","Expo SDK","Upgrade Helper"],"ja":["React Nativeアップグレード","AIエージェント","アップグレードワークフロー","依存関係の更新","Expo SDK","Upgrade Helper"],"ko":["React Native 업그레이드","AI 에이전트","업그레이드 워크플로우","종속성 업데이트","Expo SDK","Upgrade Helper"],"es":["actualizar react native","herramientas de ia para react native","migrar a react native nuevo","react native upgrade","react native update","desarrollo de aplicaciones móviles"],"fr":["mettre à jour react native","outils d''ia pour react native","migration vers react native nouveau","react native mise à jour","react native update","développement d''applications mobiles"],"de":["react native aktualisieren","ki-tools für react native","migration auf react native neu","react native update","react native aktualisierung","entwicklung von mobilen anwendungen"],"pt":["React Native","upgrade","atualização","desenvolvimento de aplicativos","ferramentas de IA","tecnologias de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["React Native","обновление","разработка приложений","ИИ Агенты","технологии разработки","мобильные приложения"],"ar":["React Native","ترقية","تطوير التطبيقات","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","تقنيات التطوير","تطبيقات الهاتف المحمول"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Mobile App Agents specializing in React Native development, needing streamlined upgrade workflows and dependency management.","zh":"适用于专注于 React Native 开发的移动应用代理，需要简化的升级工作流程和依赖管理。","ja":"React Native 開発を専門とするモバイル アプリ エージェントに適しています。ストリームライン化されたアップグレード ワークフローと依存関係の管理が必要です。","ko":"React Native 개발을 전문으로 하는 모바일 앱 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 스트림라인화된 업그레이드 워크플로우와 의존성 관리가 필요합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de aplicaciones móviles especializados en desarrollo de React Native, que necesitan flujos de trabajo de actualización optimizados y gestión de dependencias.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''applications mobiles spécialisés dans le développement React Native, nécessitant des flux de travail de mise à niveau optimisés et une gestion des dépendances.","de":"Perfekt für Mobile App-Agents, die sich auf React Native-Entwicklung spezialisieren und optimierte Upgrade-Workflows und Abhängigkeitsverwaltung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Aplicativos Móveis especializados em desenvolvimento React Native, necessitando de fluxos de atualização simplificados e gerenciamento de dependências.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов мобильных приложений, специализирующихся на разработке React Native, которым необходимы упрощенные рабочие процессы обновления и управление зависимостями.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء تطبيقات الهاتف المحمول المتخصصة في تطوير React Native، التي تحتاج إلى عمليات تحديث مبسطة وإدارة التبعيات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to navigate the React Native upgrade process, covering template diffs via Upgrade Helper, dependency updates, and Expo SDK steps, while avoiding common pitfalls and validating release notes for breaking changes.","zh":"赋予代理导航 React Native 升级过程的能力，涵盖 Upgrade Helper 的模板差异、依赖更新和 Expo SDK 步骤，同时避免常见的陷阱并验证发布说明中关于破坏性更改的内容。","ja":"エージェントが React Native のアップグレード プロセスをナビゲートする能力を提供します。Upgrade Helper のテンプレートの差、依存関係の更新、Expo SDK のステップをカバーしながら、一般的な落とし穴を避け、破壊的な変更についてのリリース ノートを検証します。","ko":"에이전트가 React Native 업그레이드 프로세스를 탐색할 수 있는 능력을 제공합니다. Upgrade Helper의 템플릿 차이, 의존성 업데이트, Expo SDK 단계를 다루면서 일반적인 함정에서 벗어나고发布 노트에서 변경 사항을 확인합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a navegar por el proceso de actualización de React Native, cubriendo las diferencias de plantillas a través de Upgrade Helper, actualizaciones de dependencias y pasos de Expo SDK, mientras evita trampas comunes y valida las notas de lanzamiento para cambios importantes.","fr":"Permet aux agents de naviguer dans le processus de mise à niveau de React Native, couvrant les différences de modèles via Upgrade Helper, les mises à jour des dépendances et les étapes de Expo SDK, tout en évitant les pièges courants et en validant les notes de version pour les changements de rupture.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, den React Native-Upgrade-Prozess zu navigieren, einschließlich Template-Diffs über Upgrade Helper, Abhängigkeits-Updates und Expo SDK-Schritte, während sie gemeinsame Fallstricke vermeiden und Veröffentlichungshinweise für wichtige Änderungen überprüfen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a navegar pelo processo de atualização do React Native, cobrindo diferenças de modelo via Upgrade Helper, atualizações de dependência e etapas do Expo SDK, ao mesmo tempo evitando armadilhas comuns e validando notas de lançamento para alterações quebradas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью ориентироваться в процессе обновления React Native, покрывая различия шаблонов через Upgrade Helper, обновления зависимостей и этапы Expo SDK, а также избегая распространенных ловушек и проверяя заметки к выпуску на наличие критических изменений.","ar":"يمكّن الوكلاء من التنقل في عملية تحديث React Native، ويتضمن ذلك اختلافات القوالب عبر Upgrade Helper، وتحديثات التبعيات، وخطوات Expo SDK، مع تجنب الفخاخ الشائعة واعتماد ملاحظات الإصدار لتغييرات كاسرة."},"useCases":{"en":["Upgrading React Native apps to newer releases","Reconciling native config changes from Upgrade Helper","Validating release notes for breaking changes and updating dependencies accordingly"],"zh":["将 React Native 应用升级到新版本","通过 Upgrade Helper 协调原生配置更改","验证发布说明中关于破坏性更改的内容并相应地更新依赖关系"],"ja":["React Native アプリを新しいリリースにアップグレードする","Upgrade Helper を使用してネイティブ構成の変更を調整する","破壊的な変更についてのリリース ノートを検証し、依存関係をそれに応じて更新する"],"ko":["React Native 애플리케이션을 새로운 릴리즈로 업그레이드하는 것","Upgrade Helper를 통해 네이티브 구성 변경을 조정","发布 노트에서 변경 사항을 확인하고 해당 변경 사항에 따라 의존성을 업데이트하는 것"],"es":["Actualización de aplicaciones React Native a versiones más recientes","Reconciliación de cambios de configuración nativa desde Upgrade Helper","Validación de notas de lanzamiento para cambios importantes y actualización de dependencias en consecuencia"],"fr":["Mise à niveau d''applications React Native vers des versions plus récentes","Réconciliation des modifications de configuration native à partir de Upgrade Helper","Validation des notes de version pour les changements de rupture et mise à jour des dépendances en conséquence"],"de":["Upgraden von React Native-Apps auf neuere Versionen","Abgleichen von nativen Konfigurationsänderungen von Upgrade Helper","Überprüfen von Veröffentlichungshinweisen für wichtige Änderungen und entsprechende Aktualisierung von Abhängigkeiten"],"pt":["Atualizar aplicativos React Native para lançamentos mais recentes","Reconciliar alterações de configuração nativa do Upgrade Helper","Validar notas de lançamento para alterações quebradas e atualizar dependências de acordo"],"ru":["Обновление приложений React Native до более новых релизов","Согласование изменений конфигурации из Upgrade Helper","Проверка заметок к выпуску на наличие критических изменений и обновление зависимостей соответственно"],"ar":["تحديث تطبيقات React Native إلى إصدارات أحدث","مصالح изменения تكوين الأصلي من Upgrade Helper","تحقق من ملاحظات الإصدار لتغييرات كاسرة وتحديث التبعيات وفقًا لذلك"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of React Native and its ecosystem","Limited to React Native upgrade workflows","Expo SDK steps may require additional configuration"],"zh":["需要了解 React Native 及其生态系统","仅限 React Native 升级工作流程","Expo SDK 步骤可能需要额外的配置"],"ja":["React Native とそのエコシステムに関する知識が必要","React Native のアップグレード ワークフローに限定","Expo SDK のステップでは追加の構成が必要になる場合があります"],"ko":["React Native 및 그 생태계에 대한 지식이 필요","React Native 업그레이드 워크플로우에만 제한","Expo SDK 단계에서는 추가 구성이 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de React Native y su ecosistema","Limitado a flujos de trabajo de actualización de React Native","Los pasos de Expo SDK pueden requerir configuración adicional"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances en React Native et son écosystème","Limité aux flux de travail de mise à niveau de React Native","Les étapes de Expo SDK peuvent nécessiter une configuration supplémentaire"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse von React Native und seinem Ökosystem","Begrenzt auf React Native-Upgrade-Workflows","Expo SDK-Schritte können zusätzliche Konfiguration erfordern"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento de React Native e seu ecossistema","Limitado a fluxos de trabalho de atualização do React Native","As etapas do Expo SDK podem exigir configuração adicional"],"ru":["Требует знания React Native и его экосистемы","Ограничен рабочими процессами обновления React Native","Этапы Expo SDK могут требовать дополнительной настройки"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة React Native ونظامه البيئي","محدود بعمليات تحديث React Native","قد تتطلب خطوات Expo SDK تكوينًا إضافيًا"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"d8100fa8d5d42b4176bebc940be651444bd6734073e400313519f422a1fb6f13","repoEtag":"W/\"fbec4e53c6069bba17bd5aecbe1a694ffb809605f9853b2bacb8420dabd913c9\"","qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('anthropics/skills/doc-coauthoring', 'official', 'anthropics', 'skills', 'anthropics/skills', 'doc-coauthoring', 74575, 7681, 60, '2026-02-24T12:03:15Z', '2026-02-24T12:03:42.216Z', '2e47d78846faeea4a56e9809c52700087a15a2155a3f293a3efbaded81398ef4', '{"id":"anthropics/skills/doc-coauthoring","name":"doc-coauthoring","description":{"zh":"本技能提供结构化的工作流程，指导用户进行协同文档创建，包括上下文收集、内容精炼和读者测试","ja":"このスキルは、ドキュメントの共同作成を支援する構造化されたワークフローを提供します","ko":"이 스킬은 문서의 공조작성을 지원하는 구조화된 워크플ロー 제공","es":"El flujo de trabajo de coautoría de documentos es una herramienta de colaboración que utiliza agentes de IA para guiar a los usuarios a través de la creación de contenido estructurado","fr":"Le flux de travail de co-écriture de documents est un outil de collaboration qui utilise des agents IA pour guider les utilisateurs à travers la création de contenu structuré","de":"Der Koautoren-Workflow für Dokumente ist ein Kollaborations-Tool, das KI-Agenten verwendet, um Benutzer durch die Erstellung von strukturiertem Inhalt zu führen","pt":"O Doc Co-Authoring é um fluxo de trabalho estruturado para a criação colaborativa de documentos, utilizando tecnologias de IA para melhorar a eficiência e a qualidade do conteúdo","ru":"Doc Co-Authoring - это структурированный рабочий процесс для совместного создания документов, использующий технологии ИИ для повышения эффективности и качества контента","ar":"_doc Co-Authoring هو عملية عمل مهيكلة لإنشاء الوثائق التعاونية، باستخدام تكنولوجيا الذكاء الاصطناعي لتحسين الفعالية وجودة المحتوى","en":"Guide users through a structured workflow for co-authoring documentation. Use when user wants to write documentation, proposals, technical specs, decision docs, or similar structured content. This workflow helps users efficiently transfer context, refine content through iteration, and verify the ..."},"owner":"anthropics","repo":"skills","repoPath":"anthropics/skills","stars":74575,"forks":7681,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T12:03:15Z","topics":["agent-skills"],"skillMd":{"name":"doc-coauthoring","description":"Guide users through a structured workflow for co-authoring documentation. Use when user wants to write documentation, proposals, technical specs, decision docs, or similar structured content. This workflow helps users efficiently transfer context, refine content through iteration, and verify the doc works for readers. Trigger when user mentions writing docs, creating proposals, drafting specs, or similar documentation tasks.","bodyPreview":"# Doc Co-Authoring Workflow\n\nThis skill provides a structured workflow for guiding users through collaborative document creation. Act as an active guide, walking users through three stages: Context Gathering, Refinement & Structure, and Reader Testing.\n\n## When to Offer This Workflow\n\n**Trigger conditions:**\n- User mentions writing documentation: \"write a doc\", \"draft a proposal\", \"create a spec\", \"write up\"\n- User mentions specific doc types: \"PRD\", \"design doc\", \"decision doc\", \"RFC\"\n- User se","body":"# Doc Co-Authoring Workflow\n\nThis skill provides a structured workflow for guiding users through collaborative document creation. Act as an active guide, walking users through three stages: Context Gathering, Refinement & Structure, and Reader Testing.\n\n## When to Offer This Workflow\n\n**Trigger conditions:**\n- User mentions writing documentation: \"write a doc\", \"draft a proposal\", \"create a spec\", \"write up\"\n- User mentions specific doc types: \"PRD\", \"design doc\", \"decision doc\", \"RFC\"\n- User seems to be starting a substantial writing task\n\n**Initial offer:**\nOffer the user a structured workflow for co-authoring the document. Explain the three stages:\n\n1. **Context Gathering**: User provides all relevant context while Claude asks clarifying questions\n2. **Refinement & Structure**: Iteratively build each section through brainstorming and editing\n3. **Reader Testing**: Test the doc with a fresh Claude (no context) to catch blind spots before others read it\n\nExplain that this approach helps ensure the doc works well when others read it (including when they paste it into Claude). Ask if they want to try this workflow or prefer to work freeform.\n\nIf user declines, work freeform. If user accepts, proceed to Stage 1.\n\n## Stage 1: Context Gathering\n\n**Goal:** Close the gap between what the user knows and what Claude knows, enabling smart guidance later.\n\n### Initial Questions\n\nStart by asking the user for meta-context about the document:\n\n1. What type of document is this? (e.g., technical spec, decision doc, proposal)\n2. Who''s the primary audience?\n3. What''s the desired impact when someone reads this?\n4. Is there a template or specific format to follow?\n5. Any other constraints or context to know?\n\nInform them they can answer in shorthand or dump information however works best for them.\n\n**If user provides a template or mentions a doc type:**\n- Ask if they have a template document to share\n- If they provide a link to a shared document, use the appropriate integration to fetch it\n- If they provide a file, read it\n\n**If user mentions editing an existing shared document:**\n- Use the appropriate integration to read the current state\n- Check for images without alt-text\n- If images exist without alt-text, explain that when others use Claude to understand the doc, Claude won''t be able to see them. Ask if they want alt-text generated. If so, request they paste each image into chat for descriptive alt-text generation.\n\n### Info Dumping\n\nOnce initial questions are answered, encourage the user to dump all the context they have. Request information such as:\n- Background on the project/problem\n- Related team discussions or shared documents\n- Why alternative solutions aren''t being used\n- Organizational context (team dynamics, past incidents, politics)\n- Timeline pressures or constraints\n- Technical architecture or dependencies\n- Stakeholder concerns\n\nAdvise them not to worry about organizing it - just get it all out. Offer multiple ways to provide context:\n- Info dump stream-of-consciousness\n- Point to team channels or threads to read\n- Link to shared documents\n\n**If integrations are available** (e.g., Slack, Teams, Google Drive, SharePoint, or other MCP servers), mention that these can be used to pull in context directly.\n\n**If no integrations are detected and in Claude.ai or Claude app:** Suggest they can enable connectors in their Claude settings to allow pulling context from messaging apps and document storage directly.\n\nInform them clarifying questions will be asked once they''ve done their initial dump.\n\n**During context gathering:**\n\n- If user mentions team channels or shared documents:\n  - If integrations available: Inform them the content will be read now, then use the appropriate integration\n  - If integrations not available: Explain lack of access. Suggest they enable connectors in Claude settings, or paste the relevant content directly.\n\n- If user mentions entities/projects that are unknown:\n  - Ask if connected tools should be searched to learn more\n  - Wait for user confirmation before searching\n\n- As user provides context, track what''s being learned and what''s still unclear\n\n**Asking clarifying questions:**\n\nWhen user signals they''ve done their initial dump (or after substantial context provided), ask clarifying questions to ensure understanding:\n\nGenerate 5-10 numbered questions based on gaps in the context.\n\nInform them they can use shorthand to answer (e.g., \"1: yes, 2: see #channel, 3: no because backwards compat\"), link to more docs, point to channels to read, or just keep info-dumping. Whatever''s most efficient for them.\n\n**Exit condition:**\nSufficient context has been gathered when questions show understanding - when edge cases and trade-offs can be asked about without needing basics explained.\n\n**Transition:**\nAsk if there''s any more context they want to provide at this stage, or if it''s time to move on to drafting the document.\n\nIf user wants to add more, let them. When ready, proceed to Stage 2.\n\n## Stage 2: Refinement & Structure\n\n**Goal:** Build the document section by section through brainstorming, curation, and iterative refinement.\n\n**Instructions to user:**\nExplain that the document will be built section by section. For each section:\n1. Clarifying questions will be asked about what to include\n2. 5-20 options will be brainstormed\n3. User will indicate what to keep/remove/combine\n4. The section will be drafted\n5. It will be refined through surgical edits\n\nStart with whichever section has the most unknowns (usually the core decision/proposal), then work through the rest.\n\n**Section ordering:**\n\nIf the document structure is clear:\nAsk which section they''d like to start with.\n\nSuggest starting with whichever section has the most unknowns. For decision docs, that''s usually the core proposal. For specs, it''s typically the technical approach. Summary sections are best left for last.\n\nIf user doesn''t know what sections they need:\nBased on the type of document and template, suggest 3-5 sections appropriate for the doc type.\n\nAsk if this structure works, or if they want to adjust it.\n\n**Once structure is agreed:**\n\nCreate the initial document structure with placeholder text for all sections.\n\n**If access to artifacts is available:**\nUse `create_file` to create an artifact. This gives both Claude and the user a scaffold to work from.\n\nInform them that the initial structure with placeholders for all sections will be created.\n\nCreate artifact with all section headers and brief placeholder text like \"[To be written]\" or \"[Content here]\".\n\nProvide the scaffold link and indicate it''s time to fill in each section.\n\n**If no access to artifacts:**\nCreate a markdown file in the working directory. Name it appropriately (e.g., `decision-doc.md`, `technical-spec.md`).\n\nInform them that the initial structure with placeholders for all sections will be created.\n\nCreate file with all section headers and placeholder text.\n\nConfirm the filename has been created and indicate it''s time to fill in each section.\n\n**For each section:**\n\n### Step 1: Clarifying Questions\n\nAnnounce work will begin on the [SECTION NAME] section. Ask 5-10 clarifying questions about what should be included:\n\nGenerate 5-10 specific questions based on context and section purpose.\n\nInform them they can answer in shorthand or just indicate what''s important to cover.\n\n### Step 2: Brainstorming\n\nFor the [SECTION NAME] section, brainstorm [5-20] things that might be included, depending on the section''s complexity. Look for:\n- Context shared that might have been forgotten\n- Angles or considerations not yet mentioned\n\nGenerate 5-20 numbered options based on section complexity. At the end, offer to brainstorm more if they want additional options.\n\n### Step 3: Curation\n\nAsk which points should be kept, removed, or combined. Request brief justifications to help learn priorities for the next sections.\n\nProvide examples:\n- \"Keep 1,4,7,9\"\n- \"Remove 3 (duplicates 1)\"\n- \"Remove 6 (audience already knows this)\"\n- \"Combine 11 and 12\"\n\n**If user gives freeform feedback** (e.g., \"looks good\" or \"I like most of it but...\") instead of numbered selections, extract their preferences and proceed. Parse what they want kept/removed/changed and apply it.\n\n### Step 4: Gap Check\n\nBased on what they''ve selected, ask if there''s anything important missing for the [SECTION NAME] section.\n\n### Step 5: Drafting\n\nUse `str_replace` to replace the placeholder text for this section with the actual drafted content.\n\nAnnounce the [SECTION NAME] section will be drafted now based on what they''ve selected.\n\n**If using artifacts:**\nAfter drafting, provide a link to the artifact.\n\nAsk them to read through it and indicate what to change. Note that being specific helps learning for the next sections.\n\n**If using a file (no artifacts):**\nAfter drafting, confirm completion.\n\nInform them the [SECTION NAME] section has been drafted in [filename]. Ask them to read through it and indicate what to change. Note that being specific helps learning for the next sections.\n\n**Key instruction for user (include when drafting the first section):**\nProvide a note: Instead of editing the doc directly, ask them to indicate what to change. This helps learning of their style for future sections. For example: \"Remove the X bullet - already covered by Y\" or \"Make the third paragraph more concise\".\n\n### Step 6: Iterative Refinement\n\nAs user provides feedback:\n- Use `str_replace` to make edits (never reprint the whole doc)\n- **If using artifacts:** Provide link to artifact after each edit\n- **If using files:** Just confirm edits are complete\n- If user edits doc directly and asks to read it: mentally note the changes they made and keep them in mind for future sections (this shows their preferences)\n\n**Continue iterating** until user is satisfied with the section.\n\n### Quality Checking\n\nAfter 3 consecutive iterations with no substantial changes, ask if anything can be removed without losing important information.\n\nWhen section is done, confirm [SECTION NAME] is complete. Ask if ready to move to the next section.\n\n**Repeat for all sections.**\n\n### Near Completion\n\nAs approaching completion (80%+ of sections done), announce intention to re-read the entire document and check for:\n- Flow and consistency across sections\n- Redundancy or contradictions\n- Anything that feels like \"slop\" or generic filler\n- Whether every sentence carries weight\n\nRead entire document and provide feedback.\n\n**When all sections are drafted and refined:**\nAnnounce all sections are drafted. Indicate intention to review the complete document one more time.\n\nReview for overall coherence, flow, completeness.\n\nProvide any final suggestions.\n\nAsk if ready to move to Reader Testing, or if they want to refine anything else.\n\n## Stage 3: Reader Testing\n\n**Goal:** Test the document with a fresh Claude (no context bleed) to verify it works for readers.\n\n**Instructions to user:**\nExplain that testing will now occur to see if the document actually works for readers. This catches blind spots - things that make sense to the authors but might confuse others.\n\n### Testing Approach\n\n**If access to sub-agents is available (e.g., in Claude Code):**\n\nPerform the testing directly without user involvement.\n\n### Step 1: Predict Reader Questions\n\nAnnounce intention to predict what questions readers might ask when trying to discover this document.\n\nGenerate 5-10 questions that readers would realistically ask.\n\n### Step 2: Test with Sub-Agent\n\nAnnounce that these questions will be tested with a fresh Claude instance (no context from this conversation).\n\nFor each question, invoke a sub-agent with just the document content and the question.\n\nSummarize what Reader Claude got right/wrong for each question.\n\n### Step 3: Run Additional Checks\n\nAnnounce additional checks will be performed.\n\nInvoke sub-agent to check for ambiguity, false assumptions, contradictions.\n\nSummarize any issues found.\n\n### Step 4: Report and Fix\n\nIf issues found:\nReport that Reader Claude struggled with specific issues.\n\nList the specific issues.\n\nIndicate intention to fix these gaps.\n\nLoop back to refinement for problematic sections.\n\n---\n\n**If no access to sub-agents (e.g., claude.ai web interface):**\n\nThe user will need to do the testing manually.\n\n### Step 1: Predict Reader Questions\n\nAsk what questions people might ask when trying to discover this document. What would they type into Claude.ai?\n\nGenerate 5-10 questions that readers would realistically ask.\n\n### Step 2: Setup Testing\n\nProvide testing instructions:\n1. Open a fresh Claude conversation: https://claude.ai\n2. Paste or share the document content (if using a shared doc platform with connectors enabled, provide the link)\n3. Ask Reader Claude the generated questions\n\nFor each question, instruct Reader Claude to provide:\n- The answer\n- Whether anything was ambiguous or unclear\n- What knowledge/context the doc assumes is already known\n\nCheck if Reader Claude gives correct answers or misinterprets anything.\n\n### Step 3: Additional Checks\n\nAlso ask Reader Claude:\n- \"What in this doc might be ambiguous or unclear to readers?\"\n- \"What knowledge or context does this doc assume readers already have?\"\n- \"Are there any internal contradictions or inconsistencies?\"\n\n### Step 4: Iterate Based on Results\n\nAsk what Reader Claude got wrong or struggled with. Indicate intention to fix those gaps.\n\nLoop back to refinement for any problematic sections.\n\n---\n\n### Exit Condition (Both Approaches)\n\nWhen Reader Claude consistently answers questions correctly and doesn''t surface new gaps or ambiguities, the doc is ready.\n\n## Final Review\n\nWhen Reader Testing passes:\nAnnounce the doc has passed Reader Claude testing. Before completion:\n\n1. Recommend they do a final read-through themselves - they own this document and are responsible for its quality\n2. Suggest double-checking any facts, links, or technical details\n3. Ask them to verify it achieves the impact they wanted\n\nAsk if they want one more review, or if the work is done.\n\n**If user wants final review, provide it. Otherwise:**\nAnnounce document completion. Provide a few final tips:\n- Consider linking this conversation in an appendix so readers can see how the doc was developed\n- Use appendices to provide depth without bloating the main doc\n- Update the doc as feedback is received from real readers\n\n## Tips for Effective Guidance\n\n**Tone:**\n- Be direct and procedural\n- Explain rationale briefly when it affects user behavior\n- Don''t try to \"sell\" the approach - just execute it\n\n**Handling Deviations:**\n- If user wants to skip a stage: Ask if they want to skip this and write freeform\n- If user seems frustrated: Acknowledge this is taking longer than expected. Suggest ways to move faster\n- Always give user agency to adjust the process\n\n**Context Management:**\n- Throughout, if context is missing on something mentioned, proactively ask\n- Don''t let gaps accumulate - address them as they come up\n\n**Artifact Management:**\n- Use `create_file` for drafting full sections\n- Use `str_replace` for all edits\n- Provide artifact link after every change\n- Never use artifacts for brainstorming lists - that''s just conversation\n\n**Quality over Speed:**\n- Don''t rush through stages\n- Each iteration should make meaningful improvements\n- The goal is a document that actually works for readers\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-24T12:03:42.216Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能协同文档编写","ja":"AIエージェントによるドキュメント共同作成","ko":"AI 에이전트를 이용한 문서 공조작성","es":"Herramientas de Coautoría de Documentos con Agentes de IA","fr":"Outils de Co-écriture de Documents avec des Agents IA","de":"Koautoren-Tools für Dokumente mit KI-Agenten","pt":"Ferramentas de IA para Coautoria de Documentos - Doc Co-A...","ru":"ИИ Агенты для Совместного Создания Документов - Doc Co-Au...","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي لتعاونية كتابة الوثائق - Doc Co-Au...","en":"doc-coauthoring"},"description":{"zh":"本技能提供结构化的工作流程，指导用户进行协同文档创建，包括上下文收集、内容精炼和读者测试","ja":"このスキルは、ドキュメントの共同作成を支援する構造化されたワークフローを提供します","ko":"이 스킬은 문서의 공조작성을 지원하는 구조화된 워크플ロー 제공","es":"El flujo de trabajo de coautoría de documentos es una herramienta de colaboración que utiliza agentes de IA para guiar a los usuarios a través de la creación...","fr":"Le flux de travail de co-écriture de documents est un outil de collaboration qui utilise des agents IA pour guider les utilisateurs à travers la création de ...","de":"Der Koautoren-Workflow für Dokumente ist ein Kollaborations-Tool, das KI-Agenten verwendet, um Benutzer durch die Erstellung von strukturiertem Inhalt zu führen","pt":"O Doc Co-Authoring é um fluxo de trabalho estruturado para a criação colaborativa de documentos, utilizando tecnologias de IA para melhorar a eficiência e a ...","ru":"Doc Co-Authoring - это структурированный рабочий процесс для совместного создания документов, использующий технологии ИИ для повышения эффективности и качест...","ar":"_doc Co-Authoring هو عملية عمل مهيكلة لإنشاء الوثائق التعاونية، باستخدام تكنولوجيا الذكاء الاصطناعي لتحسين الفعالية وجودة المحتوى","en":"Guide users through a structured workflow for co-authoring documentation. Use when user wants to write documentation, proposals, technical specs, decision do..."},"definition":{"en":"Guide users through a structured workflow for co-authoring documentation. Use when user wants to write documentation, proposals, technical specs, decision docs, or similar structured content. This workflow helps users efficiently transfer context, refine content through iteration, and verify the doc works for readers. Trigger when user mentions writing docs, creating proposals, drafting specs, or similar documentation tasks."},"features":{"zh":["结构化的工作流程","上下文收集和内容精炼","读者测试和反馈","高效的文档创建和协作","支持多种文档类型"],"ja":["構造化されたワークフロー","コンテキストの収集とコンテンツの精製","リーダーテストとフィードバック","効率的なドキュメントの作成と共同作成","複数のドキュメント形式をサポート"],"ko":["구조화된 워크플ロー","콘텍스트 수집 및 콘텐츠 정련","리더 테스트 및 피드백","효율적인 문서 생성 및 공조작성","다양한 문서 형식 지원"],"es":["Flujo de trabajo estructurado para la creación de documentos","Colaboración en tiempo real con agentes de IA","Revisión y verificación de contenido","Creación de propuestas y especificaciones técnicas","Documentos de decisión y RFC"],"fr":["Flux de travail structuré pour la création de documents","Collaboration en temps réel avec des agents IA","Révision et vérification de contenu","Création de propositions et de spécifications techniques","Documents de décision et RFC"],"de":["Strukturierter Workflow für die Erstellung von Dokumenten","Echtzeit-Kollaboration mit KI-Agenten","Überprüfung und Verifizierung von Inhalt","Erstellung von Vorschlägen und technischen Spezifikationen","Dokumente für Entscheidungen und RFC"],"pt":["Fluxo de trabalho estruturado para coautoria de documentos","Utilização de tecnologias de IA para melhorar a eficiência","Melhoria da qualidade do conteúdo através da iteração","Verificação do documento para garantir a eficácia","Integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["Структурированный рабочий процесс для совместного создания документов","Использование технологий ИИ для повышения эффективности","Повышение качества контента через итерацию","Проверка документа для обеспечения эффективности","Интеграция с инструментами разработки программного обеспечения"],"ar":["عملية عمل مهيكلة لإنشاء الوثائق التعاونية","استخدام تكنولوجيا الذكاء الاصطناعي لتحسين الفعالية","تحسين جودة المحتوى من خلال التكرار","فحص الوثيقة لضمان الفعالية","التكامل مع أدوات تطوير البرمجيات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能协同文档编写","结构化工作流程","文档创建","协作编辑","读者测试","高效文档创建"],"ja":["AIエージェントによるドキュメント共同作成","構造化されたワークフロー","ドキュメントの作成","共同編集","リーダーテスト","効率的なドキュメント作成"],"ko":["AI 에이전트를 이용한 문서 공조작성","구조화된 워크플ロー","문서 생성","공조편집","리더 테스트","효율적인 문서 생성"],"es":["agentes de IA","coautoría de documentos","colaboración en tiempo real","creación de contenido estructurado","propuestas y especificaciones técnicas","documentos de decisión","RFC","herramientas de IA para desarrolladores"],"fr":["agents IA","co-écriture de documents","collaboration en temps réel","création de contenu structuré","propositions et spécifications techniques","documents de décision","RFC","outils IA pour développeurs"],"de":["KI-Agenten","Koautoren von Dokumenten","Echtzeit-Kollaboration","Erstellung von strukturiertem Inhalt","Vorschläge und technische Spezifikationen","Dokumente für Entscheidungen","RFC","KI-Tools für Entwickler"],"pt":["Ferramentas 